API","ja":"Kotlin DSL Telegram Bot API","ko":"Kotlin DSL Telegram Bot API","es":"El skill handle-callback-query es un wrapper de la API de bot de Telegram con Kotlin DSL para manejar consultas de devolución de llamada de manera efectiva.","fr":"Le skill handle-callback-query est un wrapper de l''API de bot Telegram avec Kotlin DSL pour gérer les requêtes de rappel de manière efficace.","de":"Das Skill handle-callback-query ist ein Wrapper der Telegram-Bot-API mit Kotlin DSL zum effektiven Umgang mit Callback-Abfragen.","pt":"O handle-callback-query é uma biblioteca Kotlin que fornece uma API simples para lidar com consultas de retorno no Telegram Bot API","ru":"Handle-callback-query - это библиотека Kotlin, предоставляющая простой API для обработки запросов обратного вызова в Telegram Bot API","ar":"handle-callback-query هي مكتبة Kotlin توفر واجهة برمجة تطبيقات بسيطة لمعالجة استعلامات الرد في Telegram Bot API","en":"Telegram Bot API wrapper with handy Kotlin DSL."},"definition":{"en":"Telegram Bot API wrapper with handy Kotlin DSL."},"features":{"zh":["Kotlin DSL","Telegram Bot API","Callback Query","Handler Registration","Async Programming"],"ja":["Kotlin DSL","Telegram Bot API","Callback Query","Handler Registration","Async Programming"],"ko":["Kotlin DSL","Telegram Bot API","Callback Query","Handler Registration","Async Programming"],"es":["Registro de manejadores de consultas de devolución de llamada","Respuesta automática a consultas de devolución de llamada","Uso de Kotlin DSL para una sintaxis más clara","Compatibilidad con la API de bot de Telegram","Manejo de estados de carga y respuesta"],"fr":["Enregistrement de gestionnaires de requêtes de rappel","Réponse automatique aux requêtes de rappel","Utilisation de Kotlin DSL pour une syntaxe plus claire","Compatibilité avec l''API de bot Telegram","Gestion des états de chargement et de réponse"],"de":["Registrierung von Callback-Abfrage-Handlern","Automatische Antwort auf Callback-Abfragen","Verwendung von Kotlin DSL für eine klarere Syntax","Kompatibilität mit der Telegram-Bot-API","Verwaltung von Ladezuständen und Antworten"],"pt":["Tratamento de consultas de retorno com Kotlin DSL","Registro de manipuladores de consultas de retorno","Resposta automática às consultas de retorno","Suporte a mensagens personalizadas","Integração com o Telegram Bot API"],"ru":["Обработка запросов обратного вызова с помощью Kotlin DSL","Регистрация обработчиков запросов обратного вызова","Автоматический ответ на запросы обратного вызова","Поддержка пользовательских сообщений","Интеграция с Telegram Bot API"],"ar":["معالجة استعلامات الرد مع Kotlin DSL","تسجيل معالجات استعلامات الرد","الرد التلقائي على استعلامات الرد","دعم الرسائل المخصصة","التكامل مع Telegram Bot API"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Kotlin DSL","Telegram Bot API","Callback Query","Handler Registration","Async Programming","Kotlin Telegram Bot","Telegram Bot Kotlin DSL"],"ja":["Kotlin DSL","Telegram Bot API","Callback Query","Handler Registration","Async Programming","Kotlin Telegram Bot","Telegram Bot Kotlin DSL"],"ko":["Kotlin DSL","Telegram Bot API","Callback Query","Handler Registration","Async Programming","Kotlin Telegram Bot","Telegram Bot Kotlin DSL"],"es":["manejo de consultas de devolución de llamada","Telegram bot API","Kotlin DSL","desarrollo de bots","programación de bots","API de bot de Telegram","Kotlin para desarrollo de bots"],"fr":["gestion des requêtes de rappel","API de bot Telegram","Kotlin DSL","développement de bots","programmation de bots","API de bot Telegram","Kotlin pour développement de bots"],"de":["Umgang mit Callback-Abfragen","Telegram-Bot-API","Kotlin DSL","Entwicklung von Bots","Programmierung von Bots","Telegram-Bot-API","Kotlin für Bot-Entwicklung"],"pt":["handle-callback-query","Kotlin DSL","Telegram Bot API","tratamento de consultas de retorno","registro de manipuladores","resposta automática","mensagens personalizadas"],"ru":["handle-callback-query","Kotlin DSL","Telegram Bot API","обработка запросов обратного вызова","регистрация обработчиков","автоматический ответ","пользовательские сообщения"],"ar":["handle-callback-query","Kotlin DSL","Telegram Bot API","معالجة استعلامات الرد","تسجيل معالجات","الرد التلقائي","رسائل مخصصة"]}},"owner":"vendelieu","repo":"telegram-bot","repoPath":"vendelieu/telegram-bot","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.539Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"handle-callback-query","description":"[Bot developer] Handles inline keyboard button presses and provides user feedback via answerCallbackQuery. Use when processing callback queries, answering button clicks, or updating messages after inline button interaction.","bodyPreview":"# Handle Callback Query\n\n## Quick Start\n\nRegister a handler and **always** answer the callback query to stop the loading state:\n\n```kotlin\nbot.setFunctionality {\n    onCallbackQuery {\n        val cq = update.callbackQuery\n        answerCallbackQuery(cq.id).options { text = \"Done!\" }.send(user, bot)\n        when (cq.data) {\n            \"yes\" -> message(\"You said yes!\").send(user, bot)\n            \"no\" -> message(\"You said no.\").send(user, bot)\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Handler Registration\n\n- **D","body":"# Handle Callback Query\n\n## Quick Start\n\nRegister a handler and **always** answer the callback query to stop the loading state:\n\n```kotlin\nbot.setFunctionality {\n    onCallbackQuery {\n        val cq = update.callbackQuery\n        answerCallbackQuery(cq.id).options { text = \"Done!\" }.send(user, bot)\n        when (cq.data) {\n            \"yes\" -> message(\"You said yes!\").send(user, bot)\n            \"no\" -> message(\"You said no.\").send(user, bot)\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Handler Registration\n\n- **DSL**: `onCallbackQuery { }` — typed `ActivityCtx<CallbackQueryUpdate>`\n- **Annotation**: `@CommandHandler.CallbackQuery([\"prefix\"])` with optional `autoAnswer = true`\n\n## Accessing Callback Data\n\n- `update.callbackQuery` — the CallbackQuery\n- `callbackQuery.id` — required for answerCallbackQuery\n- `callbackQuery.data` — button data (1-64 bytes), may be null\n- `callbackQuery.from` — user who pressed\n- `callbackQuery.message` — message with the button (if any)\n\n## Answering the Query\n\n**Always call** `answerCallbackQuery` to remove the loading state:\n\n```kotlin\nanswerCallbackQuery(callbackQuery.id).send(user, bot)\n```\n\nWith options:\n\n```kotlin\nanswerCallbackQuery(callbackQuery.id).options {\n    text = \"Saved!\"           // Notification text (0-200 chars)\n    showAlert = true         // Alert instead of top notification\n    url = \"https://...\"      // URL to open (e.g. t.me/bot?start=xxx)\n    cacheTime = 60           // Cache result (seconds)\n}.send(user, bot)\n```\n\n## Parsing Callback Data\n\nUse prefixes for routing: `\"action:id\"`, `\"vote:123\"`:\n\n```kotlin\ncq.data?.split(\":\", limit = 2)?.let { (action, id) ->\n    when (action) {\n        \"vote\" -> handleVote(id.toLong())\n        \"page\" -> showPage(id.toInt())\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## @ParamMapping\n\nMaps handler parameters to keys in the parsed parameters map. Use with `@CommandHandler.CallbackQuery` when the ArgumentParser extracts named values from callback data (e.g. `page=1`, `id=123`):\n\n```kotlin\n@CommandHandler.CallbackQuery([\"vote\"], autoAnswer = true)\nsuspend fun handleVote(\n    @ParamMapping(\"id\") itemId: Long,\n    user: User,\n    bot: TelegramBot\n) {\n    message(\"Voted for $itemId\").send(user, bot)\n}\n```\n\n- `@ParamMapping(\"name\")` — parameter is resolved from `parameters[\"name\"]` (parsed by ArgumentParser)\n- Supported types: String, Int, Long, Short, Float, Double\n- Use when callback data exceeds simple routing and you need typed parameters\n\n## Updating the Message\n\nAfter handling, optionally edit the message or its markup:\n\n- `editMessageText` — change text\n- `editMessageReplyMarkup` — change/remove buttons\n\n## Reference\n\n- [AnswerCallbackQuery.kt](telegram-bot/src/commonMain/kotlin/eu/vendeli/tgbot/api/answer/AnswerCallbackQuery.kt)\n- [CallbackQuery.kt](telegram-bot/src/commonMain/kotlin/eu/vendeli/tgbot/types/common/CallbackQuery.kt)\n- [ParamMapping.kt](telegram-bot/src/commonMain/kotlin/eu/vendeli/tgbot/annotations/ParamMapping.kt)\n- [FunctionalDSLUtils.kt](telegram-bot/src/commonMain/kotlin/eu/vendeli/tgbot/utils/common/FunctionalDSLUtils.kt)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T00:56:36.696Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Telegram Bot Automation Agents requiring interactive button response handling.","zh":"Ideal for Telegram Bot Automation Agents requiring interactive button response handling.","ja":"Ideal for Telegram Bot Automation Agents requiring interactive button response handling.","ko":"Ideal for Telegram Bot Automation Agents requiring interactive button response handling.","es":"Ideal for Telegram Bot Automation Agents requiring interactive button response handling.","fr":"Ideal for Telegram Bot Automation Agents requiring interactive button response handling.","de":"Ideal for Telegram Bot Automation Agents requiring interactive button response handling.","pt":"Ideal for Telegram Bot Automation Agents requiring interactive button response handling.","ru":"Ideal for Telegram Bot Automation Agents requiring interactive button response handling.","ar":"Ideal for Telegram Bot Automation Agents requiring interactive button response handling."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables direct processing of Telegram callback queries with Kotlin DSL, automatically answering queries to stop loading states and providing structured response handling based on callback data patterns.","zh":"Enables direct processing of Telegram callback queries with Kotlin DSL, automatically answering queries to stop loading states and providing structured response handling based on callback data patterns.","ja":"Enables direct processing of Telegram callback queries with Kotlin DSL, automatically answering queries to stop loading states and providing structured response handling based on callback data patterns.","ko":"Enables direct processing of Telegram callback queries with Kotlin DSL, automatically answering queries to stop loading states and providing structured response handling based on callback data patterns.","es":"Enables direct processing of Telegram callback queries with Kotlin DSL, automatically answering queries to stop loading states and providing structured response handling based on callback data patterns.","fr":"Enables direct processing of Telegram callback queries with Kotlin DSL, automatically answering queries to stop loading states and providing structured response handling based on callback data patterns.","de":"Enables direct processing of Telegram callback queries with Kotlin DSL, automatically answering queries to stop loading states and providing structured response handling based on callback data patterns.","pt":"Enables direct processing of Telegram callback queries with Kotlin DSL, automatically answering queries to stop loading states and providing structured response handling based on callback data patterns.","ru":"Enables direct processing of Telegram callback queries with Kotlin DSL, automatically answering queries to stop loading states and providing structured response handling based on callback data patterns.","ar":"Enables direct processing of Telegram callback queries with Kotlin DSL, automatically answering queries to stop loading states and providing structured response handling based on callback data patterns."},"useCases":{"en":["Processing inline keyboard button interactions","Handling user confirmation/cancellation flows","Managing multi-step bot conversations","Responding to callback data patterns"],"zh":["Processing inline keyboard button interactions","Handling user confirmation/cancellation flows","Managing multi-step bot conversations","Responding to callback data patterns"],"ja":["Processing inline keyboard button interactions","Handling user confirmation/cancellation flows","Managing multi-step bot conversations","Responding to callback data patterns"],"ko":["Processing inline keyboard button interactions","Handling user confirmation/cancellation flows","Managing multi-step bot conversations","Responding to callback data patterns"],"es":["Processing inline keyboard button interactions","Handling user confirmation/cancellation flows","Managing multi-step bot conversations","Responding to callback data patterns"],"fr":["Processing inline keyboard button interactions","Handling user confirmation/cancellation flows","Managing multi-step bot conversations","Responding to callback data patterns"],"de":["Processing inline keyboard button interactions","Handling user confirmation/cancellation flows","Managing multi-step bot conversations","Responding to callback data patterns"],"pt":["Processing inline keyboard button interactions","Handling user confirmation/cancellation flows","Managing multi-step bot conversations","Responding to callback data patterns"],"ru":["Processing inline keyboard button interactions","Handling user confirmation/cancellation flows","Managing multi-step bot conversations","Responding to callback data patterns"],"ar":["Processing inline keyboard button interactions","Handling user confirmation/cancellation flows","Managing multi-step bot conversations","Responding to callback data patterns"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Telegram Bot API integration","Kotlin DSL specific implementation","Must always answer callback queries to stop loading state"],"zh":["Requires Telegram Bot API integration","Kotlin DSL specific implementation","Must always answer callback queries to stop loading state"],"ja":["Requires Telegram Bot API integration","Kotlin DSL specific implementation","Must always answer callback queries to stop loading state"],"ko":["Requires Telegram Bot API integration","Kotlin DSL specific implementation","Must always answer callback queries to stop loading sta