e":{"zh":"Supabase Postgres最佳实践指南","ja":"Supabase Postgresベストプラクティスガイド","ko":"Supabase Postgres 최적화 가이드","es":"Mejores prácticas de Supabase Postgres","fr":"Meilleures pratiques Supabase Postgres","de":"Supabase Postgres Best Practices","pt":"Melhores Práticas Supabase Postgres","ru":"Лучшие практики Supabase Postgres","ar":"أفضل الممارسات سوبابيس بوستجرس","en":"supabase-postgres-best-practices"},"description":{"zh":"Supabase Postgres最佳实践指南，为开发者提供Postgres性能优化的综合指南","ja":"Supabase Postgresベストプラクティスガイド，開発者向けのPostgresパフォーマンス最適化の包括的なガイド","ko":"Supabase Postgres 최적화 가이드, 개발자를 위한 Postgres 성능 최적화 종합 가이드","es":"La guía de mejores prácticas de Supabase Postgres es una guía completa para la optimización del rendimiento de Postgres, que abarca 8 categorías de reglas pa...","fr":"Le guide des meilleures pratiques Supabase Postgres est un guide complet pour l''optimisation des performances de Postgres, qui couvre 8 catégories de règles ...","de":"Der Leitfaden für die Best Practices von Supabase Postgres ist ein umfassender Leitfaden für die Leistungsoptimierung von Postgres, der 8 Kategorien von Rege...","pt":"Guia de otimização de desempenho completo para Postgres, mantido pela Supabase. Contém regras em 8 categorias, priorizadas por impacto para orientar a otimiz...","ru":"Полное руководство по оптимизации производительности Postgres, поддерживаемое Supabase. Содержит правила в 8 категориях, отсортированные по влиянию для автом...","ar":"دليل شامل لتحسين أداء بوستجرس، مدعوم من سوبابيس. يتضمن قواعد في 8 فئات، مصنفة حسب التأثير لتوجيه تحسين الاستفسارات التلقائي وتصميم المخطط","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["SQL查询优化","schema设计优化","索引实现","查询优化","数据库性能优化","连接池配置","Postgres特性优化"],"ja":["SQLクエリ最適化","スキーマ設計最適化","インデックス実装","クエリ最適化","データベースパフォーマンス最適化","コネクションプール設定","Postgres特性最適化"],"ko":["SQL 쿼리 최적화","스키마 디자인 최적화","인덱스 구현","쿼리 최적화","데이터베이스 성능 최적화","연결 풀 구성","Postgres 특성 최적화"],"es":["Optimización de consultas SQL","Diseño de esquemas eficientes","Implementación de índices","Optimización de rendimiento de la base de datos","Configuración de pooling de conexiones","Escalabilidad de la base de datos"],"fr":["Optimisation des requêtes SQL","Conception de schémas efficaces","Mise en œuvre d''index","Optimisation des performances de la base de données","Configuration du pooling de connexions","Évolutivité de la base de données"],"de":["Optimierung von SQL-Abfragen","Effizientes Schemadesign","Implementierung von Indizes","Leistungsoptimierung der Datenbank","Konfiguration des Connection-Pooling","Skalierbarkeit der Datenbank"],"pt":["Otimização de consultas","Design de esquema","Implementação de índices","Otimização de desempenho","Configuração de pooling de conexões","Escalar para melhor desempenho"],"ru":["Оптимизация запросов","Проектирование схемы","Реализация индексов","Оптимизация производительности","Настройка пулинга подключений","Масштабирование для лучшей производительности"],"ar":["تحسين الاستفسارات","تصميم المخطط","تنفيذ الفهارس","تحسين الأداء","تكوين مجموعة الاتصال","توسيع النطاق لتحسين الأداء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Supabase","Postgres","性能优化","SQL查询","schema设计","索引","查询优化","数据库性能"],"ja":["Supabase","Postgres","パフォーマンス最適化","SQLクエリ","スキーマ設計","インデックス","クエリ最適化","データベースパフォーマンス"],"ko":["Supabase","Postgres","성능 최적화","SQL 쿼리","스키마 디자인","인덱스","쿼리 최적화","데이터베이스 성능"],"es":["Supabase Postgres","mejores prácticas","optimización de rendimiento","consultas SQL","diseño de esquemas","índices","pooling de conexiones","escalabilidad"],"fr":["Supabase Postgres","meilleures pratiques","optimisation des performances","requêtes SQL","conception de schémas","index","pooling de connexions","évolutivité"],"de":["Supabase Postgres","Best Practices","Leistungsoptimierung","SQL-Abfragen","Schemadesign","Indizes","Connection-Pooling","Skalierbarkeit"],"pt":["Supabase","Postgres","otimização de desempenho","consultas SQL","design de esquema","índices","pooling de conexões","escalabilidade"],"ru":["Supabase","Postgres","оптимизация производительности","SQL-запросы","проектирование схемы","индексы","пулинг подключений","масштабируемость"],"ar":["سوبابيس","بوستجرس","تحسين الأداء","استفسارات SQL","تصميم المخطط","الفهارس","مجموعة الاتصال","توسيع النطاق"]}},"owner":"sooom1627","repo":"linkcache","repoPath":"sooom1627/linkcache","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.539Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"supabase-postgres-best-practices","description":"Postgres performance optimization and best practices from Supabase. Use this skill when writing, reviewing, or optimizing Postgres queries, schema designs, or database configurations.","version":"1.1.0","bodyPreview":"# Supabase Postgres Best Practices\n\nComprehensive performance optimization guide for Postgres, maintained by Supabase. Contains rules across 8 categories, prioritized by impact to guide automated query optimization and schema design.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n\n- Writing SQL queries or designing schemas\n- Implementing indexes or query optimization\n- Reviewing database performance issues\n- Configuring connection pooling or scaling\n- Optimizing for Postgres-specific featur","body":"# Supabase Postgres Best Practices\n\nComprehensive performance optimization guide for Postgres, maintained by Supabase. Contains rules across 8 categories, prioritized by impact to guide automated query optimization and schema design.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n\n- Writing SQL queries or designing schemas\n- Implementing indexes or query optimization\n- Reviewing database performance issues\n- Configuring connection pooling or scaling\n- Optimizing for Postgres-specific features\n- Working with Row-Level Security (RLS)\n\n## Rule Categories by Priority\n\n| Priority | Category                 | Impact      | Prefix      |\n| -------- | ------------------------ | ----------- | ----------- |\n| 1        | Query Performance        | CRITICAL    | `query-`    |\n| 2        | Connection Management    | CRITICAL    | `conn-`     |\n| 3        | Security & RLS           | CRITICAL    | `security-` |\n| 4        | Schema Design            | HIGH        | `schema-`   |\n| 5        | Concurrency & Locking    | MEDIUM-HIGH | `lock-`     |\n| 6        | Data Access Patterns     | MEDIUM      | `data-`     |\n| 7        | Monitoring & Diagnostics | LOW-MEDIUM  | `monitor-`  |\n| 8        | Advanced Features        | LOW         | `advanced-` |\n\n## How to Use\n\nRead individual rule files for detailed explanations and SQL examples:\n\n```\nreferences/query-missing-indexes.md\nreferences/schema-partial-indexes.md\nreferences/_sections.md\n```\n\nEach rule file contains:\n\n- Brief explanation of why it matters\n- Incorrect SQL example with explanation\n- Correct SQL example with explanation\n- Optional EXPLAIN output or metrics\n- Additional context and references\n- Supabase-specific notes (when applicable)\n\n## References\n\n- https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/\n- https://supabase.com/docs\n- https://wiki.postgresql.org/wiki/Performance_Optimization\n- https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/overview\n- https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/row-level-security\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T00:56:46.846Z","qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('natalialewis/CS4610-Supabase-NextJS-Starter-App/nextjs-supabase-starter', 'community', 'natalialewis', 'CS4610-Supabase-NextJS-Starter-App', 'natalialewis/CS4610-Supabase-NextJS-Starter-App', 'nextjs-supabase-starter', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.539Z', '2026-02-19T00:56:40.396Z', NULL, '{"id":"natalialewis/CS4610-Supabase-NextJS-Starter-App/nextjs-supabase-starter","name":"nextjs-supabase-starter","description":{"zh":"Next.js + Supabase 入门应用是现代 Web 应用的快速开发和部署解决方案","ja":"Next.js + Supabase スターター アプリは、モダン Web アプリの迅速な開発とデプロイのためのソリューションです","ko":"Next.js + Supabase 시작 애플리케이션은 현대적인 웹 애플리케이션의 빠른 개발 및 배포를 위한 솔루션입니다","es":"El kit de inicio de Next.js y Supabase permite crear aplicaciones web modernas con autenticación de manera eficiente","fr":"Le kit de démarrage de Next.js et Supabase permet de créer des applications web modernes avec authentification de manière efficace","de":"Das Starter-Kit von Next.js und Supabase ermöglicht die effiziente Erstellung moderner Webanwendungen mit Authentifizierung","pt":"O starter Next.js e Supabase é uma ferramenta para criar aplicações web modernas com autenticação","ru":"Стартовый проект Next.js и Supabase — это инструмент для создания современных веб-приложений с аутентификацией","ar":"إعداد Next.js و Supabase هو أداة لإنشاء تطبيقات ويب حديثة مع المصادقة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Next.js + Supabase 入门应用","ja":"Next.js + Supabase スターター アプリ","ko":"Next.js + Supabase 시작 애플리케이션","es":"Inicio de Next.js y Supabase","fr":"Début de Next.js et Supabase","de":"Next.js und Supabase Starter","pt":"Inicie com Next.js e Supabase","ru":"Начните с Next.js и Supabase","ar":"ابدأ مع Next.js و Supabase","en":"nextjs-supabase-starter"},"description":{"zh":"Next.js + Supabase 入门应用是现代 Web 应用的快速开发和部署解决方案","ja":"Next.js + Supabase スターター アプリは、モダン Web アプリの迅速な開発とデプロイのためのソリューションです","ko":"Next.js + Supabase 시작 애플리케이션은 현대적인 웹 애플리케이션의 빠른 개발 및 배포를 위한 솔루션입니다","es":"El kit de inicio de Next.js y Supabase permite crear aplicaciones web modernas con autenticación de manera eficiente","fr":"Le kit de démarrage de Next.js et Supabase permet de créer des applications web modernes avec authentification de manière efficace","de":"Das Starter-Kit von Next.js und Supabase ermöglicht die effiziente Erstellung moderner Webanwendungen mit Authentifizierung","pt":"O starter Next.js e Supabase é uma ferramenta para criar aplicações web modernas com autenticação","ru":"Стартовый проект Next.js и Supabase — это инструмент для создания современных веб-приложений с аутентификацией","ar":"إعداد Next.js و Supabase هو أداة لإنشاء تطبيقات ويب حديثة مع المصادقة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["使用最新的 Next.js 版本","遵循 Next.js 13+ App Router 约定","支持身份验证","易于设置和使用","包含现代 Web 应用的必备功能"],"ja":["最新の Next.js バージョンを使用","Next.js 13+ App Router の規約に従う","認証をサポート","簡単に設定と使用","モダン Web アプリの必須機能を含む"],"ko":["최신 Next.js 버전 사용","Next.js 13+ App Router 규약 준수","인증 지원","설치 및 사용이 쉬움","현대적인 웹 애플리케이션의 필수 기능 포함"],"es":["Uso de la última versión de Next.js","Seguimiento de las convenciones del App Router de Next.js 13+","Autenticación para aplicaciones web modernas","Documentación clara y fácil de seguir","Configuración sencilla y rápida"],"fr":["Utilisation de la dernière version de Next.js","Suivi des conventions du App Router de Next.js 13+","Authentification pour les applications web modernes","Documentation claire et facile à suivre","Configuration simple et rapide"],"de":["Verwendung der neuesten Version von Next.js","Befolgen der Konventionen des App Routers von Next.js 13+","Authentifizierung für moderne Webanwendungen","Klare und leicht verständliche Dokumentation","Einfache und schnelle Konfiguration"],"pt":["Suporte à autenticação","Integração com Supabase","Uso do App Router do Next.js","Documentação clara e concisa","Configuração fácil","Recursos essenciais para aplicações web modernas"],"ru":["Поддержка аутентификации","Интеграция с Supabase","Использование App Router Next.js","Ясная и краткая документация","Легкая настройка","Необходимые функции для современных веб-приложений"],"ar":["دعم المصادقة","التكامل مع Supabase","استخدام App Router من Next.js","توثيق واضح وموجز","إعداد سهل","ميزات أساسية لتطبيقات الويب الحديثة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Next.js","Supabase","现代 Web 应用","快速开发","部署","身份验证","App Router"],"ja":["Next.js","Supabase","モダン Web アプリ","迅速な開発","デプロイ","認証","App Router"],"ko":["Next.js","Supabase","현대적인 웹 애플리케이션","빠른 개발","배포","인증","App Router"],"es":["Next.js","Supabase","aplicaciones web modernas","autenticación","desarrollo web","starter kit","App Router","documentación clara"],"fr":["Next.js","Supabase","applications web modernes","authentification","développement web","kit de démarrage","App Router","documentation claire"],"de":["Next.js","Supabase","moderne Webanwendungen","Authentifizierung","Webentwicklung","Starter-Kit","App Router","klare Dokumentation"],"pt":["Next.js","Supabase","autenticação","aplicações web modernas","App Router","desenvolvimento web","tecnologias web","escalabilidade","documentação"],"ru":["Next.js","Supabase","аутентификация","современные веб-приложения","App Router","веб-разработка","веб-технологии","масштабируемость","документация"],"ar":["Next.js","Supabase","المصادقة","تطبيقات الويب الحديثة","App Router","تطوير الويب","تكنولوجيا الويب","القدرة على التوسيع","توثيق"]}},"owner":"natalialewis","repo":"CS4610-Supabase-NextJS-Starter-App","repoPath":"natalialewis/CS4610-Supabase-NextJS-Starter-App","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.539Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"nextjs-supabase-starter","description":"Rules and best practices for building a Next.js starter app with Supabase (auth, profiles, RLS, declarative schemas, setup script). Use when working on Next.js + Supabase integration, authentication, migrations, or this starter app codebase.","bodyPreview":"# Next.js + Supabase Starter App Rules\n\nApply these rules when implementing or modifying the starter app. Names for routes, components, and hooks are flexible—use clear, consistent names and document choices. The starter should be **well-documented**, **easy to set up**, and include essential features for a modern web app with authentication.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Next.js\n\n- **Version**: Use the latest Next.js; follow Next.js 13+ App Router conventions.\n- **App Router only**: Use the `app/` directory; do","body":"# Next.js + Supabase Starter App Rules\n\nApply these rules when implementing or modifying the starter app. Names for routes, components, and hooks are flexible—use clear, consistent names and document choices. The starter should be **well-documented**, **easy to set up**, and include essential features for a modern web app with authentication.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Next.js\n\n- **Version**: Use the latest Next.js; follow Next.js 13+ App Router conventions.\n- **App Router only**: Use the `app/` directory; do not use `pages/`.\n- **TypeScript**: Use TypeScript throughout; no `any` without justification. Use explicit semicolons at the end of statements in `.ts` and `.tsx` files.\n- **Project structure**: Organize with `app/`, `components/`, `lib/`, etc. Document structure and conventions in README.\n- **Styling**: Use Tailwind CSS primarily, and plain CSS if needed.\n- **Mobile-first**: All layout and typography must be **mobile-first**. In Tailwind, base (unprefixed) classes define styles for the smallest viewport (mobile). Use `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` only to add or override for larger screens. Do not use base classes for desktop and then scale down with breakpoints—design for mobile first, then enhance upward (e.g. base `text-sm` / `p-4`, then `md:text-base` / `md:p-6`). Use touch-friendly minimum sizes on mobile (e.g. `min-h-[2.75rem]` for buttons/links) and relax with `sm:min-h-0` or `md:` when appropriate. Page content should use `min-h-[calc(100vh-3.5rem)]` (or similar) to account for the header so vertical centering and scroll behavior are correct.\n- **Middleware**: Use Next.js middleware for Supabase token refresh; implement the refresh logic in `proxy.ts` and use it from `middleware.ts` (see Supabase section).\n- **Server vs client**: Prefer Server Components by default; add `''use client''` only where needed (e.g. forms, auth state in UI). Colocate route-specific components in route folders when it makes sense.\n- **UX**: Use `loading.tsx` and `error.tsx` in route segments for loading and error states where appropriate.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Supabase Integration\n\n- **CLI and client**: Install and configure Supabase CLI and client libraries; use `@supabase/ssr` for SSR-safe usage.\n- **Local dev**: Set up Supabase for local development; run via `npx supabase start`; setup script configures and documents this.\n- **Two client utilities**: Provide separate helpers for **server** and **client** components (e.g. `createServerClient`, `createBrowserClient` in `lib/supabase/`) using `@supabase/ssr`.\n- **Middleware**: Configure Next.js middleware for token refresh using `proxy.ts`: put the session refresh / proxy logic in `proxy.ts` and invoke it from `middleware.ts` so the session is updated on each request.\n- **Environment**: Require `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` in `.env.local`; document in README. Never expose the service_role key in client or frontend code; use only the anon key in the app.\n- **Storage** (e.g. avatars): If using Supabase Storage, create a bucket and set RLS so users can read/update only their own objects (e.g. by path or user id).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Database and Migrations\n\n- **No manual SQL**: All schema changes go through **migration files** only.\n- **Declarative schemas**: Define tables in `supabase/schemas/` (e.g. `supabase/schemas/profiles.sql`). Generate migrations with:\n  ```bash\n  npx supabase db diff -f <migration_name>\n  ```\n- **Profiles table**:\n  - Primary key: `id` referencing `auth.users(id)`.\n  - Include `updated_at` with a trigger that sets it on row update.\n  - Define in declarative schema; add trigger and RLS in migrations.\n- **Automatic profile creation**: Use a PostgreSQL trigger that:\n  - Fires **AFTER INSERT** on `auth.users`.\n  - Reads the new user’s email (and id) from the inserted row.\n  - Inserts one row into `profiles` with that `id` and email. Trigger and function live in a migration file.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Row Level Security (RLS)\n\n- **Enable RLS** on `profiles`.\n- **Policies** (use `auth.uid()`):\n  - **SELECT**: User can read only their own profile.\n  - **UPDATE**: User can update only their own profile.\n  - **INSERT**: User can insert only their own profile (backup to trigger).\n- Ensure users cannot read or modify other users’ profiles.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Authentication\n\n- **Implement**: Sign up, sign in, sign out.\n- **Protected routes**: Redirect unauthenticated users to login (e.g. from dashboard/profile).\n- **State**: Handle auth state correctly in both server and client components.\n- **Patterns**: Use consistent patterns—e.g. a `useAuth()` (or similar) hook for client components and server-side helpers (e.g. `getUser()`) for server components. Document these in README.\n- **Errors**: Handle auth errors (invalid credentials, network, etc.) and show clear messages.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Example Pages and Routes\n\nRoute names are flexible (e.g. `/auth/login`, `/account`); keep them logical and consistent.\n\n- **Home (`/`)**: Welcome, auth status, link to login/signup when logged out, link to dashboard when logged in.\n- **Login**: Email/password form, error handling, redirect to dashboard on success.\n- **Signup**: Email/password form, error handling, redirect to dashboard on success.\n- **Dashboard (protected)**: Require auth; show profile summary and link to profile; sign out.\n- **Profile (protected)**: Require auth; show profile; form to update (e.g. `full_name` and any other profile fields); **avatar upload** that allows selecting/uploading an image, stores it (e.g. Supabase Storage), updates `avatar_url` in `profiles`, displays the avatar, and includes a save/update button; handle upload and validation errors.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Setup Script\n\n- **Purpose**: One command to install deps, start Supabase, write env, run migrations. Implement as `setup.sh`, `setup.js`, or use a tool like **zx** for cross-platform support; ensure it works reliably and handles edge cases.\n- **Assumptions**: Supabase is already initialized (`supabase/` with migrations and schemas exists). Do not assume a clean machine beyond that.\n- **Idempotent**: Safe to run multiple times. If `.env.local` exists, either skip or update it. If Supabase is already running, handle gracefully (e.g. skip start or detect and continue).\n- **Steps** (in order):\n  1. `npm install`\n  2. `npx supabase start` (or detect already running)\n  3. Extract Supabase URL and anon key from `supabase start` output\n  4. Create or update `.env.local` with `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`\n  5. Run migrations: `npx supabase db reset` or `npx supabase migration up`\n  6. Print clear output showing what was done and next steps\n- **Errors**: Provide helpful error messages if something goes wrong. In README, include instructions on how to run the script and troubleshoot.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Code Organization and Documentation\n\n- **Explicit structure**: Decide where things live (e.g. `components/`, `components/ui/`, `lib/hooks/`, `lib/utils/`) and document in README so anyone using the starter understands structure and conventions.\n- **Reusable components**: Store shared UI (buttons, forms, etc.) in a documented location.\n- **Hooks and utils**: Keep custom hooks (e.g. auth) and utility functions in consistent locations; document naming and usage.\n- **README must include**: Project description and purpose; prerequisites (Node.js version, Docker for Supabase, etc.); quick start (how to run the setup script); manual setup (step-by-step if someone prefers); project structure; how to use this starter for new projects; environment variables; database schema overview; authentication flow; deployment instructions; GitHub Actions setup and configuration; troubleshooting section.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Testing\n\n- **Framework**: Use a unit test framework (e.g. Jest, Vitest).\n- **Coverage**: Include at least a few examples for:\n  - React components\n  - Utility functions\n  - Auth-related code\n- **README**: How to run tests and how to add new tests.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Deployment and CI/CD\n\n- **Deployment docs**: Document how to deploy to production (e.g. Vercel, Netlify): steps to set up the production Supabase project; how to configure environment variables in the deployment platform; how to link the production database; any platform-specific considerations (e.g. on Vercel: set env vars in project settings, use production Supabase URL/anon key, do not commit `.env.local`).\n- **Vercel**: If deploying on Vercel, use the dashboard for env vars, connect the repo, and ensure `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` and Supabase keys are set. Middleware runs on the Edge runtime by default.\n- **GitHub Actions**: Create a workflow that triggers on deployment or push to main/production branch; connects to the production Supabase instance; runs pending migrations via Supabase CLI; uses GitHub Secrets for sensitive credentials; handles errors with clear feedback. Document in README how to set up and configure the workflow and secrets.\n\n---\n\n## 11. General\n\n- **Error handling**: Include proper error handling for authentication and database operations; avoid silent failures.\n- **Comments**: Add comments in code where logic or intent is non-obvious.\n- **Naming**: Use clear, consistent names for routes, components, hooks, and functions; document in README when choices affect how others use the starter.\n\n## 12. Submission Checklist\n\n- Remove `node_modules` before submitting. Zip the project folder; do not delete the `supabase/` directory (migrations and schemas must remain).\n- Ensure the setup script is included and executable.\n- Verify README is comprehensive and clear.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T00:56:40.396Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full-Stack Development Agents needing rapid authentication-enabled web app scaffolding.","zh":"Perfect for Full-Stack Development Agents needing rapid authentication-enabled web app scaffolding.","ja":"Perfect for Full-Stack Development Agents needing rapid authentication-enabled web app scaffolding.","ko":"Perfect for Full-Stack Development Agents needing rapid authentication-enabled web app scaffolding.","es":"Perfect for Full-Stack Development Agents needing rapid authentication-enabled web app scaffolding.","fr":"Perfect for Full-Stack Development Agents needing rapid authentication-enabled web app scaffolding.","de":"Perfect for Full-Stack Development Agents needing rapid authentication-enabled web app scaffolding.","pt":"Perfect for Full-Stack Development Agents needing rapid authentication-enabled web app scaffolding.","ru":"Perfect for Full-Stack Development Agents needing rapid authentication-enabled web app scaffolding.","ar":"Perfect for Full-Stack Development Agents needing rapid authentication-enabled web app scaffolding."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to instantly scaffold modern web applications with pre-configured authentication flows using Next.js 13+ App Router and Supabase. Provides built-in user management, real-time database capabilities, and serverless function integration out-of-the-box.","zh":"Enables agents to instantly scaffold modern web applications with pre-configured authentication flows using Next.js 13+ App Router and Supabase. Provides built-in user management, real-time database capabilities, and serverless function integration out-of-the-box.","ja":"Enables agents to instantly scaffold modern web applications with pre-configured authentication flows using Next.js 13+ App Router and Supabase. Provides built-in user management, real-time database capabilities, and serverless function integration out-of-the-box.","ko":"Enables agents to instantly scaffold modern web applications with pre-configured authentication flows using Next.js 13+ App Router and Supabase. Provides built-in user management, real-time database capabilities, and serverless function integration out-of-the-box.","es":"Enables agents to instantly scaffold modern web applications with pre-configured authentication flows using Next.js 13+ App Router and Supabase. Provides built-in user management, real-time database capabilities, and serverless function integration out-of-the-box.","fr":"Enables agents to instantly scaffold modern web applications with pre-configured authentication flows using Next.js 13+ App Router and Supabase. Provides built-in user management, real-time database capabilities, and serverless function integration out-of-the-box.","de":"Enables agents to instantly scaffold modern web applications with pre-configured authentication flows using Next.js 13+ App Router and Supabase. Provides built-in user management, real-time database capabilities, and serverless function integration out-of-the-box.","pt":"Enables agents to instantly scaffold modern web applications with pre-configured authentication flows using Next.js 13+ App Router and Supabase. Provides built-in user management, real-time database capabilities, and serverless function integration out-of-the-box.","ru":"Enables agents to instantly scaffold modern web applications with pre-configured authentication flows using Next.js 13+ App Router and Supabase. Provides built-in user management, real-time database capabilities, and serverless function integration out-of-the-box.","ar":"Enables agents to instantly scaffold modern web applications with pre-configured authentication flows using Next.js 13+ App Router and Supabase. Provides built-in user management, real-time database capabilities, and serverless function integration out-of-the-box."},"useCases":{"en":["Deploying authentication-protected landing pages","Building real-time collaborative applications","Prototyping SaaS products with user management","Creating server-rendered applications with Supabase backend"],"zh":["Deploying authentication-protected landing pages","Building real-time collaborative applications","Prototyping SaaS products with user management","Creating server-rendered applications with Supabase backend"],"ja":["Deploying authentication-protected landing pages","Building real-time collaborative applications","Prototyping SaaS products with user management","Creating server-rendered applications with Supabase backend"],"ko":["Deploying authentication-protected landing pages","Building real-time collaborative applications","Prototyping SaaS products with user management","Creating server-rendered applications with Supabase backend"],"es":["Deploying authentication-protected landing pages","Building real-time collaborative applications","Prototyping SaaS products with user management","Creating server-rendered applications with Supabase backend"],"fr":["Deploying authentication-protected landing pages","Building real-time collaborative applications","Prototyping SaaS products with user management","Creating server-rendered applications with Supabase backend"],"de":["Deploying authentication-protected landing pages","Building real-time collaborative applications","Prototyping SaaS products with user management","Creating server-rendered applications with Supabase backend"],"pt":["Deploying authentication-protected landing pages","Building real-time collaborative applications","Prototyping SaaS products with user management","Creating server-rendered applications with Supabase backend"],"ru":["Deploying authentication-protected landing pages","Building real-time collaborative applications","Prototyping SaaS products with user management","Creating server-rendered applications with Supabase backend"],"ar":["Deploying authentication-protected landing pages","Building real-time collaborative applications","Prototyping SaaS products with user management","Creating server-rendered applications with Supabase backend"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Supabase project configuration","App Router conventions only (no pages directory)","Dependent on Supabase authentication services"],"zh":["Requires Supabase project configuration","App Router conventions only (no pages directory)","Dependent on Supabase authentication services"],"ja":["Requires Supabase project configuration","App Router conventions only (no pages directory)","Dependent on Supabase authentication services"],"ko":["Requires Supabase project configuration","App Router conventions only (no pages directory)","Dependent on Supabase authentication services"],"es":["Requires Supabase project configuration","App Router conventions only (no pages directory)","Dependent on Supabase authentication services"],"fr":["Requires Supabase project configuration","App Router conventions only (no pages directory)","Dependent on Supabase authentication services"],"de":["Requires Supabase project configuration","App Router conventions only (no pages directory)","Dependent on Supabase authentication services"],"pt":["Requires Supabase project configuration","App Router conventions only (no pages directory)","Dependent on Supabase authentication services"],"ru":["Requires Supabase project configuration","App Router conventions only (no pages directory)","Dependent on Supabase authentication services"],"ar":["Requires Supabase project configuration","App Router conventions only (no pages directory)","Dependent on Supabase authentication services"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
