compiladas","legibilidad del código"],"fr":["optimisation des performances","réduction des allocations","Span<T>","Memory<T>","ArrayPool<T>","ValueTask<T>","hot paths","requêtes compilées","lisibilité du code"],"de":["Leistungsoptimierung","Reduzierung von Zuweisungen","Span<T>","Memory<T>","ArrayPool<T>","ValueTask<T>","Hot-Paths","compilierte Abfragen","Code-Lesbarkeit"],"pt":["otimização de performance","redução de alocações","Span","ArrayPool","ValueTask","hot paths","desenvolvimento de aplicativos"],"ru":["оптимизация производительности","уменьшение распределения памяти","Span","ArrayPool","ValueTask","hot paths","разработка приложений"],"ar":["تحسين الأداء","تقليل التخصيص","Span","ArrayPool","ValueTask","مسارات ساخنة","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"diegoknsk","repo":"video-processing-engine-auth-lambda","repoPath":"diegoknsk/video-processing-engine-auth-lambda","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.539Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"performance-optimization","description":"Guia para otimização de performance — Span<T>, Memory<T>, ArrayPool, ValueTask, compiled queries e técnicas avançadas. Use quando a tarefa envolver performance, otimização, alocações, memory pooling ou hot paths.","bodyPreview":"# Performance Optimization — .NET\n\n## Quando Usar\n\n- **Otimização de performance**, redução de alocações\n- **Span<T>**, **Memory<T>**, **ArrayPool<T>**, **ValueTask<T>**\n- **Hot paths**, queries compiladas, zero-allocation\n- Palavras-chave: \"performance\", \"otimizar\", \"alocações\", \"Span\", \"ArrayPool\", \"rápido\", \"hot path\"\n\n⚠️ **Importante:** Otimize apenas com **profiling** (medição real). Código legível > performance prematura.\n\n## Princípios Essenciais\n\n### ✅ Fazer\n\n- Usar **Span<T>** para mani","body":"# Performance Optimization — .NET\n\n## Quando Usar\n\n- **Otimização de performance**, redução de alocações\n- **Span<T>**, **Memory<T>**, **ArrayPool<T>**, **ValueTask<T>**\n- **Hot paths**, queries compiladas, zero-allocation\n- Palavras-chave: \"performance\", \"otimizar\", \"alocações\", \"Span\", \"ArrayPool\", \"rápido\", \"hot path\"\n\n⚠️ **Importante:** Otimize apenas com **profiling** (medição real). Código legível > performance prematura.\n\n## Princípios Essenciais\n\n### ✅ Fazer\n\n- Usar **Span<T>** para manipulação de arrays/strings sem alocações (parsing, slicing)\n- Usar **ArrayPool<T>** para arrays temporários (reutilização, menos GC pressure)\n- Usar **ValueTask<T>** quando operação frequentemente completa de forma síncrona\n- **Compiled queries** (EF Core) para queries repetitivas\n- **AsNoTracking()** em EF Core para queries read-only\n- **Profiling primeiro:** medir antes de otimizar (BenchmarkDotNet)\n\n### ❌ Não Fazer\n\n- **Nunca** otimizar sem medir (profiling)\n- **Nunca** sacrificar legibilidade por micro-otimizações sem impacto\n- **Nunca** usar `Span<T>` em métodos async (usar `Memory<T>`)\n- **Nunca** esquecer de devolver arrays ao `ArrayPool` (usar `try/finally`)\n- **Nunca** assumir que \"mais rápido\" = \"melhor\" (trade-offs)\n\n**Regra de ouro:** Profile → Otimize → Meça novamente. Span<T> + ArrayPool<T> cobrem 80% dos casos.\n\n## Checklist Rápido\n\n1. **Profile primeiro:** BenchmarkDotNet ou dotTrace para identificar hot paths\n2. **Span<T>** para parsing, slicing, manipulação de strings sem alocações\n3. **ArrayPool<T>** para arrays temporários (Rent → usar → Return no `finally`)\n4. **ValueTask<T>** para operações que frequentemente completam síncronamente\n5. **AsNoTracking()** em queries EF Core read-only\n6. **Compiled queries** para queries EF Core repetitivas\n7. **Measure again:** validar que otimização teve efeito\n\n## Exemplo Mínimo\n\n**Cenário:** Parsing de CSV com Span<T> e ArrayPool<T> (zero alocações)\n\n### Span<T> — Parsing sem Alocações\n\n```csharp\n// ❌ Alocações desnecessárias\npublic static string[] ParseCsvLine(string line)\n{\n    return line.Split('',''); // Aloca array de strings\n}\n\n// ✅ Zero alocações com Span\npublic static void ParseCsvLine(ReadOnlySpan<char> line, Span<Range> ranges, out int count)\n{\n    count = 0;\n    int start = 0;\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i <= line.Length; i++)\n    {\n        if (i == line.Length || line[i] == '','')\n        {\n            ranges[count++] = new Range(start, i);\n            start = i + 1;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// Uso\nvar line = \"John,Doe,30\".AsSpan();\nSpan<Range> ranges = stackalloc Range[10]; // No stack, zero alocação\nParseCsvLine(line, ranges, out int count);\n\nfor (int i = 0; i < count; i++)\n{\n    var field = line[ranges[i]]; // ReadOnlySpan<char>, zero alocação\n    Console.WriteLine(field.ToString());\n}\n```\n\n### ArrayPool<T> — Reutilização de Arrays\n\n```csharp\nusing System.Buffers;\n\n// ❌ Alocação a cada chamada\npublic byte[] ProcessData(int size)\n{\n    var buffer = new byte[size]; // GC pressure\n    // ... processa\n    return buffer;\n}\n\n// ✅ Reutilização com ArrayPool\npublic void ProcessData(int size, Span<byte> destination)\n{\n    var buffer = ArrayPool<byte>.Shared.Rent(size); // Reutiliza array\n    \n    try\n    {\n        var span = buffer.AsSpan(0, size);\n        // ... processa span\n        span.CopyTo(destination);\n    }\n    finally\n    {\n        ArrayPool<byte>.Shared.Return(buffer); // Devolve ao pool\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### ValueTask<T> — Operações Frequentemente Síncronas\n\n```csharp\n// ✅ ValueTask quando operação pode ser síncrona (ex.: cache hit)\npublic class CachedUserRepository(IUserRepository repository, IMemoryCache cache)\n{\n    public async ValueTask<User?> GetByIdAsync(Guid id, CancellationToken ct = default)\n    {\n        // Cache hit: retorna de forma síncrona (sem alocação de Task)\n        if (cache.TryGetValue(id, out User? cached))\n            return cached;\n\n        // Cache miss: chama repositório (assíncrono)\n        var user = await repository.GetByIdAsync(id, ct);\n        if (user != null)\n            cache.Set(id, user, TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5));\n        \n        return user;\n    }\n}\n\n// ❌ Task<T> sempre aloca mesmo quando síncrono\npublic async Task<User?> GetByIdAsync(Guid id, CancellationToken ct = default)\n{\n    if (cache.TryGetValue(id, out User? cached))\n        return cached; // Ainda aloca Task<User>\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Pontos-chave:**\n- **Span<T>:** parsing, slicing, manipulação sem alocações (só código síncrono)\n- **ArrayPool<T>:** arrays temporários, reduz GC pressure (sempre Return no `finally`)\n- **ValueTask<T>:** quando operação frequentemente completa de forma síncrona\n\n## Memory<T> — Span para Async\n\n`Span<T>` não pode ser usado em métodos async (vive no stack). Use `Memory<T>`:\n\n```csharp\npublic async Task<int> ProcessAsync(Memory<byte> buffer, CancellationToken ct)\n{\n    await ReadDataAsync(buffer, ct); // Memory pode ser passado para async\n    \n    Span<byte> span = buffer.Span; // Converter para Span quando necessário\n    return ProcessBytes(span);\n}\n\nprivate int ProcessBytes(Span<byte> data)\n{\n    int sum = 0;\n    foreach (var b in data) sum += b;\n    return sum;\n}\n```\n\n## Compiled Queries (EF Core)\n\nPara queries repetitivas, compile uma vez:\n\n```csharp\nprivate static readonly Func<AppDbContext, Guid, Task<User?>> GetUserByIdQuery =\n    EF.CompileAsyncQuery((AppDbContext ctx, Guid id) =>\n        ctx.Users.AsNoTracking().FirstOrDefault(u => u.Id == id));\n\npublic async Task<User?> GetByIdAsync(Guid id, CancellationToken ct = default)\n{\n    return await GetUserByIdQuery(context, id);\n}\n```\n\n## Profiling com BenchmarkDotNet\n\n```bash\ndotnet add package BenchmarkDotNet\n```\n\n```csharp\nusing BenchmarkDotNet.Attributes;\nusing BenchmarkDotNet.Running;\n\n[MemoryDiagnoser]\npublic class ParsingBenchmark\n{\n    private const string Input = \"10,20,30,40,50\";\n\n    [Benchmark(Baseline = true)]\n    public int[] ParseWithSplit()\n    {\n        var parts = Input.Split('','');\n        var numbers = new int[parts.Length];\n        for (int i = 0; i < parts.Length; i++)\n            numbers[i] = int.Parse(parts[i]);\n        return numbers;\n    }\n\n    [Benchmark]\n    public int[] ParseWithSpan()\n    {\n        var span = Input.AsSpan();\n        Span<int> numbers = stackalloc int[5];\n        // ... parsing com span\n        return numbers.ToArray();\n    }\n}\n\n// Program.cs\nBenchmarkRunner.Run<ParsingBenchmark>();\n```\n\n## Técnicas por Cenário\n\n| Cenário | Técnica | Ganho |\n|---------|---------|-------|\n| Parsing de strings/CSV | `Span<T>` | Zero alocações |\n| Arrays temporários (loops) | `ArrayPool<T>` | -70% GC pressure |\n| Cache/operações síncronas | `ValueTask<T>` | -50% alocações |\n| Queries EF Core repetitivas | Compiled queries | +30% throughput |\n| Queries EF Core read-only | `AsNoTracking()` | +20% performance |\n\n## Referências\n\n- [Span<T> Documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.span-1)\n- [ArrayPool<T> Documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.buffers.arraypool-1)\n- [BenchmarkDotNet](https://benchmarkdotnet.org/)\n- [Performance Best Practices](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/extensions/high-performance-logging)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:14:05.058Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for .NET Agents needing advanced performance optimization techniques for reducing allocations and improving hot paths.","zh":"Perfect for .NET Agents needing advanced performance optimization techniques for reducing allocations and improving hot paths.","ja":"Perfect for .NET Agents needing advanced performance optimization techniques for reducing allocations and improving hot paths.","ko":"Perfect for .NET Agents needing advanced performance optimization techniques for reducing allocations and improving hot paths.","es":"Perfect for .NET Agents needing advanced performance optimization techniques for reducing allocations and improving hot paths.","fr":"Perfect for .NET Agents needing advanced performance optimization techniques for reducing allocations and improving hot paths.","de":"Perfect for .NET Agents needing advanced performance optimization techniques for reducing allocations and improving hot paths.","pt":"Perfect for .NET Agents needing advanced performance optimization techniques for reducing allocations and improving hot paths.","ru":"Perfect for .NET Agents needing advanced performance optimization techniques for reducing allocations and improving hot paths.","ar":"Perfect for .NET Agents needing advanced performance optimization techniques for reducing allocations and improving hot paths."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to optimize performance using Span<T>, Memory<T>, ArrayPool<T>, and ValueTask<T>, enabling zero-allocation queries and hot path optimization with profiling.","zh":"Empowers agents to optimize performance using Span<T>, Memory<T>, ArrayPool<T>, and ValueTask<T>, enabling zero-allocation queries and hot path optimization with profiling.","ja":"Empowers agents to optimize performance using Span<T>, Memory<T>, ArrayPool<T>, and ValueTask<T>, enabling zero-allocation queries and hot path optimization with profiling.","ko":"Empowers agents to optimize performance using Span<T>, Memory<T>, ArrayPool<T>, and ValueTask<T>, enabling zero-allocation queries and hot path optimization with profiling.","es":"Empowers agents to optimize performance using Span<T>, Memory<T>, ArrayPool<T>, and ValueTask<T>, enabling zero-allocation queries and hot path optimization with profiling.","fr":"Empowers agents to optimize performance using Span<T>, Memory<T>, ArrayPool<T>, and ValueTask<T>, enabling zero-allocation queries and hot path optimization with profiling.","de":"Empowers agents to optimize performance using Span<T>, Memory<T>, ArrayPool<T>, and ValueTask<T>, enabling zero-allocation queries and hot path optimization with profiling.","pt":"Empowers agents to optimize performance using Span<T>, Memory<T>, ArrayPool<T>, and ValueTask<T>, enabling zero-allocation queries and hot path optimization with profiling.","ru":"Empowers agents to optimize performance using Span<T>, Memory<T>, ArrayPool<T>, and ValueTask<T>, enabling zero-allocation queries and hot path optimization with profiling.","ar":"Empowers agents to optimize performance using Span<T>, Memory<T>, ArrayPool<T>, and ValueTask<T>, enabling zero-allocation queries and hot path optimization with profiling."},"useCases":{"en":["Optimizing AWS Lambda functions for reduced latency","Improving API Gateway performance with compiled queries","Reducing memory allocations in .NET applications"],"zh":["Optimizing AWS Lambda functions for reduced latency","Improving API Gateway performance with compiled queries","Reducing memory allocations in .NET applications"],"ja":["Optimizing AWS Lambda functions for reduced latency","Improving API Gateway performance with compiled queries","Reducing memory allocations in .NET applications"],"ko":["Optimizing AWS Lambda functions for reduced latency","Improving API Gateway performance with compiled queries","Reducing memory allocations in .NET applications"],"es":["Optimizing AWS Lambda functions for reduced latency","Improving API Gateway performance with compiled queries","Reducing memory allocations in .NET applications"],"fr":["Optimizing AWS Lambda functions for reduced latency","Improving API Gateway performance with compiled queries","Reducing memory allocations in .NET applications"],"de":["Optimizing AWS Lambda functions for reduced latency","Improving API Gateway performance with compiled queries","Reducing memory allocations in .NET applications"],"pt":["Optimizing AWS Lambda functions for reduced latency","Improving API Gateway performance with compiled queries","Reducing memory allocations in .NET applications"],"ru":["Optimizing AWS Lambda functions for reduced latency","Improving API Gateway performance with compiled queries","Reducing memory allocations in .NET applications"],"ar":["Optimizing AWS Lambda functions for reduced latency","Improving API Gateway performance with compiled queries","Reducing memory allocations in .NET applications"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires .NET environment","Profiling required for effective optimization","May require additional setup for Amazon Cognito and API Gateway integration"],"zh":["Requires .NET environment","Profiling required for effective optimization","May require additional setup for Amazon Cognito and API Gateway integration"],"ja":["Requires .NET environment","Profiling required for effective optimization","May require additional setup for Amazon Cognito and API Gateway integration"],"ko":["Requires .NET environment","Profiling required for effective optimization","May require additional setup for Amazon Cognito and API Gateway integration"],"es":["Requires .NET environment","Profiling required for effective optimization","May require additional setup for Amazon Cognito and API Gateway integration"],"fr":["Requires .NET environment","Profiling required for effective optimization","May require additional setup for Amazon Cognito and API Gateway integration"],"de":["Requires .NET environment","Profiling required for effective optimization","May require additional setup for Amazon Cognito and API Gateway integration"],"pt":["Requires .NET environment","Profiling required for effective optimization","May require additional setup for Amazon Cognito and API Gateway integration"],"ru":["Requires .NET environment","Profiling required for effective optimization","May require additional setup for Amazon Cognito and API Gateway integration"],"ar":["Requires .NET environment","Profiling required for effective optimization","May require additional setup for Amazon Cognito and API Gateway integration"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
