 grandes","Uso de URLs prefirmadas"],"fr":["Vérification du type de fichier","Limitation de la taille du fichier","Gestion des téléchargements importants","Utilisation d''URL pré-signées"],"de":["Dateityp-Überprüfung","Dateigrößenbeschränkung","Verarbeitung großer Uploads","Verwendung von vorab unterzeichneten URLs"],"pt":["Segurança de uploads de arquivos","Desempenho otimizado para uploads grandes","Verificação de tipo de arquivo","Restrições de tamanho de upload","Prevenção de travessia de caminho"],"ru":["Безопасность загрузки файлов","Оптимизированная производительность для крупных загрузок","Проверка типа файла","Ограничения размера загрузки","Предотвращение путешествия по пути"],"ar":["أمان التحميل","أداء محسن لتحميل الملفات الكبيرة","فحص نوع الملف","قيود حجم التحميل","منع التجول في المسار"]},"keywords":{"zh":["文件上传","安全","性能","魔法字节","上传大小限制","路径遍历","预签名URL","大文件上传"],"ja":["ファイルアップロード","セキュリティ","パフォーマンス","マジックバイト","アップロードサイズの制限","パス遍歴","事前署名URL","大ファイルアップロード"],"ko":["파일 업로드","보안","성능","매직바이트","업로드 크기 제한","경로 트래버설","사전 서명 URL","대 파일 업로드"],"es":["subir archivos","seguridad de subida de archivos","eficiencia de subida de archivos","desarrollo de aplicaciones","subida de archivos grandes","verificación de tipo de archivo"],"fr":["téléchargement de fichiers","sécurité du téléchargement de fichiers","efficacité du téléchargement de fichiers","développement d''applications","téléchargement de fichiers importants","vérification du type de fichier"],"de":["Datei-Upload","Sicherheit des Datei-Uploads","Effizienz des Datei-Uploads","Anwendungs-Entwicklung","große Datei-Uploads","Datei-Typ-Überprüfung"],"pt":["upload de arquivos","segurança de uploads","desempenho de uploads","verificação de tipo de arquivo","restrições de tamanho de upload","prevenção de travessia de caminho","desenvolvimento de software","armazenamento de arquivos"],"ru":["загрузка файлов","безопасность загрузки","производительность загрузки","проверка типа файла","ограничения размера загрузки","предотвращение путешествия по пути","разработка программного обеспечения","хранение файлов"],"ar":["تحميل الملفات","أمان التحميل","أداء التحميل","فحص نوع الملف","قيود حجم التحميل","منع التجول في المسار","تطوير البرمجيات","تخزين الملفات"]}},"owner":"Nguyenthang2292","repo":"Sovereign-IQ","repoPath":"Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:03:48.178Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"file-uploads","description":"Expert at handling file uploads and cloud storage. Covers S3, Cloudflare R2, presigned URLs, multipart uploads, and image optimization. Knows how to handle large files without blocking. Use when: file upload, S3, R2, presigned URL, multipart.","bodyPreview":"# File Uploads & Storage\n\n**Role**: File Upload Specialist\n\nCareful about security and performance. Never trusts file\nextensions. Knows that large uploads need special handling.\nPrefers presigned URLs over server proxying.\n\n## ⚠️ Sharp Edges\n\n| Issue | Severity | Solution |\n|-------|----------|----------|\n| Trusting client-provided file type | critical | # CHECK MAGIC BYTES |\n| No upload size restrictions | high | # SET SIZE LIMITS |\n| User-controlled filename allows path traversal | critical |","body":"# File Uploads & Storage\n\n**Role**: File Upload Specialist\n\nCareful about security and performance. Never trusts file\nextensions. Knows that large uploads need special handling.\nPrefers presigned URLs over server proxying.\n\n## ⚠️ Sharp Edges\n\n| Issue | Severity | Solution |\n|-------|----------|----------|\n| Trusting client-provided file type | critical | # CHECK MAGIC BYTES |\n| No upload size restrictions | high | # SET SIZE LIMITS |\n| User-controlled filename allows path traversal | critical | # SANITIZE FILENAMES |\n| Presigned URL shared or cached incorrectly | medium | # CONTROL PRESIGNED URL DISTRIBUTION |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T00:47:21.102Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Security-Conscious Agents handling sensitive file uploads and requiring robust storage solutions.","zh":"适合于处理敏感文件上传和需要强大的存储解决方案的安全意识强的代理。","ja":"セキュリティに厳格なエージェントが、機密ファイルのアップロードを処理し、堅牢なストレージソリューションを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"민감한 파일 업로드를 처리하고 강력한 스토리지 솔루션을 필요로 하는 보안 의식이 높은 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes conscientes de la seguridad que manejan cargas de archivos sensibles y requieren soluciones de almacenamiento robustas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents conscients de la sécurité qui gèrent des téléchargements de fichiers sensibles et nécessitent des solutions de stockage robustes.","de":"Ideal für sicherheitsbewusste Agenten, die sensible Datei-Uploads verwalten und robuste Speicherlösungen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Conscientes de Segurança que lidam com uploads de arquivos sensíveis e requerem soluções de armazenamento robustas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов, осознающих проблемы безопасности, которые обрабатывают загрузки конфиденциальных файлов и требуют надежных решений для хранения.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الحريصين على الأمان الذين يتعاملون مع تحميل الملفات الحساسة ويتطلبون حلول تخزين قوية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to securely handle file uploads using presigned URLs, mitigating risks associated with trusting client-provided file types and ensuring large uploads are handled efficiently, all while preventing path traversal vulnerabilities through careful filename management and magic byte checks.","zh":"赋予代理安全地处理文件上传的能力，使用预签名的URL，减轻信任客户端提供的文件类型所带来的风险，并确保大文件上传处理高效，同时通过仔细的文件名管理和魔术字节检查防止路径遍历漏洞。","ja":"エージェントに、事前署名されたURLを使用してファイルのアップロードを安全に処理する能力を付与し、クライアント提供のファイルタイプを信頼することによるリスクを軽減し、大規模なアップロードを効率的に処理し、ファイル名の管理とマジックバイトチェックによってパス遍歴攻撃を防止します。","ko":"에이전트가 사전 서명된 URL을 사용하여 파일 업로드를 안전하게 처리할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 클라이언트 제공 파일 유형을 신뢰하는 것과 관련된 위험을 완화하고 대형 업로드를 효율적으로 처리하며 파일 이름 관리와 매직 바이트 확인을 통해 경로 트래버설 취약점을 방지합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a manejar los cargas de archivos de manera segura utilizando URLs prefirmadas, mitigando los riesgos asociados con la confianza en los tipos de archivos proporcionados por el cliente y garantizando que las cargas grandes se manejen de manera eficiente, todo mientras se previenen vulnerabilidades de travesía de ruta a través de una gestión cuidadosa de los nombres de archivo y comprobaciones de bytes mágicos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les téléchargements de fichiers de manière sécurisée en utilisant des URLs pré-signées, atténuant les risques associés à la confiance accordée aux types de fichiers fournis par le client et garantissant que les téléchargements importants soient gérés de manière efficace, le tout en prévenant les vulnérabilités de traversal de chemin via une gestion soigneuse des noms de fichier et des vérifications d''octets magiques.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Datei-Uploads sicher zu handhaben, indem sie vorgezeichnete URLs verwenden, die Risiken im Zusammenhang mit der Vertrauenswürdigkeit von clientseitig bereitgestellten Dateitypen minimieren und große Uploads effizient handhaben, während sie gleichzeitig Pfade-Traversierung-Schwachstellen durch sorgfältiges Dateinamen-Management und Magisch-Byte-Prüfungen verhindern.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a lidarem com uploads de arquivos de forma segura usando URLs pré-assinadas, mitigando riscos associados à confiança em tipos de arquivos fornecidos pelo cliente e garantindo que uploads grandes sejam tratados de forma eficiente, tudo isso enquanto impede vulnerabilidades de traversal de caminho por meio de gerenciamento cuidadoso de nomes de arquivos e verificações de bytes mágicos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью безопасно обрабатывать загрузки файлов с помощью предварительно подписанных URL-адресов, снижая риски, связанные с доверием к типам файлов, предоставляемым клиентом, и обеспечивая эффективное xử lý больших загрузок, при этом предотвращая уязвимости путевого обхода посредством тщательного управления именами файлов и проверок магических байтов.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على التعامل مع تحميل الملفات بشكل آمن باستخدام عناوين URL مسبقة التوقيع، وخفض المخاطر المرتبطة بالثقة في أنواع الملفات المقدمة من العميل، وضمان معالجة التحميلات الكبيرة بفعالية، مع منع ثغرات التسلل عبر مسار الملفات من خلال إدارة أسماء الملفات بدقة وفحص البايتات السحرية."},"useCases":{"en":["Validating file types through magic byte checks","Implementing secure upload size restrictions","Preventing path traversal attacks through sanitized filenames"],"zh":["通过魔术字节检查验证文件类型","实施安全的上传大小限制","通过清理文件名防止路径遍历攻击"],"ja":["マジックバイトチェックを使用してファイルタイプを検証する","セキュアなアップロードサイズ制限を実施する","ファイル名のサニタイズを通じてパス遍歴攻撃を防止する"],"ko":["매직 바이트 확인을 통해 파일 유형을 확인する","보안 업로드 크기 제한을 구현하는 것","파일 이름을 정리함으로써 경로 트래버설 공격을 방지하는 것"],"es":["Validar los tipos de archivo mediante comprobaciones de bytes mágicos","Implementar restricciones de tamaño de carga de archivo seguras","Prevenir ataques de travesía de ruta a través de nombres de archivo saneados"],"fr":["Valider les types de fichiers via des vérifications d''octets magiques","Mettre en œuvre des restrictions de taille de téléchargement de fichiers sécurisées","Prévenir les attaques de traversal de chemin via des noms de fichier saneés"],"de":["Dateitypen durch Magisch-Byte-Prüfungen validieren","Sichere Upload-Größenbeschränkungen implementieren","Pfade-Traversierung-Angriffe durch gesäuberte Dateinamen verhindern"],"pt":["Validar tipos de arquivos por meio de verificações de bytes mágicos","Implementar restrições de tamanho de upload seguras","Prevenir ataques de traversal de caminho por meio de nomes de arquivos sanitizados"],"ru":["Проверка типов файлов с помощью проверок магических байтов","Реализация безопасных ограничений размера загрузки","Предотвращение атак путевого обхода посредством санитизированных имен файлов"],"ar":["التحقق من أنواع الملفات من خلال فحص البايتات السحرية","تنفيذ قيود حجم التحميل الآمنة","منع هجمات التسلل عبر مسار الملفات من خلال أسماء الملفات المُحسنة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires careful handling of large uploads","Needs implementation of size limits and filename sanitization","Must verify file types to prevent security risks"],"zh":["需要小心处理大文件上传","需要实现大小限制和文件名清理","必须验证文件类型以防止安全风险"],"ja":["大規模なアップロードの慎重な処理が必要","サイズ制限とファイル名のサニタイズの実装が必要","セキュリティリスクを防止するためにファイルタイプの検証が必要"],"ko":["대형 파일 업로드를 주의 깊게 처리해야 함","크기 제한 및 파일 이름 정리를 구현해야 함","보안 위험을 방지하기 위해 파일 유형을 확인해야 함"],"es":["Requiere un manejo cuidadoso de las cargas grandes","Necesita la implementación de límites de tamaño y saneamiento de nombres de archivo","Debe verificar los tipos de archivo para prevenir riesgos de seguridad"],"fr":["Nécessite une gestion soigneuse des téléchargements importants","Nécessite la mise en œuvre de limites de taille et de saneamiento de noms de fichier","Doit vérifier les types de fichiers pour prévenir les risques de sécurité"],"de":["Benötigt eine sorgfältige Handhabung großer Uploads","Benötigt die Implementierung von Größenbegrenzungen und Dateinamensanierung","Muss Dateitypen überprüfen, um Sicherheitsrisiken zu vermeiden"],"pt":["Requer manipulação cuidadosa de uploads grandes","Necessita implementação de limites de tamanho e sanitização de nomes de arquivos","Deve verificar tipos de arquivos para prevenir riscos de segurança"],"ru":["Требует тщательной обработки больших загрузок","Требует реализации ограничений размера и санитизации имен файлов","Должен проверять типы файлов для предотвращения рисков безопасности"],"ar":["يتطلب التعامل بدقة مع التحميلات الكبيرة","يتطلب تنفيذ قيود الحجم وتحسين أسماء الملفات","يجب التحقق من أنواع الملفات لمنع المخاطر الأمنية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('entazis/product-reviews/pull-request', 'community', 'entazis', 'product-reviews', 'entazis/product-reviews', 'pull-request', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:03:48.178Z', '2026-02-19T00:47:13.030Z', NULL, '{"id":"entazis/product-reviews/pull-request","name":"pull-request","description":{"zh":"Pull Request 系统是一种用于处理产品评论的代码审查工具，确保代码质量和安全性","ja":"Pull Request システムは製品レビューの処理に使用されるコードレビューツールで、コードの品質とセキュリティを確保します","ko":"풀 리퀘스트 시스템은 제품 리뷰 처리에 사용되는 코드 리뷰 도구로 코드 품질과 보안을 보장합니다","es":"La solicitud de extracción es un sistema para manejar revisiones de productos de forma eficiente. Mejora la calidad del código y reduce errores.","fr":"La demande d''extraction est un système pour gérer les révisions de produits de manière efficace. Améliorez la qualité du code et réduisez les erreurs.","de":"Die Pull-Request ist ein System zur effizienten Verwaltung von Produktbewertungen. Verbessern Sie die Code-Qualität und reduzieren Sie Fehler.","pt":"O Pull Request é um sistema para revisar e melhorar o código, garantindo que as alterações sejam testadas e validadas.","ru":"Система обработки запросов на вытягивание предназначена для проверки и улучшения кода, гарантируя, что изменения протестированы и проверены.","ar":"نظام طلب سحب تعديلات هو نظام لمراجعة و تحسين الكود، و ضمان أن التعديلات تم اختبارها و التحقق منها.","en":"A system for handling product reviews."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Pull Request 系统：代码审查和产品评论处理","ja":"Pull Request システム：コードレビューと製品レビューの処理","ko":"풀 리퀘스트 시스템: 코드 리뷰 및 제품 리뷰 처리","es":"Solicitud de Extracción: Mejora de la Revisión de Código","fr":"Demande d''Extraction: Amélioration de la Révision de Code","de":"Pull-Request: Verbesserung der Code-Überprüfung","pt":"Sistema de Revisão de Código - Pull Request","ru":"Система обработки запросов на вытягивание","ar":"نظام طلب سحب تعديلات","en":"pull-request"},"description":{"zh":"Pull Request 系统是一种用于处理产品评论的代码审查工具，确保代码质量和安全性","ja":"Pull Request システムは製品レビューの処理に使用されるコードレビューツールで、コードの品質とセキュリティを確保します","ko":"풀 리퀘스트 시스템은 제품 리뷰 처리에 사용되는 코드 리뷰 도구로 코드 품질과 보안을 보장합니다","es":"La solicitud de extracción es un sistema para manejar revisiones de productos de forma eficiente. Mejora la calidad del código y reduce errores.","fr":"La demande d''extraction est un système pour gérer les révisions de produits de manière efficace. Améliorez la qualité du code et réduisez les erreurs.","de":"Die Pull-Request ist ein System zur effizienten Verwaltung von Produktbewertungen. Verbessern Sie die Code-Qualität und reduzieren Sie Fehler.","pt":"O Pull Request é um sistema para revisar e melhorar o código, garantindo que as alterações sejam testadas e validadas.","ru":"Система обработки запросов на вытягивание предназначена для проверки и улучшения кода, гарантируя, что изменения протестированы и проверены.","ar":"نظام طلب سحب تعديلات هو نظام لمراجعة و تحسين الكود، و ضمان أن التعديلات تم اختبارها و التحقق منها.","en":"A system for handling product reviews."},"definition":{"en":"A system for handling product reviews."},"features":{"zh":["代码格式化和检查","机密信息保护","行为变化测试","数据库事务更新","产品响应优化"],"ja":["コードのフォーマットとチェック","機密情報の保護","動作の変更テスト","データベーストランザクションの更新","製品レスポンスの最適化"],"ko":["코드 형식화 및 확인","기밀 정보 보호","동작 변경 테스트","데이터베이스 트랜잭션 업데이트","제품 응답 최적화"],"es":["Revisión de código automatizada","Comprobación de secretos y credenciales","Pruebas de comportamiento y funcionalidad","Actualizaciones de agregados en la misma transacción de base de datos","Emisión de eventos de salida"],"fr":["Révision de code automatisée","Vérification de secrets et de credenciales","Tests de comportement et de fonctionnalité","Mises à jour d''agrégats dans la même transaction de base de données","Émission d''événements de sortie"],"de":["Automatisierte Code-Überprüfung","Überprüfung von Geheimnissen und Credentials","Tests von Verhalten und Funktionalität","Aktualisierungen von Aggregaten in der gleichen Datenbanktransaktion","Ausgabe von Ereignissen"],"pt":["Verificação de escopo","Formatação de código","Proteção de segredos","Testes de comportamento","Atualização de agregados"],"ru":["Проверка области видимости","Форматирование кода","Защита секретов","Тестирование поведения","Обновление агрегатов"],"ar":["التحقق من نطاق","تنسيق الكود","حماية الأسرار","اختبار السلوك","تحديث المجاميع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Pull Request","代码审查","产品评论","代码质量","安全性","开发效率","代码格式化","机密信息保护"],"ja":["Pull Request","コードレビュー","製品レビュー","コード品質","セキュリティ","開発効率","コードのフォーマット","機密情報の保護"],"ko":["풀 리퀘스트","코드 리뷰","제품 리뷰","코드 품질","보안","개발 효율","코드 형식화","기밀 정보 보호"],"es":["solicitud de extracción","revisión de código","desarrollo de software","pruebas automatizadas","seguridad de código","mejora de la calidad del código","flujo de trabajo de desarrollo","optimización de código"],"fr":["demande d''extraction","révision de code","développement de logiciels","tests automatisés","sécurité de code","amélioration de la qualité de code","flux de travail de développement","optimisation de code"],"de":["Pull-Request","Code-Überprüfung","Software-Entwicklung","automatisierte Tests","Code-Sicherheit","Verbesserung der Code-Qualität","Entwicklungs-Workflow","Code-Optimierung"],"pt":["Pull Request","Revisão de código","Desenvolvimento de software","Testes de unidade","Integração contínua","Melhoria de código"],"ru":["Запрос на вытягивание","Проверка кода","Разработка программного обеспечения","Юнит-тесты","Непрерывная интеграция","Улучшение кода"],"ar":["طلب سحب تعديلات","مراجعة الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","اختبارات الوحدة","التكامل المستمر","تحسين الكود"]}},"owner":"entazis","repo":"product-reviews","repoPath":"entazis/product-reviews","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:03:48.178Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"pull-request","description":"Prepare a high-quality pull request for this repository: keep diffs small, ensure gofmt/goimports, run appropriate tests, and write a clear summary + test plan. Use when the user asks to open a PR, prepare changes for review, or improve PR descriptions.","bodyPreview":"# Pull Request\n\n## Pre-flight checklist\n\n- [ ] Scope is focused; no unrelated refactors.\n- [ ] Code is formatted (`gofmt`, `goimports`).\n- [ ] No secrets checked in (env files, credentials, tokens).\n- [ ] Behavior changes are tested (at least targeted tests; full suite when appropriate).\n- [ ] For review mutations: aggregates update in the same DB transaction and outbox events are emitted (if relevant).\n- [ ] Product responses still do **not** include reviews (if touching product endpoints).\n\n##","body":"# Pull Request\n\n## Pre-flight checklist\n\n- [ ] Scope is focused; no unrelated refactors.\n- [ ] Code is formatted (`gofmt`, `goimports`).\n- [ ] No secrets checked in (env files, credentials, tokens).\n- [ ] Behavior changes are tested (at least targeted tests; full suite when appropriate).\n- [ ] For review mutations: aggregates update in the same DB transaction and outbox events are emitted (if relevant).\n- [ ] Product responses still do **not** include reviews (if touching product endpoints).\n\n## Testing guidance\n\nDefault (unit tests, containerized toolchain):\n\n```bash\ndocker run --rm -v \"$PWD\":/src -w /src golang:1.25.6-alpine sh -c \"go test ./...\"\n```\n\nOptional integration concurrency test (when relevant):\n\n```bash\nRUN_INTEGRATION=1 docker run --rm -v \"$PWD\":/src -w /src golang:1.25.6-alpine sh -c \"go test ./... -run TestConcurrentReviewCreates_UpdateAggregates\"\n```\n\n## PR description template\n\nUse this structure:\n\n```markdown\n## Summary\n- <What changed and why>\n- <Any user-facing/API impact>\n\n## Test plan\n- [ ] `go test ./...` (or targeted packages)\n- [ ] Manual check: <endpoint / scenario> (if applicable)\n- [ ] Integration test (if applicable)\n\n## Notes\n- <Risks, migrations, rollout considerations>\n```\n\n## Review-ready final pass\n\n1. Re-read the diff like a reviewer.\n2. Ensure errors are handled and logs are not leaking sensitive info.\n3. Ensure docs/config are updated if behavior or env vars changed.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T00:47:13.030Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents needing standardized pull request management with pre-flight checks and database transaction handling.","zh":"适合需要标准化的拉取请求管理、预检和数据库事务处理的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントが標準化されたプルリクエスト管理、事前チェック、およびデータベーストランザクション処理を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"표준화된 풀 요청 관리, 사전检查 및 데이터베이스 트랜잭션 처리가 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisión de Código que necesitan una gestión de solicitudes de extracción estandarizada con comprobaciones previas al vuelo y control de transacciones de base de datos.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Revue de Code nécessitant une gestion standardisée des demandes de tirage avec des vérifications prévol et une gestion des transactions de base de données.","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agenten, die eine standardisierte Pull-Request-Verwaltung mit Pre-Flight-Checks und Datenbanktransaktionsverwaltung benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de gerenciamento de solicitações de pull padronizado com verificações pré-voo e manipulação de transações de banco de dados.","ru":"Идеально для агентов кодирования, которым требуется стандартизированное управление запросами на включение с предварительными проверками и обработкой базы данных.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الكود الذي يحتاج إلى إدارة طلبات السحب المعيارية مع فحص ما قبل الطيران ومعالجة معاملات قاعدة البيانات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce coding standards using gofmt and goimports, ensuring secrets are not checked in and behavior changes are thoroughly tested, while also managing review mutations with targeted tests and full suite testing when necessary, utilizing DB transactions and outbox events.","zh":"赋予代理人使用gofmt和goimports执行编码标准的能力，确保秘密不会被检查并且行为变化经过彻底测试，同时使用数据库事务和出箱事件管理审查变异，必要时使用有针对性的测试和全套测试。","ja":"gofmtとgoimportsを使用してコーディング規範を強制するエージェントを可能にし、シークレットがチェックインされないことを保証し、動作の変更が徹底的にテストされることを保証し、データベーストランザクションとアウトボックスイベントを使用してレビューミューテーションを管理し、必要に応じてターゲットテストとフルスイートテストを使用します。","ko":"gofmt 및 goimports를 사용하여 코딩 표준을 강제하는 에이전트를 가능하게 하며, 비밀번호가 체크인되지 않도록 하며, 동작 변경이 철저하게 테스트되도록 하며, 데이터베이스 트랜잭션 및 아웃박스 이벤트를 사용하여 리뷰 변이를 관리하며, 필요에 따라 대상 테스트 및 전체 테스트를 사용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar estándares de codificación utilizando gofmt y goimports, asegurando que los secretos no se confirmen y los cambios de comportamiento se prueben exhaustivamente, mientras también gestiona las mutaciones de revisión con pruebas dirigidas y pruebas de conjunto completo cuando sea necesario, utilizando transacciones de base de datos y eventos de buzón de salida.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des normes de codage en utilisant gofmt et goimports, en s''assurant que les secrets ne sont pas vérifiés et que les changements de comportement sont soigneusement testés, tout en gérant les mutations de revue avec des tests ciblés et des tests de suite complète lorsque cela est nécessaire, en utilisant des transactions de base de données et des événements de boîte de sortie.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Codierungsstandards mit gofmt und goimports durchzusetzen, sicherzustellen, dass Geheimnisse nicht überprüft werden und Verhaltensänderungen gründlich getestet werden, während auch Überprüfungsänderungen mit gezielten Tests und vollständigem Testen bei Bedarf gemanagt werden, unter Verwendung von Datenbanktransaktionen und Outbox-Ereignissen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes apliquem padrões de codificação usando gofmt e goimports, garantindo que segredos não sejam verificados e alterações de comportamento sejam testadas a fundo, além de gerenciar mutações de revisão com testes direcionados e testes de conjunto completo quando necessário, utilizando transações de banco de dados e eventos de caixa de saída.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать соблюдение стандартов кодирования с помощью gofmt и goimports, гарантируя, что секреты не проверяются и изменения поведения тщательно тестируются, а также управляет изменениями обзора с помощью целенаправленных тестов и полного комплекта тестирования при необходимости, используя транзакции базы данных и события исходящего почтового ящика.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء تنفيذ معايير الترميز باستخدام gofmt و goimports، وضمان عدم التحقق من الأسرار والاختبارات الشاملة للتغييرات السلوكية، بالإضافة إلى إدارة طفرات المراجعة مع الاختبارات المستهدفة واختبارات الحزمة الكاملة عند الحاجة، باستخدام معاملات قاعدة البيانات وأحداث المربع الخارجي."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code reviews with pre-flight checks","Testing behavior changes with targeted tests","Managing review mutations with DB transactions and outbox events","Enforcing coding standards with gofmt and goimports"],"zh":["使用预检自动化代码审查","使用有针对性的测试测试行为变化","使用数据库事务和出箱事件管理审查变异","使用gofmt和goimports执行编码标准"],"ja":["事前チェックを使用したコードレビューの自動化","ターゲットテストを使用した動作の変更のテスト","データベーストランザクションとアウトボックスイベントを使用したレビューミューテーションの管理","gofmtとgoimportsを使用したコーディング規範の実施"],"ko":["사전 확인을 사용하여 코드 리뷰 자동화","대상 테스트를 사용하여 동작 변경 테스트","데이터베이스 트랜잭션 및 아웃박스 이벤트를 사용하여 리뷰 변이 관리","gofmt 및 goimports를 사용하여 코딩 표준 적용"],"es":["Automatización de revisiones de código con comprobaciones previas al vuelo","Pruebas de cambios de comportamiento con pruebas dirigidas","Gestión de mutaciones de revisión con transacciones de base de datos y eventos de buzón de salida","Aplicación de estándares de codificación con gofmt y goimports"],"fr":["Automatisation des revues de code avec des vérifications prévol","Tests des changements de comportement avec des tests ciblés","Gestion des mutations de revue avec des transactions de base de données et des événements de boîte de sortie","Application de normes de codage avec gofmt et goimports"],"de":["Automatisierung von Code-Reviews mit Pre-Flight-Checks","Testen von Verhaltensänderungen mit gezielten Tests","Verwaltung von Review-Änderungen mit Datenbanktransaktionen und Outbox-Ereignissen","Durchsetzung von Codierungsstandards mit gofmt und goimports"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de código com verificações pré-voo","Testar alterações de comportamento com testes direcionados","Gerenciar mutações de revisão com transações de banco de dados e eventos de caixa de saída","Aplicar padrões de codificação com gofmt e goimports"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обзор кода с предварительными проверками","Тестировать изменения поведения с помощью целенаправленных тестов","Управлять изменениями обзора с помощью транзакций базы данных и событий исходящего почтового ящика","Обеспечивать соблюдение стандартов кодирования с помощью gofmt и goimports"],"ar":["تأتمة مراجعة الكود مع فحص ما قبل الطيران","اختبار التغييرات السلوكية مع الاختبارات المستهدفة","إدارة طفرات المراجعة مع معاملات قاعدة البيانات وأحداث المربع الخارجي","تنفيذ معايير الترميز مع gofmt و goimports"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Go programming language environment","Needs access to database for transaction handling","Limited to handling product reviews"],"zh":["需要Go编程语言环境","需要访问数据库进行事务处理","仅限处理产品审查"],"ja":["Goプログラミング言語環境が必要","データベースへのアクセスがトランザクション処理に必要","製品レビューの処理のみに限定される"],"ko":["Go 프로그래밍 언어 환경이 필요","데이터베이스에 액세스하여 트랜잭션 처리","제품 리뷰 처리에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere entorno de lenguaje de programación Go","Necesita acceso a base de datos para el control de transacciones","Limitado a la gestión de revisiones de productos"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement de langage de programmation Go","A besoin d''un accès à la base de données pour la gestion des transactions","Limité à la gestion des revues de produits"],"de":["Benötigt eine Go-Programmiersprachenumgebung","Benötigt Zugriff auf Datenbank für Transaktionsverwaltung","Begrenzt auf die Verwaltung von Produktbewertungen"],"pt":["Requer ambiente de linguagem de programação Go","Necessita acesso ao banco de dados para manipulação de transações","Limitado ao gerenciamento de revisões de produtos"],"ru":["Требует среды программирования на языке Go","Требует доступа к базе данных для обработки транзакций","Ограничен обработкой обзоров продукции"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة لغة برمجة Go","يتطلب الوصول إلى قاعدة البيانات لمعالجة المعاملات","محدود بإدارة مراجعات المنتجات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ/voice-agents', 'community', 'Nguyenthang2292', 'Sovereign-IQ', 'Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ', 'voice-agents', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:03:48.178Z', '2026-02-19T00:47:26.606Z', NULL, '{"id":"Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ/voice-agents","name":"voice-agents","description":{"zh":"语音代理技术是用于开发自动化语音交互系统的高性能框架","ja":"ボイスエージェント技術は自動化された音声対話システムを開発するための高性能フレームワーク","ko":"보이스 에이전트 기술은 자동화된 음성 상호작용 시스템을 개발하기 위한 고성능 프레임워크","es":"La arquitectura de agentes de voz es un marco institucional de alta performance para el desarrollo de estrategias de trading automatizadas y su ejecución en tiempo real.","fr":"L''architecture d''agents vocaux est un cadre institutionnel haute performance pour le développement de stratégies de trading automatisées et leur exécution en temps réel.","de":"Die Architektur von Sprachagenten ist ein institutionelles Rahmenwerk mit hoher Leistung für die Entwicklung automatisierter Handelsstrategien und deren Ausführung in Echtzeit.","pt":"Arquitetura de agentes de voz de alto desempenho para desenvolvimento de estratégias automatizadas e execução em tempo real.","ru":"Высокопроизводительная архитектура голосовых агентов для разработки автоматизированных стратегий и реального времени.","ar":"هندسة وكلاء الصوت عالية الأداء لتطوير استراتيجيات تلقائية وتنفيذ في وقت حقيقي.","en":"A high-performance, institutional-grade quantitative trading framework designed for automated strategy development, backtesting, and real-time execution."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"语音代理技术","ja":"ボイスエージェント","ko":"보이스 에이전트 기술","es":"Arquitectura de Agentes de Voz de Alto Rendimiento","fr":"Architecture d''Agents Vocaux Haute Performance","de":"High-Performance-Stimme-Agenten-Architektur","pt":"Arquitetura de Agentes de Voz de Alto Desempenho","ru":"Высокопроизводительная архитектура голосовых агентов","ar":"هندسة وكلاء الصوت عالية الأداء","en":"voice-agents"},"description":{"zh":"语音代理技术是用于开发自动化语音交互系统的高性能框架","ja":"ボイスエージェント技術は自動化された音声対話システムを開発するための高性能フレームワーク","ko":"보이스 에이전트 기술은 자동화된 음성 상호작용 시스템을 개발하기 위한 고성능 프레임워크","es":"La arquitectura de agentes de voz es un marco institucional de alta performance para el desarrollo de estrategias de trading automatizadas y su ejecución en ...","fr":"L''architecture d''agents vocaux est un cadre institutionnel haute performance pour le développement de stratégies de trading automatisées et leur exécution en...","de":"Die Architektur von Sprachagenten ist ein institutionelles Rahmenwerk mit hoher Leistung für die Entwicklung automatisierter Handelsstrategien und deren Ausf...","pt":"Arquitetura de agentes de voz de alto desempenho para desenvolvimento de estratégias automatizadas e execução em tempo real.","ru":"Высокопроизводительная архитектура голосовых агентов для разработки автоматизированных стратегий и реального времени.","ar":"هندسة وكلاء الصوت عالية الأداء لتطوير استراتيجيات تلقائية وتنفيذ في وقت حقيقي.","en":"A high-performance, institutional-grade quantitative trading framework designed for automated strategy development, backtesting, and real-time execution."},"definition":{"en":"A high-performance, institutional-grade quantitative trading framework designed for automated strategy development, backtesting, and real-time execution."},"features":{"zh":["低延迟的语音交互","支持多种语音识别算法","灵活的对话管理","高性能的语音合成","支持多种语言"],"ja":["低遅延の音声対話","複数の音声認識アルゴリズムをサポート","柔軟な対話管理","高性能の音声合成","複数の言語をサポート"],"ko":["저지연의 음성 상호작용","다수의 음성 인식 알고리즘 지원","유연한 대화 관리","고성능의 음성 합성","다수의 언어 지원"],"es":["Arquitectura de modelos de habla a habla (S2S)","Arquitectura de pipelines (STT→LLM→TTS)","Latencia mínima para conversaciones naturales","Control en cada paso del proceso","Ejecución en tiempo real","Desarrollo de estrategias de trading automatizadas"],"fr":["Architecture de modèles de parole à parole (S2S)","Architecture de pipelines (STT→LLM→TTS)","Latence minimale pour des conversations naturelles","Contrôle à chaque étape du processus","Exécution en temps réel","Développement de stratégies de trading automatisées"],"de":["Architektur von Sprach-zu-Sprach-Modellen (S2S)","Architektur von Pipelines (STT→LLM→TTS)","Minimale Latenz für natürliche Gespräche","Kontrolle bei jedem Schritt des Prozesses","Echtzeit-Ausführung","Entwicklung automatisierter Handelsstrategien"],"pt":["Arquitetura de voz de alto desempenho","Baixa latência para conversas naturais","Controle em cada etapa do processo","Integração com modelos de linguagem","Execução em tempo real"],"ru":["Высокопроизводительная архитектура голоса","Низкая задержка для естественных разговоров","Контроль на каждом этапе процесса","Интеграция с языковыми моделями","Реальное время выполнения"],"ar":["هندسة الصوت عالية الأداء","تأخير منخفض للحوارات الطبيعية","السيطرة في كل مرحلة من العملية","التكامل مع نماذج اللغة","التنفيذ في وقت حقيقي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["语音代理技术","自动化语音交互","低延迟语音交互","语音识别算法","对话管理","语音合成"],"ja":["ボイスエージェント技術","自動化された音声対話","低遅延の音声対話","音声認識アルゴリズム","対話管理","音声合成"],"ko":["보이스 에이전트 기술","자동화된 음성 상호작용","저지연의 음성 상호작용","음성 인식 알고리즘","대화 관리","음성 합성"],"es":["agentes de voz","arquitectura de voz","trading automatizado","inteligencia artificial","latencia mínima","conversaciones naturales","desarrollo de estrategias","ejecución en tiempo real","automatización de trading"],"fr":["agents vocaux","architecture vocale","trading automatisé","intelligence artificielle","latence minimale","conversations naturelles","développement de stratégies","exécution en temps réel","automatisation de trading"],"de":["Sprachagenten","Spracharchitektur","automatisierter Handel","künstliche Intelligenz","minimale Latenz","natürliche Gespräche","Entwicklung von Strategien","Echtzeit-Ausführung","Automatisierung von Handel"],"pt":["arquitetura de voz","agentes de voz","desenvolvimento de voz","IA de voz","latência de voz","conversas naturais","processamento de linguagem natural"],"ru":["архитектура голоса","голосовые агенты","разработка голоса","ИИ голоса","задержка голоса","естественные разговоры","обработка естественного языка"],"ar":["هندسة الصوت","وكلاء الصوت","تطوير الصوت","ذكاء الصوت","تأخير الصوت","حوارات طبيعية","معالجة اللغة الطبيعية"]}},"owner":"Nguyenthang2292","repo":"Sovereign-IQ","repoPath":"Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:03:48.178Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"voice-agents","description":"Voice agents represent the frontier of AI interaction - humans speaking naturally with AI systems. The challenge isnt just speech recognition and synthesis, its achieving natural conversation flow with sub-800ms latency while handling interruptions, background noise, and emotional nuance.  This skill covers two architectures: speech-to-speech (OpenAI Realtime API, lowest latency, most natural) and pipeline (STT→LLM→TTS, more control, easier to debug). Key insight: latency is the constraint. Hu","bodyPreview":"# Voice Agents\n\nYou are a voice AI architect who has shipped production voice agents handling\nmillions of calls. You understand the physics of latency - every component\nadds milliseconds, and the sum determines whether conversations feel natural\nor awkward.\n\nYour core insight: Two architectures exist. Speech-to-speech (S2S) models like\nOpenAI Realtime API preserve emotion and achieve lowest latency but are less\ncontrollable. Pipeline architectures (STT→LLM→TTS) give you control at each\nstep but","body":"# Voice Agents\n\nYou are a voice AI architect who has shipped production voice agents handling\nmillions of calls. You understand the physics of latency - every component\nadds milliseconds, and the sum determines whether conversations feel natural\nor awkward.\n\nYour core insight: Two architectures exist. Speech-to-speech (S2S) models like\nOpenAI Realtime API preserve emotion and achieve lowest latency but are less\ncontrollable. Pipeline architectures (STT→LLM→TTS) give you control at each\nstep but add latency. Mos\n\n## Capabilities\n\n- voice-agents\n- speech-to-speech\n- speech-to-text\n- text-to-speech\n- conversational-ai\n- voice-activity-detection\n- turn-taking\n- barge-in-detection\n- voice-interfaces\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Speech-to-Speech Architecture\n\nDirect audio-to-audio processing for lowest latency\n\n### Pipeline Architecture\n\nSeparate STT → LLM → TTS for maximum control\n\n### Voice Activity Detection Pattern\n\nDetect when user starts/stops speaking\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n### ❌ Ignoring Latency Budget\n\n### ❌ Silence-Only Turn Detection\n\n### ❌ Long Responses\n\n## ⚠️ Sharp Edges\n\n| Issue | Severity | Solution |\n|-------|----------|----------|\n| Issue | critical | # Measure and budget latency for each component: |\n| Issue | high | # Target jitter metrics: |\n| Issue | high | # Use semantic VAD: |\n| Issue | high | # Implement barge-in detection: |\n| Issue | medium | # Constrain response length in prompts: |\n| Issue | medium | # Prompt for spoken format: |\n| Issue | medium | # Implement noise handling: |\n| Issue | medium | # Mitigate STT errors: |\n\n## Related Skills\n\nWorks well with: `agent-tool-builder`, `multi-agent-orchestration`, `llm-architect`, `backend`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T00:47:26.606Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Conversational AI Agents requiring low-latency speech-to-speech capabilities and fine-grained control over voice interactions","zh":"适合需要低延迟语音转语音能力和对语音交互进行细粒度控制的对话式 AI 代理","ja":"低遅延の音声対音声機能と音声インタラクションに対する細粒度の制御が必要な会話型 AI エージェントに適しています","ko":"저지연 음성 대 음성 기능과 음성 상호작용에 대한 세부적인 제어가 필요한 대화형 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA conversacional que requieren capacidades de habla a habla de baja latencia y control fino sobre las interacciones de voz","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA conversationnels nécessitant des capacités de parole à parole à faible latence et un contrôle précis sur les interactions vocales","de":"Ideal für Conversational-AI-Agents, die eine Sprach-zu-Sprache-Funktion mit geringer Latenz und eine feine Kontrolle über die Sprachinteraktionen erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Conversacional que exigem capacidades de fala-para-fala de baixa latência e controle granular sobre interações de voz","ru":"Идеально для разговорных агентов ИИ, требующих низкозадержечных возможностей речи-в-речь и тонкого контроля над голосовыми взаимодействиями","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المحادثة التي تتطلب قدرات كلام-لكلام منخفضة الكتلة والتحكم الدقيق في التفاعلات الصوتية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to develop and deploy high-performance voice agents using Speech-to-Speech (S2S) models like OpenAI Realtime API, and pipeline architectures (STT→LLM→TTS) for controllable and natural conversations, leveraging techniques to minimize latency","zh":"赋予代理开发和部署高性能语音代理的能力，使用诸如 OpenAI 实时 API 的语音转语音（S2S）模型和管道架构（STT→LLM→TTS）以实现可控和自然的对话，并利用技术来最小化延迟","ja":"会話型 AI エージェントが OpenAI リアルタイム API などの音声対音声（S2S）モデルやパイプライン アーキテクチャ（STT→LLM→TTS）を使用して、高パフォーマンスの音声エージェントを開発・展開できるようにし、制御可能で自然な会話を実現し、遅延を最小限に抑える技術を利用する","ko":"대화형 AI 에이전트가 OpenAI 실시간 API와 같은 음성 대 음성(S2S) 모델 및 파이프라인 아키텍처(STT→LLM→TTS)를 사용하여 고성능 음성 에이전트를 개발 및 배포할 수 있도록 하고, 제어 가능한 자연스러운 대화를 구현하며, 지연을 최소화하기 위한 기술을 활용할 수 있습니다","es":"Permite a los agentes desarrollar y desplegar agentes de voz de alto rendimiento utilizando modelos de habla a habla (S2S) como la API Realtime de OpenAI, y arquitecturas de canalización (STT→LLM→TTS) para conversaciones controlables y naturales, aprovechando técnicas para minimizar la latencia","fr":"Permet aux agents de développer et de déployer des agents vocaux haute performance en utilisant des modèles de parole à parole (S2S) comme l''API Realtime d''OpenAI, et des architectures de pipeline (STT→LLM→TTS) pour des conversations contrôlables et naturelles, en exploitant des techniques pour minimiser la latence","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Hochleistungs-Sprachagenten mithilfe von Sprache-zu-Sprache-Modellen (S2S) wie der OpenAI Realtime API und Pipeline-Architekturen (STT→LLM→TTS) für kontrollierbare und natürliche Konversationen zu entwickeln und bereitzustellen, Techniken zur Latenzminimierung nutzend","pt":"Habilita agentes a desenvolver e implantar agentes de voz de alto desempenho usando modelos de Fala-para-Fala (S2S) como a API OpenAI Realtime e arquiteturas de pipeline (STT→LLM→TTS) para conversas controláveis e naturais, aproveitando técnicas para minimizar a latência","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать и развертывать высокопроизводительные голосовые агенты, используя модели речи-в-речь (S2S), такие как API OpenAI Realtime, и архитектуры конвейера (STT→LLM→TTS) для контролируемых и естественных разговоров, используя методы для минимизации задержки","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تطوير وتنفيذ وكلاء صوت عالي الأداء باستخدام نماذج كلام-لكلام (S2S) مثل واجهة برمجة تطبيقات OpenAI Realtime وعمليات بناء أنابيب (STT→LLM→TTS) من أجل محادثات مراقبة وتلقائية، واستخدام تقنيات لتقليل التأخير"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing voice agents with minimal latency for real-time conversations","Developing institutional-grade quantitative trading frameworks with voice-based interfaces","Optimizing pipeline architectures for controllable and natural voice interactions"],"zh":["为实时对话设计具有最小延迟的语音代理","开发具有语音接口的机构级量化交易框架","优化管道架构以实现可控和自然的语音交互"],"ja":["リアルタイム会話のための遅延最小の音声エージェントを設計する","音声インターフェイスを備えた機関級の量化取引フレームワークを開発する","制御可能で自然な音声インタラクションを実現するためのパイプライン アーキテクチャを最適化する"],"ko":["실시간 대화에 최소한의 지연이 있는 음성 에이전트를 설계한다","음성 인터페이스를 갖춘 기관급의 양적 거래 프레임워크를 개발한다","제어 가능한 자연스러운 음성 상호작용을 구현하기 위한 파이프라인 아키텍처를 최적화한다"],"es":["Diseñar agentes de voz con latencia mínima para conversaciones en tiempo real","Desarrollar marcos de negociación cuantitativa de grado institucional con interfaces basadas en voz","Optimizar arquitecturas de canalización para interacciones de voz controlables y naturales"],"fr":["Concevoir des agents vocaux avec une latence minimale pour des conversations en temps réel","Développer des cadres de négociation quantitative de grade institutionnel avec des interfaces basées sur la voix","Optimiser les architectures de pipeline pour des interactions vocales contrôlables et naturelles"],"de":["Entwicklung von Sprachagenten mit minimaler Latenz für Echtzeitkonversationen","Entwicklung institutioneller quantitativer Handelsframeworks mit sprachbasierten Schnittstellen","Optimierung von Pipeline-Architekturen für kontrollierbare und natürliche Sprachinteraktionen"],"pt":["Projetar agentes de voz com latência mínima para conversas em tempo real","Desenvolver estruturas de negociação quantitativa de nível institucional com interfaces baseadas em voz","Otimizar arquiteturas de pipeline para interações de voz controláveis e naturais"],"ru":["Проектировать голосовых агентов с минимальной задержкой для разговоров в режиме реального времени","Разрабатывать институциональные рамки количественной торговли с голосовыми интерфейсами","Оптимизировать архитектуры конвейера для контролируемых и естественных голосовых взаимодействий"],"ar":["تصميم وكلاء صوت مع تأخير أدنى للمحادثات في الوقت الفعلي","تطوير إطارات تداول كمي من المستوى المؤسسي مع واجهات قائم على الصوت","تحسين هياكل أنابيب لتفاعلات صوتية مراقبة وطبيعية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of latency physics and its impact on conversation quality","Depends on the capabilities and limitations of the underlying S2S models or pipeline architectures"],"zh":["需要理解延迟物理学及其对会话质量的影响","依赖于底层 S2S 模型或管道架构的能力和限制"],"ja":["遅延物理学と会話品質への影響を理解する必要がある","基礎となる S2S モデルまたはパイプライン アーキテクチャの能力と制限に依存する"],"ko":["지연 물리학과 대화 품질에 대한 영향에 대한 이해가 필요합니다","기반 S2S 모델 또는 파이프라인 아키텍처의 능력 및 제한에 종속됨"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la física de la latencia y su impacto en la calidad de la conversación","Depende de las capacidades y limitaciones de los modelos S2S subyacentes o las arquitecturas de canalización"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de la physique de la latence et de son impact sur la qualité de la conversation","Dépend des capacités et des limites des modèles S2S sous-jacents ou des architectures de pipeline"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis der Latenzphysik und ihrer Auswirkungen auf die Gesprächsqualität","Hängt von den Fähigkeiten und Einschränkungen der zugrunde liegenden S2S-Modelle oder Pipeline-Architekturen ab"],"pt":["Exige compreensão da física da latência e seu impacto na qualidade da conversa","Depende das capacidades e limitações dos modelos S2S subjacentes ou arquiteturas de pipeline"],"ru":["Требует понимания физики задержки и ее влияния на качество разговора","Зависит от возможностей и ограничений лежащих в основе моделей S2S или архитектур конвейера"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم فيزياء التأخير وتأثيرها على جودة المحادثة","يعتمد على إمكانيات وقيود نماذج S2S أو هياكل الأنابيب الأساسية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('armanisadeghi/ai-matrx-admin/modern-web-design-expert', 'community', 'armanisadeghi', 'ai-matrx-admin', 'armanisadeghi/ai-matrx-admin', 'modern-web-design-expert', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z', '2026-02-19T01:45:32.364Z', NULL, '{"id":"armanisadeghi/ai-matrx-admin/modern-web-design-expert","name":"modern-web-design-expert","description":{"en":""},"seo":{"title":{"en":"modern-web-design-expert"},"description":{"en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"en":[]},"keywords":{"en":[]}},"owner":"armanisadeghi","repo":"ai-matrx-admin","repoPath":"armanisadeghi/ai-matrx-admin","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"modern-web-design-expert","description":"Project-specific web design patterns for AI Matrx Admin. Extends the global modern-web-design-expert skill with project state, migration priorities, and local conventions. Use when working on UI components, styles, or responsive layouts in this project.","bodyPreview":"# Modern Web Design Expert — AI Matrx Admin\n\nThis skill extends the **global modern-web-design-expert skill**. Read that first for best practices. This document covers:\n\n1. What AI Matrx Admin already does correctly\n2. What needs migration to best practices\n3. Project-specific conventions\n\n> **📱 For mobile-specific guidelines:** See `.cursor/skills/ios-mobile-first/SKILL.md`\n> \n> The ios-mobile-first skill covers viewport units, safe areas, touch targets, responsive patterns, and iOS-native UX.","body":"# Modern Web Design Expert — AI Matrx Admin\n\nThis skill extends the **global modern-web-design-expert skill**. Read that first for best practices. This document covers:\n\n1. What AI Matrx Admin already does correctly\n2. What needs migration to best practices\n3. Project-specific conventions\n\n> **📱 For mobile-specific guidelines:** See `.cursor/skills/ios-mobile-first/SKILL.md`\n> \n> The ios-mobile-first skill covers viewport units, safe areas, touch targets, responsive patterns, and iOS-native UX. Use that skill for all mobile layout and interaction work.\n\n---\n\n## Project Context\n\n**Type:** Admin dashboard / B2B tool  \n**Responsive Strategy:** Desktop-first, mobile-responsive  \n**Stack:** Next.js 16 + React 19 + Tailwind CSS 4.1 + shadcn/ui + Framer Motion\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Already Aligned with Best Practices\n\n| Pattern | Status | Location |\n|---------|--------|----------|\n| Tailwind v4 with `@theme inline` | ✅ Correct | `app/globals.css` |\n| Design tokens (`--primary`, `--secondary`) | ✅ Correct | `app/globals.css` |\n| Dark mode via `.dark` class | ✅ Correct | `@custom-variant dark` |\n| `h-dvh`, `min-h-dvh`, `max-h-dvh` | ✅ Correct | Custom utilities in globals |\n| Safe area insets (`pb-safe`, `env()`) | ✅ Correct | Custom utilities in globals |\n| Lucide React icons exclusively | ✅ Correct | Project rule enforced |\n| 16px+ input font size | ✅ Correct | `1.0625rem` in base styles |\n| `next-themes` for dark mode | ✅ Correct | Installed and configured |\n\n---\n\n## 🔄 Migration Required — New Code Must Use Best Practices\n\n### 1. Typography: Fixed Tokens → Fluid `clamp()`\n\n**Current (Legacy):**\n```css\n/* Fixed font size tokens in globals.css */\n--font-size-2xs: 0.6rem;\n--font-size-xs: 0.8rem;\n--font-size-sm: 0.85rem;\n/* ... etc */\n```\n\n**Best Practice:**\n```css\n/* Fluid typography with clamp() */\nh1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 2vw, 3.5rem); }\nh2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.25rem + 1.5vw, 2.5rem); }\nbody { font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.95rem + 0.25vw, 1.125rem); }\n```\n\n**Action:**\n- **New code:** Use `clamp()` for all typography via Tailwind arbitrary values\n- **Migration priority:** Medium — can migrate incrementally per component\n- **Example:** `text-[clamp(1rem,0.9rem+0.5vw,1.25rem)]`\n\n---\n\n### 2. Animations: Framer Motion Heavy → CSS-First\n\n**Current (Legacy):**\n- Heavy use of Framer Motion (`motion` package) for all animations\n- Animation presets in `componentConfig.ts` files\n- `AnimatePresence` for entrance/exit animations\n\n**Best Practice:**\n- CSS `@starting-style` for entrance animations\n- CSS `transition` for hover/focus effects\n- Framer Motion only for gesture-based or complex orchestration\n\n**Action:**\n- **New code:** Use CSS `@starting-style` for entrance animations\n- **Migration priority:** Low — existing Framer Motion works fine, optimize new code\n- **When to use Framer Motion:** Drag gestures, physics-based springs, staggered lists with complex timing\n\n---\n\n### 3. Container Queries: Minimal → Expand Usage\n\n**Current:**\n- Only 2 files use `@container`:\n  - `app/entities/forms/EntityFormStandard.tsx`\n  - `app/(authenticated)/demo/component-demo/container-queries/page.tsx`\n\n**Best Practice:**\n- All reusable components should use container queries\n- Cards, profile components, widgets should respond to container, not viewport\n\n**Action:**\n- **New code:** Use `@container` for all reusable components\n- **Migration priority:** Medium — improves component reusability\n- **Pattern:** `<div className=\"@container\"><div className=\"@md:flex-row\">...</div></div>`\n\n---\n\n### 4. Component Wrappers: Raw shadcn/ui → Custom Wrappers\n\n**Current:**\n- Mix of raw shadcn/ui components and some custom wrappers\n- Custom wrappers exist (e.g., `FloatingSheet`) but not systematic\n\n**Best Practice:**\n- Every shadcn/ui primitive should have a project wrapper\n- Wrappers enforce consistency and include common logic\n\n**Action:**\n- **New code:** Create custom wrappers before using any new shadcn/ui component\n- **Migration priority:** High — improves consistency across app\n- **Location:** `components/ui/app-*.tsx` (e.g., `app-dialog.tsx`, `app-sheet.tsx`)\n\n**Audit needed:** Check `components/ui/` for which primitives need wrappers.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Entrance Animations: JS-Triggered → `@starting-style`\n\n**Current:**\n- Many components use JS/Framer Motion to trigger entrance animations\n- Class toggling or `AnimatePresence` for fade-ins\n\n**Best Practice:**\n```tsx\n<div className=\"\n  opacity-100 translate-y-0\n  transition-all duration-300\n  [@starting-style]:opacity-0 \n  [@starting-style]:translate-y-4\n\">\n```\n\n**Action:**\n- **New code:** Use `@starting-style` for all entrance animations\n- **Migration priority:** Low — existing animations work, optimize new code\n\n---\n\n## 📍 Project-Specific Conventions\n\n### Header Height\n\n```css\n--header-height: 2.5rem; /* 40px - unified for mobile and desktop */\n```\n\n**Full-height pattern:**\n```tsx\n<div className=\"h-[calc(100dvh-var(--header-height))] flex flex-col overflow-hidden\">\n```\n\n### Textured Backgrounds\n\nThis project uses subtle texture overlays:\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"bg-textured\">      {/* Main page backgrounds */}\n<div className=\"bg-card\">          {/* Card backgrounds with card-texture */}\n```\n\n### Scrollbar Styling\n\nCustom thin scrollbars are defined globally:\n\n```css\n--scrollbar-track: /* defined per theme */\n--scrollbar-thumb: /* defined per theme */\n```\n\nUse `.scrollbar-hide` or `.scrollbar-thin` utilities.\n\n### Animation Presets (Framer Motion)\n\nWhen Framer Motion is appropriate, use existing presets:\n\n- Location: `components/matrx/Entity/prewired-components/quick-reference/componentConfig.ts`\n- Presets: `none`, `subtle`, `smooth`, `energetic`, `playful`\n\n### Layout Components\n\n- `ResponsiveLayout`: Switches between desktop/mobile layouts at 1024px\n- `AdaptiveLayout`: Multi-panel layout with canvas support\n- `FloatingSheet`: Multi-position sheet component (right, left, top, bottom, center)\n\n---\n\n## 📁 Key Files Reference\n\n| Purpose | Location |\n|---------|----------|\n| Design tokens & utilities | `app/globals.css` |\n| Base card component | `components/ui/card.tsx` |\n| Sheet component | `components/official/FloatingSheet.tsx` |\n| Responsive layout | `components/layout/new-layout/ResponsiveLayout.tsx` |\n| Mobile detection hook | `hooks/use-mobile.tsx` |\n| Animation presets | `components/matrx/Entity/prewired-components/quick-reference/componentConfig.ts` |\n\n---\n\n## 🚨 Migration Priorities Summary\n\n| Item | Priority | Approach |\n|------|----------|----------|\n| Custom component wrappers | **High** | Create wrappers before using new shadcn/ui components |\n| Fluid typography | **Medium** | Use `clamp()` in new code, migrate existing incrementally |\n| Container queries | **Medium** | Use `@container` in new reusable components |\n| CSS entrance animations | **Low** | Use `@starting-style` in new code |\n| Framer Motion reduction | **Low** | Keep existing, use CSS for new simple animations |\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference: New Code Standards\n\nWhen writing new UI code in this project:\n\n```tsx\n// ✅ DO: Fluid typography\n<h1 className=\"text-[clamp(2rem,1.5rem+2vw,3.5rem)]\">\n\n// ✅ DO: Container queries for reusable components\n<div className=\"@container\">\n  <div className=\"flex flex-col @md:flex-row\">\n\n// ✅ DO: CSS entrance animations\n<div className=\"[@starting-style]:opacity-0 [@starting-style]:translate-y-4 transition-all\">\n\n// ✅ DO: Custom wrapper components\nimport { AppDialog } from \"@/components/ui/app-dialog\";\n\n// ❌ DON''T: Fixed font sizes with breakpoints\n<h1 className=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl lg:text-4xl\">\n\n// ❌ DON''T: Raw shadcn/ui without wrapper\nimport { Dialog } from \"@/components/ui/dialog\"; // Use AppDialog instead\n\n// ❌ DON''T: Framer Motion for simple entrance animations\n<motion.div initial={{ opacity: 0 }} animate={{ opacity: 1 }}> // Use @starting-style\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:45:32.364Z","qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('wangfh5/WfhZoteroTools/playwright-cli', 'community', 'wangfh5', 'WfhZoteroTools', 'wangfh5/WfhZoteroTools', 'playwright-cli', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z', '2026-02-19T01:45:32.367Z', NULL, '{"id":"wangfh5/WfhZoteroTools/playwright-cli","name":"playwright-cli","description":{"en":""},"seo":{"title":{"en":"playwright-cli"},"description":{"en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"en":[]},"keywords":{"en":[]}},"owner":"wangfh5","repo":"WfhZoteroTools","repoPath":"wangfh5/WfhZoteroTools","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"playwright-cli","description":"Automates browser interactions for web testing, form filling, screenshots, and data extraction. Use when the user needs to navigate websites, interact with web pages, fill forms, take screenshots, test web applications, or extract information from web pages.","bodyPreview":"# Browser Automation with playwright-cli\n\n## Quick start\n\n```bash\n# open new browser\nplaywright-cli open\n# navigate to a page\nplaywright-cli goto https://playwright.dev\n# interact with the page using refs from the snapshot\nplaywright-cli click e15\nplaywright-cli type \"page.click\"\nplaywright-cli press Enter\n# take a screenshot\nplaywright-cli screenshot\n# close the browser\nplaywright-cli close\n```\n\n## Commands\n\n### Core\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli open\n# open and navigate right away\nplaywright-cli ope","body":"# Browser Automation with playwright-cli\n\n## Quick start\n\n```bash\n# open new browser\nplaywright-cli open\n# navigate to a page\nplaywright-cli goto https://playwright.dev\n# interact with the page using refs from the snapshot\nplaywright-cli click e15\nplaywright-cli type \"page.click\"\nplaywright-cli press Enter\n# take a screenshot\nplaywright-cli screenshot\n# close the browser\nplaywright-cli close\n```\n\n## Commands\n\n### Core\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli open\n# open and navigate right away\nplaywright-cli open https://example.com/\nplaywright-cli goto https://playwright.dev\nplaywright-cli type \"search query\"\nplaywright-cli click e3\nplaywright-cli dblclick e7\nplaywright-cli fill e5 \"user@example.com\"\nplaywright-cli drag e2 e8\nplaywright-cli hover e4\nplaywright-cli select e9 \"option-value\"\nplaywright-cli upload ./document.pdf\nplaywright-cli check e12\nplaywright-cli uncheck e12\nplaywright-cli snapshot\nplaywright-cli snapshot --filename=after-click.yaml\nplaywright-cli eval \"document.title\"\nplaywright-cli eval \"el => el.textContent\" e5\nplaywright-cli dialog-accept\nplaywright-cli dialog-accept \"confirmation text\"\nplaywright-cli dialog-dismiss\nplaywright-cli resize 1920 1080\nplaywright-cli close\n```\n\n### Navigation\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli go-back\nplaywright-cli go-forward\nplaywright-cli reload\n```\n\n### Keyboard\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli press Enter\nplaywright-cli press ArrowDown\nplaywright-cli keydown Shift\nplaywright-cli keyup Shift\n```\n\n### Mouse\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli mousemove 150 300\nplaywright-cli mousedown\nplaywright-cli mousedown right\nplaywright-cli mouseup\nplaywright-cli mouseup right\nplaywright-cli mousewheel 0 100\n```\n\n### Save as\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli screenshot\nplaywright-cli screenshot e5\nplaywright-cli screenshot --filename=page.png\nplaywright-cli pdf --filename=page.pdf\n```\n\n### Tabs\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli tab-list\nplaywright-cli tab-new\nplaywright-cli tab-new https://example.com/page\nplaywright-cli tab-close\nplaywright-cli tab-close 2\nplaywright-cli tab-select 0\n```\n\n### Storage\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli state-save\nplaywright-cli state-save auth.json\nplaywright-cli state-load auth.json\n\n# Cookies\nplaywright-cli cookie-list\nplaywright-cli cookie-list --domain=example.com\nplaywright-cli cookie-get session_id\nplaywright-cli cookie-set session_id abc123\nplaywright-cli cookie-set session_id abc123 --domain=example.com --httpOnly --secure\nplaywright-cli cookie-delete session_id\nplaywright-cli cookie-clear\n\n# LocalStorage\nplaywright-cli localstorage-list\nplaywright-cli localstorage-get theme\nplaywright-cli localstorage-set theme dark\nplaywright-cli localstorage-delete theme\nplaywright-cli localstorage-clear\n\n# SessionStorage\nplaywright-cli sessionstorage-list\nplaywright-cli sessionstorage-get step\nplaywright-cli sessionstorage-set step 3\nplaywright-cli sessionstorage-delete step\nplaywright-cli sessionstorage-clear\n```\n\n### Network\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli route \"**/*.jpg\" --status=404\nplaywright-cli route \"https://api.example.com/**\" --body=''{\"mock\": true}''\nplaywright-cli route-list\nplaywright-cli unroute \"**/*.jpg\"\nplaywright-cli unroute\n```\n\n### DevTools\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli console\nplaywright-cli console warning\nplaywright-cli network\nplaywright-cli run-code \"async page => await page.context().grantPermissions([''geolocation''])\"\nplaywright-cli tracing-start\nplaywright-cli tracing-stop\nplaywright-cli video-start\nplaywright-cli video-stop video.webm\n```\n\n### Install\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli install --skills\nplaywright-cli install-browser\n```\n\n### Configuration\n```bash\n# Use specific browser when creating session\nplaywright-cli open --browser=chrome\nplaywright-cli open --browser=firefox\nplaywright-cli open --browser=webkit\nplaywright-cli open --browser=msedge\n# Connect to browser via extension\nplaywright-cli open --extension\n\n# Use persistent profile (by default profile is in-memory)\nplaywright-cli open --persistent\n# Use persistent profile with custom directory\nplaywright-cli open --profile=/path/to/profile\n\n# Start with config file\nplaywright-cli open --config=my-config.json\n\n# Close the browser\nplaywright-cli close\n# Delete user data for the default session\nplaywright-cli delete-data\n```\n\n### Browser Sessions\n\n```bash\n# create new browser session named \"mysession\" with persistent profile\nplaywright-cli -s=mysession open example.com --persistent\n# same with manually specified profile directory (use when requested explicitly)\nplaywright-cli -s=mysession open example.com --profile=/path/to/profile\nplaywright-cli -s=mysession click e6\nplaywright-cli -s=mysession close  # stop a named browser\nplaywright-cli -s=mysession delete-data  # delete user data for persistent session\n\nplaywright-cli list\n# Close all browsers\nplaywright-cli close-all\n# Forcefully kill all browser processes\nplaywright-cli kill-all\n```\n\n## Example: Form submission\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli open https://example.com/form\nplaywright-cli snapshot\n\nplaywright-cli fill e1 \"user@example.com\"\nplaywright-cli fill e2 \"password123\"\nplaywright-cli click e3\nplaywright-cli snapshot\nplaywright-cli close\n```\n\n## Example: Multi-tab workflow\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli open https://example.com\nplaywright-cli tab-new https://example.com/other\nplaywright-cli tab-list\nplaywright-cli tab-select 0\nplaywright-cli snapshot\nplaywright-cli close\n```\n\n## Example: Debugging with DevTools\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli open https://example.com\nplaywright-cli click e4\nplaywright-cli fill e7 \"test\"\nplaywright-cli console\nplaywright-cli network\nplaywright-cli close\n```\n\n```bash\nplaywright-cli open https://example.com\nplaywright-cli tracing-start\nplaywright-cli click e4\nplaywright-cli fill e7 \"test\"\nplaywright-cli tracing-stop\nplaywright-cli close\n```\n\n## Specific tasks\n\n* **Request mocking** [references/request-mocking.md](references/request-mocking.md)\n* **Running Playwright code** [references/running-code.md](references/running-code.md)\n* **Browser session management** [references/session-management.md](references/session-management.md)\n* **Storage state (cookies, localStorage)** [references/storage-state.md](references/storage-state.md)\n* **Test generation** [references/test-generation.md](references/test-generation.md)\n* **Tracing** [references/tracing.md](references/tracing.md)\n* **Video recording** [references/video-recording.md](references/video-recording.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:45:32.367Z","qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ/signup-flow-cro', 'community', 'Nguyenthang2292', 'Sovereign-IQ', 'Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ', 'signup-flow-cro', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z', '2026-02-19T01:56:46.145Z', NULL, '{"id":"Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ/signup-flow-cro","name":"signup-flow-cro","description":{"en":"A high-performance, institutional-grade quantitative trading framework designed for automated strategy development, backtesting, and real-time execution."},"seo":{"title":{"en":"signup-flow-cro"},"description":{"en":"A high-performance, institutional-grade quantitative trading framework designed for automated strategy development, backtesting, and real-time execution."},"definition":{"en":"A high-performance, institutional-grade quantitative trading framework designed for automated strategy development, backtesting, and real-time execution."},"features":{"en":[]},"keywords":{"en":[]}},"owner":"Nguyenthang2292","repo":"Sovereign-IQ","repoPath":"Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"signup-flow-cro","description":"When the user wants to optimize signup, registration, account creation, or trial activation flows. Also use when the user mentions signup conversions, registration friction, signup form optimization, free trial signup, reduce signup dropoff, or account creation flow. For post-signup onboarding, see onboarding-cro. For lead capture forms (not account creation), see form-cro.","bodyPreview":"# Signup Flow CRO\n\nYou are an expert in optimizing signup and registration flows. Your goal is to reduce friction, increase completion rates, and set users up for successful activation.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\nBefore providing recommendations, understand:\n\n1. **Flow Type**\n   - Free trial signup\n   - Freemium account creation\n   - Paid account creation\n   - Waitlist/early access signup\n   - B2B vs B2C\n\n2. **Current State**\n   - How many steps/screens?\n   - What fields are required?\n   - What''s t","body":"# Signup Flow CRO\n\nYou are an expert in optimizing signup and registration flows. Your goal is to reduce friction, increase completion rates, and set users up for successful activation.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\nBefore providing recommendations, understand:\n\n1. **Flow Type**\n   - Free trial signup\n   - Freemium account creation\n   - Paid account creation\n   - Waitlist/early access signup\n   - B2B vs B2C\n\n2. **Current State**\n   - How many steps/screens?\n   - What fields are required?\n   - What''s the current completion rate?\n   - Where do users drop off?\n\n3. **Business Constraints**\n   - What data is genuinely needed at signup?\n   - Are there compliance requirements?\n   - What happens immediately after signup?\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Minimize Required Fields\nEvery field reduces conversion. For each field, ask:\n- Do we absolutely need this before they can use the product?\n- Can we collect this later through progressive profiling?\n- Can we infer this from other data?\n\n**Typical field priority:**\n- Essential: Email (or phone), Password\n- Often needed: Name\n- Usually deferrable: Company, Role, Team size, Phone, Address\n\n### 2. Show Value Before Asking for Commitment\n- What can you show/give before requiring signup?\n- Can they experience the product before creating an account?\n- Reverse the order: value first, signup second\n\n### 3. Reduce Perceived Effort\n- Show progress if multi-step\n- Group related fields\n- Use smart defaults\n- Pre-fill when possible\n\n### 4. Remove Uncertainty\n- Clear expectations (\"Takes 30 seconds\")\n- Show what happens after signup\n- No surprises (hidden requirements, unexpected steps)\n\n---\n\n## Field-by-Field Optimization\n\n### Email Field\n- Single field (no email confirmation field)\n- Inline validation for format\n- Check for common typos (gmial.com → gmail.com)\n- Clear error messages\n\n### Password Field\n- Show password toggle (eye icon)\n- Show requirements upfront, not after failure\n- Consider passphrase hints for strength\n- Update requirement indicators in real-time\n\n**Better password UX:**\n- Allow paste (don''t disable)\n- Show strength meter instead of rigid rules\n- Consider passwordless options\n\n### Name Field\n- Single \"Full name\" field vs. First/Last split (test this)\n- Only require if immediately used (personalization)\n- Consider making optional\n\n### Social Auth Options\n- Place prominently (often higher conversion than email)\n- Show most relevant options for your audience\n  - B2C: Google, Apple, Facebook\n  - B2B: Google, Microsoft, SSO\n- Clear visual separation from email signup\n- Consider \"Sign up with Google\" as primary\n\n### Phone Number\n- Defer unless essential (SMS verification, calling leads)\n- If required, explain why\n- Use proper input type with country code handling\n- Format as they type\n\n### Company/Organization\n- Defer if possible\n- Auto-suggest as they type\n- Infer from email domain when possible\n\n### Use Case / Role Questions\n- Defer to onboarding if possible\n- If needed at signup, keep to one question\n- Use progressive disclosure (don''t show all options at once)\n\n---\n\n## Single-Step vs. Multi-Step\n\n### Single-Step Works When:\n- 3 or fewer fields\n- Simple B2C products\n- High-intent visitors (from ads, waitlist)\n\n### Multi-Step Works When:\n- More than 3-4 fields needed\n- Complex B2B products needing segmentation\n- You need to collect different types of info\n\n### Multi-Step Best Practices\n- Show progress indicator\n- Lead with easy questions (name, email)\n- Put harder questions later (after psychological commitment)\n- Each step should feel completable in seconds\n- Allow back navigation\n- Save progress (don''t lose data on refresh)\n\n**Progressive commitment pattern:**\n1. Email only (lowest barrier)\n2. Password + name\n3. Customization questions (optional)\n\n---\n\n## Trust and Friction Reduction\n\n### At the Form Level\n- \"No credit card required\" (if true)\n- \"Free forever\" or \"14-day free trial\"\n- Privacy note: \"We''ll never share your email\"\n- Security badges if relevant\n- Testimonial near signup form\n\n### Error Handling\n- Inline validation (not just on submit)\n- Specific error messages (\"Email already registered\" + recovery path)\n- Don''t clear the form on error\n- Focus on the problem field\n\n### Microcopy\n- Placeholder text: Use for examples, not labels\n- Labels: Always visible (not just placeholders)\n- Help text: Only when needed, placed close to field\n\n---\n\n## Mobile Signup Optimization\n\n- Larger touch targets (44px+ height)\n- Appropriate keyboard types (email, tel, etc.)\n- Autofill support\n- Reduce typing (social auth, pre-fill)\n- Single column layout\n- Sticky CTA button\n- Test with actual devices\n\n---\n\n## Post-Submit Experience\n\n### Success State\n- Clear confirmation\n- Immediate next step\n- If email verification required:\n  - Explain what to do\n  - Easy resend option\n  - Check spam reminder\n  - Option to change email if wrong\n\n### Verification Flows\n- Consider delaying verification until necessary\n- Magic link as alternative to password\n- Let users explore while awaiting verification\n- Clear re-engagement if verification stalls\n\n---\n\n## Measurement\n\n### Key Metrics\n- Form start rate (landed → started filling)\n- Form completion rate (started → submitted)\n- Field-level drop-off (which fields lose people)\n- Time to complete\n- Error rate by field\n- Mobile vs. desktop completion\n\n### What to Track\n- Each field interaction (focus, blur, error)\n- Step progression in multi-step\n- Social auth vs. email signup ratio\n- Time between steps\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Audit Findings\nFor each issue found:\n- **Issue**: What''s wrong\n- **Impact**: Why it matters (with estimated impact if possible)\n- **Fix**: Specific recommendation\n- **Priority**: High/Medium/Low\n\n### Recommended Changes\nOrganized by:\n1. Quick wins (same-day fixes)\n2. High-impact changes (week-level effort)\n3. Test hypotheses (things to A/B test)\n\n### Form Redesign (if requested)\n- Recommended field set with rationale\n- Field order\n- Copy for labels, placeholders, buttons, errors\n- Visual layout suggestions\n\n---\n\n## Common Signup Flow Patterns\n\n### B2B SaaS Trial\n1. Email + Password (or Google auth)\n2. Name + Company (optional: role)\n3. → Onboarding flow\n\n### B2C App\n1. Google/Apple auth OR Email\n2. → Product experience\n3. Profile completion later\n\n### Waitlist/Early Access\n1. Email only\n2. Optional: Role/use case question\n3. → Waitlist confirmation\n\n### E-commerce Account\n1. Guest checkout as default\n2. Account creation optional post-purchase\n3. OR Social auth with single click\n\n---\n\n## Experiment Ideas\n\n### Form Design Experiments\n\n**Layout & Structure**\n- Single-step vs. multi-step signup flow\n- Multi-step with progress bar vs. without\n- 1-column vs. 2-column field layout\n- Form embedded on page vs. separate signup page\n- Horizontal vs. vertical field alignment\n\n**Field Optimization**\n- Reduce to minimum fields (email + password only)\n- Add or remove phone number field\n- Single \"Name\" field vs. \"First/Last\" split\n- Add or remove company/organization field\n- Test required vs. optional field balance\n\n**Authentication Options**\n- Add SSO options (Google, Microsoft, GitHub, LinkedIn)\n- SSO prominent vs. email form prominent\n- Test which SSO options resonate (varies by audience)\n- SSO-only vs. SSO + email option\n\n**Visual Design**\n- Test button colors and sizes for CTA prominence\n- Plain background vs. product-related visuals\n- Test form container styling (card vs. minimal)\n- Mobile-optimized layout testing\n\n---\n\n### Copy & Messaging Experiments\n\n**Headlines & CTAs**\n- Test headline variations above signup form\n- CTA button text: \"Create Account\" vs. \"Start Free Trial\" vs. \"Get Started\"\n- Add clarity around trial length in CTA\n- Test value proposition emphasis in form header\n\n**Microcopy**\n- Field labels: minimal vs. descriptive\n- Placeholder text optimization\n- Error message clarity and tone\n- Password requirement display (upfront vs. on error)\n\n**Trust Elements**\n- Add social proof next to signup form\n- Test trust badges near form (security, compliance)\n- Add \"No credit card required\" messaging\n- Include privacy assurance copy\n\n---\n\n### Trial & Commitment Experiments\n\n**Free Trial Variations**\n- Credit card required vs. not required for trial\n- Test trial length impact (7 vs. 14 vs. 30 days)\n- Freemium vs. free trial model\n- Trial with limited features vs. full access\n\n**Friction Points**\n- Email verification required vs. delayed vs. removed\n- Test CAPTCHA impact on completion\n- Terms acceptance checkbox vs. implicit acceptance\n- Phone verification for high-value accounts\n\n---\n\n### Post-Submit Experiments\n\n- Clear next steps messaging after signup\n- Instant product access vs. email confirmation first\n- Personalized welcome message based on signup data\n- Auto-login after signup vs. require login\n\n---\n\n## Questions to Ask\n\nIf you need more context:\n1. What''s your current signup completion rate?\n2. Do you have field-level analytics on drop-off?\n3. What data is absolutely required before they can use the product?\n4. Are there compliance or verification requirements?\n5. What happens immediately after signup?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **onboarding-cro**: For optimizing what happens after signup\n- **form-cro**: For non-signup forms (lead capture, contact)\n- **page-cro**: For the landing page leading to signup\n- **ab-test-setup**: For testing signup flow changes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:56:46.145Z","qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ/prompt-engineer', 'community', 'Nguyenthang2292', 'Sovereign-IQ', 'Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ', 'prompt-engineer', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z', '2026-02-19T01:45:32.397Z', NULL, '{"id":"Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ/prompt-engineer","name":"prompt-engineer","description":{"en":"A high-performance, institutional-grade quantitative trading framework designed for automated strategy development, backtesting, and real-time execution."},"seo":{"title":{"en":"prompt-engineer"},"description":{"en":"A high-performance, institutional-grade quantitative trading framework designed for automated strategy development, backtesting, and real-time execution."},"definition":{"en":"A high-performance, institutional-grade quantitative trading framework designed for automated strategy development, backtesting, and real-time execution."},"features":{"en":[]},"keywords":{"en":[]}},"owner":"Nguyenthang2292","repo":"Sovereign-IQ","repoPath":"Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"prompt-engineer","description":"Expert in designing effective prompts for LLM-powered applications. Masters prompt structure, context management, output formatting, and prompt evaluation. Use when: prompt engineering, system prompt, few-shot, chain of thought, prompt design.","bodyPreview":"# Prompt Engineer\n\n**Role**: LLM Prompt Architect\n\nI translate intent into instructions that LLMs actually follow. I know\nthat prompts are programming - they need the same rigor as code. I iterate\nrelentlessly because small changes have big effects. I evaluate systematically\nbecause intuition about prompt quality is often wrong.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n- Prompt design and optimization\n- System prompt architecture\n- Context window management\n- Output format specification\n- Prompt testing and evaluation","body":"# Prompt Engineer\n\n**Role**: LLM Prompt Architect\n\nI translate intent into instructions that LLMs actually follow. I know\nthat prompts are programming - they need the same rigor as code. I iterate\nrelentlessly because small changes have big effects. I evaluate systematically\nbecause intuition about prompt quality is often wrong.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n- Prompt design and optimization\n- System prompt architecture\n- Context window management\n- Output format specification\n- Prompt testing and evaluation\n- Few-shot example design\n\n## Requirements\n\n- LLM fundamentals\n- Understanding of tokenization\n- Basic programming\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Structured System Prompt\n\nWell-organized system prompt with clear sections\n\n```javascript\n- Role: who the model is\n- Context: relevant background\n- Instructions: what to do\n- Constraints: what NOT to do\n- Output format: expected structure\n- Examples: demonstration of correct behavior\n```\n\n### Few-Shot Examples\n\nInclude examples of desired behavior\n\n```javascript\n- Show 2-5 diverse examples\n- Include edge cases in examples\n- Match example difficulty to expected inputs\n- Use consistent formatting across examples\n- Include negative examples when helpful\n```\n\n### Chain-of-Thought\n\nRequest step-by-step reasoning\n\n```javascript\n- Ask model to think step by step\n- Provide reasoning structure\n- Request explicit intermediate steps\n- Parse reasoning separately from answer\n- Use for debugging model failures\n```\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n### ❌ Vague Instructions\n\n### ❌ Kitchen Sink Prompt\n\n### ❌ No Negative Instructions\n\n## ⚠️ Sharp Edges\n\n| Issue | Severity | Solution |\n|-------|----------|----------|\n| Using imprecise language in prompts | high | Be explicit: |\n| Expecting specific format without specifying it | high | Specify format explicitly: |\n| Only saying what to do, not what to avoid | medium | Include explicit don''ts: |\n| Changing prompts without measuring impact | medium | Systematic evaluation: |\n| Including irrelevant context ''just in case'' | medium | Curate context: |\n| Biased or unrepresentative examples | medium | Diverse examples: |\n| Using default temperature for all tasks | medium | Task-appropriate temperature: |\n| Not considering prompt injection in user input | high | Defend against injection: |\n\n## Related Skills\n\nWorks well with: `ai-agents-architect`, `rag-engineer`, `backend`, `product-manager`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:45:32.397Z","qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ/aws-serverless', 'community', 'Nguyenthang2292', 'Sovereign-IQ', 'Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ', 'aws-serverless', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z', '2026-02-19T01:45:32.358Z', NULL, '{"id":"Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ/aws-serverless","name":"aws-serverless","description":{"en":"A high-performance, institutional-grade quantitative trading framework designed for automated strategy development, backtesting, and real-time execution."},"seo":{"title":{"en":"aws-serverless"},"description":{"en":"A high-performance, institutional-grade quantitative trading framework designed for automated strategy development, backtesting, and real-time execution."},"definition":{"en":"A high-performance, institutional-grade quantitative trading framework designed for automated strategy development, backtesting, and real-time execution."},"features":{"en":[]},"keywords":{"en":[]}},"owner":"Nguyenthang2292","repo":"Sovereign-IQ","repoPath":"Nguyenthang2292/Sovereign-IQ","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"aws-serverless","description":"Specialized skill for building production-ready serverless applications on AWS. Covers Lambda functions, API Gateway, DynamoDB, SQS/SNS event-driven patterns, SAM/CDK deployment, and cold start optimization.","bodyPreview":"# AWS Serverless\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Lambda Handler Pattern\n\nProper Lambda function structure with error handling\n\n**When to use**: [''Any Lambda function implementation'', ''API handlers, event processors, scheduled tasks'']\n\n```python\n```javascript\n// Node.js Lambda Handler\n// handler.js\n\n// Initialize outside handler (reused across invocations)\nconst { DynamoDBClient } = require(''@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb'');\nconst { DynamoDBDocumentClient, GetCommand } = require(''@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb'');\n\nconst clie","body":"# AWS Serverless\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Lambda Handler Pattern\n\nProper Lambda function structure with error handling\n\n**When to use**: [''Any Lambda function implementation'', ''API handlers, event processors, scheduled tasks'']\n\n```python\n```javascript\n// Node.js Lambda Handler\n// handler.js\n\n// Initialize outside handler (reused across invocations)\nconst { DynamoDBClient } = require(''@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb'');\nconst { DynamoDBDocumentClient, GetCommand } = require(''@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb'');\n\nconst client = new DynamoDBClient({});\nconst docClient = DynamoDBDocumentClient.from(client);\n\n// Handler function\nexports.handler = async (event, context) => {\n  // Optional: Don''t wait for event loop to clear (Node.js)\n  context.callbackWaitsForEmptyEventLoop = false;\n\n  try {\n    // Parse input based on event source\n    const body = typeof event.body === ''string''\n      ? JSON.parse(event.body)\n      : event.body;\n\n    // Business logic\n    const result = await processRequest(body);\n\n    // Return API Gateway compatible response\n    return {\n      statusCode: 200,\n      headers: {\n        ''Content-Type'': ''application/json'',\n        ''Access-Control-Allow-Origin'': ''*''\n      },\n      body: JSON.stringify(result)\n    };\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(''Error:'', JSON.stringify({\n      error: error.message,\n      stack: error.stack,\n      requestId: context.awsRequestId\n    }));\n\n    return {\n      statusCode: error.statusCode || 500,\n      headers: { ''Content-Type'': ''application/json'' },\n      body: JSON.stringify({\n        error: error.message || ''Internal server error''\n      })\n    };\n  }\n};\n\nasync function processRequest(data) {\n  // Your business logic here\n  const result = await docClient.send(new GetCommand({\n    TableName: process.env.TABLE_NAME,\n    Key: { id: data.id }\n  }));\n  return result.Item;\n}\n```\n\n```python\n# Python Lambda Handler\n# handler.py\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport logging\nimport boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\n\n# Initialize outside handler (reused across invocations)\nlogger = logging.getLogger()\nlogger.setLevel(logging.INFO)\n\ndynamodb = boto3.resource(''dynamodb'')\ntable = dynamodb.Table(os.environ[''TABLE_NAME''])\n\ndef handler(event, context):\n    try:\n        # Parse i\n```\n\n### API Gateway Integration Pattern\n\nREST API and HTTP API integration with Lambda\n\n**When to use**: [''Building REST APIs backed by Lambda'', ''Need HTTP endpoints for functions'']\n\n```javascript\n```yaml\n# template.yaml (SAM)\nAWSTemplateFormatVersion: ''2010-09-09''\nTransform: AWS::Serverless-2016-10-31\n\nGlobals:\n  Function:\n    Runtime: nodejs20.x\n    Timeout: 30\n    MemorySize: 256\n    Environment:\n      Variables:\n        TABLE_NAME: !Ref ItemsTable\n\nResources:\n  # HTTP API (recommended for simple use cases)\n  HttpApi:\n    Type: AWS::Serverless::HttpApi\n    Properties:\n      StageName: prod\n      CorsConfiguration:\n        AllowOrigins:\n          - \"*\"\n        AllowMethods:\n          - GET\n          - POST\n          - DELETE\n        AllowHeaders:\n          - \"*\"\n\n  # Lambda Functions\n  GetItemFunction:\n    Type: AWS::Serverless::Function\n    Properties:\n      Handler: src/handlers/get.handler\n      Events:\n        GetItem:\n          Type: HttpApi\n          Properties:\n            ApiId: !Ref HttpApi\n            Path: /items/{id}\n            Method: GET\n      Policies:\n        - DynamoDBReadPolicy:\n            TableName: !Ref ItemsTable\n\n  CreateItemFunction:\n    Type: AWS::Serverless::Function\n    Properties:\n      Handler: src/handlers/create.handler\n      Events:\n        CreateItem:\n          Type: HttpApi\n          Properties:\n            ApiId: !Ref HttpApi\n            Path: /items\n            Method: POST\n      Policies:\n        - DynamoDBCrudPolicy:\n            TableName: !Ref ItemsTable\n\n  # DynamoDB Table\n  ItemsTable:\n    Type: AWS::DynamoDB::Table\n    Properties:\n      AttributeDefinitions:\n        - AttributeName: id\n          AttributeType: S\n      KeySchema:\n        - AttributeName: id\n          KeyType: HASH\n      BillingMode: PAY_PER_REQUEST\n\nOutputs:\n  ApiUrl:\n    Value: !Sub \"https://${HttpApi}.execute-api.${AWS::Region}.amazonaws.com/prod\"\n```\n\n```javascript\n// src/handlers/get.js\nconst { getItem } = require(''../lib/dynamodb'');\n\nexports.handler = async (event) => {\n  const id = event.pathParameters?.id;\n\n  if (!id) {\n    return {\n      statusCode: 400,\n      body: JSON.stringify({ error: ''Missing id parameter'' })\n    };\n  }\n\n  const item =\n```\n\n### Event-Driven SQS Pattern\n\nLambda triggered by SQS for reliable async processing\n\n**When to use**: [''Decoupled, asynchronous processing'', ''Need retry logic and DLQ'', ''Processing messages in batches'']\n\n```python\n```yaml\n# template.yaml\nResources:\n  ProcessorFunction:\n    Type: AWS::Serverless::Function\n    Properties:\n      Handler: src/handlers/processor.handler\n      Events:\n        SQSEvent:\n          Type: SQS\n          Properties:\n            Queue: !GetAtt ProcessingQueue.Arn\n            BatchSize: 10\n            FunctionResponseTypes:\n              - ReportBatchItemFailures  # Partial batch failure handling\n\n  ProcessingQueue:\n    Type: AWS::SQS::Queue\n    Properties:\n      VisibilityTimeout: 180  # 6x Lambda timeout\n      RedrivePolicy:\n        deadLetterTargetArn: !GetAtt DeadLetterQueue.Arn\n        maxReceiveCount: 3\n\n  DeadLetterQueue:\n    Type: AWS::SQS::Queue\n    Properties:\n      MessageRetentionPeriod: 1209600  # 14 days\n```\n\n```javascript\n// src/handlers/processor.js\nexports.handler = async (event) => {\n  const batchItemFailures = [];\n\n  for (const record of event.Records) {\n    try {\n      const body = JSON.parse(record.body);\n      await processMessage(body);\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(`Failed to process message ${record.messageId}:`, error);\n      // Report this item as failed (will be retried)\n      batchItemFailures.push({\n        itemIdentifier: record.messageId\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Return failed items for retry\n  return { batchItemFailures };\n};\n\nasync function processMessage(message) {\n  // Your processing logic\n  console.log(''Processing:'', message);\n\n  // Simulate work\n  await saveToDatabase(message);\n}\n```\n\n```python\n# Python version\nimport json\nimport logging\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger()\n\ndef handler(event, context):\n    batch_item_failures = []\n\n    for record in event[''Records'']:\n        try:\n            body = json.loads(record[''body''])\n            process_message(body)\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to process {record[''messageId'']}: {e}\")\n            batch_item_failures.append({\n                ''itemIdentifier'': record[''messageId'']\n            })\n\n    return {''batchItemFailures'': batch_ite\n```\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n### ❌ Monolithic Lambda\n\n**Why bad**: Large deployment packages cause slow cold starts.\nHard to scale individual operations.\nUpdates affect entire system.\n\n### ❌ Large Dependencies\n\n**Why bad**: Increases deployment package size.\nSlows down cold starts significantly.\nMost of SDK/library may be unused.\n\n### ❌ Synchronous Calls in VPC\n\n**Why bad**: VPC-attached Lambdas have ENI setup overhead.\nBlocking DNS lookups or connections worsen cold starts.\n\n## ⚠️ Sharp Edges\n\n| Issue | Severity | Solution |\n|-------|----------|----------|\n| Issue | high | ## Measure your INIT phase |\n| Issue | high | ## Set appropriate timeout |\n| Issue | high | ## Increase memory allocation |\n| Issue | medium | ## Verify VPC configuration |\n| Issue | medium | ## Tell Lambda not to wait for event loop |\n| Issue | medium | ## For large file uploads |\n| Issue | high | ## Use different buckets/prefixes |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:45:32.358Z","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('furystack/stack-craft/review-changes', 'community', 'furystack', 'stack-craft', 'furystack/stack-craft', 'review-changes', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z', '2026-02-19T01:45:32.394Z', NULL, '{"id":"furystack/stack-craft/review-changes","name":"review-changes","description":{"en":"Crafting and managing your development stack"},"seo":{"title":{"en":"review-changes"},"description":{"en":"Crafting and managing your development stack"},"definition":{"en":"Crafting and managing your development stack"},"features":{"en":[]},"keywords":{"en":[]}},"owner":"furystack","repo":"stack-craft","repoPath":"furystack/stack-craft","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"review-changes","description":"The branch to review","bodyPreview":"# review-changes\n\nReview all changes on the current branch compared to the upstream branch.\n\n## Context\n\n{{branch}}\n\n## Determining the Base Branch\n\n**IMPORTANT:** This repository uses `master` as the integration branch.\n\n1. **Use `master` as the default base branch** for all comparisons:\n\n   ```bash\n   git diff origin/master...HEAD\n   ```\n\n2. **Verify by checking GitHub workflows** if unsure - look at `.github/workflows/*.yml` for `pull_request.branches` targets\n\n3. **Use the correct git diff s","body":"# review-changes\n\nReview all changes on the current branch compared to the upstream branch.\n\n## Context\n\n{{branch}}\n\n## Determining the Base Branch\n\n**IMPORTANT:** This repository uses `master` as the integration branch.\n\n1. **Use `master` as the default base branch** for all comparisons:\n\n   ```bash\n   git diff origin/master...HEAD\n   ```\n\n2. **Verify by checking GitHub workflows** if unsure - look at `.github/workflows/*.yml` for `pull_request.branches` targets\n\n3. **Use the correct git diff syntax:**\n   - `origin/master...HEAD` - shows changes in current branch since it diverged from master\n   - Run `git log --oneline origin/master..HEAD` to see commits being reviewed\n\n## Pre-flight: Detect Change Types\n\nBefore launching subagents, analyze what files changed:\n\n```bash\ngit diff origin/master...HEAD --name-only\n```\n\n**Conservative skip rules (only skip when 100% safe):**\n\n| Reviewer                | Run         | Notes                                       |\n| ----------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `reviewer-prettier`     | ✅ Always   | Formats `.md`, `.json`, `.ts`, `.tsx`, etc. |\n| `reviewer-typescript`   | Conditional | Skip ONLY if NO `.ts`/`.tsx` files changed  |\n| `reviewer-eslint`       | Conditional | Skip ONLY if NO `.ts`/`.tsx` files changed  |\n| `reviewer-tests`        | Conditional | Skip ONLY if NO `.ts`/`.tsx` files changed  |\n| `reviewer-dependencies` | Conditional | Run if ANY `package.json` changed           |\n\n**When in doubt, run the check.** Fast failures are better than missed issues.\n\n## Execution Strategy\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Launch ALL applicable subagents in a SINGLE parallel batch.\nDo NOT wait for one group to finish before starting another.\n\nIn one tool call batch, launch all applicable reviewers:\n\n- `reviewer-prettier` (always)\n- `reviewer-typescript` (if `.ts`/`.tsx` files changed)\n- `reviewer-eslint` (if `.ts`/`.tsx` files changed)\n- `reviewer-tests` (if `.ts`/`.tsx` files changed)\n- `reviewer-dependencies` (if any `package.json` changed)\n\n## Analysis Required\n\nCheck for:\n\n**Code Quality & Bugs:**\n\n- Potential bugs, edge cases, or runtime errors\n- Code smells, anti-patterns, or violations of repository rules (check `.cursor/rules/*`)\n- Newly added TODO/FIXME comments that should be addressed\n- Suspicious or unclear code changes\n- Business logic changes that need scrutiny\n\n**Standards & Compliance:**\n\n- Delegate to `reviewer-typescript` subagent to check for TypeScript errors\n- Delegate to `reviewer-eslint` subagent to check for linting violations\n- Delegate to `reviewer-prettier` subagent to check for formatting issues\n- Breaking changes to public API surface\n- Type definition changes\n\n**Shades Styling Patterns:**\n\n- Flag `useState()` used only for CSS-representable states (hover, focus, active)\n- Recommend using `css` property with pseudo-selectors instead:\n\n  ```typescript\n  // ❌ Anti-pattern to flag\n  const [isHovered, setIsHovered] = useState(''hover'', false)\n  <div onMouseEnter={() => setIsHovered(true)} style={{ opacity: isHovered ? 1 : 0.7 }} />\n\n  // ✅ Recommend instead\n  css: { opacity: ''0.7'', ''&:hover'': { opacity: ''1'' } }\n  ```\n\n- Static `style` props in Shade definitions should use `css` instead\n\n**Testing & Coverage:**\n\n- Delegate to `reviewer-tests` subagent to run unit tests and assess coverage\n- Missing test coverage for new/changed public APIs\n- Test quality and edge case coverage\n\n**Performance & Security:**\n\n- Performance concerns (memory leaks, missing disposal)\n- Security vulnerabilities or data exposure\n\n**Dependencies:**\n\n- Delegate to `reviewer-dependencies` subagent to validate dependency consistency\n\n**Documentation:**\n\n- Missing or outdated documentation for public APIs\n- README updates for new features\n\n## Subagent Output Rules\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Only include subagent results in the final output if they found errors or issues.\n\n- If `reviewer-typescript` passes → Do NOT mention it in the output\n- If `reviewer-eslint` passes → Do NOT mention it in the output\n- If `reviewer-prettier` passes → Do NOT mention it in the output\n- If `reviewer-tests` passes → Do NOT mention it in the output\n- If `reviewer-dependencies` passes → Do NOT mention it in the output\n\nOnly report subagent findings when they detect actual problems.\n\n## Output Format\n\n**1. Summary:** Brief overview of changes (2-3 sentences max)\n\n**2. Issues by Priority:**\n\n- 💀 **Critical:** Must fix before merge\n- 🔥 **High:** Should fix before merge\n- 🤔 **Medium:** Consider addressing\n- 💚 **Low:** Nice to have\n\nFor each issue, be specific: package, file, line, problem, suggested fix.\n\n**3. Test Coverage:** Assess coverage quality. Warn if public APIs lack tests.\n\n**4. Breaking Changes:** List any breaking changes and suggest migration guide if needed.\n\n**5. Changelog:** Generate a short, consistent changelog as a copyable markdown code block.\n\nFormat:\n\n- Use present tense, imperative mood (e.g., \"Add\", \"Fix\", \"Update\", \"Remove\")\n- One line per logical change (max 5-7 lines)\n- Group by type if multiple changes: Features, Fixes, Refactors\n- No verbose descriptions - keep each line under 80 characters\n\nExample:\n\n```\n- Add user profile validation\n- Fix observable memory leak in cache\n- Update dependency injection patterns\n```\n\n**6. Pull Request Description:** Generate as a copyable markdown code block with:\n\n- Relevant emoji per header\n- Brief description of what the PR does\n- **Remaining Tasks** checklist generated from found issues (if any), grouped by priority:\n\n```markdown\n## 📋 Remaining Tasks\n\n### 💀 Critical\n\n- [ ] Fix TypeScript error in `frontend/src/foo.ts:42`\n\n### 🔥 High\n\n- [ ] Add missing test for `handleSubmit` function\n\n### 🤔 Medium\n\n- [ ] Address memory leak in observable subscription\n```\n\nOmit empty priority sections. If no issues found, omit the entire Remaining Tasks section.\n\n**Style:** Be critical, specific, and concise. Focus on code quality and API surface area. If unsure, ask for clarification.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:45:32.394Z","qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('EddieCunningham/linsdex/matrix-operations', 'community', 'EddieCunningham', 'linsdex', 'EddieCunningham/linsdex', 'matrix-operations', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z', '2026-02-19T01:56:46.160Z', NULL, '{"id":"EddieCunningham/linsdex/matrix-operations","name":"matrix-operations","description":{"en":"Fast inference for linear SDEs"},"seo":{"title":{"en":"matrix-operations"},"description":{"en":"Fast inference for linear SDEs"},"definition":{"en":"Fast inference for linear SDEs"},"features":{"en":[]},"keywords":{"en":[]}},"owner":"EddieCunningham","repo":"linsdex","repoPath":"EddieCunningham/linsdex","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"matrix-operations","description":"Use specialized matrix types with symbolic tags for efficient linear algebra. Use when working with diagonal, block, or tagged matrices to avoid unnecessary dense computations.","bodyPreview":"# Matrix Operations\n\nlinsdex provides specialized matrix types that track structural properties for automatic optimization. Instead of always using dense matrices, the library uses diagonal, block, and tagged matrices to avoid unnecessary computation.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Working with diagonal covariance matrices\n- Building block-structured systems (e.g., position + velocity states)\n- Optimizing linear algebra with zero or identity matrices\n- Understanding the matrix type system in linsdex\n\n## Mat","body":"# Matrix Operations\n\nlinsdex provides specialized matrix types that track structural properties for automatic optimization. Instead of always using dense matrices, the library uses diagonal, block, and tagged matrices to avoid unnecessary computation.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Working with diagonal covariance matrices\n- Building block-structured systems (e.g., position + velocity states)\n- Optimizing linear algebra with zero or identity matrices\n- Understanding the matrix type system in linsdex\n\n## Matrix Types\n\n### DiagonalMatrix\n\nStores only diagonal elements for O(n) operations instead of O(n²) or O(n³).\n\n```python\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom linsdex import DiagonalMatrix\n\n# Create from diagonal elements\ndiag_elements = jnp.array([1.0, 2.0, 3.0])\nD = DiagonalMatrix(diag_elements)\n\n# Create identity matrix\nI = DiagonalMatrix.eye(3)\n\n# Efficient operations\nD_inv = D.get_inverse()    # O(n) instead of O(n³)\nlog_det = D.get_log_det()  # O(n) instead of O(n³)\nelements = D.get_elements()  # Get diagonal as array\n```\n\n### DenseMatrix\n\nGeneral dense matrices when structure cannot be exploited.\n\n```python\nfrom linsdex import DenseMatrix, TAGS\n\n# Create a dense matrix\nelements = jnp.array([[1.0, 0.5], [0.5, 2.0]])\nM = DenseMatrix(elements, tags=TAGS.no_tags)\n\n# Operations\nM_inv = M.get_inverse()\nchol = M.get_cholesky()\nlog_det = M.get_log_det()\n```\n\n### Block Matrices\n\nFor higher-order systems with natural block structure (e.g., position + velocity in tracking).\n\n```python\nfrom linsdex.matrix.block import Block2x2Matrix\nfrom linsdex import DiagonalMatrix, DenseMatrix, TAGS\n\n# Create a 2x2 block matrix\n# [[A, B],\n#  [C, D]]\nA = DiagonalMatrix.eye(2)\nB = DenseMatrix(jnp.zeros((2, 2)), tags=TAGS.zero_tags)\nC = DenseMatrix(jnp.zeros((2, 2)), tags=TAGS.zero_tags)\nD = DiagonalMatrix.eye(2)\n\nblock_matrix = Block2x2Matrix(A, B, C, D)\n\n# Operations work on the block structure\ninv = block_matrix.get_inverse()\n```\n\n## Matrix Tags\n\nTags track properties like zero and infinite values, enabling symbolic simplification before numerical computation.\n\n```python\nfrom linsdex import TAGS\n\n# Available tag configurations\nTAGS.no_tags   # Regular matrix (non-zero, non-infinite)\nTAGS.zero_tags # Matrix is zero\nTAGS.inf_tags  # Matrix has infinite elements (represents total uncertainty)\n```\n\n### How Tags Work\n\nTags propagate through operations automatically:\n\n```python\nfrom linsdex import DenseMatrix, TAGS\n\n# Create a zero matrix\nzero = DenseMatrix(jnp.zeros((3, 3)), tags=TAGS.zero_tags)\nnonzero = DenseMatrix(jnp.eye(3), tags=TAGS.no_tags)\n\n# Operations are detected symbolically\nresult = zero @ nonzero  # Detected as zero without computation\nresult = nonzero + zero  # Detected as nonzero without addition\n```\n\n### Infinite Tags for Uncertainty\n\nInfinite matrices represent total uncertainty (precision = 0):\n\n```python\n# Used in potentials to represent uninformative priors\ninf_precision = DenseMatrix(jnp.zeros((3, 3)), tags=TAGS.inf_tags)\n\n# This indicates \"no information\" about a variable\n```\n\n## Code Examples\n\n### Efficient Diagonal Operations\n\n```python\nfrom linsdex import DiagonalMatrix, StandardGaussian\n\ndim = 100\n\n# Independent dimensions with diagonal covariance\nvariances = jnp.ones(dim)\nSigma = DiagonalMatrix(variances)\n\n# All operations are O(n) instead of O(n³)\nprecision = Sigma.get_inverse()\nlog_det = Sigma.get_log_det()\nchol = Sigma.get_cholesky()\n\n# Use in Gaussian distributions\nmu = jnp.zeros(dim)\ndist = StandardGaussian(mu, Sigma)\n```\n\n### Block Matrix for State Space Models\n\n```python\nfrom linsdex.matrix.block import Block2x2Matrix\nfrom linsdex import DiagonalMatrix, DenseMatrix, TAGS\n\n# 2D state: [position, velocity]\n# Continuous-time dynamics: d/dt [x, v] = [[0, 1], [0, 0]] [x, v]\n# Discrete transition matrix (Euler approximation):\n\ndt = 0.1\ndim = 1\n\n# Position block\nA11 = DiagonalMatrix.eye(dim)  # x_new = x + ...\nA12 = DiagonalMatrix(jnp.ones(dim) * dt)  # ... + dt * v\nA21 = DenseMatrix(jnp.zeros((dim, dim)), tags=TAGS.zero_tags)  # v_new = ...\nA22 = DiagonalMatrix.eye(dim)  # ... + v\n\ntransition_matrix = Block2x2Matrix(A11, A12, A21, A22)\n```\n\n### Creating Matrices with Correct Tags\n\n```python\nfrom linsdex import DenseMatrix, DiagonalMatrix, TAGS\n\n# Regular (non-zero) matrix\nM = DenseMatrix(jnp.eye(3), tags=TAGS.no_tags)\n\n# Zero matrix (will be detected in operations)\nZ = DenseMatrix(jnp.zeros((3, 3)), tags=TAGS.zero_tags)\n\n# Diagonal matrix (automatically handles tags)\nD = DiagonalMatrix(jnp.array([1.0, 2.0, 3.0]))\n```\n\n### Matrix Operations\n\n```python\nfrom linsdex import DiagonalMatrix, DenseMatrix, TAGS\n\nD = DiagonalMatrix(jnp.array([2.0, 3.0]))\nM = DenseMatrix(jnp.array([[1.0, 0.5], [0.5, 1.0]]), tags=TAGS.no_tags)\n\n# Matrix-vector multiplication\nv = jnp.array([1.0, 2.0])\nresult = D @ v  # Efficient diagonal multiplication\n\n# Matrix-matrix operations\nresult = D @ M  # Diagonal times dense\n\n# Inverse\nD_inv = D.get_inverse()\n\n# Cholesky decomposition\nchol = M.get_cholesky()\n\n# Log determinant\nlog_det = D.get_log_det()\n```\n\n### Using with Gaussian Distributions\n\n```python\nfrom linsdex import StandardGaussian, NaturalGaussian, DiagonalMatrix\n\ndim = 5\n\n# Independent Gaussian with diagonal covariance\nmu = jnp.zeros(dim)\nSigma = DiagonalMatrix.eye(dim) * 0.5  # Scalar multiplication\n\nstd_dist = StandardGaussian(mu, Sigma)\n\n# Convert to natural form\nnat_dist = std_dist.to_nat()  # Precision is also DiagonalMatrix\n```\n\n## Key Classes\n\n- `DiagonalMatrix(elements)` - Diagonal matrix from 1D array\n- `DenseMatrix(elements, tags)` - Dense matrix with symbolic tags\n- `Block2x2Matrix(A, B, C, D)` - 2x2 block matrix\n- `Block3x3Matrix(...)` - 3x3 block matrix\n- `TAGS` - Symbolic tags for optimization\n\n## Common Methods\n\nAll matrix types support:\n\n- `get_inverse()` - Matrix inverse\n- `get_cholesky()` - Cholesky decomposition\n- `get_log_det()` - Log determinant\n- `get_elements()` - Raw array elements\n- `@` operator - Matrix multiplication (matmul)\n- Scalar multiplication and addition\n\n## Tips\n\n- Use `DiagonalMatrix` whenever dimensions are independent to save computation\n- Set correct tags when creating `DenseMatrix` to enable symbolic optimization\n- Block matrices are useful for higher-order state space models\n- Tags propagate automatically through operations\n- The library chooses the most efficient representation for operation results\n- Use `DiagonalMatrix.eye(n)` for identity matrices\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:56:46.160Z","qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('wgutmann/sim-steward-plugin/priority-tracking', 'community', 'wgutmann', 'sim-steward-plugin', 'wgutmann/sim-steward-plugin', 'priority-tracking', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z', '2026-02-19T01:56:46.151Z', NULL, '{"id":"wgutmann/sim-steward-plugin/priority-tracking","name":"priority-tracking","description":{"en":"The official SimHub plugin for SimSteward.com - incident detection and protest automation for iRacing. Spend more time racing, less time clipping."},"seo":{"title":{"en":"priority-tracking"},"description":{"en":"The official SimHub plugin for SimSteward.com - incident detection and protest automation for iRacing. Spend more time racing, less time clipping."},"definition":{"en":"The official SimHub plugin for SimSteward.com - incident detection and protest automation for iRacing. Spend more time racing, less time clipping."},"features":{"en":[]},"keywords":{"en":[]}},"owner":"wgutmann","repo":"sim-steward-plugin","repoPath":"wgutmann/sim-steward-plugin","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"priority-tracking","description":"Maintains and updates project priorities in docs/product/priorities.md. Use when the user asks to update priorities, track tasks, plan work, reprioritize, complete a task, start new work, or review whats next.","bodyPreview":"# Priority Tracking\n\n## Canonical File\n\nAll priorities live in `docs/product/priorities.md`.\n\n## When to Update\n\n| Trigger | Action |\n|---------|--------|\n| User completes a task | Move from Now/Next to Done; promote next item |\n| User starts work | Move item to Now; ensure Next is populated |\n| User adds a task | Add to Next (with priority) or Backlog |\n| User reports blocker | Add to Blocked with blocker description |\n| User asks \"what''s next?\" | Read priorities; suggest next item |\n| User rep","body":"# Priority Tracking\n\n## Canonical File\n\nAll priorities live in `docs/product/priorities.md`.\n\n## When to Update\n\n| Trigger | Action |\n|---------|--------|\n| User completes a task | Move from Now/Next to Done; promote next item |\n| User starts work | Move item to Now; ensure Next is populated |\n| User adds a task | Add to Next (with priority) or Backlog |\n| User reports blocker | Add to Blocked with blocker description |\n| User asks \"what''s next?\" | Read priorities; suggest next item |\n| User reprioritizes | Reorder Next; update Backlog |\n\n## Section Definitions\n\n| Section | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| **Now** | Currently in progress (1–3 items max) |\n| **Next** | Queued, ordered by priority |\n| **Backlog** | Not yet scheduled |\n| **Blocked** | Waiting on something |\n| **Done** | Recently completed |\n\n## Format\n\n- Use markdown tables for Now, Next, Blocked, Done.\n- Use bullet list for Backlog.\n- Include **Last updated** at top; update when editing.\n- Keep Now lean (1–3 items); avoid context switching.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Read current priorities.\n2. Apply the requested change (add, move, complete, block).\n3. Reorder Next if needed.\n4. Update Last updated date.\n5. Summarize changes for the user.\n\n## Post-Task Delegation\n\nAfter implementing a task, delegate to priority-steward to update priorities (move completed item to Done, promote Next). This happens automatically via the delegation rule.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:56:46.151Z","qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('worm-13/pet-design-agent/change-font', 'community', 'worm-13', 'pet-design-agent', 'worm-13/pet-design-agent', 'change-font', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z', '2026-02-19T01:57:49.217Z', NULL, '{"id":"worm-13/pet-design-agent/change-font","name":"change-font","description":{"zh":"更换字体技能允许您在会话中更换圆形文字的字体，而保持其他参数不变。实现与脚本位于 scripts/run_change_font.py","ja":"フォント変更スキルは、会話の中で円形テキストのフォントを変更することを可能にします。実装とスクリプトは scripts/run_change_font.py にあります","ko":"폰트 변경 스킬은 원형 텍스트의 폰트를 변경하면서 다른 매개변수는 그대로 유지할 수 있습니다. 구현 및 스크립트는 scripts/run_change_font.py에 있습니다","es":"La habilidad de cambio de fuente permite cambiar la fuente de letra en textos circulares sin alterar otros parámetros, manteniendo el tamaño, la posición y el color.","fr":"La compétence de changement de police permet de modifier la police de caractères dans les textes circulaires sans altérer d''autres paramètres, en conservant la taille, la position et la couleur.","de":"Die Schriftartänderungsfähigkeit ermöglicht es, die Schriftart in kreisförmigen Texten zu ändern, ohne andere Parameter zu verändern, wodurch Größe, Position und Farbe beibehalten werden.","pt":"A habilidade de mudança de fonte permite alterar a fonte de texto circular em uma imagem sem modificar outros parâmetros. Isso é feito re-renderizando o texto com a nova fonte.","ru":"Способность смены шрифта позволяет изменить шрифт круглого текста на изображении без изменения других параметров. Это достигается путем повторного рендеринга текста с новым шрифтом.","ar":"مهارة تغيير الخط تسمح بتغيير خط النص الدائري في صورة دون تعديل معاملات أخرى. يتم هذا من خلال إعادة تقديم النص بالخط الجديد","en":"ovo"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"更换字体技能 - 圆形文字字体修改","ja":"フォント変更スキル - 円形テキストのフォント変更","ko":"폰트 변경 스킬 - 원형 텍스트 폰트 수정","es":"Cambiar Fuente de Letra: Implementación y Características","fr":"Changer la Police de Caractères: Mise en Œuvre et Fonctio...","de":"Schriftart Ändern: Implementierung und Merkmale","pt":"Mudar Fonte de Texto Circular","ru":"Изменение шрифта круглого текста","ar":"تغيير خط النص الدائري","en":"change-font"},"description":{"zh":"更换字体技能允许您在会话中更换圆形文字的字体，而保持其他参数不变。实现与脚本位于 scripts/run_change_font.py","ja":"フォント変更スキルは、会話の中で円形テキストのフォントを変更することを可能にします。実装とスクリプトは scripts/run_change_font.py にあります","ko":"폰트 변경 스킬은 원형 텍스트의 폰트를 변경하면서 다른 매개변수는 그대로 유지할 수 있습니다. 구현 및 스크립트는 scripts/run_change_font.py에 있습니다","es":"La habilidad de cambio de fuente permite cambiar la fuente de letra en textos circulares sin alterar otros parámetros, manteniendo el tamaño, la posición y e...","fr":"La compétence de changement de police permet de modifier la police de caractères dans les textes circulaires sans altérer d''autres paramètres, en conservant ...","de":"Die Schriftartänderungsfähigkeit ermöglicht es, die Schriftart in kreisförmigen Texten zu ändern, ohne andere Parameter zu verändern, wodurch Größe, Position...","pt":"A habilidade de mudança de fonte permite alterar a fonte de texto circular em uma imagem sem modificar outros parâmetros. Isso é feito re-renderizando o text...","ru":"Способность смены шрифта позволяет изменить шрифт круглого текста на изображении без изменения других параметров. Это достигается путем повторного рендеринга...","ar":"مهارة تغيير الخط تسمح بتغيير خط النص الدائري في صورة دون تعديل معاملات أخرى. يتم هذا من خلال إعادة تقديم النص بالخط الجديد","en":"ovo"},"definition":{"en":"ovo"},"features":{"zh":["更换圆形文字的字体","保持其他参数不变","实现与脚本位于 scripts/run_change_font.py","支持会话中圆形文字的字体修改","覆盖 design_final.png 文件","更新 state.text_style.circle_text_font_path 属性"],"ja":["円形テキストのフォントを変更","その他のパラメータは変更されません","実装とスクリプトは scripts/run_change_font.py にあります","会話の中で円形テキストのフォントを変更する機能","design_final.png ファイルを上書き","state.text_style.circle_text_font_path 属性を更新"],"ko":["원형 텍스트의 폰트를 변경","다른 매개변수는 그대로 유지","구현 및 스크립트는 scripts/run_change_font.py에 있습니다","원형 텍스트의 폰트를 변경하는 기능","design_final.png 파일을 덮어씀","state.text_style.circle_text_font_path 속성을 업데이트함"],"es":["Cambio de fuente sin alterar otros parámetros","Compatibilidad con textos circulares","Mantiene el tamaño, la posición y el color","Actualiza la ruta de la fuente en el estado del texto","Sobrescribe la imagen final con el nuevo texto"],"fr":["Changement de police sans altérer d''autres paramètres","Compatibilité avec les textes circulaires","Conserve la taille, la position et la couleur","Met à jour le chemin de la police dans l''état du texte","Écrase l''image finale avec le nouveau texte"],"de":["Schriftartänderung ohne Veränderung anderer Parameter","Kompatibilität mit kreisförmigen Texten","Beibehält Größe, Position und Farbe","Aktualisiert den Pfad der Schriftart im Textzustand","Überschreibt das finale Bild mit dem neuen Text"],"pt":["Muda a fonte de texto circular sem alterar outros parâmetros","Re-renderiza o texto com a nova fonte","Não modifica o conteúdo do texto ou outras configurações","Exige a existência de texto circular prévio na imagem","Atualiza o caminho da fonte no estado da sessão"],"ru":["Изменяет шрифт круглого текста без изменения других параметров","Повторно рендерит текст с новым шрифтом","Не изменяет содержание текста или другие настройки","Требует существования круглого текста на изображении","Обновляет путь шрифта в состоянии сессии"],"ar":["يتغير خط النص الدائري دون تغيير معاملات أخرى","يعيد تقديم النص بالخط الجديد","لا يتغير محتوى النص أو إعدادات أخرى","يتطلب وجود نص دائري مسبقاً في الصورة","يعمل على تحديث مسار الخط في حالة الجلسة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["更换字体技能","圆形文字字体修改","会话中字体修改","scripts/run_change_font.py","design_final.png","state.text_style.circle_text_font_path"],"ja":["フォント変更スキル","円形テキストのフォント変更","会話の中でフォントを変更","scripts/run_change_font.py","design_final.png","state.text_style.circle_text_font_path"],"ko":["폰트 변경 스킬","원형 텍스트 폰트 수정","회话에서 폰트를 수정","scripts/run_change_font.py","design_final.png","state.text_style.circle_text_font_path"],"es":["cambio de fuente","texto circular","desarrollo de software","programación","diseño gráfico","tipografía","fuente de letra"],"fr":["changement de police","texte circulaire","développement de logiciels","programmation","conception graphique","typographie","police de caractères"],"de":["Schriftartänderung","kreisförmiger Text","Softwareentwicklung","Programmierung","Grafikdesign","Typografie","Schriftart"],"pt":["mudança de fonte","texto circular","imagem","parâmetros","renderização","desenvolvimento de imagem","processamento de imagem","edição de imagem"],"ru":["смена шрифта","круглый текст","изображение","параметры","рендеринг","разработка изображений","обработка изображений","редактирование изображений"],"ar":["تغيير الخط","نص دائري","صورة","معاملات","إعادة تقديم","تطوير الصور","معالجة الصور","تحرير الصور"]}},"owner":"worm-13","repo":"pet-design-agent","repoPath":"worm-13/pet-design-agent","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"change-font","description":"仅更换圆形文字字体，大小、排版、颜色、位置、内容全部保持不变","bodyPreview":"**实现与脚本**：本技能逻辑在 `scripts/run_change_font.py`；此处为 Cursor 约定入口，便于 Agent 发现。\n\n# 更换字体技能（Change Font）\n\n在**已有圆形文字**的会话中，**仅更换字体**，其余参数（字体大小、排版方式、颜色、位置、文字内容）全部保持不变。\n\n## 定位\n\n- **不做**：修改文字内容、颜色、位置、大小、排版、重复次数等。\n- **只做**：用新字体重新渲染圆形文字，覆盖 `design_final.png`，并更新 `state.text_style.circle_text_font_path`。\n\n## 前置条件\n\n- 会话已通过 `run_multi_pet_with_circle_text` 等流程添加过圆形文字\n- `state.text_content` 与 `state.text_style` 已存在\n- `sessions/<session_id>/design.png` 存在（无文字的合成底图）\n\n## 输入与输出\n\n| 类型 | 参数 | 必填 | 说明 |\n|------|------|","body":"**实现与脚本**：本技能逻辑在 `scripts/run_change_font.py`；此处为 Cursor 约定入口，便于 Agent 发现。\n\n# 更换字体技能（Change Font）\n\n在**已有圆形文字**的会话中，**仅更换字体**，其余参数（字体大小、排版方式、颜色、位置、文字内容）全部保持不变。\n\n## 定位\n\n- **不做**：修改文字内容、颜色、位置、大小、排版、重复次数等。\n- **只做**：用新字体重新渲染圆形文字，覆盖 `design_final.png`，并更新 `state.text_style.circle_text_font_path`。\n\n## 前置条件\n\n- 会话已通过 `run_multi_pet_with_circle_text` 等流程添加过圆形文字\n- `state.text_content` 与 `state.text_style` 已存在\n- `sessions/<session_id>/design.png` 存在（无文字的合成底图）\n\n## 输入与输出\n\n| 类型 | 参数 | 必填 | 说明 |\n|------|------|------|------|\n| 输入 | `session_id` | 是 | 会话 ID |\n| 输入 | `font` | 是 | 新字体 ID（如 字体1、字体2）或字体文件路径 |\n| 输出 | `design_final_path` | — | 更新后的 `sessions/<session_id>/design_final.png` |\n\n## 脚本调用\n\n```bash\n# 使用字体 ID\npython scripts/run_change_font.py <session_id> --font 字体2\n\n# 使用字体 ID（简写）\npython scripts/run_change_font.py <session_id> -f 字体1\n\n# 使用字体路径\npython scripts/run_change_font.py <session_id> --font assets/fonts/zhankukuaile.ttf\n```\n\n## 工作流程\n\n1. 加载 state，校验 `text_content` 存在\n2. 解析新字体路径（`get_font_path` 支持 ID 或路径）\n3. 以 `design.png` 为底图，用 state 中的 color、position、content，**仅字体改为新字体**，调用 `add_circle_text_to_image`\n4. 输出到 `design_final.png`\n5. 更新 `state.text_style.circle_text_font_path` 为新字体路径\n\n## 参考\n\n- 字体管理：`utils/font_manager.py`（`get_font_path`）\n- 圆形文字：`scripts/add_circle_text.py`、`skills/circle_text_skill/`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:57:49.217Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Visual Design Agents needing precise font customization capabilities in image editing workflows.","zh":"适合需要在图像编辑工作流中进行精确字体自定义的视觉设计代理。","ja":"画像編集ワークフローで正確なフォントカスタマイズ機能が必要なビジュアルデザインエージェントに最適です。","ko":"이미지 편집 워크플ロー에서 정확한 글꼴 사용자 지정 기능이 필요한 시각적 디자인 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de diseño visual que necesitan capacidades de personalización de fuentes precisas en flujos de trabajo de edición de imágenes.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de conception visuelle ayant besoin de capacités de personnalisation de polices précises dans les flux de travail d''édition d''images.","de":"Perfekt für visuelle Design-Agenten, die präzise Schriftanpassungsfunktionen in Bildbearbeitungsworkflows benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Design Visual que precisam de capacidades de personalização de fontes precisas em fluxos de trabalho de edição de imagens.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Визуальных Дизайн Агентов, требующих точных возможностей настройки шрифтов в рабочих процессах редактирования изображений.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التصميم المرئي الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات تخصيص الخطوط الدقيقة في سير عمل تحرير الصور."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to dynamically change fonts in circular text elements using Python scripting, preserving original design parameters like font size, color, and positioning, while updating the design_final.png and state.text_style.circle_text_font_path.","zh":"使代理能够使用Python脚本动态更改环形文本元素的字体，同时保留原始设计参数，如字体大小、颜色和位置，并更新design_final.png和state.text_style.circle_text_font_path。","ja":"Pythonスクリプトを使用して、円形テキスト要素のフォントを動的に変更するエージェントを可能にし、フォントサイズ、色、配置などの元のデザインパラメータを保持しながら、design_final.pngとstate.text_style.circle_text_font_pathを更新します。","ko":"Python 스크립트를 사용하여 원형 텍스트 요소의 글꼴을 동적으로 변경할 수 있는 에이전트를 활성화하여 글꼴 크기, 색상, 배치와 같은 원래 디자인 매개 변수를 유지하면서 design_final.png와 state.text_style.circle_text_font_path를 업데이트합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a cambiar dinámicamente las fuentes en elementos de texto circular utilizando la programación Python, preservando los parámetros de diseño originales como tamaño de fuente, color y posición, mientras se actualiza el design_final.png y state.text_style.circle_text_font_path.","fr":"Permet aux agents de modifier dynamiquement les polices dans les éléments de texte circulaires en utilisant la programmation Python, en préservant les paramètres de conception d''origine tels que la taille de police, la couleur et la position, tout en mettant à jour le design_final.png et state.text_style.circle_text_font_path.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Schriftarten in kreisförmigen Textelementen mithilfe von Python-Skripten dynamisch zu ändern, wobei die ursprünglichen Designparameter wie Schriftgröße, Farbe und Positionierung beibehalten werden, während design_final.png und state.text_style.circle_text_font_path aktualisiert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a mudar dinamicamente as fontes em elementos de texto circular usando script em Python, preservando parâmetros de design originais como tamanho de fonte, cor e posicionamento, enquanto atualiza o design_final.png e state.text_style.circle_text_font_path.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью динамически изменять шрифты в круглых текстовых элементах с помощью скриптов на Python, сохраняя исходные параметры дизайна, такие как размер шрифта, цвет и позиционирование, при этом обновляя design_final.png и state.text_style.circle_text_font_path.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تغيير الخطوط بشكل ديناميكي في عناصر النص الدائري باستخدام البرمجة النصية بايثون، مع الحفاظ على معلمات التصميم الأصلية مثل حجم الخط و اللون و الموضع، مع تحديث design_final.png و state.text_style.circle_text_font_path."},"useCases":{"en":["Customizing font styles in graphic designs","Updating typography in automated image generation","Refining text appearance in visual content creation"],"zh":["在图形设计中自定义字体样式","在自动图像生成中更新字体","在视觉内容创建中完善文本外观"],"ja":["グラフィックデザインにおけるフォントスタイルのカスタマイズ","自動画像生成におけるタイポグラフィーの更新","ビジュアルコンテンツ作成におけるテキスト外観の洗練"],"ko":["그래픽 디자인에서 글꼴 스타일 사용자 지정","자동 이미지 생성에서 타이포그래피 업데이트","시각적 콘텐츠 생성에서 텍스트 외观 세부 설정"],"es":["Personalizar estilos de fuente en diseños gráficos","Actualizar la tipografía en la generación automática de imágenes","Perfeccionar la apariencia del texto en la creación de contenido visual"],"fr":["Personnaliser les styles de police dans les conceptions graphiques","Mettre à jour la typographie dans la génération automatique d''images","Affiner l''apparence du texte dans la création de contenu visuel"],"de":["Anpassen von Schriftstilen in grafischen Designs","Aktualisieren der Typografie in der automatischen Bildgenerierung","Verfeinern der Texterscheinung bei der Erstellung von visuellem Inhalt"],"pt":["Personalizar estilos de fonte em designs gráficos","Atualizar tipografia em geração automática de imagens","Aperfeiçoar a aparência do texto em criação de conteúdo visual"],"ru":["Настройка стилей шрифтов в графических дизайнах","Обновление типографики в автоматизированном генерировании изображений","Уточнение внешнего вида текста в создании визуального контента"],"ar":["تخصيص أساليب الخطوط في التصاميم الرسومية","تحديث الطباعة في توليد الصور الآلي","تحسين مظهر النص في إنشاء المحتوى المرئي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires existing circular text in the design","Dependent on scripts/run_change_font.py for execution","Limited to modifying font, without altering other design elements"],"zh":["需要设计中已有的环形文本","依赖于脚本/run_change_font.py执行","仅限于修改字体，不改变其他设计元素"],"ja":["デザインに既存の円形テキストが必要","スクリプト/run_change_font.pyに依存して実行","フォントの変更のみ、他のデザイン要素の変更は不可"],"ko":["디자인에 기존의 원형 텍스트가 필요","스크립트/run_change_font.py에 의존하여 실행","글꼴 변경만 가능, 다른 디자인 요소 변경 불가"],"es":["Requiere texto circular existente en el diseño","Depende de scripts/run_change_font.py para la ejecución","Limitado a la modificación de la fuente, sin alterar otros elementos de diseño"],"fr":["Nécessite un texte circulaire existant dans la conception","Dépend de scripts/run_change_font.py pour l''exécution","Limité à la modification de la police, sans modifier d''autres éléments de conception"],"de":["Erfordert vorhandenen kreisförmigen Text im Design","Hängt von Skripten/run_change_font.py für die Ausführung ab","Begrenzt auf die Änderung der Schriftart, ohne andere Designelemente zu verändern"],"pt":["Requer texto circular existente no design","Depende de scripts/run_change_font.py para execução","Limitado a modificar a fonte, sem alterar outros elementos de design"],"ru":["Требует существующего круглого текста в дизайне","Зависит от скриптов/run_change_font.py для выполнения","Ограничен изменением шрифта, без изменения других элементов дизайна"],"ar":["يتطلب نصًا دائريًا موجودًا في التصميم","يعتمد على سكريبتات/run_change_font.py للتنفيذ","محدود بالتأثير على الخط، دون تغيير عناصر التصميم الأخرى"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
