a","Verificación de que los commits abordan las vulnerabilidades de seguridad"],"fr":["Analyse différentielle pour vérifier les commits","Validation des commits de remediation","Analyse des plages de commits pour les modèles d''introduction de bogues","Cross-référence des modifications de code avec les recommandations d''audit","Vérification que les commits traitent les vulnérabilités de sécurité"],"de":["Differenzanalyse zur Überprüfung von Commits","Validierung von Remediation-Commits","Analyse von Commit-Bereichen für Fehler-Einführungs-Muster","Cross-Referenzierung von Code-Änderungen mit Audit-Empfehlungen","Überprüfung, ob Commits Sicherheitslücken beheben"],"pt":["Análise diferencial de commits","Verificação de descobertas de segurança","Validação de commits de remediação","Análise de padrões de introdução de bugs","Cruzamento de alterações de código com recomendações de auditoria"],"ru":["Дифференциальный анализ коммитов","Проверка обнаружений безопасности","Валидация коммитов исправления","Анализ паттернов введения багов","Пересечение изменений кода с рекомендациями аудита"],"ar":["تحليل تفاضلي للإصدارات","تحقق من نتائج الفحص الأمني","تحقق من صحة إصلاحات التعديلات","تحليل أنماط إدخال العيوب","التعاطف بين تغييرات الشفرة وتوصيات التدقيق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码安全审查","提交代码验证","安全问题解决","bug 引入检测","代码变更分析","安全审计报告","Fix Review","代码安全"],"ja":["コードセキュリティ審査","コード提出の検証","セキュリティ問題の解決","バグ導入の検出","コード変更の分析","セキュリティ審査レポート","Fix Review","コードセキュリティ"],"ko":["코드 보안審查","코드 제출 검증","보안 문제 해결","버그 도입 감지","코드 변경 분석","보안審查 보고서","Fix Review","코드 보안"],"es":["análisis de revisión de errores","verificación de commits","seguridad de código","vulnerabilidades de seguridad","remediation commits","análisis de código","auditoría de seguridad","desarrollo de software seguro"],"fr":["analyse de révision de bogues","vérification de commits","sécurité de code","vulnérabilités de sécurité","commits de remediation","analyse de code","audit de sécurité","développement de logiciels sécurisés"],"de":["Fehlerüberprüfungsanalyse","Überprüfung von Commits","Codesicherheit","Sicherheitslücken","Remediation-Commits","Code-Analyse","Sicherheitsaudit","sichere Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["análise de segurança","commits de segurança","remediação de segurança","análise de código","segurança de software","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["анализ безопасности","коммиты безопасности","исправление безопасности","анализ кода","безопасность программного обеспечения","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تحليل الأمان","إصدارات الأمان","إصلاح الأمان","تحليل الشفرة","أمان البرمجيات","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"andrescardonas7","repo":"salchipapa-web","repoPath":"andrescardonas7/salchipapa-web","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fix-review","description":">","bodyPreview":"# Fix Review\n\nDifferential analysis to verify commits address security findings without introducing bugs.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Reviewing fix branches against security audit reports\n- Validating that remediation commits actually address findings\n- Checking if specific findings (TOB-XXX format) have been fixed\n- Analyzing commit ranges for bug introduction patterns\n- Cross-referencing code changes with audit recommendations\n\n## When NOT to Use\n\n- Initial security audits (use audit-context-building o","body":"# Fix Review\n\nDifferential analysis to verify commits address security findings without introducing bugs.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Reviewing fix branches against security audit reports\n- Validating that remediation commits actually address findings\n- Checking if specific findings (TOB-XXX format) have been fixed\n- Analyzing commit ranges for bug introduction patterns\n- Cross-referencing code changes with audit recommendations\n\n## When NOT to Use\n\n- Initial security audits (use audit-context-building or differential-review)\n- Code review without a specific baseline or finding set\n- Greenfield development with no prior audit\n- Documentation-only changes\n\n---\n\n## Rationalizations (Do Not Skip)\n\n| Rationalization | Why It''s Wrong | Required Action |\n|-----------------|----------------|-----------------|\n| \"The commit message says it fixes TOB-XXX\" | Messages lie; code tells truth | Verify the actual code change addresses the finding |\n| \"Small fix, no new bugs possible\" | Small changes cause big bugs | Analyze all changes for anti-patterns |\n| \"I''ll check the important findings\" | All findings matter | Systematically check every finding |\n| \"The tests pass\" | Tests may not cover the fix | Verify fix logic, not just test status |\n| \"Same developer, they know the code\" | Familiarity breeds blind spots | Fresh analysis of every change |\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Input Requirements\n\n| Input | Required | Format |\n|-------|----------|--------|\n| Source commit | Yes | Git commit hash or ref (baseline before fixes) |\n| Target commit(s) | Yes | One or more commit hashes to analyze |\n| Security report | No | Local path, URL, or Google Drive link |\n\n### Finding Status Values\n\n| Status | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| FIXED | Code change directly addresses the finding |\n| PARTIALLY_FIXED | Some aspects addressed, others remain |\n| NOT_ADDRESSED | No relevant changes found |\n| CANNOT_DETERMINE | Insufficient context to verify |\n\n---\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Phase 1: Input Gathering\n\nCollect required inputs from user:\n\n```\nSource commit:  [hash/ref before fixes]\nTarget commit:  [hash/ref to analyze]\nReport:         [optional: path, URL, or \"none\"]\n```\n\nIf user provides multiple target commits, process each separately with the same source.\n\n### Phase 2: Report Retrieval\n\nWhen a security report is provided, retrieve it based on format:\n\n**Local file (PDF, MD, JSON, HTML):**\nRead the file directly using the Read tool. Claude processes PDFs natively.\n\n**URL:**\nFetch web content using the WebFetch tool.\n\n**Google Drive URL that fails:**\nSee `references/report-parsing.md` for Google Drive fallback logic using `gdrive` CLI.\n\n### Phase 3: Finding Extraction\n\nParse the report to extract findings:\n\n**Trail of Bits format:**\n- Look for \"Detailed Findings\" section\n- Extract findings matching pattern: `TOB-[A-Z]+-[0-9]+`\n- Capture: ID, title, severity, description, affected files\n\n**Other formats:**\n- Numbered findings (Finding 1, Finding 2)\n- Severity-based sections (Critical, High, Medium, Low)\n- JSON with `findings` array\n\nSee `references/report-parsing.md` for detailed parsing strategies.\n\n### Phase 4: Commit Analysis\n\nFor each target commit, analyze the commit range:\n\n```bash\n# Get commit list from source to target\ngit log <source>..<target> --oneline\n\n# Get full diff\ngit diff <source>..<target>\n\n# Get changed files\ngit diff <source>..<target> --name-only\n```\n\nFor each commit in the range:\n1. Examine the diff for bug introduction patterns\n2. Check for security anti-patterns (see `references/bug-detection.md`)\n3. Map changes to relevant findings\n\n### Phase 5: Finding Verification\n\nFor each finding in the report:\n\n1. **Identify relevant commits** - Match by:\n   - File paths mentioned in finding\n   - Function/variable names in finding description\n   - Commit messages referencing the finding ID\n\n2. **Verify the fix** - Check that:\n   - The root cause is addressed (not just symptoms)\n   - The fix follows the report''s recommendation\n   - No new vulnerabilities are introduced\n\n3. **Assign status** - Based on evidence:\n   - FIXED: Clear code change addresses the finding\n   - PARTIALLY_FIXED: Some aspects fixed, others remain\n   - NOT_ADDRESSED: No relevant changes\n   - CANNOT_DETERMINE: Need more context\n\n4. **Document evidence** - For each finding:\n   - Commit hash(es) that address it\n   - Specific file and line changes\n   - How the fix addresses the root cause\n\nSee `references/finding-matching.md` for detailed matching strategies.\n\n### Phase 6: Output Generation\n\nGenerate two outputs:\n\n**1. Report file (`FIX_REVIEW_REPORT.md`):**\n\n```markdown\n# Fix Review Report\n\n**Source:** <commit>\n**Target:** <commit>\n**Report:** <path or \"none\">\n**Date:** <date>\n\n## Executive Summary\n\n[Brief overview: X findings reviewed, Y fixed, Z concerns]\n\n## Finding Status\n\n| ID | Title | Severity | Status | Evidence |\n|----|-------|----------|--------|----------|\n| TOB-XXX-1 | Finding title | High | FIXED | abc123 |\n| TOB-XXX-2 | Another finding | Medium | NOT_ADDRESSED | - |\n\n## Bug Introduction Concerns\n\n[Any potential bugs or regressions detected in the changes]\n\n## Per-Commit Analysis\n\n### Commit abc123: \"Fix reentrancy in withdraw()\"\n\n**Files changed:** contracts/Vault.sol\n**Findings addressed:** TOB-XXX-1\n**Concerns:** None\n\n[Detailed analysis]\n\n## Recommendations\n\n[Any follow-up actions needed]\n```\n\n**2. Conversation summary:**\n\nProvide a concise summary in the conversation:\n- Total findings: X\n- Fixed: Y\n- Not addressed: Z\n- Concerns: [list any bug introduction risks]\n\n---\n\n## Bug Detection\n\nAnalyze commits for security anti-patterns. Key patterns to watch:\n- Access control weakening (modifiers removed)\n- Validation removal (require/assert deleted)\n- Error handling reduction (try/catch removed)\n- External call reordering (state after call)\n- Integer operation changes (SafeMath removed)\n- Cryptographic weakening\n\nSee `references/bug-detection.md` for comprehensive detection patterns and examples.\n\n---\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n**differential-review:** For initial security review of changes (before audit)\n\n**issue-writer:** To format findings into formal audit reports\n\n**audit-context-building:** For deep context when analyzing complex fixes\n\n---\n\n## Tips for Effective Reviews\n\n**Do:**\n- Verify the actual code change, not just commit messages\n- Check that fixes address root causes, not symptoms\n- Look for unintended side effects in adjacent code\n- Cross-reference multiple findings that may interact\n- Document evidence for every status assignment\n\n**Don''t:**\n- Trust commit messages as proof of fix\n- Skip findings because they seem minor\n- Assume passing tests mean correct fixes\n- Ignore changes outside the \"fix\" scope\n- Mark FIXED without clear evidence\n\n---\n\n## Reference Files\n\nFor detailed guidance, consult:\n\n- **`references/finding-matching.md`** - Strategies for matching commits to findings\n- **`references/bug-detection.md`** - Comprehensive anti-pattern detection\n- **`references/report-parsing.md`** - Parsing different report formats, Google Drive fallback\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:57:47.150Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing differential analysis for security findings and bug detection.","zh":"非常适合需要针对安全发现和 bug 检测进行差异分析的代码审查代理。","ja":"セキュリティの発見とバグ検出のための差分分析が必要なコードレビューエージェントに最適です。","ko":"보안 발견과 버그 검출을 위한 차이점 분석이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan análisis diferencial para hallazgos de seguridad y detección de errores.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant une analyse différentielle pour les résultats de sécurité et la détection de bogues.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agenten, die eine differentielle Analyse für Sicherheitsergebnisse und Fehlererkennung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de análise diferencial para achados de segurança e detecção de bugs.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодового обзора, которым необходим дифференциальный анализ для результатов проверки безопасности и обнаружения ошибок.","ar":"مثالي لعميل استعراض الشفرة الذي يحتاج إلى تحليل تفاضلي للنتائج الأمنية واكتشاف العيوب."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to verify commits against security audit reports, validating remediation commits and checking for bug introduction patterns using differential analysis, all while cross-referencing code changes with audit recommendations in TOB-XXX format.","zh":"赋予代理验证提交与安全审计报告，验证补救提交并使用差异分析检查 bug 介绍模式，同时将代码更改与 TOB-XXX 格式的审计建议进行交叉引用。","ja":"エージェントにセキュリティ監査レポートに対するコミットの検証、補償コミットの検証、差分分析を使用したバグ導入パターンのチェック、コード変更と TOB-XXX 形式の監査推奨事項の交差参照を実行する機能を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 보안 감사 보고서에 대한 커밋을 검증하고, 차이점 분석을 사용하여 버그 도입 패턴을 확인하고, 코드 변경 사항을 TOB-XXX 형식의 감사 권장 사항과 교차 참조하는 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a verificar los commits contra informes de auditoría de seguridad, validando commits de remediación y verificando patrones de introducción de errores utilizando análisis diferencial, todo mientras se cruzan referencias de cambios de código con recomendaciones de auditoría en formato TOB-XXX.","fr":"Permet aux agents de vérifier les commits contre les rapports d''audit de sécurité, en validant les commits de remédiation et en vérifiant les modèles d''introduction de bogues à l''aide de l''analyse différentielle, le tout en faisant référence aux modifications de code avec les recommandations d''audit au format TOB-XXX.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Commits gegen Sicherheitsauditberichte zu überprüfen, Remediations-Commits zu validieren und Muster für die Einführung von Fehlern unter Verwendung der differentiellen Analyse zu überprüfen, während Codeänderungen mit Auditempfehlungen im TOB-XXX-Format referenziert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a verificar commits contra relatórios de auditoria de segurança, validando commits de remediação e verificando padrões de introdução de bugs usando análise diferencial, tudo isso cruzando referências de alterações de código com recomendações de auditoria no formato TOB-XXX.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять коммиты против отчетов о безопасности, проверяя исправление уязвимостей и выявляя закономерности введения ошибок с помощью дифференциального анализа, при этом сопоставляя изменения кода с рекомендациями аудита в формате TOB-XXX.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من التحقق من التعديلات مقابل تقارير التدقيق الأمني، واعتماد تعديلات الإصلاح ومراقبة أنماط إدخال العيوب باستخدام التحليل التفاضلي، مع إجراء مرجعية متقاطعة للتعديلات على الشفرة مع التوصيات الأمنية بالتنسيق TOB-XXX."},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing fix branches against security audit reports","Validating remediation commits to ensure they address specific findings","Analyzing commit ranges for bug introduction patterns"],"zh":["审查安全审计报告的修复分支","验证补救提交以确保解决特定发现","分析提交范围以检查 bug 介绍模式"],"ja":["セキュリティ監査レポートに対する修正ブランチのレビュー","特定の発見に対処することを確認するための補償コミットの検証","バグ導入パターンのチェックのためのコミット範囲の分析"],"ko":["보안 감사 보고서에 대한 수정 분기점 검토","특정 발견을 해결하는지 확인하기 위한 보완 커밋 검증","버그 도입 패턴 확인을 위한 커밋 범위 분석"],"es":["Revisar ramas de solución frente a informes de auditoría de seguridad","Validar commits de remediación para asegurarse de que abordan hallazgos específicos","Analizar rangos de commits para patrones de introducción de errores"],"fr":["Réviser les branches de correction par rapport aux rapports d''audit de sécurité","Valider les commits de remédiation pour s''assurer qu''ils abordent des résultats spécifiques","Analyser les plages de commits pour les modèles d''introduction de bogues"],"de":["Überprüfen von Fix-Zweigen gegenüber Sicherheitsauditberichten","Validieren von Remediations-Commits, um sicherzustellen, dass sie bestimmte Ergebnisse ansprechen","Analysieren von Commit-Bereichen für Fehler-Einführungs-Muster"],"pt":["Revisar branches de correção contra relatórios de auditoria de segurança","Validar commits de remediação para garantir que eles abordem achados específicos","Analysar intervalos de commits para padrões de introdução de bugs"],"ru":["Просмотр веток исправления против отчетов о безопасности","Проверка коммитов исправления для обеспечения решения конкретных проблем","Анализ диапазонов коммитов для выявления закономерностей введения ошибок"],"ar":["مراجعة فروع الإصلاح مقابل تقارير التدقيق الأمني","التأكد من تعديلات الإصلاح لتأكيد معالجتها للنتائج المحددة","تحليل مدى التعديلات لاكتشاف أنماط إدخال العيوب"]},"limitations":{"en":["Not suitable for initial security audits","Requires security audit reports for comparison"],"zh":["不适合初始安全审计","需要安全审计报告进行比较"],"ja":["初期のセキュリティ監査には不向き","比較のためのセキュリティ監査レポートが必要"],"ko":["초기 보안 감사에는 적합하지 않음","비교를 위한 보안 감사 보고서가 필요"],"es":["No es adecuado para auditorías de seguridad iniciales","Requiere informes de auditoría de seguridad para la comparación"],"fr":["N''est pas adapté aux audits de sécurité initiaux","Nécessite des rapports d''audit de sécurité pour la comparaison"],"de":["Nicht geeignet für erste Sicherheitsaudits","Benötigt Sicherheitsauditberichte für den Vergleich"],"pt":["Não é adequado para auditorias de segurança iniciais","Requer relatórios de auditoria de segurança para comparação"],"ru":["Не подходит для начальных аудитов безопасности","Требует отчетов о безопасности для сравнения"],"ar":["غير مناسب لتدقيق الأمان الأولي","يتطلب تقارير التدقيق الأمني للمقارنة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Sherloock/LoopTimer/timer-domain-modeling', 'community', 'Sherloock', 'LoopTimer', 'Sherloock/LoopTimer', 'timer-domain-modeling', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z', '2026-02-19T01:57:49.722Z', NULL, '{"id":"Sherloock/LoopTimer/timer-domain-modeling","name":"timer-domain-modeling","description":{"zh":"保持计时器模型在整个应用中的一致性，确保 TypeScript 类型、Zod 验证和默认值的正确性","ja":"タイマーモデルの一貫性をアプリ全体で維持し、TypeScript の型、Zod の検証、デフォルト値の正しさを確保","ko":"타이머 모델의 일관성을 전체 애플리케이션에서 유지하고, TypeScript 유형, Zod 검증 및 기본값의 올바름을 보장","es":"Mantén la consistencia en el modelado de temporizadores a través de la UI, acciones y rutas de API. Aprende a definir tipos en TypeScript y validar en fronteras con Zod.","fr":"Assurez la cohérence dans la modélisation de temporisation à travers l''UI, les actions et les routes API. Découvrez comment définir des types en TypeScript et valider aux frontières avec Zod.","de":"Halten Sie die Konsistenz bei der Timer-Modellierung über die Benutzeroberfläche, Aktionen und API-Routen hinweg aufrecht. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Typen in TypeScript definieren und an Grenzen mit Zod validieren.","pt":"Este guia apresenta práticas recomendadas para manter a consistência na modelagem de temporizador em todo o aplicativo.","ru":"Этот гид представляет рекомендуемые практики для поддержания согласованности в моделировании таймера на протяжении всего приложения.","ar":"يقدم هذا الدليل ممارسات موحدة للحفاظ على الاتساق في نمذجة تایمر في جميع أنحاء التطبيق.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Timer 域模型一致性","ja":"タイマー ドメイン モデリング","ko":"타이머 도메인 모델링","es":"Modelado de temporizadores consistentes","fr":"Modélisation de temporisation cohérente","de":"Konsistente Timer-Modellierung","pt":"Modelagem de Temporizador: Consistência em UI, API e Prisma","ru":"Моделирование таймера: поддержание согласованности в UI, ...","ar":"نمذجة 타이مر: الاتساق في و