Bibliothek für erweiterte Berechnungen","Kommandozeilen-Schnittstelle für Skripte und Automatisierung"],"pt":["Arquitetura de monorepo para otimização de desempenho","REST API com Flask 3.0 e SQLAlchemy","Frontend com React 19 e TypeScript","Biblioteca core com Python e NumPy","Interface gráfica de usuário com PyQt6","Scripts e CLI com Python e PowerShell"],"ru":["Архитектура монорепо для оптимизации производительности","REST API с Flask 3.0 и SQLAlchemy","Фронтенд с React 19 и TypeScript","Ядро библиотеки с Python и NumPy","Графический интерфейс пользователя с PyQt6","Скрипты и CLI с Python и PowerShell"],"ar":["هندسة مونوريبو لتحسين الأداء","REST API مع Flask 3.0 و SQLAlchemy","واجهة المستخدم الأمامية مع React 19 و TypeScript","مكتبة النواة مع Python و NumPy","واجهة المستخدم الرسومية مع PyQt6","스크립تات و CLI مع Python و PowerShell"]},"keywords":{"zh":["dynoai","harley-davidson","v-twin","engine","tuning","python","react","flask","numpy","pyqt6"],"ja":["dynoai","harley-davidson","v-twin","engine","tuning","python","react","flask","numpy","pyqt6"],"ko":["dynoai","harley-davidson","v-twin","engine","tuning","python","react","flask","numpy","pyqt6"],"es":["optimización de motocicletas","DynoAI","Flask","React","motocicletas Harley-Davidson","inteligencia artificial","desarrollo de software","motor V-twin","API REST"],"fr":["optimisation de motos","DynoAI","Flask","React","motos Harley-Davidson","intelligence artificielle","développement de logiciels","moteur V-twin","API REST"],"de":["Motorrad-Optimierung","DynoAI","Flask","React","Harley-Davidson-Motorräder","künstliche Intelligenz","Software-Entwicklung","V-twin-Motor","REST-API"],"pt":["DynoAI Domain Expert","otimização de desempenho de motocicletas","tecnologia de ponta","motocicletas Harley-Davidson","V-twin","Python","NumPy","React","TypeScript","Flask"],"ru":["DynoAI Domain Expert","оптимизация производительности мотоциклов","передовые технологии","мотоциклы Harley-Davidson","V-twin","Python","NumPy","React","TypeScript","Flask"],"ar":["DynoAI Domain Expert","تحسين أداء الدراجات النارية","تقنيات متقدمة","دراجات نارية هارلي ديفيدسون","V-twin","Python","NumPy","React","TypeScript","Flask"]}},"owner":"rob9206","repo":"DynoAI_3","repoPath":"rob9206/DynoAI_3","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dynoai-domain-expert","description":"Provides domain knowledge for the DynoAI dyno-tuning platform including VE math, JetDrive hardware protocols, ECU calibration concepts, and architecture ownership. Use when editing any DynoAI source file, discussing tuning logic, or when the user mentions VE tables, AFR, JetDrive, ECU calibration, cylinder balance, or zone classification.","bodyPreview":"# DynoAI Domain Expert\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nDynoAI is a monorepo for deterministic dyno tuning of Harley-Davidson motorcycles (V-twin engines). It consists of:\n\n| Layer | Stack | Root |\n|-------|-------|------|\n| REST API | Flask 3.0, SQLAlchemy, Flasgger | `api/` |\n| Frontend | React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind, Radix/shadcn | `frontend/` |\n| Core Library | Python, NumPy, Pandas | `dynoai/` |\n| Desktop GUI | PyQt6 | `gui/` |\n| Scripts/CLI | Python, PowerShell, Batch | `scripts/` |\n\nVer","body":"# DynoAI Domain Expert\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nDynoAI is a monorepo for deterministic dyno tuning of Harley-Davidson motorcycles (V-twin engines). It consists of:\n\n| Layer | Stack | Root |\n|-------|-------|------|\n| REST API | Flask 3.0, SQLAlchemy, Flasgger | `api/` |\n| Frontend | React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind, Radix/shadcn | `frontend/` |\n| Core Library | Python, NumPy, Pandas | `dynoai/` |\n| Desktop GUI | PyQt6 | `gui/` |\n| Scripts/CLI | Python, PowerShell, Batch | `scripts/` |\n\nVersion single source: `dynoai/version.py`\n\n## Key File Ownership Map\n\n| Responsibility | Owner Files |\n|---|---|\n| VE correction math | `dynoai/core/ve_math.py` |\n| Auto-tune pipeline | `api/services/autotune_workflow.py` |\n| VE apply workflow (frontend) | `frontend/src/utils/veApply/veApplyCore.ts` |\n| Zone classification | `frontend/src/utils/veApply/zoneClassification.ts` |\n| Cylinder balance | `frontend/src/utils/veApply/cylinderBalance.ts` |\n| Confidence/clamp | `frontend/src/utils/veApply/confidenceCalculator.ts` |\n| Coverage metrics | `frontend/src/utils/veApply/coverageCalculator.ts` |\n| VE bounds enforcement | `frontend/src/utils/veApply/veBounds.ts` |\n| Safety validation | `frontend/src/utils/veApply/veApplyValidation.ts` |\n| Flask app + blueprint registration | `api/app.py` |\n| Custom exceptions | `api/errors.py` |\n| Centralized config | `api/config.py` |\n| Auth (API key) | `api/auth.py` |\n| Rate limiting | `api/rate_limit.py` |\n| Shared TS types | `frontend/src/types/veApplyTypes.ts`, `frontend/src/lib/types.ts` |\n| Axios client | `frontend/src/lib/api.ts` |\n| Route definitions | `frontend/src/App.tsx` |\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### VE (Volumetric Efficiency) Tables\n\nA 2D grid indexed by RPM (rows) and MAP/kPa (columns). Each cell holds a VE percentage representing how much of the theoretical cylinder volume actually fills with air. The ECU uses VE to calculate fuel injection pulse width.\n\n**Correction math (v2.0.0, default):**\n```\nVE_correction = AFR_measured / AFR_target\n```\nA correction of 1.077 means +7.7% more fuel needed. Legacy v1.0.0 used `1 + (AFR_error * 0.07)`.\n\n**AFR targets vary by MAP:**\n```\n20-30 kPa: 14.7 (stoich)    70 kPa: 13.0\n40 kPa: 14.5                80 kPa: 12.8\n50 kPa: 14.0                90 kPa: 12.5\n60 kPa: 13.5               100 kPa: 12.2\n```\n\n### Zones\n\nEvery VE cell belongs to a zone based on its RPM and MAP coordinates:\n\n| Zone | MAP (kPa) | RPM | Weight | Typical riding |\n|------|-----------|-----|--------|----------------|\n| cruise | 31-69 | 1200-5500 | 5 | ~70% of miles |\n| partThrottle | 70-94 | 1200-5500 | 4 | Roll-on accel |\n| wot | 95+ | 1200-5500 | 2 | Full power pulls |\n| decel | <=30 | 1200-5500 | 1 | Engine braking |\n| edge | any | <1200 or >5500 | 1 | Idle/redline |\n\nZone determines confidence thresholds and coverage weighting.\n\n### Confidence and Clamping\n\nHit count (number of data samples in a cell) determines confidence:\n\n| Confidence | Clamp limit | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| high | +/-7% | Trustworthy data |\n| medium | +/-5% | Some uncertainty |\n| low | +/-3% | Uncertain, conservative |\n| skip | null | Below minHits, preserve base VE |\n\nEach zone has its own `minHits`, `mediumHits`, `highHits` thresholds (e.g., cruise needs 100 hits for high confidence).\n\n### Cylinder Balance (V-Twin Specific)\n\nFront and rear cylinders are analyzed separately. Key metrics:\n- **Systematic bias**: weighted average of `(rear/front - 1) * 100`. Positive = rear needs more fuel.\n- **Localized imbalance**: max absolute difference across cells.\n- Warnings at >2% systematic bias or >5% localized imbalance.\n- Both cylinders must have >= 3 hits per cell for inclusion.\n\n### VE Bounds Presets\n\n| Preset | Range | Enforcement | Use case |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| na_harley | 15-115% | enforce | Stock/mild cams |\n| stage_1 | 15-120% | enforce | Stage 1 cams |\n| stage_2 | 15-125% | enforce | Stage 2+ cams |\n| boosted | 10-200% | warn only | Turbo/supercharged |\n| custom | 0-999% | warn only | No enforcement |\n\n### Coverage\n\nZone-weighted metric: `sum(sufficientCells * weight) / sum(totalCells * weight)`. Grades: A (>=90%), B (>=75%), C (>=60%), D (>=40%), F (<40%). Warns if cruise zone < 60%.\n\n## Safety Constraints (CRITICAL)\n\n1. **Deterministic math only** -- no ML/AI in the VE correction path. Corrections use pure arithmetic.\n2. **Bounded adjustments** -- default max correction +/-15% per session. Extreme corrections (>+/-25%) block the apply entirely.\n3. **Dual-cylinder requirement** -- both front and rear data required; partial data blocks apply.\n4. **VE bounds enforcement** -- physical limits prevent impossible VE values.\n5. **Zero-hit cells untouched** -- cells with no data always get correction = 1.0 (no change).\n6. **Convergence over perfection** -- large errors are corrected incrementally across multiple sessions rather than in one step.\n\n## JetDrive Hardware Integration\n\nJetDrive is Dynojet''s real-time data acquisition hardware for dynos.\n\n**Discovery protocol:**\n- UDP multicast on port `22344`\n- Primary group: `224.0.2.10`\n- Alternatives: `239.255.60.60`, `224.0.0.1`, `239.192.0.1`\n- Packets: up to 4096 bytes UDP datagrams\n\n**Auto-tune pipeline:**\n1. Import log (Power Vision CSV, JetDrive CSV, or DataFrame)\n2. Filter signals (lowpass RC=500ms, outlier rejection at 2 sigma)\n3. Bin data into RPM x MAP grid (11 RPM x 9 MAP = 99 cells)\n4. Calculate AFR error per cell vs targets\n5. Convert to VE corrections with clamping\n6. Export: PVV XML, TuneLab script, CSV grids, manifest.json\n\n## Error Handling Patterns\n\nAll Flask routes use `api/errors.py`:\n- `@with_error_handling` decorator catches exceptions\n- Custom classes: `ValidationError` (400), `NotFoundError` (404), `AnalysisError` (500), `JetDriveError` (502), etc.\n- Standardized JSON responses with request ID tracking\n\n## Additional Resources\n\nFor architecture details and file ownership, see [architecture-map.md](architecture-map.md).\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:57:49.732Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Automotive Analysis Agents needing advanced Harley-Davidson V-twin engine tuning capabilities with Python and NumPy","zh":"适合需要高级哈雷戴维森 V 型引擎调校能力的汽车分析代理，支持 Python 和 NumPy","ja":"Python および NumPy を使用したハーレーダビッドソン V ツインエンジンの高度な調整機能を必要とする自動車分析エージェントに適しています","ko":"파이썬과 NumPy를 사용한 하ーレ이다비드슨 Vツイン 엔진의 고급 튜닝 기능이 필요한 자동차 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis Automotriz que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de ajuste de motores V-twin de Harley-Davidson con Python y NumPy","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse automobile ayant besoin de capacités de réglage avancées du moteur V-twin Harley-Davidson avec Python et NumPy","de":"Perfekt für Automotive-Analyse-Agents, die erweiterte Harley-Davidson V-twin-Motortuning-Funktionen mit Python und NumPy benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise Automotiva que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de ajuste de motores V-twin da Harley-Davidson com Python e NumPy","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа автомобилей, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности настройки двигателей V-twin Harley-Davidson с Python и NumPy","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل المركبات التي تحتاج إلى возможности متقدمة لضبط محرك V-twin من Harley-Davidson باستخدام Python و NumPy"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform deterministic dyno tuning of Harley-Davidson motorcycles using Flask 3.0, SQLAlchemy, and React 19, while leveraging Python, NumPy, and Pandas for core library functionality and PyQt6 for desktop GUI interactions","zh":"赋予代理使用 Flask 3.0、SQLAlchemy 和 React 19 进行哈雷戴维森摩托车的确定性发动机调校，并利用 Python、NumPy 和 Pandas 进行核心库功能，同时使用 PyQt6 进行桌面 GUI 交互","ja":"Flask 3.0、SQLAlchemy、React 19 を使用してハーレーダビッドソン・モトクロッサーに決定論的なダイノ調整を実行し、Python、NumPy、Pandas を使用してコアライブラリの機能を提供し、PyQt6 を使用してデスクトップ GUI のやり取りを実現するエージェントをEmpowerする","ko":"Flask 3.0, SQLAlchemy, React 19를 사용하여 하ーレ이다비드슨 모터사이클의 결정적 동력 튜닝을 수행하며, 파이썬, NumPy, Pandas를 사용하여 핵심 라이브러리 기능을 제공하고, PyQt6를 사용하여 데스크톱 GUI 상호 작용을 제공하는 에이전트를 강화합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar un ajuste de dinamómetro determinista de motocicletas Harley-Davidson utilizando Flask 3.0, SQLAlchemy y React 19, al mismo tiempo que aprovecha Python, NumPy y Pandas para la funcionalidad de la biblioteca principal y PyQt6 para interacciones de GUI de escritorio","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer un réglage de dyno déterministe des motocyclettes Harley-Davidson en utilisant Flask 3.0, SQLAlchemy et React 19, tout en exploitant Python, NumPy et Pandas pour la fonctionnalité de bibliothèque principale et PyQt6 pour les interactions GUI de bureau","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, ein deterministisches Dyno-Tuning von Harley-Davidson-Motorrädern durchzuführen, indem Flask 3.0, SQLAlchemy und React 19 verwendet werden, während Python, NumPy und Pandas für die Kernbibliotheksfunktionalität und PyQt6 für Desktop-GUI-Interaktionen genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar ajustes dinâmicos determinísticos de motocicletas Harley-Davidson usando Flask 3.0, SQLAlchemy e React 19, aproveitando Python, NumPy e Pandas para funcionalidade da biblioteca central e PyQt6 para interações de GUI de desktop","ru":"Позволяет агентам выполнять детерминированную настройку двигателей мотоциклов Harley-Davidson с помощью Flask 3.0, SQLAlchemy и React 19, используя Python, NumPy и Pandas для основных функций библиотеки и PyQt6 для взаимодействия с графическим интерфейсом пользователя","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من أداء ضبط ديناميكي محدد لموتوسيكلات Harley-Davidson باستخدام Flask 3.0 و SQLAlchemy و React 19، مع الاستفادة من Python و NumPy و Pandas لوظائف المكتبة الأساسية و PyQt6 للتفاعلات مع واجهة المستخدم الرسومية"},"useCases":{"en":["Tuning V-twin engines for optimal performance","Analyzing dyno data with Python and Pandas","Generating REST API endpoints with Flask 3.0 for engine tuning data"],"zh":["为获得最佳性能而调校 V 型引擎","使用 Python 和 Pandas 分析动力数据","使用 Flask 3.0 生成 REST API 端点以进行引擎调校数据交互"],"ja":["最適な性能を実現するために V ツインエンジンを調整する","Python と Pandas を使用してダイノデータを分析する","Flask 3.0 を使用してエンジントゥーニングデータの REST API エンドポイントを生成する"],"ko":["최적의 성능을 얻기 위해 Vツイン 엔진을 튜닝하는 것","파이썬과 Pandas를 사용하여 동력 데이터를 분석하는 것","Flask 3.0를 사용하여 엔진 튜닝 데이터의 REST API 엔드포인트를 생성하는 것"],"es":["Ajuste de motores V-twin para un rendimiento óptimo","Análisis de datos de dinamómetro con Python y Pandas","Generación de puntos de conexión de API REST con Flask 3.0 para datos de ajuste de motores"],"fr":["Réglage des moteurs V-twin pour des performances optimales","Analyse des données de dyno avec Python et Pandas","Génération de points de terminaison d''API REST avec Flask 3.0 pour les données de réglage du moteur"],"de":["Einstellung von V-twin-Motoren für optimale Leistung","Analyse von Dyno-Daten mit Python und Pandas","Erzeugung von REST-API-Endpunkten mit Flask 3.0 für Motor-Tuning-Daten"],"pt":["Ajuste de motores V-twin para desempenho ótimo","Análise de dados de dinamômetro com Python e Pandas","Geração de pontos finais de API REST com Flask 3.0 para dados de ajuste de motor"],"ru":["Настройка двигателей V-twin для оптимальной производительности","Анализ данных динамометра с помощью Python и Pandas","Генерация точек REST API с помощью Flask 3.0 для данных настройки двигателя"],"ar":["ضبط محركات V-twin لأداء مثالي","تحليل بيانات جهاز الاختبار الديناميكي باستخدام Python و Pandas","توليد نقاط نهاية API REST باستخدام Flask 3.0 لبيانات ضبط المحرك"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python expertise","Specific to Harley-Davidson V-twin engines","Dependent on Flask 3.0 and SQLAlchemy for API interactions"],"zh":["需要 Python 的专业知识","仅适用于哈雷戴维森 V 型引擎","依赖 Flask 3.0 和 SQLAlchemy 进行 API 交互"],"ja":["Python の専門知識が必要","ハーレーダビッドソン V ツインエンジンのみに対応","Flask 3.0 と SQLAlchemy に依存して API のやり取りを実行"],"ko":["파이썬 전문 지식이 필요함","하레다비드슨 Vツイン 엔진만 해당함","Flask 3.0와 SQLAlchemy에 의존하여 API 상호 작용을 수행함"],"es":["Requiere experiencia en Python","Específico para motores V-twin de Harley-Davidson","Dependiente de Flask 3.0 y SQLAlchemy para interacciones de API"],"fr":["Nécessite une expertise en Python","Spécifique aux moteurs V-twin Harley-Davidson","Dépendant de Flask 3.0 et SQLAlchemy pour les interactions API"],"de":["Benötigt Python-Expertise","Spezifisch für Harley-Davidson V-twin-Motoren","Abhängig von Flask 3.0 und SQLAlchemy für API-Interaktionen"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento em Python","Específico para motores V-twin da Harley-Davidson","Dependente de Flask 3.0 e SQLAlchemy para interações de API"],"ru":["Требует знаний Python","Специфичен для двигателей V-twin Harley-Davidson","Зависит от Flask 3.0 и SQLAlchemy для взаимодействия с API"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بايثون","محدد لمحركات V-twin من Harley-Davidson","يعتمد على Flask 3.0 و SQLAlchemy للتفاعلات مع API"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('consultantvision/trackatool-ties/skill-creator', 'community', 'consultantvision', 'trackatool-ties', 'consultantvision/trackatool-ties', 'skill-creator', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z', '2026-02-19T01:58:35.184Z', NULL, '{"id":"consultantvision/trackatool-ties/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"TIE Scan仪器跟踪和管理系统是一种模块化的解决方案，提供专用工作流和工具","ja":"TIE Scan機器追跡と管理システムは、モジュール化されたソリューションであり、専用のワークフローとツールを提供する","ko":"TIE Scan 기기 추적 및 관리 시스템은 모듈화된 솔루션으로 전문적인 작업 흐름과 도구를 제공합니다","es":"TIE Scan es un sistema de seguimiento y gestión de instrumentos que proporciona flujos de trabajo especializados y conocimientos procedimentales","fr":"TIE Scan est un système de suivi et de gestion d''instruments qui fournit des flux de travail spécialisés et des connaissances procédurales","de":"TIE Scan ist ein Instrumenten-Tracking- und Management-System, das spezialisierte Workflows und prozedurales Wissen bereitstellt","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes, estendendo as capacidades do Claude com conhecimento especializado.","ru":"Создатель навыков предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков, расширяя возможности Claude с помощью специализированных знаний.","ar":"مبتكر المهارات يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة، توسع قدرات Claude مع المعرفة المتخصصة.","en":"TIE Scan instrument tracking and management system"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"TIE Scan仪器跟踪和管理系统","ja":"TIE Scan機器追跡と管理システム","ko":"TIE Scan 기기 추적 및 관리 시스템","es":"TIE Scan: sistema de seguimiento y gestión de instrumentos","fr":"TIE Scan : système de suivi et de gestion d''instruments","de":"TIE Scan: Instrumenten-Tracking- und Management-System","pt":"Criador de Habilidades: Sistema de Gerenciamento de Instr...","ru":"Создатель навыков: система отслеживания и управления инст...","ar":"مبتكر المهارات: نظام تتبع وإدارة أدوات مسح TIE","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"TIE Scan仪器跟踪和管理系统是一种模块化的解决方案，提供专用工作流和工具","ja":"TIE Scan機器追跡と管理システムは、モジュール化されたソリューションであり、専用のワークフローとツールを提供する","ko":"TIE Scan 기기 추적 및 관리 시스템은 모듈화된 솔루션으로 전문적인 작업 흐름과 도구를 제공합니다","es":"TIE Scan es un sistema de seguimiento y gestión de instrumentos que proporciona flujos de trabajo especializados y conocimientos procedimentales","fr":"TIE Scan est un système de suivi et de gestion d''instruments qui fournit des flux de travail spécialisés et des connaissances procédurales","de":"TIE Scan ist ein Instrumenten-Tracking- und Management-System, das spezialisierte Workflows und prozedurales Wissen bereitstellt","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes, estendendo as capacidades do Claude com conhecimento especializado.","ru":"Создатель навыков предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков, расширяя возможности Claude с помощью специализированных знаний.","ar":"مبتكر المهارات يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة، توسع قدرات Claude مع المعرفة المتخصصة.","en":"TIE Scan instrument tracking and management system"},"definition":{"en":"TIE Scan instrument tracking and management system"},"features":{"zh":["专用工作流","模块化设计","仪器跟踪和管理","高效的工作流程","可扩展的系统"],"ja":["専用ワークフロー","モジュール化設計","機器追跡と管理","効率的なワークフロー","拡張可能なシステム"],"ko":["전문적인 작업 흐름","모듈화된 설계","기기 추적 및 관리","효율적인 작업 흐름","확장 가능한 시스템"],"es":["Seguimiento y gestión de instrumentos","Flujos de trabajo especializados","Conocimientos procedimentales","Integración con Claude","Ampliación de capacidades de Claude"],"fr":["Suivi et gestion d''instruments","Flux de travail spécialisés","Connaissances procédurales","Intégration avec Claude","Élargissement des capacités de Claude"],"de":["Instrumenten-Tracking und -Management","Spezialisierte Workflows","Prozedurales Wissen","Integration mit Claude","Erweiterung der Claude-Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["Sistema de gerenciamento de instrumentos TIE Scan","Orientação para criar habilidades eficazes","Conhecimento especializado para estender as capacidades do Claude","Fluxos de trabalho especializados","Ferramentas e workflows personalizados"],"ru":["Система отслеживания и управления инструментами TIE Scan","Руководство по созданию эффективных навыков","Специализированные знания для расширения возможностей Claude","Специализированные рабочие процессы","Пользовательские инструменты и рабочие процессы"],"ar":["نظام تتبع وإدارة أدوات مسح TIE","إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة","معرفة متخصصة لتوسيع قدرات Claude","عمليات عمل متخصصة","أدوات وعمليات عمل مخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["TIE Scan","仪器跟踪","管理系统","模块化解决方案","专用工作流","高效工作流程"],"ja":["TIE Scan","機器追跡","管理システム","モジュール化ソリューション","専用ワークフロー","効率的なワークフロー"],"ko":["TIE Scan","기기 추적","관리 시스템","모듈화된 솔루션","전문적인 작업 흐름","효율적인 작업 흐름"],"es":["TIE Scan","sistema de seguimiento de instrumentos","gestión de instrumentos","flujos de trabajo especializados","conocimientos procedimentales","desarrollo de habilidades de Claude"],"fr":["TIE Scan","système de suivi d''instruments","gestion d''instruments","flux de travail spécialisés","connaissances procédurales","développement de compétences de Claude"],"de":["TIE Scan","Instrumenten-Tracking-System","Instrumenten-Management","spezialisierte Workflows","prozedurales Wissen","Entwicklung von Claude-Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["criador de habilidades","sistema de gerenciamento de instrumentos TIE Scan","conhecimento especializado","fluxos de trabalho especializados","ferramentas personalizadas","desenvolvimento de habilidades","extensão de capacidades do Claude"],"ru":["создатель навыков","система отслеживания и управления инструментами TIE Scan","специализированные знания","специализированные рабочие процессы","пользовательские инструменты","разработка навыков","расширение возможностей Claude"],"ar":["مبتكر المهارات","نظام تتبع وإدارة أدوات مسح TIE","معرفة متخصصة","عمليات عمل متخصصة","أدوات مخصصة","تطوير المهارات","توسيع قدرات Claude"]}},"owner":"consultantvision","repo":"trackatool-ties","repoPath":"consultantvision/trackatool-ties","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   └── description: (required)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields. These are the only fields that Claude reads to determine when the skill gets used, thus it is very important to be clear and comprehensive in describing what the skill is, and when it should be used.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:58:35.184Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents like Claude needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions","zh":"适用于像 Claude 这样的高级 AI 智能体，需要专门的知识和工作流扩展","ja":"Claude のように特殊な知識とワークフロー拡張が必要な高度な AI エージェントに適している","ko":"클라우드와 같은 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 전문 지식과 워크플로 확장이 필요함","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA avanzados como Claude que necesitan conocimientos especializados y extensiones de flujo de trabajo","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA avancés comme Claude nécessitant des connaissances spécialisées et des extensions de workflow","de":"Ideal für fortschrittliche KI-Agenten wie Claude, die spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Workflow-Erweiterungen benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados como Claude que necessitam de conhecimento especializado e extensões de fluxo de trabalho","ru":"Идеально для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как Claude, требующих специализированных знаний и расширений рабочего процесса","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكيين المتقدمين مثل Claude الذين يحتاجون إلى معرفة متخصصة وتوسيعات سير العمل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create modular, self-contained packages extending capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools, utilizing procedural knowledge and transforming general-purpose agents into specialized ones with multi-step workflows","zh":"赋予代理创建模块化、自包含的软件包的能力，扩展其能力，利用专门的知识、工作流和工具，并利用程序化知识，将通用代理转化为具有多步骤工作流的专用代理","ja":"エージェントがモジュラーで自己完結したパッケージを作成し、特殊な知識、ワークフロー、ツールを利用して能力を拡張し、手続き型の知識を利用して汎用エージェントを多段階のワークフローを持つ特殊なエージェントに変換する","ko":"에이전트가 모듈화된 패키지를 생성하고, 전문 지식, 워크플로, 도구를 사용하여 능력을 확장하며, 절차 지식을 활용하여 일반 에이전트를 다단계 워크플로우를 갖는 전문 에이전트로 변환하는 것을 가능하게 함","es":"Permite a los agentes crear paquetes modulares y autocontenidos que amplían las capacidades con conocimientos especializados, flujos de trabajo y herramientas, utilizando conocimientos procedimentales y transformando agentes de propósito general en agentes especializados con flujos de trabajo de varios pasos","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des packages modulaires et autocontenus qui étendent les capacités avec des connaissances spécialisées, des flux de travail et des outils, en utilisant des connaissances procédurales et en transformant des agents à usage général en agents spécialisés avec des flux de travail à plusieurs étapes","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, modulare, selbstenthaltene Pakete zu erstellen, die die Fähigkeiten mit spezialisierten Kenntnissen, Workflows und Tools erweitern, indem sie prozedurale Kenntnisse nutzen und allgemeine Agenten in spezialisierte mit Mehrschritt-Workflows umwandeln","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar pacotes modulares, autocontidos que estendem as capacidades com conhecimento especializado, fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas, utilizando conhecimento procedural e transformando agentes de propósito geral em especializados com fluxos de trabalho de vários passos","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать модульные, самодостаточные пакеты, расширяющие возможности с помощью специализированных знаний, рабочих процессов и инструментов, используя процедурные знания и превращая агентов общего назначения в специализированные с многоступенчатыми рабочими процессами","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء حزم موديلرية ومتضمنة herself التي توسع القدرات باستخدام المعرفة المتخصصة وسير العمل والأدوات، باستخدام المعرفة الإجرائية وتحويل الوكلاء العامة إلى متخصصة ذات سير عمل متعددة المراحل"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating domain-specific onboarding guides","Developing procedural knowledge for tasks","Extending agent capabilities with specialized tools"],"zh":["创建特定领域的入门指南","开发任务的程序化知识","使用专门的工具扩展代理能力"],"ja":["特定ドメインのオンボーディングガイドを作成する","タスクの手続き型の知識を開発する","特殊なツールを使用してエージェントの能力を拡張する"],"ko":["도메인별 온보딩 가이드 생성","작업을 위한 절차 지식 개발","전문 도구를 사용하여 에이전트 능력 확장"],"es":["Crear guías de incorporación específicas del dominio","Desarrollar conocimientos procedimentales para tareas","Ampliar las capacidades de los agentes con herramientas especializadas"],"fr":["Créer des guides d''intégration spécifiques au domaine","Développer des connaissances procédurales pour les tâches","Étendre les capacités des agents avec des outils spécialisés"],"de":["Erstellung domänenspezifischer Onboarding-Leitfäden","Entwicklung prozeduraler Kenntnisse für Aufgaben","Erweiterung der Agentenfähigkeiten mit spezialisierten Tools"],"pt":["Criação de guias de integração específicos de domínio","Desenvolvimento de conhecimento procedural para tarefas","Extensão das capacidades do agente com ferramentas especializadas"],"ru":["Создание руководств по интеграции для конкретных доменов","Разработка процедурных знаний для задач","Расширение возможностей агента с помощью специализированных инструментов"],"ar":["إنشاء أدلة إعدادเฉพาะ المجال","تطوير المعرفة الإجرائية للمهام","توسيع قدرات الوكيل باستخدام أدوات متخصصة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of modular package creation","Limited to Claude''s capabilities and extensions"],"zh":["需要了解模块化包创建","仅限于 Claude 的能力和扩展"],"ja":["モジュラーなパッケージの作成を理解する必要がある","Claude の能力と拡張機能に限定される"],"ko":["모듈 패키지 생성에 대한 이해가 필요함","클라우드의 능력 및 확장 기능에 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la creación de paquetes modulares","Limitado a las capacidades y extensiones de Claude"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de la création de packages modulaires","Limité aux capacités et extensions de Claude"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis für die Erstellung modularer Pakete","Begrenzt auf die Fähigkeiten und Erweiterungen von Claude"],"pt":["Exige compreensão da criação de pacotes modulares","Limitado às capacidades e extensões do Claude"],"ru":["Требует понимания создания модульных пакетов","Ограничен возможностями и расширениями Claude"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم إنشاء حزم موديلرية","محدود بالقدرات والتوسعات الخاصة بـ Claude"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
