фронтенда","искусственный интеллект","минималистский дизайн","психология пользователя","система цветов","безопасность фронтенда","извлечение контекста кода","применение патчей"],"ar":["تنمية الواجهة الأمامية","الذكاء الاصطناعي","التصميم المينيمالي","علم النفس","نظام الألوان","أمان الواجهة الأمامية","استخراج سياق الكود","تطبيق تصحيحات"]}},"owner":"HaoNgo232","repo":"Synapse-Desktop","repoPath":"HaoNgo232/Synapse-Desktop","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"frontend-design","description":"Design thinking and decision-making for web UI. Use when designing components, layouts, color schemes, typography, or creating aesthetic interfaces. Teaches principles, not fixed values.","bodyPreview":"# Frontend Design System\n\n> **Philosophy:** Every pixel has purpose. Restraint is luxury. User psychology drives decisions.\n> **Core Principle:** THINK, don''t memorize. ASK, don''t assume.\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Selective Reading Rule (MANDATORY)\n\n**Read REQUIRED files always, OPTIONAL only when needed:**\n\n| File | Status | When to Read |\n|------|--------|--------------|\n| [ux-psychology.md](ux-psychology.md) | 🔴 **REQUIRED** | Always read first! |\n| [color-system.md](color-system.md) | ⚪ Optional | Color/","body":"# Frontend Design System\n\n> **Philosophy:** Every pixel has purpose. Restraint is luxury. User psychology drives decisions.\n> **Core Principle:** THINK, don''t memorize. ASK, don''t assume.\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Selective Reading Rule (MANDATORY)\n\n**Read REQUIRED files always, OPTIONAL only when needed:**\n\n| File | Status | When to Read |\n|------|--------|--------------|\n| [ux-psychology.md](ux-psychology.md) | 🔴 **REQUIRED** | Always read first! |\n| [color-system.md](color-system.md) | ⚪ Optional | Color/palette decisions |\n| [typography-system.md](typography-system.md) | ⚪ Optional | Font selection/pairing |\n| [visual-effects.md](visual-effects.md) | ⚪ Optional | Glassmorphism, shadows, gradients |\n| [animation-guide.md](animation-guide.md) | ⚪ Optional | Animation needed |\n| [motion-graphics.md](motion-graphics.md) | ⚪ Optional | Lottie, GSAP, 3D |\n| [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md) | ⚪ Optional | Context templates |\n\n> 🔴 **ux-psychology.md = ALWAYS READ. Others = only if relevant.**\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Runtime Scripts\n\n**Execute these for audits (don''t read, just run):**\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `scripts/ux_audit.py` | UX Psychology & Accessibility Audit | `python scripts/ux_audit.py <project_path>` |\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL: ASK BEFORE ASSUMING (MANDATORY)\n\n> **STOP! If the user''s request is open-ended, DO NOT default to your favorites.**\n\n### When User Prompt is Vague, ASK:\n\n**Color not specified?** Ask:\n> \"What color palette do you prefer? (blue/green/orange/neutral/other?)\"\n\n**Style not specified?** Ask: \n> \"What style are you going for? (minimal/bold/retro/futuristic/organic?)\"\n\n**Layout not specified?** Ask:\n> \"Do you have a layout preference? (single column/grid/asymmetric/full-width?)\"\n\n### ⛔ DEFAULT TENDENCIES TO AVOID (ANTI-SAFE HARBOR):\n\n| AI Default Tendency | Why It''s Bad | Think Instead |\n|---------------------|--------------|---------------|\n| **Bento Grids (Modern Cliché)** | Used in every AI design | Why does this content NEED a grid? |\n| **Hero Split (Left/Right)** | Predictable & Boring | How about Massive Typography or Vertical Narrative? |\n| **Mesh/Aurora Gradients** | The \"new\" lazy background | What''s a radical color pairing? |\n| **Glassmorphism** | AI''s idea of \"premium\" | How about solid, high-contrast flat? |\n| **Deep Cyan / Fintech Blue** | Safe harbor from purple ban | Why not Red, Black, or Neon Green? |\n| **\"Orchestrate / Empower\"** | AI-generated copywriting | How would a human say this? |\n| Dark background + neon glow | Overused, \"AI look\" | What does the BRAND actually need? |\n| **Rounded everything** | Generic/Safe | Where can I use sharp, brutalist edges? |\n\n> 🔴 **\"Every ''safe'' structure you choose brings you one step closer to a generic template. TAKE RISKS.\"**\n\n---\n\n## 1. Constraint Analysis (ALWAYS FIRST)\n\nBefore any design work, ANSWER THESE or ASK USER:\n\n| Constraint | Question | Why It Matters |\n|------------|----------|----------------|\n| **Timeline** | How much time? | Determines complexity |\n| **Content** | Ready or placeholder? | Affects layout flexibility |\n| **Brand** | Existing guidelines? | May dictate colors/fonts |\n| **Tech** | What stack? | Affects capabilities |\n| **Audience** | Who exactly? | Drives all visual decisions |\n\n### Audience → Design Approach\n\n| Audience | Think About |\n|----------|-------------|\n| **Gen Z** | Bold, fast, mobile-first, authentic |\n| **Millennials** | Clean, minimal, value-driven |\n| **Gen X** | Familiar, trustworthy, clear |\n| **Boomers** | Readable, high contrast, simple |\n| **B2B** | Professional, data-focused, trust |\n| **Luxury** | Restrained elegance, whitespace |\n\n---\n\n## 2. UX Psychology Principles\n\n### Core Laws (Internalize These)\n\n| Law | Principle | Application |\n|-----|-----------|-------------|\n| **Hick''s Law** | More choices = slower decisions | Limit options, use progressive disclosure |\n| **Fitts'' Law** | Bigger + closer = easier to click | Size CTAs appropriately |\n| **Miller''s Law** | ~7 items in working memory | Chunk content into groups |\n| **Von Restorff** | Different = memorable | Make CTAs visually distinct |\n| **Serial Position** | First/last remembered most | Key info at start/end |\n\n### Emotional Design Levels\n\n```\nVISCERAL (instant)  → First impression: colors, imagery, overall feel\nBEHAVIORAL (use)    → Using it: speed, feedback, efficiency\nREFLECTIVE (memory) → After: \"I like what this says about me\"\n```\n\n### Trust Building\n\n- Security indicators on sensitive actions\n- Social proof where relevant\n- Clear contact/support access\n- Consistent, professional design\n- Transparent policies\n\n---\n\n## 3. Layout Principles\n\n### Golden Ratio (φ = 1.618)\n\n```\nUse for proportional harmony:\n├── Content : Sidebar = roughly 62% : 38%\n├── Each heading size = previous × 1.618 (for dramatic scale)\n├── Spacing can follow: sm → md → lg (each × 1.618)\n```\n\n### 8-Point Grid Concept\n\n```\nAll spacing and sizing in multiples of 8:\n├── Tight: 4px (half-step for micro)\n├── Small: 8px\n├── Medium: 16px\n├── Large: 24px, 32px\n├── XL: 48px, 64px, 80px\n└── Adjust based on content density\n```\n\n### Key Sizing Principles\n\n| Element | Consideration |\n|---------|---------------|\n| **Touch targets** | Minimum comfortable tap size |\n| **Buttons** | Height based on importance hierarchy |\n| **Inputs** | Match button height for alignment |\n| **Cards** | Consistent padding, breathable |\n| **Reading width** | 45-75 characters optimal |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Color Principles\n\n### 60-30-10 Rule\n\n```\n60% → Primary/Background (calm, neutral base)\n30% → Secondary (supporting areas)\n10% → Accent (CTAs, highlights, attention)\n```\n\n### Color Psychology (For Decision Making)\n\n| If You Need... | Consider Hues | Avoid |\n|----------------|---------------|-------|\n| Trust, calm | Blue family | Aggressive reds |\n| Growth, nature | Green family | Industrial grays |\n| Energy, urgency | Orange, red | Passive blues |\n| Luxury, creativity | Deep Teal, Gold, Emerald | Cheap-feeling brights |\n| Clean, minimal | Neutrals | Overwhelming color |\n\n### Selection Process\n\n1. **What''s the industry?** (narrows options)\n2. **What''s the emotion?** (picks primary)\n3. **Light or dark mode?** (sets foundation)\n4. **ASK USER** if not specified\n\nFor detailed color theory: [color-system.md](color-system.md)\n\n---\n\n## 5. Typography Principles\n\n### Scale Selection\n\n| Content Type | Scale Ratio | Feel |\n|--------------|-------------|------|\n| Dense UI | 1.125-1.2 | Compact, efficient |\n| General web | 1.25 | Balanced (most common) |\n| Editorial | 1.333 | Readable, spacious |\n| Hero/display | 1.5-1.618 | Dramatic impact |\n\n### Pairing Concept\n\n```\nContrast + Harmony:\n├── DIFFERENT enough for hierarchy\n├── SIMILAR enough for cohesion\n└── Usually: display + neutral, or serif + sans\n```\n\n### Readability Rules\n\n- **Line length**: 45-75 characters optimal\n- **Line height**: 1.4-1.6 for body text\n- **Contrast**: Check WCAG requirements\n- **Size**: 16px+ for body on web\n\nFor detailed typography: [typography-system.md](typography-system.md)\n\n---\n\n## 6. Visual Effects Principles\n\n### Glassmorphism (When Appropriate)\n\n```\nKey properties:\n├── Semi-transparent background\n├── Backdrop blur\n├── Subtle border for definition\n└── ⚠️ **WARNING:** Standard blue/white glassmorphism is a modern cliché. Use it radically or not at all.\n```\n\n### Shadow Hierarchy\n\n```\nElevation concept:\n├── Higher elements = larger shadows\n├── Y-offset > X-offset (light from above)\n├── Multiple layers = more realistic\n└── Dark mode: may need glow instead\n```\n\n### Gradient Usage\n\n```\nHarmonious gradients:\n├── Adjacent colors on wheel (analogous)\n├── OR same hue, different lightness\n├── Avoid harsh complementary pairs\n├── 🚫 **NO Mesh/Aurora Gradients** (floating blobs)\n└── VARY from project to project radically\n```\n\nFor complete effects guide: [visual-effects.md](visual-effects.md)\n\n---\n\n## 7. Animation Principles\n\n### Timing Concept\n\n```\nDuration based on:\n├── Distance (further = longer)\n├── Size (larger = slower)\n├── Importance (critical = clear)\n└── Context (urgent = fast, luxury = slow)\n```\n\n### Easing Selection\n\n| Action | Easing | Why |\n|--------|--------|-----|\n| Entering | Ease-out | Decelerate, settle in |\n| Leaving | Ease-in | Accelerate, exit |\n| Emphasis | Ease-in-out | Smooth, deliberate |\n| Playful | Bounce | Fun, energetic |\n\n### Performance\n\n- Animate only transform and opacity\n- Respect reduced-motion preference\n- Test on low-end devices\n\nFor animation patterns: [animation-guide.md](animation-guide.md), for advanced: [motion-graphics.md](motion-graphics.md)\n\n---\n\n## 8. \"Wow Factor\" Checklist\n\n### Premium Indicators\n\n- [ ] Generous whitespace (luxury = breathing room)\n- [ ] Subtle depth and dimension\n- [ ] Smooth, purposeful animations\n- [ ] Attention to detail (alignment, consistency)\n- [ ] Cohesive visual rhythm\n- [ ] Custom elements (not all defaults)\n\n### Trust Builders\n\n- [ ] Security cues where appropriate\n- [ ] Social proof / testimonials\n- [ ] Clear value proposition\n- [ ] Professional imagery\n- [ ] Consistent design language\n\n### Emotional Triggers\n\n- [ ] Hero that evokes intended emotion\n- [ ] Human elements (faces, stories)\n- [ ] Progress/achievement indicators\n- [ ] Moments of delight\n\n---\n\n## 9. Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n### ❌ Lazy Design Indicators\n\n- Default system fonts without consideration\n- Stock imagery that doesn''t match\n- Inconsistent spacing\n- Too many competing colors\n- Walls of text without hierarchy\n- Inaccessible contrast\n\n### ❌ AI Tendency Patterns (AVOID!)\n\n- **Same colors every project**\n- **Dark + neon as default**\n- **Purple/violet everything (PURPLE BAN ✅)**\n- **Bento grids for simple landing pages**\n- **Mesh Gradients & Glow Effects**\n- **Same layout structure / Vercel clone**\n- **Not asking user preferences**\n\n### ❌ Dark Patterns (Unethical)\n\n- Hidden costs\n- Fake urgency\n- Forced actions\n- Deceptive UI\n- Confirmshaming\n\n---\n\n## 10. Decision Process Summary\n\n```\nFor EVERY design task:\n\n1. CONSTRAINTS\n   └── What''s the timeline, brand, tech, audience?\n   └── If unclear → ASK\n\n2. CONTENT\n   └── What content exists?\n   └── What''s the hierarchy?\n\n3. STYLE DIRECTION\n   └── What''s appropriate for context?\n   └── If unclear → ASK (don''t default!)\n\n4. EXECUTION\n   └── Apply principles above\n   └── Check against anti-patterns\n\n5. REVIEW\n   └── \"Does this serve the user?\"\n   └── \"Is this different from my defaults?\"\n   └── \"Would I be proud of this?\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Reference Files\n\nFor deeper guidance on specific areas:\n\n- [color-system.md](color-system.md) - Color theory and selection process\n- [typography-system.md](typography-system.md) - Font pairing and scale decisions\n- [visual-effects.md](visual-effects.md) - Effects principles and techniques\n- [animation-guide.md](animation-guide.md) - Motion design principles\n- [motion-graphics.md](motion-graphics.md) - Advanced: Lottie, GSAP, SVG, 3D, Particles\n- [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md) - Context-specific templates\n- [ux-psychology.md](ux-psychology.md) - User psychology deep dive\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n| Skill | When to Use |\n|-------|-------------|\n| **frontend-design** (this) | Before coding - Learn design principles (color, typography, UX psychology) |\n| **[web-design-guidelines](../web-design-guidelines/SKILL.md)** | After coding - Audit for accessibility, performance, and best practices |\n\n## Post-Design Workflow\n\nAfter implementing your design, run the audit:\n\n```\n1. DESIGN   → Read frontend-design principles ← YOU ARE HERE\n2. CODE     → Implement the design\n3. AUDIT    → Run web-design-guidelines review\n4. FIX      → Address findings from audit\n```\n\n> **Next Step:** After coding, use `web-design-guidelines` skill to audit your implementation for accessibility, focus states, animations, and performance issues.\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** Design is THINKING, not copying. Every project deserves fresh consideration based on its unique context and users. **Avoid the Modern SaaS Safe Harbor!**\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T02:04:04.573Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Development Agents needing UX-driven codebase analysis and safe patch implementation.","zh":"非常适合需要基于UX驱动的代码库分析和安全补丁实施的前端开发代理。","ja":"UX駆動のコードベース分析と安全なパッチ実装を必要とするフロントエンド開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"UX 기반 코드베이스 분석 및 안전한 패치 구현이 필요한 프론트엔드 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo frontend que necesitan un análisis de código basado en UX y una implementación de parches segura.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement frontend nécessitant une analyse de codebase orientée UX et une mise en œuvre de correctifs sécurisés.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine UX-getriebene Codebase-Analyse und eine sichere Patch-Implementierung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Frontend que necessitam de análise de código baseada em UX e implementação de patches seguros.","ru":"Идеально для агентов по разработке фронтэнда, которым необходим анализ кодовой базы, основанный на UX, и безопасная реализация патчей.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تطوير الواجهة الأمامية الذي يحتاج إلى تحليل شفرة قائم على تجربة المستخدم وتطبيق تصحيحات آمنة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to extract critical frontend context and apply AI-suggested patches with preview capabilities. Directly leverages UX psychology principles and color system documentation for informed design decisions.","zh":"使代理能够提取关键的前端上下文，并应用AI建议的补丁，具有预览功能。直接利用UX心理学原理和色彩系统文档以进行明智的设计决策。","ja":"エージェントが重要なフロントエンドのコンテキストを抽出し、AIによって提案されたパッチをプレビュー機能で適用できるようにします。UX心理学の原則とカラーシステムのドキュメントを直接利用して、情報に基づいた設計決定を下します。","ko":"에이전트가 중요한 프론트엔드 컨텍스트를 추출하고 AI가 제안한 패치를 미리 보기 기능으로 적용할 수 있도록 합니다. UX 심리학 원칙과 색상 시스템 문서를 직접 활용하여 정보에 기반한 설계 결정을 내릴 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes extraer el contexto frontend crítico y aplicar parches sugeridos por IA con capacidades de vista previa. Utiliza directamente principios de psicología de UX y documentación del sistema de colores para tomar decisiones de diseño informadas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''extraire le contexte frontal critique et d''appliquer des correctifs suggérés par l''IA avec des capacités d''aperçu. Utilise directement les principes de psychologie UX et la documentation du système de couleurs pour prendre des décisions de conception éclairées.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, kritischen Frontend-Kontext zu extrahieren und AI-vorgeschlagene Patches mit Vorschau-Funktionen anzuwenden. Nutzt direkt UX-Psychologie-Prinzipien und Farbsystem-Dokumentation für informierte Designentscheidungen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes extraiam o contexto frontal crítico e apliquem patches sugeridos por IA com capacidades de pré-visualização. Utiliza diretamente os princípios de psicologia da UX e a documentação do sistema de cores para tomar decisões de design informadas.","ru":"Позволяет агентам извлекать критический контекст фронтэнда и применять патчи, предложенные ИИ, с возможностями предварительного просмотра. Прямо использует принципы психологии UX и документацию системы цветов для принятия обоснованных решений по дизайну.","ar":"يمكن للعميل استخراج السياق الأمامي الحرج وتطبيق تصحيحات مقترحة بواسطة الذكاء الاصطناعي مع إمكانيات المعاينة. يستخدم مباشرة مبادئ علم نفس تجربة المستخدم وتوثيق نظام الألوان لاتخاذ قرارات التصميم الم 知رة."},"useCases":{"en":["Extracting UX psychology requirements before code generation","Applying color system-compliant design patches","Previewing AI-suggested frontend changes before implementation","Analyzing design system documentation for context-aware development"],"zh":["代码生成前提取UX心理学要求","应用符合色彩系统的设计补丁","实现前预览AI建议的前端更改","分析设计系统文档以进行上下文感知开发"],"ja":["コード生成前にUX心理学の要件を抽出すること","カラーシステムに準拠した設計パッチを適用すること","実装前にAIによって提案されたフロントエンドの変更をプレビューすること","コンテキストに応じた開発のためのデザインシステムのドキュメントを分析すること"],"ko":["코드 생성 전에 UX 심리학 요구 사항 추출","색상 시스템 규격의 디자인 패치 적용","구현 전에 AI 제안 프론트엔드 변경 사항 미리 보기","컨텍스트 인식 개발을 위한 디자인 시스템 문서 분석"],"es":["Extraer requisitos de psicología de UX antes de la generación de código","Aplicar parches de diseño compatibles con el sistema de colores","Previsualizar los cambios frontend sugeridos por la IA antes de la implementación","Analizar la documentación del sistema de diseño para el desarrollo consciente del contexto"],"fr":["Extraire les exigences de psychologie UX avant la génération de code","Appliquer des correctifs de conception compatibles avec le système de couleurs","Prévisualiser les modifications frontend suggérées par l''IA avant la mise en œuvre","Analyser la documentation du système de conception pour le développement conscient du contexte"],"de":["UX-Psychologie-Anforderungen vor der Codegenerierung extrahieren","Farbsystem-konforme Design-Patches anwenden","AI-vorgeschlagene Frontend-Änderungen vor der Implementierung vorab anzeigen","Design-System-Dokumentation für kontextbewusste Entwicklung analysieren"],"pt":["Extrair requisitos de psicologia da UX antes da geração de código","Aplicar patches de design compatíveis com o sistema de cores","Visualizar alterações de frontend sugeridas por IA antes da implementação","Analizar a documentação do sistema de design para desenvolvimento consciente do contexto"],"ru":["Извлекать требования психологии UX до генерации кода","Применять патчи дизайна, совместимые с системой цветов","Просматривать изменения фронтэнда, предложенные ИИ, до реализации","Анализировать документацию системы дизайна для контекстно-зависимой разработки"],"ar":["استخراج متطلبات علم نفس تجربة المستخدم قبل توليد الشفرة","تطبيق تصحيحات التصميم المتوافقة مع نظام الألوان","معاينة التغييرات الأمامية المقترحة بواسطة الذكاء الاصطناعي قبل التنفيذ","تحليل توثيق نظام التصميم للتنمية المتنبئة بالسياق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to ux-psychology.md file always","Needs filesystem access for codebase context extraction","Color system knowledge optional but recommended for full functionality"],"zh":["始终需要访问ux-psychology.md文件","需要文件系统访问以提取代码库上下文","色彩系统知识可选但推荐用于全功能"],"ja":["ux-psychology.mdファイルへのアクセスが常に必要","コードベースのコンテキストを抽出するためにファイルシステムへのアクセスが必要","カラーシステムの知識はオプションですが、フル機能を使用するために推奨されます"],"ko":["ux-psychology.md 파일에 항상 액세스해야 함","코드베이스 컨텍스트 추출을 위해 파일 시스템 액세스가 필요함","색상 시스템 지식은 선택 사항이지만 전체 기능을 사용하기 위해 권장됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso al archivo ux-psychology.md siempre","Necesita acceso al sistema de archivos para la extracción de contexto de código","Conocimiento del sistema de colores opcional pero recomendado para la funcionalidad completa"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au fichier ux-psychology.md à tout moment","Nécessite un accès au système de fichiers pour l''extraction du contexte de codebase","Connaissance du système de couleurs facultative mais recommandée pour une fonctionnalité complète"],"de":["Erfordert immer Zugriff auf die Datei ux-psychology.md","Benötigt Dateisystem-Zugriff für die Kontextextraktion der Codebase","Farbsystem-Kenntnisse optional, aber für die volle Funktionalität empfohlen"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao arquivo ux-psychology.md sempre","Necessita acesso ao sistema de arquivos para extração de contexto de código base","Conhecimento do sistema de cores é opcional, mas recomendado para funcionalidade completa"],"ru":["Требует доступа к файлу ux-psychology.md всегда","Требует доступа к файловой системе для извлечения контекста кодовой базы","Знание системы цветов является опциональным, но рекомендуется для полной функциональности"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى ملف ux-psychology.md دائمًا","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى نظام الملفات لاستخراج سياق قاعدة الشفرة","معرفة نظام الألوان هو اختياري ولكن يوصى به للوظائف الكاملة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
