o de documentação técnica clara e precisa","Adesão a padrões de documentação","Integração com o processo de contribuição","Suporte à equipe de desenvolvimento","Melhoria da qualidade da documentação"],"ru":["Создание ясной и точной технической документации","Соответствие стандартам документации","Интеграция с процессом внесения вклада","Поддержка команды разработчиков","Улучшение качества документации"],"ar":["إنشاء وثائق فنية واضحة ودقيقة","الامتثال لمعايير الوثائق","التكامل مع عملية المساهمة","دعم فريق التطوير","تحسين جودة الوثائق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技术文档写作","docs-writer 技能","文档标准","代码库","贡献过程","项目标准","技术文档","写作技能"],"ja":["技術文書作成","docs-writer スキル","文書標準","コードベース","貢献プロセス","プロジェクト標準","技術文書","作成スキル"],"ko":["기술 문서 작성","docs-writer 스킬","문서 표준","코드베이스","기여 프로세스","프로젝트 표준","기술 문서","작성 스킬"],"es":["documentación técnica","modelo de integración AI","desarrollo de software","creación de contenido","estándares de documentación","proceso de contribución","calidad del contenido"],"fr":["documentation technique","modèle d''intégration IA","développement de logiciels","création de contenu","normes de documentation","processus de contribution","qualité du contenu"],"de":["technische Dokumentation","Integrations-AI-Modell","Software-Entwicklung","Inhalts-Erstellung","Dokumentationsstandards","Beitragprozess","Inhalts-Qualität"],"pt":["documentação técnica","ferramenta de documentação","desenvolvedores","documentação clara","padrões de documentação","processo de contribuição"],"ru":["техническая документация","инструмент для документации","разработчики","ясная документация","стандарты документации","процесс внесения вклада"],"ar":["الوثائق الفنية","أداة للوثائق","المطورين","الوثائق الواضحة","معايير الوثائق","عملية المساهمة"]}},"owner":"krsjenmt","repo":"krsjen.ai","repoPath":"krsjenmt/krsjen.ai","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.541Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"docs-writer","description":"","bodyPreview":"# `docs-writer` skill instructions\n\nAs an expert technical writer and editor for the Gemini CLI project, you produce\naccurate, clear, and consistent documentation. When asked to write, edit, or\nreview documentation, you must ensure the content strictly adheres to the\nprovided documentation standards and accurately reflects the current codebase.\nAdhere to the contribution process in `CONTRIBUTING.md` and the following\nproject standards.\n\n## Phase 1: Documentation standards\n\nAdhering to these prin","body":"# `docs-writer` skill instructions\n\nAs an expert technical writer and editor for the Gemini CLI project, you produce\naccurate, clear, and consistent documentation. When asked to write, edit, or\nreview documentation, you must ensure the content strictly adheres to the\nprovided documentation standards and accurately reflects the current codebase.\nAdhere to the contribution process in `CONTRIBUTING.md` and the following\nproject standards.\n\n## Phase 1: Documentation standards\n\nAdhering to these principles and standards when writing, editing, and reviewing.\n\n### Voice and tone\nAdopt a tone that balances professionalism with a helpful, conversational\napproach.\n\n- **Perspective and tense:** Address the reader as \"you.\" Use active voice and\n  present tense (e.g., \"The API returns...\").\n- **Tone:** Professional, friendly, and direct. \n- **Clarity:** Use simple vocabulary. Avoid jargon, slang, and marketing hype.\n- **Global Audience:** Write in standard US English. Avoid idioms and cultural\n  references.\n- **Requirements:** Be clear about requirements (\"must\") vs. recommendations\n  (\"we recommend\"). Avoid \"should.\"\n- **Word Choice:** Avoid \"please\" and anthropomorphism (e.g., \"the server\n  thinks\"). Use contractions (don''t, it''s).\n\n### Language and grammar\nWrite precisely to ensure your instructions are unambiguous.\n\n- **Abbreviations:** Avoid Latin abbreviations; use \"for example\" (not \"e.g.\")\n  and \"that is\" (not \"i.e.\").\n- **Punctuation:** Use the serial comma. Place periods and commas inside\n  quotation marks.\n- **Dates:** Use unambiguous formats (e.g., \"January 22, 2026\").\n- **Conciseness:** Use \"lets you\" instead of \"allows you to.\" Use precise,\n  specific verbs.\n- **Examples:** Use meaningful names in examples; avoid placeholders like\n  \"foo\" or \"bar.\"\n\n### Formatting and syntax\nApply consistent formatting to make documentation visually organized and\naccessible.\n\n- **Overview paragraphs:** Every heading must be followed by at least one\n  introductory overview paragraph before any lists or sub-headings.\n- **Text wrap:** Wrap text at 80 characters (except long links or tables).\n- **Casing:** Use sentence case for headings, titles, and bolded text.\n- **Naming:** Always refer to the project as `Gemini CLI` (never\n  `the Gemini CLI`).\n- **Lists:** Use numbered lists for sequential steps and bulleted lists\n  otherwise. Keep list items parallel in structure.\n- **UI and code:** Use **bold** for UI elements and `code font` for filenames,\n  snippets, commands, and API elements. Focus on the task when discussing\n  interaction.\n- **Links:** Use descriptive anchor text; avoid \"click here.\" Ensure the link\n  makes sense out of context.\n- **Accessibility:** Use semantic HTML elements correctly (headings, lists, \n  tables).\n- **Media:** Use lowercase hyphenated filenames. Provide descriptive alt text\n  for all images.\n\n### Structure\n- **BLUF:** Start with an introduction explaining what to expect.\n- **Experimental features:** If a feature is clearly noted as experimental,\nadd the following note immediately after the introductory paragraph:\n  `> **Note:** This is a preview feature currently under active development.`\n- **Headings:** Use hierarchical headings to support the user journey.\n- **Procedures:** \n  - Introduce lists of steps with a complete sentence.\n  - Start each step with an imperative verb.\n  - Number sequential steps; use bullets for non-sequential lists.\n  - Put conditions before instructions (e.g., \"On the Settings page, click...\").\n  - Provide clear context for where the action takes place.\n  - Indicate optional steps clearly (e.g., \"Optional: ...\").\n- **Elements:** Use bullet lists, tables, notes (`> **Note:**`), and warnings \n  (`> **Warning:**`).\n- **Avoid using a table of contents:** If a table of contents is present, remove\n  it.\n- **Next steps:** Conclude with a \"Next steps\" section if applicable.\n\n## Phase 2: Preparation\nBefore modifying any documentation, thoroughly investigate the request and the\nsurrounding context. \n\n1.  **Clarify:** Understand the core request. Differentiate between writing new\n    content and editing existing content. If the request is ambiguous (e.g.,\n    \"fix the docs\"), ask for clarification.\n2.  **Investigate:** Examine relevant code (primarily in `packages/`) for\n    accuracy.\n3.  **Audit:** Read the latest versions of relevant files in `docs/`.\n4.  **Connect:** Identify all referencing pages if changing behavior. Check if\n    `docs/sidebar.json` needs updates.\n5.  **Plan:** Create a step-by-step plan before making changes.\n\n## Phase 3: Execution\nImplement your plan by either updating existing files or creating new ones\nusing the appropriate file system tools. Use `replace` for small edits and\n`write_file` for new files or large rewrites.\n\n### Editing existing documentation\nFollow these additional steps when asked to review or update existing\ndocumentation.\n\n- **Gaps:** Identify areas where the documentation is incomplete or no longer\n  reflects existing code.\n- **Structure:** Apply \"Structure (New Docs)\" rules (BLUF, headings, etc.) when \n  adding new sections to existing pages.\n- **Tone:** Ensure the tone is active and engaging. Use \"you\" and contractions.\n- **Clarity:** Correct awkward wording, spelling, and grammar. Rephrase\n  sentences to make them easier for users to understand.\n- **Consistency:** Check for consistent terminology and style across all edited\n  documents.\n\n\n## Phase 4: Verification and finalization\nPerform a final quality check to ensure that all changes are correctly formatted\nand that all links are functional.\n\n1.  **Accuracy:** Ensure content accurately reflects the implementation and\n  technical behavior.\n2.  **Self-review:** Re-read changes for formatting, correctness, and flow.\n3.  **Link check:** Verify all new and existing links leading to or from modified\n    pages.\n4.  **Format:** Once all changes are complete, ask to execute `npm run format`\n    to ensure consistent formatting across the project. If the user confirms,\n    execute the command.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T02:06:13.027Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing to produce accurate and clear documentation adhering to specific project standards","zh":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing to produce accurate and clear documentation adhering to specific project standards","ja":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing to produce accurate and clear documentation adhering to specific project standards","ko":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing to produce accurate and clear documentation adhering to specific project standards","es":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing to produce accurate and clear documentation adhering to specific project standards","fr":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing to produce accurate and clear documentation adhering to specific project standards","de":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing to produce accurate and clear documentation adhering to specific project standards","pt":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing to produce accurate and clear documentation adhering to specific project standards","ru":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing to produce accurate and clear documentation adhering to specific project standards","ar":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing to produce accurate and clear documentation adhering to specific project standards"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality documentation following the contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md and adhering to provided documentation standards, ensuring consistency and accuracy in technical writing using Markdown format","zh":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality documentation following the contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md and adhering to provided documentation standards, ensuring consistency and accuracy in technical writing using Markdown format","ja":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality documentation following the contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md and adhering to provided documentation standards, ensuring consistency and accuracy in technical writing using Markdown format","ko":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality documentation following the contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md and adhering to provided documentation standards, ensuring consistency and accuracy in technical writing using Markdown format","es":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality documentation following the contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md and adhering to provided documentation standards, ensuring consistency and accuracy in technical writing using Markdown format","fr":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality documentation following the contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md and adhering to provided documentation standards, ensuring consistency and accuracy in technical writing using Markdown format","de":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality documentation following the contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md and adhering to provided documentation standards, ensuring consistency and accuracy in technical writing using Markdown format","pt":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality documentation following the contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md and adhering to provided documentation standards, ensuring consistency and accuracy in technical writing using Markdown format","ru":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality documentation following the contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md and adhering to provided documentation standards, ensuring consistency and accuracy in technical writing using Markdown format","ar":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality documentation following the contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md and adhering to provided documentation standards, ensuring consistency and accuracy in technical writing using Markdown format"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating documentation updates to reflect current codebase changes","Generating user manuals and guides following strict documentation standards","Reviewing and editing existing documentation for clarity and consistency"],"zh":["Automating documentation updates to reflect current codebase changes","Generating user manuals and guides following strict documentation standards","Reviewing and editing existing documentation for clarity and consistency"],"ja":["Automating documentation updates to reflect current codebase changes","Generating user manuals and guides following strict documentation standards","Reviewing and editing existing documentation for clarity and consistency"],"ko":["Automating documentation updates to reflect current codebase changes","Generating user manuals and guides following strict documentation standards","Reviewing and editing existing documentation for clarity and consistency"],"es":["Automating documentation updates to reflect current codebase changes","Generating user manuals and guides following strict documentation standards","Reviewing and editing existing documentation for clarity and consistency"],"fr":["Automating documentation updates to reflect current codebase changes","Generating user manuals and guides following strict documentation standards","Reviewing and editing existing documentation for clarity and consistency"],"de":["Automating documentation updates to reflect current codebase changes","Generating user manuals and guides following strict documentation standards","Reviewing and editing existing documentation for clarity and consistency"],"pt":["Automating documentation updates to reflect current codebase changes","Generating user manuals and guides following strict documentation standards","Reviewing and editing existing documentation for clarity and consistency"],"ru":["Automating documentation updates to reflect current codebase changes","Generating user manuals and guides following strict documentation standards","Reviewing and editing existing documentation for clarity and consistency"],"ar":["Automating documentation updates to reflect current codebase changes","Generating user manuals and guides following strict documentation standards","Reviewing and editing existing documentation for clarity and consistency"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to specific project standards and documentation guidelines","Must follow contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md"],"zh":["Requires adherence to specific project standards and documentation guidelines","Must follow contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md"],"ja":["Requires adherence to specific project standards and documentation guidelines","Must follow contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md"],"ko":["Requires adherence to specific project standards and documentation guidelines","Must follow contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md"],"es":["Requires adherence to specific project standards and documentation guidelines","Must follow contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md"],"fr":["Requires adherence to specific project standards and documentation guidelines","Must follow contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md"],"de":["Requires adherence to specific project standards and documentation guidelines","Must follow contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md"],"pt":["Requires adherence to specific project standards and documentation guidelines","Must follow contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md"],"ru":["Requires adherence to specific project standards and documentation guidelines","Must follow contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md"],"ar":["Requires adherence to specific project standards and documentation guidelines","Must follow contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
