direct object references, find IDOR vulnerabilities, exploit broken access control, enumerate user IDs or object references, or bypass authorization to access other users data. It provides comprehensive guidance for detecting, exploiting, and remediating IDOR vulnerabilities in web applications.","version":"1.1","bodyPreview":"# IDOR Vulnerability Testing\n\n## Purpose\n\nProvide systematic methodologies for identifying and exploiting Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerabilities in web applications. This skill covers both database object references and static file references, detection techniques using parameter manipulation and enumeration, exploitation via Burp Suite, and remediation strategies for securing applications against unauthorized access.\n\n## Inputs / Prerequisites\n\n- **Target Web Application**: URL","body":"# IDOR Vulnerability Testing\n\n## Purpose\n\nProvide systematic methodologies for identifying and exploiting Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerabilities in web applications. This skill covers both database object references and static file references, detection techniques using parameter manipulation and enumeration, exploitation via Burp Suite, and remediation strategies for securing applications against unauthorized access.\n\n## Inputs / Prerequisites\n\n- **Target Web Application**: URL of application with user-specific resources\n- **Multiple User Accounts**: At least two test accounts to verify cross-user access\n- **Burp Suite or Proxy Tool**: Intercepting proxy for request manipulation\n- **Authorization**: Written permission for security testing\n- **Understanding of Application Flow**: Knowledge of how objects are referenced (IDs, filenames)\n\n## Outputs / Deliverables\n\n- **IDOR Vulnerability Report**: Documentation of discovered access control bypasses\n- **Proof of Concept**: Evidence of unauthorized data access across user contexts\n- **Affected Endpoints**: List of vulnerable API endpoints and parameters\n- **Impact Assessment**: Classification of data exposure severity\n- **Remediation Recommendations**: Specific fixes for identified vulnerabilities\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n### 1. Understand IDOR Vulnerability Types\n\n#### Direct Reference to Database Objects\nOccurs when applications reference database records via user-controllable parameters:\n```\n# Original URL (authenticated as User A)\nexample.com/user/profile?id=2023\n\n# Manipulation attempt (accessing User B''s data)\nexample.com/user/profile?id=2022\n```\n\n#### Direct Reference to Static Files\nOccurs when applications expose file paths or names that can be enumerated:\n```\n# Original URL (User A''s receipt)\nexample.com/static/receipt/205.pdf\n\n# Manipulation attempt (User B''s receipt)\nexample.com/static/receipt/200.pdf\n```\n\n### 2. Reconnaissance and Setup\n\n#### Create Multiple Test Accounts\n```\nAccount 1: \"attacker\" - Primary testing account\nAccount 2: \"victim\" - Account whose data we attempt to access\n```\n\n#### Identify Object References\nCapture and analyze requests containing:\n- Numeric IDs in URLs: `/api/user/123`\n- Numeric IDs in parameters: `?id=123&action=view`\n- Numeric IDs in request body: `{\"userId\": 123}`\n- File paths: `/download/receipt_123.pdf`\n- GUIDs/UUIDs: `/profile/a1b2c3d4-e5f6-...`\n\n#### Map User IDs\n```\n# Access user ID endpoint (if available)\nGET /api/user-id/\n\n# Note ID patterns:\n# - Sequential integers (1, 2, 3...)\n# - Auto-incremented values\n# - Predictable patterns\n```\n\n### 3. Detection Techniques\n\n#### URL Parameter Manipulation\n```\n# Step 1: Capture original authenticated request\nGET /api/user/profile?id=1001 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=attacker_session\n\n# Step 2: Modify ID to target another user\nGET /api/user/profile?id=1000 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=attacker_session\n\n# Vulnerable if: Returns victim''s data with attacker''s session\n```\n\n#### Request Body Manipulation\n```\n# Original POST request\nPOST /api/address/update HTTP/1.1\nContent-Type: application/json\nCookie: session=attacker_session\n\n{\"id\": 5, \"userId\": 1001, \"address\": \"123 Attacker St\"}\n\n# Modified request targeting victim\n{\"id\": 5, \"userId\": 1000, \"address\": \"123 Attacker St\"}\n```\n\n#### HTTP Method Switching\n```\n# Original GET request may be protected\nGET /api/admin/users/1000 → 403 Forbidden\n\n# Try alternative methods\nPOST /api/admin/users/1000 → 200 OK (Vulnerable!)\nPUT /api/admin/users/1000 → 200 OK (Vulnerable!)\n```\n\n### 4. Exploitation with Burp Suite\n\n#### Manual Exploitation\n```\n1. Configure browser proxy through Burp Suite\n2. Login as \"attacker\" user\n3. Navigate to profile/data page\n4. Enable Intercept in Proxy tab\n5. Capture request with user ID\n6. Modify ID to victim''s ID\n7. Forward request\n8. Observe response for victim''s data\n```\n\n#### Automated Enumeration with Intruder\n```\n1. Send request to Intruder (Ctrl+I)\n2. Clear all payload positions\n3. Select ID parameter as payload position\n4. Configure attack type: Sniper\n5. Payload settings:\n   - Type: Numbers\n   - Range: 1 to 10000\n   - Step: 1\n6. Start attack\n7. Analyze responses for 200 status codes\n```\n\n#### Battering Ram Attack for Multiple Positions\n```\n# When same ID appears in multiple locations\nPUT /api/addresses/§5§/update HTTP/1.1\n\n{\"id\": §5§, \"userId\": 3}\n\nAttack Type: Battering Ram\nPayload: Numbers 1-1000\n```\n\n### 5. Common IDOR Locations\n\n#### API Endpoints\n```\n/api/user/{id}\n/api/profile/{id}\n/api/order/{id}\n/api/invoice/{id}\n/api/document/{id}\n/api/message/{id}\n/api/address/{id}/update\n/api/address/{id}/delete\n```\n\n#### File Downloads\n```\n/download/invoice_{id}.pdf\n/static/receipts/{id}.pdf\n/uploads/documents/{filename}\n/files/reports/report_{date}_{id}.xlsx\n```\n\n#### Query Parameters\n```\n?userId=123\n?orderId=456\n?documentId=789\n?file=report_123.pdf\n?account=user@email.com\n```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### IDOR Testing Checklist\n\n| Test | Method | Indicator of Vulnerability |\n|------|--------|---------------------------|\n| Increment/Decrement ID | Change `id=5` to `id=4` | Returns different user''s data |\n| Use Victim''s ID | Replace with known victim ID | Access granted to victim''s resources |\n| Enumerate Range | Test IDs 1-1000 | Find valid records of other users |\n| Negative Values | Test `id=-1` or `id=0` | Unexpected data or errors |\n| Large Values | Test `id=99999999` | System information disclosure |\n| String IDs | Change format `id=user_123` | Logic bypass |\n| GUID Manipulation | Modify UUID portions | Predictable UUID patterns |\n\n### Response Analysis\n\n| Status Code | Interpretation |\n|-------------|----------------|\n| 200 OK | Potential IDOR - verify data ownership |\n| 403 Forbidden | Access control working |\n| 404 Not Found | Resource doesn''t exist |\n| 401 Unauthorized | Authentication required |\n| 500 Error | Potential input validation issue |\n\n### Common Vulnerable Parameters\n\n| Parameter Type | Examples |\n|----------------|----------|\n| User identifiers | `userId`, `uid`, `user_id`, `account` |\n| Resource identifiers | `id`, `pid`, `docId`, `fileId` |\n| Order/Transaction | `orderId`, `transactionId`, `invoiceId` |\n| Message/Communication | `messageId`, `threadId`, `chatId` |\n| File references | `filename`, `file`, `document`, `path` |\n\n## Constraints and Limitations\n\n### Operational Boundaries\n- Requires at least two valid user accounts for verification\n- Some applications use session-bound tokens instead of IDs\n- GUID/UUID references harder to enumerate but not impossible\n- Rate limiting may restrict enumeration attempts\n- Some IDOR requires chained vulnerabilities to exploit\n\n### Detection Challenges\n- Horizontal privilege escalation (user-to-user) vs vertical (user-to-admin)\n- Blind IDOR where response doesn''t confirm access\n- Time-based IDOR in asynchronous operations\n- IDOR in websocket communications\n\n### Legal Requirements\n- Only test applications with explicit authorization\n- Document all testing activities and findings\n- Do not access, modify, or exfiltrate real user data\n- Report findings through proper disclosure channels\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1: Basic ID Parameter IDOR\n```\n# Login as attacker (userId=1001)\n# Navigate to profile page\n\n# Original request\nGET /api/profile?id=1001 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=abc123\n\n# Response: Attacker''s profile data\n\n# Modified request (targeting victim userId=1000)\nGET /api/profile?id=1000 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=abc123\n\n# Vulnerable Response: Victim''s profile data returned!\n```\n\n### Example 2: IDOR in Address Update Endpoint\n```\n# Intercept address update request\nPUT /api/addresses/5/update HTTP/1.1\nContent-Type: application/json\nCookie: session=attacker_session\n\n{\n  \"id\": 5,\n  \"userId\": 1001,\n  \"street\": \"123 Main St\",\n  \"city\": \"Test City\"\n}\n\n# Modify userId to victim''s ID\n{\n  \"id\": 5,\n  \"userId\": 1000,  # Changed from 1001\n  \"street\": \"Hacked Address\",\n  \"city\": \"Exploit City\"\n}\n\n# If 200 OK: Address created under victim''s account\n```\n\n### Example 3: Static File IDOR\n```\n# Download own receipt\nGET /api/download/5 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=attacker_session\n\n# Response: PDF of attacker''s receipt (order #5)\n\n# Attempt to access other receipts\nGET /api/download/3 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=attacker_session\n\n# Vulnerable Response: PDF of victim''s receipt (order #3)!\n```\n\n### Example 4: Burp Intruder Enumeration\n```\n# Configure Intruder attack\nTarget: PUT /api/addresses/§1§/update\nPayload Position: Address ID in URL and body\n\nAttack Configuration:\n- Type: Battering Ram\n- Payload: Numbers 0-20, Step 1\n\nBody Template:\n{\n  \"id\": §1§,\n  \"userId\": 3\n}\n\n# Analyze results:\n# - 200 responses indicate successful modification\n# - Check victim''s account for new addresses\n```\n\n### Example 5: Horizontal to Vertical Escalation\n```\n# Step 1: Enumerate user roles\nGET /api/user/1 → {\"role\": \"user\", \"id\": 1}\nGET /api/user/2 → {\"role\": \"user\", \"id\": 2}\nGET /api/user/3 → {\"role\": \"admin\", \"id\": 3}\n\n# Step 2: Access admin functions with discovered ID\nGET /api/admin/dashboard?userId=3 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=regular_user_session\n\n# If accessible: Vertical privilege escalation achieved\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Issue: All Requests Return 403 Forbidden\n**Cause**: Server-side access control is implemented\n**Solution**:\n```\n# Try alternative attack vectors:\n1. HTTP method switching (GET → POST → PUT)\n2. Add X-Original-URL or X-Rewrite-URL headers\n3. Try parameter pollution: ?id=1001&id=1000\n4. URL encoding variations: %31%30%30%30 for \"1000\"\n5. Case variations for string IDs\n```\n\n### Issue: Application Uses UUIDs Instead of Sequential IDs\n**Cause**: Randomized identifiers reduce enumeration risk\n**Solution**:\n```\n# UUID discovery techniques:\n1. Check response bodies for leaked UUIDs\n2. Search JavaScript files for hardcoded UUIDs\n3. Check API responses that list multiple objects\n4. Look for UUID patterns in error messages\n5. Try UUID v1 (time-based) prediction if applicable\n```\n\n### Issue: Session Token Bound to User\n**Cause**: Application validates session against requested resource\n**Solution**:\n```\n# Advanced bypass attempts:\n1. Test for IDOR in unauthenticated endpoints\n2. Check password reset/email verification flows\n3. Look for IDOR in file upload/download\n4. Test API versioning: /api/v1/ vs /api/v2/\n5. Check mobile API endpoints (often less protected)\n```\n\n### Issue: Rate Limiting Blocks Enumeration\n**Cause**: Application implements request throttling\n**Solution**:\n```\n# Bypass techniques:\n1. Add delays between requests (Burp Intruder throttle)\n2. Rotate IP addresses (proxy chains)\n3. Target specific high-value IDs instead of full range\n4. Use different endpoints for same resources\n5. Test during off-peak hours\n```\n\n### Issue: Cannot Verify IDOR Impact\n**Cause**: Response doesn''t clearly indicate data ownership\n**Solution**:\n```\n# Verification methods:\n1. Create unique identifiable data in victim account\n2. Look for PII markers (name, email) in responses\n3. Compare response lengths between users\n4. Check for timing differences in responses\n5. Use secondary indicators (creation dates, metadata)\n```\n\n## Remediation Guidance\n\n### Implement Proper Access Control\n```python\n# Django example - validate ownership\ndef update_address(request, address_id):\n    address = Address.objects.get(id=address_id)\n    \n    # Verify ownership before allowing update\n    if address.user != request.user:\n        return HttpResponseForbidden(\"Unauthorized\")\n    \n    # Proceed with update\n    address.update(request.data)\n```\n\n### Use Indirect References\n```python\n# Instead of: /api/address/123\n# Use: /api/address/current-user/billing\n\ndef get_address(request):\n    # Always filter by authenticated user\n    address = Address.objects.filter(user=request.user).first()\n    return address\n```\n\n### Server-Side Validation\n```python\n# Always validate on server, never trust client input\ndef download_receipt(request, receipt_id):\n    receipt = Receipt.objects.filter(\n        id=receipt_id,\n        user=request.user  # Critical: filter by current user\n    ).first()\n    \n    if not receipt:\n        return HttpResponseNotFound()\n    \n    return FileResponse(receipt.file)\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:59:34.306Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Security Agents needing advanced vulnerability assessment capabilities for identifying Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerabilities","zh":"非常适合需要高级漏洞评估能力的安全代理，以识别不安全的直接对象引用（IDOR）漏洞","ja":"セキュリティエージェントが不安全な直接オブジェクト参照（IDOR）脆弱性を識別するための高度な脆弱性評価機能を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"보안 에이전트가 불안전한 직접 객체 참조(IDOR) 취약점을 식별하는 데 필요한 고급 취약점 평가 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de seguridad que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de evaluación de vulnerabilidades para identificar vulnerabilidades de referencia de objeto directa insegura (IDOR)","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de sécurité ayant besoin de capacités avancées d''évaluation des vulnérabilités pour identifier les vulnérabilités de référence d''objet directe non sécurisée (IDOR)","de":"Perfekt für Sicherheitsagenten, die erweiterte Schwachstellenbewertungsfunktionen zur Identifizierung von unsicheren direkten Objektverweisen (IDOR) benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Segurança que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de avaliação de vulnerabilidades para identificar vulnerabilidades de Referência Direta de Objeto Insegura (IDOR)","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов безопасности, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности оценки уязвимостей для выявления уязвимостей не安全ной прямой ссылки на объект (IDOR)","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأمنيين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات تقييم متقدمة للتحرك لتحديد الثغرات الأمنية في الإشارة المباشرة غير الآمنة للموضوع (IDOR)"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically detect and exploit IDOR vulnerabilities in web applications using parameter manipulation, enumeration, and Burp Suite, enhancing their ability to secure applications against unauthorized access via database object references and static file references","zh":"使代理能够系统地检测和利用IDOR漏洞在Web应用程序中使用参数操纵、枚举和Burp Suite，增强他们保护应用程序免受未经授权访问数据库对象引用和静态文件引用的能力","ja":"エージェントがパラメータ操作、列挙、Burp Suiteを使用してWebアプリケーションの中のIDOR脆弱性を体系的に検出および悪用できるようにし、データベースオブジェクト参照および静的ファイル参照による未承認アクセスからアプリケーションを保護する能力を強化","ko":"에이전트가 매개 변수 조작, 열거 및 Burp Suite를 사용하여 웹 애플리케이션에서 IDOR 취약성을 체계적으로 감지하고 악용할 수 있도록 하여 데이터베이스 객체 참조 및 정적 파일 참조에 의한 비인가 액세스로부터 애플리케이션을 보호할 수 있는 능력을 향상","es":"Habilita a los agentes a detectar sistemáticamente y explotar vulnerabilidades IDOR en aplicaciones web utilizando manipulación de parámetros, enumeración y Burp Suite, mejorando su capacidad para proteger aplicaciones contra accesos no autorizados a través de referencias de objetos de bases de datos y referencias de archivos estáticos","fr":"Permet aux agents de détecter systématiquement et d''exploiter les vulnérabilités IDOR dans les applications Web en utilisant la manipulation de paramètres, l''énumération et Burp Suite, améliorant ainsi leur capacité à sécuriser les applications contre les accès non autorisés via des références d''objets de base de données et des références de fichiers statiques","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, IDOR-Schwachstellen in Webanwendungen systematisch zu erkennen und auszunutzen, indem sie Parametermanipulation, Enumeration und Burp Suite verwenden, und verbessert damit ihre Fähigkeit, Anwendungen gegen unbefugten Zugriff über Datenbankobjektverweise und statische Dateiverweise zu sichern","pt":"Habilita os agentes a detectar sistematicamente e explorar vulnerabilidades IDOR em aplicações web usando manipulação de parâmetros, enumeração e Burp Suite, melhorando sua capacidade de proteger aplicações contra acessos não autorizados via referências de objeto de banco de dados e referências de arquivos estáticos","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью систематически обнаруживать и использовать уязвимости IDOR в веб-приложениях с помощью манипуляции параметрами, перечисления и Burp Suite, повышая их способность защищать приложения от несанкционированного доступа через ссылки на объекты базы данных и статические файловые ссылки","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على الكشف المنهجي واستغلال الثغرات الأمنية IDOR في التطبيقات الويب باستخدام مанипуляت Parameter وترقيم وبرب سويت ، مما يعزز قدرتهم على حماية التطبيقات من الوصول غير المصرح به عبر مراجع الكائنات قاعدة البيانات والمراجع الملفات الثابتة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating IDOR vulnerability testing for web applications","Generating exploit payloads using Burp Suite for penetration testing","Detecting insecure direct object references in static files and database queries"],"zh":["为Web应用程序自动化IDOR漏洞测试","使用Burp Suite生成渗透测试的利用有效载荷","在静态文件和数据库查询中检测不安全的直接对象引用"],"ja":["WebアプリケーションのIDOR脆弱性テストを自動化する","Burp Suiteを使用してペネトレーションテストの利用ペイロードを生成する","静的ファイルおよびデータベースクエリの中の不安全な直接オブジェクト参照を検出する"],"ko":["웹 애플리케이션의 IDOR 취약성 테스트 자동화","Burp Suite를 사용하여 침투 테스트에 대한 악용 페이로드 생성","정적 파일 및 데이터베이스 쿼리에서 불안전한 직접 객체 참조 감지"],"es":["Automatizar las pruebas de vulnerabilidad IDOR para aplicaciones web","Generar payloads de explotación utilizando Burp Suite para pruebas de penetración","Detectar referencias de objeto directo inseguras en archivos estáticos y consultas de bases de datos"],"fr":["Automatiser les tests de vulnérabilité IDOR pour les applications Web","Générer des charges utiles d''exploitation à l''aide de Burp Suite pour les tests de pénétration","Détecter les références d''objet directes non sécurisées dans les fichiers statiques et les requêtes de base de données"],"de":["Automatisieren von IDOR-Schwachstellentests für Webanwendungen","Erzeugen von Exploit-Payloads mit Burp Suite für Penetrationstests","Erkennen unsicherer direkter Objektverweise in statischen Dateien und Datenbankabfragen"],"pt":["Automatizar testes de vulnerabilidade IDOR para aplicações web","Gerar payloads de exploração usando Burp Suite para testes de penetração","Detectar referências diretas inseguras de objetos em arquivos estáticos e consultas de banco de dados"],"ru":["Автоматизировать тестирование уязвимостей IDOR для веб-приложений","Генерировать полезные нагрузки для эксплуатации с помощью Burp Suite для тестирования на проникновение","Обнаруживать не安全ные прямые ссылки на объекты в статических файлах и запросах базы данных"],"ar":["أتمتة اختبار الثغرات الأمنية IDOR للتطبيقات الويب","توليد حمولات الاستغلال باستخدام برب سويت لاختبار الاختراق","الكشف عن المراجع المباشرة غير الآمنة للكائنات في الملفات الثابتة và استفسارات قاعدة البيانات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Burp Suite for exploitation","Limited to web applications with accessible URLs","Needs expertise in parameter manipulation and enumeration techniques"],"zh":["需要Burp Suite进行利用","仅限于具有可访问URL的Web应用程序","需要参数操纵和枚举技术的专业知识"],"ja":["悪用にはBurp Suiteが必要","アクセス可能なURLを持つWebアプリケーションに限定される","パラメータ操作および列挙技術の専門知識が必要"],"ko":["악용을 위해 Burp Suite가 필요","접근 가능한 URL을 갖는 웹 애플리케이션으로 제한","매개 변수 조작 및 열거 기술에 대한 전문 지식 필요"],"es":["Requiere Burp Suite para la explotación","Limitado a aplicaciones web con URLs accesibles","Requiere experiencia en técnicas de manipulación y enumeración de parámetros"],"fr":["Nécessite Burp Suite pour l''exploitation","Limité aux applications Web avec des URL accessibles","Nécessite une expertise dans les techniques de manipulation et d''énumération de paramètres"],"de":["Benötigt Burp Suite für die Ausnutzung","Begrenzt auf Webanwendungen mit zugänglichen URLs","Benötigt Fachwissen in Parametermanipulations- und Enumerierungstechniken"],"pt":["Exige Burp Suite para exploração","Limitado a aplicações web com URLs acessíveis","Necessita de especialização em técnicas de manipulação de parâmetros e enumeração"],"ru":["Требует Burp Suite для эксплуатации","Ограничен веб-приложениями с доступными URL-адресами","Требует опыта в техниках манипуляции параметрами и перечисления"],"ar":["يتطلب برب سويت للاستغلال","محدود للتطبيقات الويب ذات عناوين URL القابلة للوصول","يحتاج إلى خبرة في تقنيات مаниب毕شن المعاملات وترقيم"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/rag-engineer', 'community', 'claudiodearaujo', 'IzaCenter', 'claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter', 'rag-engineer', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.541Z', '2026-02-19T02:22:43.724Z', NULL, '{"id":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/rag-engineer","name":"rag-engineer","description":{"en":""},"seo":{"title":{"en":"rag-engineer"},"description":{"en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"en":[]},"keywords":{"en":[]}},"owner":"claudiodearaujo","repo":"IzaCenter","repoPath":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.541Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rag-engineer","description":"Expert in building Retrieval-Augmented Generation systems. Masters embedding models, vector databases, chunking strategies, and retrieval optimization for LLM applications. Use when: building RAG, vector search, embeddings, semantic search, document retrieval.","bodyPreview":"# RAG Engineer\n\n**Role**: RAG Systems Architect\n\nI bridge the gap between raw documents and LLM understanding. I know that\nretrieval quality determines generation quality - garbage in, garbage out.\nI obsess over chunking boundaries, embedding dimensions, and similarity\nmetrics because they make the difference between helpful and hallucinating.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n- Vector embeddings and similarity search\n- Document chunking and preprocessing\n- Retrieval pipeline design\n- Semantic search implementa","body":"# RAG Engineer\n\n**Role**: RAG Systems Architect\n\nI bridge the gap between raw documents and LLM understanding. I know that\nretrieval quality determines generation quality - garbage in, garbage out.\nI obsess over chunking boundaries, embedding dimensions, and similarity\nmetrics because they make the difference between helpful and hallucinating.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n- Vector embeddings and similarity search\n- Document chunking and preprocessing\n- Retrieval pipeline design\n- Semantic search implementation\n- Context window optimization\n- Hybrid search (keyword + semantic)\n\n## Requirements\n\n- LLM fundamentals\n- Understanding of embeddings\n- Basic NLP concepts\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Semantic Chunking\n\nChunk by meaning, not arbitrary token counts\n\n```javascript\n- Use sentence boundaries, not token limits\n- Detect topic shifts with embedding similarity\n- Preserve document structure (headers, paragraphs)\n- Include overlap for context continuity\n- Add metadata for filtering\n```\n\n### Hierarchical Retrieval\n\nMulti-level retrieval for better precision\n\n```javascript\n- Index at multiple chunk sizes (paragraph, section, document)\n- First pass: coarse retrieval for candidates\n- Second pass: fine-grained retrieval for precision\n- Use parent-child relationships for context\n```\n\n### Hybrid Search\n\nCombine semantic and keyword search\n\n```javascript\n- BM25/TF-IDF for keyword matching\n- Vector similarity for semantic matching\n- Reciprocal Rank Fusion for combining scores\n- Weight tuning based on query type\n```\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n### ❌ Fixed Chunk Size\n\n### ❌ Embedding Everything\n\n### ❌ Ignoring Evaluation\n\n## ⚠️ Sharp Edges\n\n| Issue | Severity | Solution |\n|-------|----------|----------|\n| Fixed-size chunking breaks sentences and context | high | Use semantic chunking that respects document structure: |\n| Pure semantic search without metadata pre-filtering | medium | Implement hybrid filtering: |\n| Using same embedding model for different content types | medium | Evaluate embeddings per content type: |\n| Using first-stage retrieval results directly | medium | Add reranking step: |\n| Cramming maximum context into LLM prompt | medium | Use relevance thresholds: |\n| Not measuring retrieval quality separately from generation | high | Separate retrieval evaluation: |\n| Not updating embeddings when source documents change | medium | Implement embedding refresh: |\n| Same retrieval strategy for all query types | medium | Implement hybrid search: |\n\n## Related Skills\n\nWorks well with: `ai-agents-architect`, `prompt-engineer`, `database-architect`, `backend`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T02:22:43.724Z","qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/copy-editing', 'community', 'claudiodearaujo', 'IzaCenter', 'claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter', 'copy-editing', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:03:48.179Z', '2026-02-19T01:59:48.997Z', NULL, '{"id":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/copy-editing","name":"copy-editing","description":{"zh":"复制编辑专家通过系统性的编辑技术，增强营销文案的转化率，专注于核心信息","ja":"コピー編集の専門家は、体系的な編集技術で、マーケティング文案の転換率を向上させる","ko":"복사 편집 전문가는 시스템적인 편집 기술을 통해 마케팅 문구의 전환률을 향상","es":"La edición de copias es el proceso de mejorar el contenido existente mediante pasadas de edición enfocadas","fr":"L''édition de copies est le processus d''amélioration du contenu existant par des passes d''édition ciblées","de":"Die Bearbeitung von Kopien ist der Prozess der Verbesserung des bestehenden Inhalts durch fokussierte Bearbeitungsdurchgänge","pt":"A edição de cópia é uma técnica de otimização de conteúdo que melhora a eficácia do texto de marketing. Aprenda a aplicar princípios de edição para aumentar a conversão.","ru":"Копи-редактирование - это техника оптимизации контента, которая улучшает эффективность маркетингового текста. Узнайте, как применять принципы редактирования, чтобы увеличить конверсию.","ar":"تحرير النسخ هو تقنية لتحسين المحتوى التي تحسن فعالية نص التسويق. تعلم كيفية تطبيق مبادئ التحرير لزيادة التحويل","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"复制编辑专家：提升营销文案转化率","ja":"コピー編集の専門家：マーケティング文案の転換率を向上させる","ko":"복사 편집 전문가: 마케팅 문구 전환률 향상","es":"Edición de copias: Mejora tu contenido","fr":"Édition de copies : Améliorez votre contenu","de":"Kopieren bearbeiten: Verbessern Sie Ihren Inhalt","pt":"Edição de Cópia: Otimização de Conteúdo para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Копи-редактирование: оптимизация контента для разработчиков","ar":"تحرير النسخ: تحسين المحتوى للمطورين","en":"copy-editing"},"description":{"zh":"复制编辑专家通过系统性的编辑技术，增强营销文案的转化率，专注于核心信息","ja":"コピー編集の専門家は、体系的な編集技術で、マーケティング文案の転換率を向上させる","ko":"복사 편집 전문가는 시스템적인 편집 기술을 통해 마케팅 문구의 전환률을 향상","es":"La edición de copias es el proceso de mejorar el contenido existente mediante pasadas de edición enfocadas","fr":"L''édition de copies est le processus d''amélioration du contenu existant par des passes d''édition ciblées","de":"Die Bearbeitung von Kopien ist der Prozess der Verbesserung des bestehenden Inhalts durch fokussierte Bearbeitungsdurchgänge","pt":"A edição de cópia é uma técnica de otimização de conteúdo que melhora a eficácia do texto de marketing. Aprenda a aplicar princípios de edição para aumentar ...","ru":"Копи-редактирование - это техника оптимизации контента, которая улучшает эффективность маркетингового текста. Узнайте, как применять принципы редактирования,...","ar":"تحرير النسخ هو تقنية لتحسين المحتوى التي تحسن فعالية نص التسويق. تعلم كيفية تطبيق مبادئ التحرير لزيادة التحويل","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["系统性的编辑技术","增强核心信息","提升转化率","专注于营销文案","多维编辑"],"ja":["体系的な編集技術","コアメッセージの強化","転換率の向上","マーケティング文案への焦点","多次元編集"],"ko":["시스템적인 편집 기술","핵심 정보 강화","전환률 향상","마케팅 문구에 대한 집중","다차원 편집"],"es":["Enfoque en la mejora del mensaje principal","Pases de edición enfocados en una dimensión","No se cambia el mensaje principal","Mejora de la conversión y el marketing","Edición sistemática del contenido"],"fr":["Focus sur l''amélioration du message principal","Passes d''édition ciblées sur une dimension","Le message principal n''est pas modifié","Amélioration de la conversion et du marketing","Édition systématique du contenu"],"de":["Fokus auf die Verbesserung der Hauptnachricht","Bearbeitungsdurchgänge auf eine Dimension fokussiert","Die Hauptnachricht wird nicht geändert","Verbesserung der Konversion und des Marketings","Systematische Bearbeitung des Inhalts"],"pt":["Técnicas de edição de cópia para melhorar a conversão","Princípios de edição para preservar a mensagem central","Otimização de conteúdo para aumentar a eficácia do texto","Melhoria da clareza e da concisão do texto","Técnicas de reescrita para melhorar a fluidez do texto"],"ru":["Техники копи-редактирования для улучшения конверсии","Принципы редактирования для сохранения центрального сообщения","Оптимизация контента для увеличения эффективности текста","Улучшение ясности и краткости текста","Техники переписывания для улучшения плавности текста"],"ar":["تقنيات تحرير النسخ لتحسين التحويل","مبادئ التحرير للحفاظ على الرسالة المركزية","تحسين المحتوى لزيادة فعالية النص","تحسين وضوح و concisão النص","تقنيات إعادة الكتابة لتحسين سلاسة النص"]},"keywords":{"zh":["复制编辑","营销文案","转化率","编辑技术","核心信息","多维编辑"],"ja":["コピー編集","マーケティング文案","転換率","編集技術","コアメッセージ","多次元編集"],"ko":["복사 편집","마케팅 문구","전환률","편집 기술","핵심 정보","다차원 편집"],"es":["edición de copias","mejora de contenido","conversión","marketing","edición sistemática","copias de marketing","edición de copias para conversión"],"fr":["édition de copies","amélioration de contenu","conversion","marketing","édition systématique","copies de marketing","édition de copies pour conversion"],"de":["Kopien bearbeiten","Inhaltsverbesserung","Konversion","Marketing","systematische Bearbeitung","Marketing-Kopien","Kopienbearbeitung für Konversion"],"pt":["edição de cópia","otimização de conteúdo","conversão","texto de marketing","princípios de edição","técnicas de edição","reescrita","clareza","concisão"],"ru":["копи-редактирование","оптимизация контента","конверсия","маркетинговый текст","принципы редактирования","техники редактирования","переписывание","ясность","краткость"],"ar":["تحرير النسخ","تحسين المحتوى","التحويل","نص التسويق","مبادئ التحرير","تقنيات التحرير","إعادة الكتابة","وضوح","concisão"]}},"owner":"claudiodearaujo","repo":"IzaCenter","repoPath":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:03:48.179Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"copy-editing","description":"When the user wants to edit, review, or improve existing marketing copy. Also use when the user mentions edit this copy, review my copy, copy feedback, proofread, polish this, make this better, or copy sweep. This skill provides a systematic approach to editing marketing copy through multiple focused passes.","bodyPreview":"# Copy Editing\n\nYou are an expert copy editor specializing in marketing and conversion copy. Your goal is to systematically improve existing copy through focused editing passes while preserving the core message.\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nGood copy editing isn''t about rewriting—it''s about enhancing. Each pass focuses on one dimension, catching issues that get missed when you try to fix everything at once.\n\n**Key principles:**\n- Don''t change the core message; focus on enhancing it\n- Multiple focused pa","body":"# Copy Editing\n\nYou are an expert copy editor specializing in marketing and conversion copy. Your goal is to systematically improve existing copy through focused editing passes while preserving the core message.\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nGood copy editing isn''t about rewriting—it''s about enhancing. Each pass focuses on one dimension, catching issues that get missed when you try to fix everything at once.\n\n**Key principles:**\n- Don''t change the core message; focus on enhancing it\n- Multiple focused passes beat one unfocused review\n- Each edit should have a clear reason\n- Preserve the author''s voice while improving clarity\n\n---\n\n## The Seven Sweeps Framework\n\nEdit copy through seven sequential passes, each focusing on one dimension. After each sweep, loop back to check previous sweeps aren''t compromised.\n\n### Sweep 1: Clarity\n\n**Focus:** Can the reader understand what you''re saying?\n\n**What to check:**\n- Confusing sentence structures\n- Unclear pronoun references\n- Jargon or insider language\n- Ambiguous statements\n- Missing context\n\n**Common clarity killers:**\n- Sentences trying to say too much\n- Abstract language instead of concrete\n- Assuming reader knowledge they don''t have\n- Burying the point in qualifications\n\n**Process:**\n1. Read through quickly, highlighting unclear parts\n2. Don''t correct yet—just note problem areas\n3. After marking issues, recommend specific edits\n4. Verify edits maintain the original intent\n\n**After this sweep:** Confirm the \"Rule of One\" (one main idea per section) and \"You Rule\" (copy speaks to the reader) are intact.\n\n---\n\n### Sweep 2: Voice and Tone\n\n**Focus:** Is the copy consistent in how it sounds?\n\n**What to check:**\n- Shifts between formal and casual\n- Inconsistent brand personality\n- Mood changes that feel jarring\n- Word choices that don''t match the brand\n\n**Common voice issues:**\n- Starting casual, becoming corporate\n- Mixing \"we\" and \"the company\" references\n- Humor in some places, serious in others (unintentionally)\n- Technical language appearing randomly\n\n**Process:**\n1. Read aloud to hear inconsistencies\n2. Mark where tone shifts unexpectedly\n3. Recommend edits that smooth transitions\n4. Ensure personality remains throughout\n\n**After this sweep:** Return to Clarity Sweep to ensure voice edits didn''t introduce confusion.\n\n---\n\n### Sweep 3: So What\n\n**Focus:** Does every claim answer \"why should I care?\"\n\n**What to check:**\n- Features without benefits\n- Claims without consequences\n- Statements that don''t connect to reader''s life\n- Missing \"which means...\" bridges\n\n**The So What test:**\nFor every statement, ask \"Okay, so what?\" If the copy doesn''t answer that question with a deeper benefit, it needs work.\n\n❌ \"Our platform uses AI-powered analytics\"\n*So what?*\n✅ \"Our AI-powered analytics surface insights you''d miss manually—so you can make better decisions in half the time\"\n\n**Common So What failures:**\n- Feature lists without benefit connections\n- Impressive-sounding claims that don''t land\n- Technical capabilities without outcomes\n- Company achievements that don''t help the reader\n\n**Process:**\n1. Read each claim and literally ask \"so what?\"\n2. Highlight claims missing the answer\n3. Add the benefit bridge or deeper meaning\n4. Ensure benefits connect to real reader desires\n\n**After this sweep:** Return to Voice and Tone, then Clarity.\n\n---\n\n### Sweep 4: Prove It\n\n**Focus:** Is every claim supported with evidence?\n\n**What to check:**\n- Unsubstantiated claims\n- Missing social proof\n- Assertions without backup\n- \"Best\" or \"leading\" without evidence\n\n**Types of proof to look for:**\n- Testimonials with names and specifics\n- Case study references\n- Statistics and data\n- Third-party validation\n- Guarantees and risk reversals\n- Customer logos\n- Review scores\n\n**Common proof gaps:**\n- \"Trusted by thousands\" (which thousands?)\n- \"Industry-leading\" (according to whom?)\n- \"Customers love us\" (show them saying it)\n- Results claims without specifics\n\n**Process:**\n1. Identify every claim that needs proof\n2. Check if proof exists nearby\n3. Flag unsupported assertions\n4. Recommend adding proof or softening claims\n\n**After this sweep:** Return to So What, Voice and Tone, then Clarity.\n\n---\n\n### Sweep 5: Specificity\n\n**Focus:** Is the copy concrete enough to be compelling?\n\n**What to check:**\n- Vague language (\"improve,\" \"enhance,\" \"optimize\")\n- Generic statements that could apply to anyone\n- Round numbers that feel made up\n- Missing details that would make it real\n\n**Specificity upgrades:**\n\n| Vague | Specific |\n|-------|----------|\n| Save time | Save 4 hours every week |\n| Many customers | 2,847 teams |\n| Fast results | Results in 14 days |\n| Improve your workflow | Cut your reporting time in half |\n| Great support | Response within 2 hours |\n\n**Common specificity issues:**\n- Adjectives doing the work nouns should do\n- Benefits without quantification\n- Outcomes without timeframes\n- Claims without concrete examples\n\n**Process:**\n1. Highlight vague words and phrases\n2. Ask \"Can this be more specific?\"\n3. Add numbers, timeframes, or examples\n4. Remove content that can''t be made specific (it''s probably filler)\n\n**After this sweep:** Return to Prove It, So What, Voice and Tone, then Clarity.\n\n---\n\n### Sweep 6: Heightened Emotion\n\n**Focus:** Does the copy make the reader feel something?\n\n**What to check:**\n- Flat, informational language\n- Missing emotional triggers\n- Pain points mentioned but not felt\n- Aspirations stated but not evoked\n\n**Emotional dimensions to consider:**\n- Pain of the current state\n- Frustration with alternatives\n- Fear of missing out\n- Desire for transformation\n- Pride in making smart choices\n- Relief from solving the problem\n\n**Techniques for heightening emotion:**\n- Paint the \"before\" state vividly\n- Use sensory language\n- Tell micro-stories\n- Reference shared experiences\n- Ask questions that prompt reflection\n\n**Process:**\n1. Read for emotional impact—does it move you?\n2. Identify flat sections that should resonate\n3. Add emotional texture while staying authentic\n4. Ensure emotion serves the message (not manipulation)\n\n**After this sweep:** Return to Specificity, Prove It, So What, Voice and Tone, then Clarity.\n\n---\n\n### Sweep 7: Zero Risk\n\n**Focus:** Have we removed every barrier to action?\n\n**What to check:**\n- Friction near CTAs\n- Unanswered objections\n- Missing trust signals\n- Unclear next steps\n- Hidden costs or surprises\n\n**Risk reducers to look for:**\n- Money-back guarantees\n- Free trials\n- \"No credit card required\"\n- \"Cancel anytime\"\n- Social proof near CTA\n- Clear expectations of what happens next\n- Privacy assurances\n\n**Common risk issues:**\n- CTA asks for commitment without earning trust\n- Objections raised but not addressed\n- Fine print that creates doubt\n- Vague \"Contact us\" instead of clear next step\n\n**Process:**\n1. Focus on sections near CTAs\n2. List every reason someone might hesitate\n3. Check if the copy addresses each concern\n4. Add risk reversals or trust signals as needed\n\n**After this sweep:** Return through all previous sweeps one final time: Heightened Emotion, Specificity, Prove It, So What, Voice and Tone, Clarity.\n\n---\n\n## Quick-Pass Editing Checks\n\nUse these for faster reviews when a full seven-sweep process isn''t needed.\n\n### Word-Level Checks\n\n**Cut these words:**\n- Very, really, extremely, incredibly (weak intensifiers)\n- Just, actually, basically (filler)\n- In order to (use \"to\")\n- That (often unnecessary)\n- Things, stuff (vague)\n\n**Replace these:**\n\n| Weak | Strong |\n|------|--------|\n| Utilize | Use |\n| Implement | Set up |\n| Leverage | Use |\n| Facilitate | Help |\n| Innovative | New |\n| Robust | Strong |\n| Seamless | Smooth |\n| Cutting-edge | New/Modern |\n\n**Watch for:**\n- Adverbs (usually unnecessary)\n- Passive voice (switch to active)\n- Nominalizations (verb → noun: \"make a decision\" → \"decide\")\n\n### Sentence-Level Checks\n\n- One idea per sentence\n- Vary sentence length (mix short and long)\n- Front-load important information\n- Max 3 conjunctions per sentence\n- No more than 25 words (usually)\n\n### Paragraph-Level Checks\n\n- One topic per paragraph\n- Short paragraphs (2-4 sentences for web)\n- Strong opening sentences\n- Logical flow between paragraphs\n- White space for scannability\n\n---\n\n## Copy Editing Checklist\n\n### Before You Start\n- [ ] Understand the goal of this copy\n- [ ] Know the target audience\n- [ ] Identify the desired action\n- [ ] Read through once without editing\n\n### Clarity (Sweep 1)\n- [ ] Every sentence is immediately understandable\n- [ ] No jargon without explanation\n- [ ] Pronouns have clear references\n- [ ] No sentences trying to do too much\n\n### Voice & Tone (Sweep 2)\n- [ ] Consistent formality level throughout\n- [ ] Brand personality maintained\n- [ ] No jarring shifts in mood\n- [ ] Reads well aloud\n\n### So What (Sweep 3)\n- [ ] Every feature connects to a benefit\n- [ ] Claims answer \"why should I care?\"\n- [ ] Benefits connect to real desires\n- [ ] No impressive-but-empty statements\n\n### Prove It (Sweep 4)\n- [ ] Claims are substantiated\n- [ ] Social proof is specific and attributed\n- [ ] Numbers and stats have sources\n- [ ] No unearned superlatives\n\n### Specificity (Sweep 5)\n- [ ] Vague words replaced with concrete ones\n- [ ] Numbers and timeframes included\n- [ ] Generic statements made specific\n- [ ] Filler content removed\n\n### Heightened Emotion (Sweep 6)\n- [ ] Copy evokes feeling, not just information\n- [ ] Pain points feel real\n- [ ] Aspirations feel achievable\n- [ ] Emotion serves the message authentically\n\n### Zero Risk (Sweep 7)\n- [ ] Objections addressed near CTA\n- [ ] Trust signals present\n- [ ] Next steps are crystal clear\n- [ ] Risk reversals stated (guarantee, trial, etc.)\n\n### Final Checks\n- [ ] No typos or grammatical errors\n- [ ] Consistent formatting\n- [ ] Links work (if applicable)\n- [ ] Core message preserved through all edits\n\n---\n\n## Common Copy Problems & Fixes\n\n### Problem: Wall of Features\n**Symptom:** List of what the product does without why it matters\n**Fix:** Add \"which means...\" after each feature to bridge to benefits\n\n### Problem: Corporate Speak\n**Symptom:** \"Leverage synergies to optimize outcomes\"\n**Fix:** Ask \"How would a human say this?\" and use those words\n\n### Problem: Weak Opening\n**Symptom:** Starting with company history or vague statements\n**Fix:** Lead with the reader''s problem or desired outcome\n\n### Problem: Buried CTA\n**Symptom:** The ask comes after too much buildup, or isn''t clear\n**Fix:** Make the CTA obvious, early, and repeated\n\n### Problem: No Proof\n**Symptom:** \"Customers love us\" with no evidence\n**Fix:** Add specific testimonials, numbers, or case references\n\n### Problem: Generic Claims\n**Symptom:** \"We help businesses grow\"\n**Fix:** Specify who, how, and by how much\n\n### Problem: Mixed Audiences\n**Symptom:** Copy tries to speak to everyone, resonates with no one\n**Fix:** Pick one audience and write directly to them\n\n### Problem: Feature Overload\n**Symptom:** Listing every capability, overwhelming the reader\n**Fix:** Focus on 3-5 key benefits that matter most to the audience\n\n---\n\n## Working with Copy Sweeps\n\nWhen editing collaboratively:\n\n1. **Run a sweep and present findings** - Show what you found, why it''s an issue\n2. **Recommend specific edits** - Don''t just identify problems; propose solutions\n3. **Request the updated copy** - Let the author make final decisions\n4. **Verify previous sweeps** - After each round of edits, re-check earlier sweeps\n5. **Repeat until clean** - Continue until a full sweep finds no new issues\n\nThis iterative process ensures each edit doesn''t create new problems while respecting the author''s ownership of the copy.\n\n---\n\n## Questions to Ask\n\nIf you need more context:\n1. What''s the goal of this copy? (Awareness, conversion, retention)\n2. Who''s the target audience?\n3. What action should readers take?\n4. What''s the brand voice? (Casual, professional, playful, authoritative)\n5. Are there specific concerns or known issues?\n6. What proof/evidence do you have available?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **copywriting**: For writing new copy from scratch (use this skill to edit after your first draft is complete)\n- **page-cro**: For broader page optimization beyond copy\n- **marketing-psychology**: For understanding why certain edits improve conversion\n- **ab-test-setup**: For testing copy variations\n\n---\n\n## When to Use Each Skill\n\n| Task | Skill to Use |\n|------|--------------|\n| Writing new page copy from scratch | copywriting |\n| Reviewing and improving existing copy | copy-editing (this skill) |\n| Editing copy you just wrote | copy-editing (this skill) |\n| Structural or strategic page changes | page-cro |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:59:48.997Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Language Agents specializing in content refinement and marketing copy optimization.","zh":"非常适合专门从事内容精炼和营销文案优化的语言代理。","ja":"コンテンツの洗練やマーケティングコピーの最適化を専門とする言語エージェントに最適です。","ko":"콘텐츠 정련 및 마케팅 사본 최적화를 전문으로 하는 언어 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Lenguaje especializados en refinamiento de contenido y optimización de copias de marketing.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Langage spécialisés dans l''affinement de contenu et l''optimisation de copies de marketing.","de":"Perfekt für Sprachagenten, die auf Inhaltsverfeinerung und Marketing-Kopie-Optimierung spezialisiert sind.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Linguagem especializados em refinamento de conteúdo e otimização de cópia de marketing.","ru":"Идеально для языковых агентов, специализирующихся на усовершенствовании контента и оптимизации маркетинговых копий.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء اللغويين المتخصصين في تعدين المحتوى وتحسين نسخ الترويج"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically enhance existing copy through focused editing passes, preserving core messages while applying key principles like multiple focused passes and core message preservation, utilizing dimensions such as clarity, coherence, and conversion optimization.","zh":"赋予代理人通过有针对性的编辑过程系统地增强现有文案的能力，同时保留核心信息并应用关键原则，如多次有针对性的编辑过程和核心信息保留，利用诸如清晰度、连贯性和转化率优化等维度。","ja":"エージェントが、複数のフォーカスされたパスやコアメッセージの保存などの重要な原則を適用しながら、クリアランス、連貫性、コンバージョン最適化などの次元を利用して、核心メッセージを保ちながら既存のコピーを体系的に強化することを可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 핵심 메시지를 보존하면서도 여러 차례의 집중 편집 과정을 통해 기존의 사본을 체계적으로 향상시키는 것을 가능하게 하며, 명확성, 일관성, 전환 최적화 등의 차원을 사용하여 핵심 원칙을 적용할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a mejorar sistemáticamente las copias existentes a través de pasadas de edición enfocadas, preservando los mensajes básicos mientras se aplican principios clave como múltiples pasadas enfocadas y preservación del mensaje básico, utilizando dimensiones como claridad, coherencia y optimización de conversión.","fr":"Autorise les agents à améliorer systématiquement les copies existantes à travers des passes d''édition ciblées, préservant les messages de base tout en appliquant des principes clés tels que des passes ciblées multiples et préservation du message de base, en utilisant des dimensions telles que la clarté, la cohérence et l''optimisation de conversion.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, bestehende Kopien systematisch durch fokussierte Editierdurchläufe zu verbessern, wobei die Kernbotschaften erhalten bleiben, während wichtige Grundsätze wie mehrere fokussierte Durchläufe und Erhalt der Kernbotschaft angewendet werden, unter Nutzung von Dimensionen wie Klarheit, Kohärenz und Konversionsoptimierung.","pt":"Permite que os agentes aprimorem sistematicamente as cópias existentes por meio de edições focadas, preservando as mensagens principais e aplicando princípios-chave como várias edições focadas e preservação da mensagem principal, utilizando dimensões como clareza, coerência e otimização de conversão.","ru":"Позволяет агентам систематически улучшать существующие копии посредством сосредоточенных редакционных проходов, сохраняя основные сообщения и применяя ключевые принципы, такие как несколько сосредоточенных проходов и сохранение основного сообщения, используя размеры, такие как ясность, связность и оптимизация конверсии.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تحسين النسخ الحالية بطريقة منهجية من خلال прохождения تحريرية محددة، مع الحفاظ على الرسائل الأساسية وتطبيق مبادئ رئيسية مثل прохождения متعددة محددة والحفاظ على الرسالة الأساسية، باستخدام أبعاد مثل الوضوح والترابط وتحسين التحويل"},"useCases":{"en":["Refining marketing copy for improved conversion rates","Enhancing blog posts for better readability and engagement","Optimizing product descriptions for e-commerce platforms"],"zh":["为提高转化率而优化营销文案","为了提高可读性和参与度而增强博客文章","为电子商务平台优化产品描述"],"ja":["コンバージョン率の向上のためにマーケティングコピーを最適化する","読みやすさとエンゲージメントの向上のためにブログ記事を強化する","電子商取引プラットフォームの製品説明を最適化する"],"ko":["전환율을 높이기 위한 마케팅 사본의 최적화","가독성과 참여도를 높이기 위한 블로그 게시물의 강화","전자상거래 플랫폼의 제품 설명 최적화"],"es":["Refinamiento de copias de marketing para mejorar las tasas de conversión","Mejora de publicaciones de blog para una mejor legibilidad y compromiso","Optimización de descripciones de productos para plataformas de comercio electrónico"],"fr":["Affinement de copies de marketing pour améliorer les taux de conversion","Amélioration de billets de blog pour une meilleure lisibilité et engagement","Optimisation de descriptions de produits pour les plateformes de commerce électronique"],"de":["Verfeinerung von Marketing-Kopien zur Verbesserung der Konversionsraten","Verbesserung von Blog-Beiträgen für eine bessere Lesbarkeit und Bindung","Optimierung von Produktbeschreibungen für E-Commerce-Plattformen"],"pt":["Refinamento de cópia de marketing para taxas de conversão aprimoradas","Melhoria de posts de blog para melhor legibilidade e engajamento","Otimização de descrições de produtos para plataformas de comércio eletrônico"],"ru":["Усовершенствование маркетинговых копий для улучшения конверсионных ставок","Улучшение постов в блогах для лучшей читаемости и вовлеченности","Оптимизация описаний продуктов для электронных коммерческих платформ"],"ar":["تعدين نسخ الترويج لتحسين معدلات التحويل","تحسين منشورات المدونة لقراءة أفضل ومشاركة أكبر","تحسين وصفات المنتجات منصات التجارة الإلكترونية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of marketing and conversion copy principles","Preserves core message, limiting scope for complete rewrites"],"zh":["需要了解营销和转化文案原则","保留核心信息，限制完全重写的范围"],"ja":["マーケティングとコンバージョンコピーの原則の理解が必要","コアメッセージを保存するため、完全な書き直しの範囲が制限される"],"ko":["마케팅 및 전환 사본 원칙에 대한 이해가 필요함","핵심 메시지를 보존하므로 완전한 리ライト의 범위가 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de principios de copias de marketing y conversión","Preserva el mensaje básico, limitando el alcance para reescrituras completas"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes de copies de marketing et de conversion","Préserve le message de base, limitant la portée pour des réécritures complètes"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis von Marketing- und Konversions-Kopie-Grundsätzen","Bewahrt die Kernbotschaft, wodurch der Umfang für vollständige Neufassungen begrenzt wird"],"pt":["Exige compreensão de princípios de cópia de marketing e conversão","Preserva a mensagem principal, limitando o escopo para reescritas completas"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов маркетинговых копий и конверсии","Сохраняет основное сообщение, ограничивая объем для полных переписываний"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ نسخ الترويج والتحويل","الحفاظ على الرسالة الأساسية، وحدود نطاق لإعادة الكتابة الكاملة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Dknight203/AesopIDE/copy-editing', 'community', 'Dknight203', 'AesopIDE', 'Dknight203/AesopIDE', 'copy-editing', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:03:48.179Z', '2026-02-19T01:59:48.593Z', NULL, '{"id":"Dknight203/AesopIDE/copy-editing","name":"copy-editing","description":{"zh":"复制编辑是指通过系统的编辑过程，增强核心信息的传达，而不改变其本质","ja":"コピー編集は、体系的な編集プロセスを通じて核心メッセージを強化すること","ko":"복사 편집은 체계적인 편집 과정을 통해 핵심 메시지를 강화하는 것을 의미","es":"La edición de copias es un proceso sistemático para mejorar el contenido existente, preservando el mensaje central","fr":"L''édition de copies est un processus systématique pour améliorer le contenu existant, en préservant le message central","de":"Die Kopienbearbeitung ist ein systematischer Prozess, um den bestehenden Inhalt zu verbessern und die zentrale Botschaft zu bewahren","pt":"Edição de cópia é o processo de melhorar o conteúdo de marketing através de passes de edição focados","ru":"Копирайтинг - это процесс улучшения маркетингового контента через целенаправленные редакторские проходы","ar":"تحرير النسخ هو عملية تحسين محتوى التسويق من خلال مرور تحرير متعمق","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"专业的复制编辑技术","ja":"コピー編集の専門技術","ko":"복사 편집 전문 기술","es":"Edición de copias: mejora tu contenido con precisión","fr":"Édition de copies : améliorez votre contenu avec précision","de":"Kopienbearbeitung: verbessern Sie Ihren Inhalt mit Präzision","pt":"Edição de Cópia: Otimização de Conteúdo","ru":"Копирайтинг: Редактирование и Оптимизация","ar":"تحرير النسخ: تحسين المحتوى","en":"copy-editing"},"description":{"zh":"复制编辑是指通过系统的编辑过程，增强核心信息的传达，而不改变其本质","ja":"コピー編集は、体系的な編集プロセスを通じて核心メッセージを強化すること","ko":"복사 편집은 체계적인 편집 과정을 통해 핵심 메시지를 강화하는 것을 의미","es":"La edición de copias es un proceso sistemático para mejorar el contenido existente, preservando el mensaje central","fr":"L''édition de copies est un processus systématique pour améliorer le contenu existant, en préservant le message central","de":"Die Kopienbearbeitung ist ein systematischer Prozess, um den bestehenden Inhalt zu verbessern und die zentrale Botschaft zu bewahren","pt":"Edição de cópia é o processo de melhorar o conteúdo de marketing através de passes de edição focados","ru":"Копирайтинг - это процесс улучшения маркетингового контента через целенаправленные редакторские проходы","ar":"تحرير النسخ هو عملية تحسين محتوى التسويق من خلال مرور تحرير متعمق","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"definition":{"en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"features":{"zh":["系统的编辑过程","增强核心信息的传达","不改变核心信息的本质","多次编辑过程","专注于一个维度"],"ja":["体系的な編集プロセス","核心メッセージの強化","核心メッセージの本質の変更なし","複数回の編集プロセス","一つの次元に焦点を当てる"],"ko":["체계적인 편집 과정","핵심 메시지의 강화","핵심 메시지의 본质의 변경 없음","複数回의 편집 과정","하나의 차원에 집중"],"es":["Enfoque sistemático para la edición de copias","Mejora del contenido sin alterar el mensaje central","Énfasis en la claridad y la eficacia","Proceso de edición paso a paso","Optimización del contenido para la conversión"],"fr":["Approche systématique pour l''édition de copies","Amélioration du contenu sans altérer le message central","Accent sur la clarté et l''efficacité","Processus d''édition étape par étape","Optimisation du contenu pour la conversion"],"de":["Systematischer Ansatz für die Kopienbearbeitung","Verbesserung des Inhalts ohne die zentrale Botschaft zu verändern","Konzentration auf Klarheit und Effektivität","Schrittweiser Bearbeitungsprozess","Optimierung des Inhalts für die Konversion"],"pt":["Melhoria do conteúdo de marketing","Técnicas de edição de cópia especializadas","Preservação da mensagem central","Foco em uma dimensão por vez","Aumento da eficácia do marketing"],"ru":["Улучшение маркетингового контента","Специализированные техники копирайтинга","Сохранение основного сообщения","Фокус на одной размерности за раз","Повышение эффективности маркетинга"],"ar":["تحسين محتوى التسويق","تقنيات تحرير النسخ المتخصصة","الحفاظ على الرسالة الأساسية","التركيز على بعد واحد في كل مرة","زيادة فعالية التسويق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["复制编辑","核心信息","编辑技术","系统编辑","增强传达","不改变本质"],"ja":["コピー編集","核心メッセージ","編集技術","体系的な編集","強化伝達","本質の変更なし"],"ko":["복사 편집","핵심 메시지","편집 기술","체계적인 편집","강화 전달","본질의 변경 없음"],"es":["edición de copias","mejora de contenido","optimización de conversión","copywriting","redacción de copias","edición de texto"],"fr":["édition de copies","amélioration de contenu","optimisation de conversion","copywriting","rédaction de copies","édition de texte"],"de":["Kopienbearbeitung","Inhaltsverbesserung","Konversionsoptimierung","Copywriting","Texterstellung","Inhaltsbearbeitung"],"pt":["edição de cópia","otimização de conteúdo","marketing de conversão","copywriting","técnica de edição","melhoria de conteúdo"],"ru":["копирайтинг","оптимизация контента","маркетинг конверсии","редактирование копии","техника редактирования","улучшение контента"],"ar":["تحرير النسخ","تحسين المحتوى","تسويق التحويل","كتابة المحتوى","تقنية التحرير","تحسين المحتوى"]}},"owner":"Dknight203","repo":"AesopIDE","repoPath":"Dknight203/AesopIDE","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:03:48.179Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"copy-editing","description":"When the user wants to edit, review, or improve existing marketing copy. Also use when the user mentions edit this copy, review my copy, copy feedback, proofread, polish this, make this better, or copy sweep. This skill provides a systematic approach to editing marketing copy through multiple focused passes.","bodyPreview":"# Copy Editing\n\nYou are an expert copy editor specializing in marketing and conversion copy. Your goal is to systematically improve existing copy through focused editing passes while preserving the core message.\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nGood copy editing isn''t about rewriting—it''s about enhancing. Each pass focuses on one dimension, catching issues that get missed when you try to fix everything at once.\n\n**Key principles:**\n- Don''t change the core message; focus on enhancing it\n- Multiple focused pa","body":"# Copy Editing\n\nYou are an expert copy editor specializing in marketing and conversion copy. Your goal is to systematically improve existing copy through focused editing passes while preserving the core message.\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nGood copy editing isn''t about rewriting—it''s about enhancing. Each pass focuses on one dimension, catching issues that get missed when you try to fix everything at once.\n\n**Key principles:**\n- Don''t change the core message; focus on enhancing it\n- Multiple focused passes beat one unfocused review\n- Each edit should have a clear reason\n- Preserve the author''s voice while improving clarity\n\n---\n\n## The Seven Sweeps Framework\n\nEdit copy through seven sequential passes, each focusing on one dimension. After each sweep, loop back to check previous sweeps aren''t compromised.\n\n### Sweep 1: Clarity\n\n**Focus:** Can the reader understand what you''re saying?\n\n**What to check:**\n- Confusing sentence structures\n- Unclear pronoun references\n- Jargon or insider language\n- Ambiguous statements\n- Missing context\n\n**Common clarity killers:**\n- Sentences trying to say too much\n- Abstract language instead of concrete\n- Assuming reader knowledge they don''t have\n- Burying the point in qualifications\n\n**Process:**\n1. Read through quickly, highlighting unclear parts\n2. Don''t correct yet—just note problem areas\n3. After marking issues, recommend specific edits\n4. Verify edits maintain the original intent\n\n**After this sweep:** Confirm the \"Rule of One\" (one main idea per section) and \"You Rule\" (copy speaks to the reader) are intact.\n\n---\n\n### Sweep 2: Voice and Tone\n\n**Focus:** Is the copy consistent in how it sounds?\n\n**What to check:**\n- Shifts between formal and casual\n- Inconsistent brand personality\n- Mood changes that feel jarring\n- Word choices that don''t match the brand\n\n**Common voice issues:**\n- Starting casual, becoming corporate\n- Mixing \"we\" and \"the company\" references\n- Humor in some places, serious in others (unintentionally)\n- Technical language appearing randomly\n\n**Process:**\n1. Read aloud to hear inconsistencies\n2. Mark where tone shifts unexpectedly\n3. Recommend edits that smooth transitions\n4. Ensure personality remains throughout\n\n**After this sweep:** Return to Clarity Sweep to ensure voice edits didn''t introduce confusion.\n\n---\n\n### Sweep 3: So What\n\n**Focus:** Does every claim answer \"why should I care?\"\n\n**What to check:**\n- Features without benefits\n- Claims without consequences\n- Statements that don''t connect to reader''s life\n- Missing \"which means...\" bridges\n\n**The So What test:**\nFor every statement, ask \"Okay, so what?\" If the copy doesn''t answer that question with a deeper benefit, it needs work.\n\n❌ \"Our platform uses AI-powered analytics\"\n*So what?*\n✅ \"Our AI-powered analytics surface insights you''d miss manually—so you can make better decisions in half the time\"\n\n**Common So What failures:**\n- Feature lists without benefit connections\n- Impressive-sounding claims that don''t land\n- Technical capabilities without outcomes\n- Company achievements that don''t help the reader\n\n**Process:**\n1. Read each claim and literally ask \"so what?\"\n2. Highlight claims missing the answer\n3. Add the benefit bridge or deeper meaning\n4. Ensure benefits connect to real reader desires\n\n**After this sweep:** Return to Voice and Tone, then Clarity.\n\n---\n\n### Sweep 4: Prove It\n\n**Focus:** Is every claim supported with evidence?\n\n**What to check:**\n- Unsubstantiated claims\n- Missing social proof\n- Assertions without backup\n- \"Best\" or \"leading\" without evidence\n\n**Types of proof to look for:**\n- Testimonials with names and specifics\n- Case study references\n- Statistics and data\n- Third-party validation\n- Guarantees and risk reversals\n- Customer logos\n- Review scores\n\n**Common proof gaps:**\n- \"Trusted by thousands\" (which thousands?)\n- \"Industry-leading\" (according to whom?)\n- \"Customers love us\" (show them saying it)\n- Results claims without specifics\n\n**Process:**\n1. Identify every claim that needs proof\n2. Check if proof exists nearby\n3. Flag unsupported assertions\n4. Recommend adding proof or softening claims\n\n**After this sweep:** Return to So What, Voice and Tone, then Clarity.\n\n---\n\n### Sweep 5: Specificity\n\n**Focus:** Is the copy concrete enough to be compelling?\n\n**What to check:**\n- Vague language (\"improve,\" \"enhance,\" \"optimize\")\n- Generic statements that could apply to anyone\n- Round numbers that feel made up\n- Missing details that would make it real\n\n**Specificity upgrades:**\n\n| Vague | Specific |\n|-------|----------|\n| Save time | Save 4 hours every week |\n| Many customers | 2,847 teams |\n| Fast results | Results in 14 days |\n| Improve your workflow | Cut your reporting time in half |\n| Great support | Response within 2 hours |\n\n**Common specificity issues:**\n- Adjectives doing the work nouns should do\n- Benefits without quantification\n- Outcomes without timeframes\n- Claims without concrete examples\n\n**Process:**\n1. Highlight vague words and phrases\n2. Ask \"Can this be more specific?\"\n3. Add numbers, timeframes, or examples\n4. Remove content that can''t be made specific (it''s probably filler)\n\n**After this sweep:** Return to Prove It, So What, Voice and Tone, then Clarity.\n\n---\n\n### Sweep 6: Heightened Emotion\n\n**Focus:** Does the copy make the reader feel something?\n\n**What to check:**\n- Flat, informational language\n- Missing emotional triggers\n- Pain points mentioned but not felt\n- Aspirations stated but not evoked\n\n**Emotional dimensions to consider:**\n- Pain of the current state\n- Frustration with alternatives\n- Fear of missing out\n- Desire for transformation\n- Pride in making smart choices\n- Relief from solving the problem\n\n**Techniques for heightening emotion:**\n- Paint the \"before\" state vividly\n- Use sensory language\n- Tell micro-stories\n- Reference shared experiences\n- Ask questions that prompt reflection\n\n**Process:**\n1. Read for emotional impact—does it move you?\n2. Identify flat sections that should resonate\n3. Add emotional texture while staying authentic\n4. Ensure emotion serves the message (not manipulation)\n\n**After this sweep:** Return to Specificity, Prove It, So What, Voice and Tone, then Clarity.\n\n---\n\n### Sweep 7: Zero Risk\n\n**Focus:** Have we removed every barrier to action?\n\n**What to check:**\n- Friction near CTAs\n- Unanswered objections\n- Missing trust signals\n- Unclear next steps\n- Hidden costs or surprises\n\n**Risk reducers to look for:**\n- Money-back guarantees\n- Free trials\n- \"No credit card required\"\n- \"Cancel anytime\"\n- Social proof near CTA\n- Clear expectations of what happens next\n- Privacy assurances\n\n**Common risk issues:**\n- CTA asks for commitment without earning trust\n- Objections raised but not addressed\n- Fine print that creates doubt\n- Vague \"Contact us\" instead of clear next step\n\n**Process:**\n1. Focus on sections near CTAs\n2. List every reason someone might hesitate\n3. Check if the copy addresses each concern\n4. Add risk reversals or trust signals as needed\n\n**After this sweep:** Return through all previous sweeps one final time: Heightened Emotion, Specificity, Prove It, So What, Voice and Tone, Clarity.\n\n---\n\n## Quick-Pass Editing Checks\n\nUse these for faster reviews when a full seven-sweep process isn''t needed.\n\n### Word-Level Checks\n\n**Cut these words:**\n- Very, really, extremely, incredibly (weak intensifiers)\n- Just, actually, basically (filler)\n- In order to (use \"to\")\n- That (often unnecessary)\n- Things, stuff (vague)\n\n**Replace these:**\n\n| Weak | Strong |\n|------|--------|\n| Utilize | Use |\n| Implement | Set up |\n| Leverage | Use |\n| Facilitate | Help |\n| Innovative | New |\n| Robust | Strong |\n| Seamless | Smooth |\n| Cutting-edge | New/Modern |\n\n**Watch for:**\n- Adverbs (usually unnecessary)\n- Passive voice (switch to active)\n- Nominalizations (verb → noun: \"make a decision\" → \"decide\")\n\n### Sentence-Level Checks\n\n- One idea per sentence\n- Vary sentence length (mix short and long)\n- Front-load important information\n- Max 3 conjunctions per sentence\n- No more than 25 words (usually)\n\n### Paragraph-Level Checks\n\n- One topic per paragraph\n- Short paragraphs (2-4 sentences for web)\n- Strong opening sentences\n- Logical flow between paragraphs\n- White space for scannability\n\n---\n\n## Copy Editing Checklist\n\n### Before You Start\n- [ ] Understand the goal of this copy\n- [ ] Know the target audience\n- [ ] Identify the desired action\n- [ ] Read through once without editing\n\n### Clarity (Sweep 1)\n- [ ] Every sentence is immediately understandable\n- [ ] No jargon without explanation\n- [ ] Pronouns have clear references\n- [ ] No sentences trying to do too much\n\n### Voice & Tone (Sweep 2)\n- [ ] Consistent formality level throughout\n- [ ] Brand personality maintained\n- [ ] No jarring shifts in mood\n- [ ] Reads well aloud\n\n### So What (Sweep 3)\n- [ ] Every feature connects to a benefit\n- [ ] Claims answer \"why should I care?\"\n- [ ] Benefits connect to real desires\n- [ ] No impressive-but-empty statements\n\n### Prove It (Sweep 4)\n- [ ] Claims are substantiated\n- [ ] Social proof is specific and attributed\n- [ ] Numbers and stats have sources\n- [ ] No unearned superlatives\n\n### Specificity (Sweep 5)\n- [ ] Vague words replaced with concrete ones\n- [ ] Numbers and timeframes included\n- [ ] Generic statements made specific\n- [ ] Filler content removed\n\n### Heightened Emotion (Sweep 6)\n- [ ] Copy evokes feeling, not just information\n- [ ] Pain points feel real\n- [ ] Aspirations feel achievable\n- [ ] Emotion serves the message authentically\n\n### Zero Risk (Sweep 7)\n- [ ] Objections addressed near CTA\n- [ ] Trust signals present\n- [ ] Next steps are crystal clear\n- [ ] Risk reversals stated (guarantee, trial, etc.)\n\n### Final Checks\n- [ ] No typos or grammatical errors\n- [ ] Consistent formatting\n- [ ] Links work (if applicable)\n- [ ] Core message preserved through all edits\n\n---\n\n## Common Copy Problems & Fixes\n\n### Problem: Wall of Features\n**Symptom:** List of what the product does without why it matters\n**Fix:** Add \"which means...\" after each feature to bridge to benefits\n\n### Problem: Corporate Speak\n**Symptom:** \"Leverage synergies to optimize outcomes\"\n**Fix:** Ask \"How would a human say this?\" and use those words\n\n### Problem: Weak Opening\n**Symptom:** Starting with company history or vague statements\n**Fix:** Lead with the reader''s problem or desired outcome\n\n### Problem: Buried CTA\n**Symptom:** The ask comes after too much buildup, or isn''t clear\n**Fix:** Make the CTA obvious, early, and repeated\n\n### Problem: No Proof\n**Symptom:** \"Customers love us\" with no evidence\n**Fix:** Add specific testimonials, numbers, or case references\n\n### Problem: Generic Claims\n**Symptom:** \"We help businesses grow\"\n**Fix:** Specify who, how, and by how much\n\n### Problem: Mixed Audiences\n**Symptom:** Copy tries to speak to everyone, resonates with no one\n**Fix:** Pick one audience and write directly to them\n\n### Problem: Feature Overload\n**Symptom:** Listing every capability, overwhelming the reader\n**Fix:** Focus on 3-5 key benefits that matter most to the audience\n\n---\n\n## Working with Copy Sweeps\n\nWhen editing collaboratively:\n\n1. **Run a sweep and present findings** - Show what you found, why it''s an issue\n2. **Recommend specific edits** - Don''t just identify problems; propose solutions\n3. **Request the updated copy** - Let the author make final decisions\n4. **Verify previous sweeps** - After each round of edits, re-check earlier sweeps\n5. **Repeat until clean** - Continue until a full sweep finds no new issues\n\nThis iterative process ensures each edit doesn''t create new problems while respecting the author''s ownership of the copy.\n\n---\n\n## Questions to Ask\n\nIf you need more context:\n1. What''s the goal of this copy? (Awareness, conversion, retention)\n2. Who''s the target audience?\n3. What action should readers take?\n4. What''s the brand voice? (Casual, professional, playful, authoritative)\n5. Are there specific concerns or known issues?\n6. What proof/evidence do you have available?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **copywriting**: For writing new copy from scratch (use this skill to edit after your first draft is complete)\n- **page-cro**: For broader page optimization beyond copy\n- **marketing-psychology**: For understanding why certain edits improve conversion\n- **ab-test-setup**: For testing copy variations\n\n---\n\n## When to Use Each Skill\n\n| Task | Skill to Use |\n|------|--------------|\n| Writing new page copy from scratch | copywriting |\n| Reviewing and improving existing copy | copy-editing (this skill) |\n| Editing copy you just wrote | copy-editing (this skill) |\n| Structural or strategic page changes | page-cro |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:59:48.593Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Language Agents specializing in content refinement, such as Claude Code or AutoGPT, seeking advanced copy-editing capabilities.","zh":"适合专门从事内容精炼的语言代理，如 Claude Code 或 AutoGPT，寻求高级复制编辑功能。","ja":"コンテンツの洗練を専門とする言語エージェント、たとえば Claude Code または AutoGPT が、高度なコピー編集機能を求める場合に適しています。","ko":"컨텐츠 정련을 전문으로 하는 언어 에이전트, 즉 Claude Code 또는 AutoGPT와 같은 경우, 고급 복사 편집 기능을 찾는 경우 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Lenguaje especializados en refinamiento de contenido, como Claude Code o AutoGPT, que buscan capacidades de edición de copias avanzadas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de langage spécialisés dans le raffinement de contenu, tels que Claude Code ou AutoGPT, qui recherchent des capacités de révision de copie avancées.","de":"Ideal für Sprachagenten, die auf Inhaltsverfeinerung spezialisiert sind, wie Claude Code oder AutoGPT, die erweiterte Kopierbearbeitungsfunktionen suchen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Linguagem especializados em refinamento de conteúdo, como Claude Code ou AutoGPT, que buscam capacidades avançadas de edição de cópia.","ru":"Идеально для языковых агентов, специализирующихся на доработке контента, таких как Claude Code или AutoGPT, которые стремятся к расширенным возможностям редактирования копии.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء اللغويين المتخصصين في تحسين المحتوى، مثل Claude Code أو AutoGPT، الذين يبحثون عن قدرات متقدمة لتعديل النسخ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically enhance marketing and conversion copy through focused editing passes, preserving core messages while adhering to key principles like not changing the core message and utilizing multiple focused passes, all within a structured framework inspired by the AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI.","zh":"赋予代理商通过有针对性的编辑过程系统地增强营销和转换复制，同时保留核心信息并遵循关键原则，如不改变核心信息和利用多个有针对性的过程，所有这些都在受 AesopIDE 启发的结构化框架内，并采用 Antigravity 风格的 UI。","ja":"エージェントに、マーケティングとコンバージョンのコピーを、焦点を当てた編集プロセスを通じて、体系的に強化する力を与え、コアメッセージを保持し、コアメッセージを変更しないことや複数の焦点を当てたプロセスを利用するなどの重要な原則に従い、AesopIDE にインスパイアされた構造化フレームワーク内で、アンチグラビティ風の UI を使用します。","ko":"에이전트가 마케팅 및 전환 복사를 체계적으로 강화할 수 있도록 하는 동시에 핵심 메시지를 유지하고 핵심 메시지를 변경하지 않으며 여러 가지 집중적인 프로세스를 활용하는 등 주요 원칙을 준수하고 AesopIDE에서 영감을 받은 구조화된 프레임 워크 내에서 안티 그래비티 스타일의 UI를 사용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a mejorar sistemáticamente el marketing y la copia de conversión a través de pases de edición enfocados, preservando los mensajes básicos mientras se adhieren a principios clave como no cambiar el mensaje básico y utilizar múltiples pases enfocados, todo dentro de un marco estructurado inspirado en AesopIDE con una interfaz de usuario inspirada en Antigravity.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''améliorer systématiquement le marketing et la copie de conversion à travers des passes d''édition ciblées, en préservant les messages essentiels tout en respectant des principes clés tels que ne pas modifier le message essentiel et en utilisant plusieurs passes ciblées, le tout dans un cadre structuré inspiré de AesopIDE avec une interface utilisateur inspirée de Antigravity.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Marketing- und Konvertierungskopien systematisch durch fokussierte Bearbeitungsdurchgänge zu verbessern, wobei die Kernbotschaften erhalten bleiben und wichtige Grundsätze wie die Unveränderlichkeit der Kernbotschaft und die Verwendung mehrerer fokussierter Durchgänge eingehalten werden, alles innerhalb eines strukturierten Rahmens, der von AesopIDE mit Antigravity-inspirierter Benutzeroberfläche inspiriert ist.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a melhorar sistematicamente o marketing e a cópia de conversão por meio de passes de edição focados, preservando as mensagens principais ao mesmo tempo em que adere a princípios importantes, como não alterar a mensagem principal e utilizar várias passes focadas, tudo dentro de uma estrutura organizada inspirada no AesopIDE com interface do usuário inspirada na Antigravity.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью систематически улучшать маркетинг и копию для конверсии через сосредоточенные редакторские проходы, сохраняя основные сообщения, при этом соблюдая ключевые принципы, такие как не изменение основного сообщения и использование нескольких сосредоточенных проходов, все в рамках структурированной основы, вдохновленной AesopIDE с интерфейсом пользователя, вдохновленным Antigravity.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تحسين التسويق ونسخ التحويل بشكل منهجي من خلال مرور تحرير متعمق، مع الحفاظ على الرسائل الأساسية في الوقت نفسه اتباع المبادئ الرئيسية مثل عدم تغيير الرسالة الأساسية واستخدام عدة مرور متعمق، كل ذلك في إطار منظم مستوحى من AesopIDE مع واجهة مستخدم مستوحاة من Antigravity."},"useCases":{"en":["Refining marketing copy for improved conversion rates","Enhancing existing content without altering its core message","Systematically editing copy through multiple focused passes"],"zh":["改进转换率的营销复制精炼","在不改变核心信息的情况下增强现有内容","通过多个有针对性的过程系统地编辑复制"],"ja":["コンバージョン率の改善のためのマーケティングコピーの洗練","コアメッセージを変更せずに既存のコンテンツを強化する","複数の焦点を当てたプロセスを通じて体系的にコピーを編集する"],"ko":["전환율 개선을 위한 마케팅 복사 정련","핵심 메시지를 변경하지 않고 기존 콘텐츠 강화","여러 가지 집중적인 프로세스를 통해 체계적으로 복사 편집"],"es":["Refinar la copia de marketing para mejorar las tasas de conversión","Mejorar el contenido existente sin alterar su mensaje básico","Editar sistemáticamente la copia a través de múltiples pases enfocados"],"fr":["Raffiner la copie de marketing pour améliorer les taux de conversion","Améliorer le contenu existant sans altérer son message essentiel","Éditer systématiquement la copie à travers plusieurs passes ciblées"],"de":["Die Marketing-Kopie für verbesserte Konvertierungsraten verfeinern","Bestehenden Inhalt ohne Veränderung seiner Kernbotschaft verbessern","Kopien systematisch durch mehrere fokussierte Durchgänge bearbeiten"],"pt":["Aperfeiçoar a cópia de marketing para melhorar as taxas de conversão","Melhorar o conteúdo existente sem alterar sua mensagem principal","Editar sistematicamente a cópia por meio de várias passes focadas"],"ru":["Усовершенствовать маркетинговую копию для улучшения показателей конверсии","Улучшить существующий контент без изменения его основного сообщения","Систематически редактировать копию через несколько сосредоточенных проходов"],"ar":["تحسين نسخة التسويق لتحسين معدلات التحويل","تحسين المحتوى الحالي دون تغيير رسالته الأساسية","تحرير النسخ بشكل منهجي من خلال عدة مرور متعمق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of marketing and conversion copy principles","Focused on enhancing existing copy rather than generating new content"],"zh":["需要了解营销和转换复制原则","专注于增强现有复制而不是生成新内容"],"ja":["マーケティングとコンバージョンのコピーの原則を理解する必要があります","既存のコピーを強化することに焦点を当て、新しいコンテンツを生成するのではなく"],"ko":["마케팅 및 전환 복사 원리를 이해해야 함","기존 복사를 강화하는 것에 중점을 두고 새로운 콘텐츠를 생성하는 것이 아닌"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios de marketing y copia de conversión","Se centra en mejorar la copia existente en lugar de generar nuevo contenido"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes de marketing et de copie de conversion","Se concentre sur l''amélioration de la copie existante plutôt que sur la génération de nouveau contenu"],"de":["Benötigt ein Verständnis der Marketing- und Konvertierungskopie-Grundsätze","Konzentriert sich auf die Verbesserung der bestehenden Kopie anstelle der Generierung von neuem Inhalt"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos princípios de marketing e cópia de conversão","Focado em melhorar a cópia existente em vez de gerar novo conteúdo"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов маркетинга и копии для конверсии","Сосредоточен на улучшении существующей копии, а не на генерации нового контента"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ التسويق ونسخ التحويل","يركز على تحسين النسخ الحالية بدلاً من توليد محتوى جديد"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/neon-postgres', 'community', 'claudiodearaujo', 'IzaCenter', 'claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter', 'neon-postgres', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:03:48.179Z', '2026-02-19T01:59:54.850Z', NULL, '{"id":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/neon-postgres","name":"neon-postgres","description":{"zh":"Neon Postgres技能提供PostgreSQL连接池和服务器端驱动，支持Prisma和Drizzle等ORM框架","ja":"Neon Postgresスキルは、PostgreSQL接続プールとサーバーレスドライバーを提供し、PrismaやDrizzleなどのORMフレームワークをサポートします","ko":"Neon Postgres 스킬은 PostgreSQL 연결 풀링 및 서버리스 드라이버를 제공하며, Prisma 및 Drizzle 등의 ORM 프레임워크를 지원합니다","es":"Neon Postgres es una base de datos relacional que se integra con Prisma y Drizzle para aplicaciones serverless y edge. Ofrece connection pooling para mejorar el rendimiento","fr":"Neon Postgres est une base de données relationnelle qui s''intègre avec Prisma et Drizzle pour des applications serverless et edge. Elle offre un pool de connexions pour améliorer les performances","de":"Neon Postgres ist eine relationale Datenbank, die sich mit Prisma und Drizzle für serverless- und Edge-Anwendungen integriert. Sie bietet Connection-Pooling, um die Leistung zu verbessern","pt":"O Neon Postgres é uma solução de banco de dados que oferece conexão poolizada com o Prisma e driver serverless com o Drizzle","ru":"Neon Postgres - это решение для баз данных, которое предлагает пул соединений с Prisma и серверный драйвер с Drizzle","ar":"نيون بوستجرس هو حل قواعد البيانات الذي يقدم اتصال المجموعة مع Prisma وسائق خالي من الخادم مع Drizzle","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Neon Postgres技能：PostgreSQL连接池和服务器端驱动","ja":"Neon Postgresスキル：PostgreSQL接続プールとサーバーレスドライバー","ko":"Neon Postgres 스킬: PostgreSQL 연결 풀링 및 서버리스 드라이버","es":"Neon Postgres: Integración con Prisma y Drizzle","fr":"Neon Postgres : Intégration avec Prisma et Drizzle","de":"Neon Postgres: Integration mit Prisma und Drizzle","pt":"Neon Postgres: Soluções de Banco de Dados","ru":"Neon Postgres: Решения для баз данных","ar":"نيون بوستجرس: حلول قواعد البيانات","en":"neon-postgres"},"description":{"zh":"Neon Postgres技能提供PostgreSQL连接池和服务器端驱动，支持Prisma和Drizzle等ORM框架","ja":"Neon Postgresスキルは、PostgreSQL接続プールとサーバーレスドライバーを提供し、PrismaやDrizzleなどのORMフレームワークをサポートします","ko":"Neon Postgres 스킬은 PostgreSQL 연결 풀링 및 서버리스 드라이버를 제공하며, Prisma 및 Drizzle 등의 ORM 프레임워크를 지원합니다","es":"Neon Postgres es una base de datos relacional que se integra con Prisma y Drizzle para aplicaciones serverless y edge. Ofrece connection pooling para mejorar...","fr":"Neon Postgres est une base de données relationnelle qui s''intègre avec Prisma et Drizzle pour des applications serverless et edge. Elle offre un pool de conn...","de":"Neon Postgres ist eine relationale Datenbank, die sich mit Prisma und Drizzle für serverless- und Edge-Anwendungen integriert. Sie bietet Connection-Pooling,...","pt":"O Neon Postgres é uma solução de banco de dados que oferece conexão poolizada com o Prisma e driver serverless com o Drizzle","ru":"Neon Postgres - это решение для баз данных, которое предлагает пул соединений с Prisma и серверный драйвер с Drizzle","ar":"نيون بوستجرس هو حل قواعد البيانات الذي يقدم اتصال المجموعة مع Prisma وسائق خالي من الخادم مع Drizzle","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["PostgreSQL连接池","服务器端驱动","支持Prisma","支持Drizzle","连接池最大10K连接","支持边缘计算和服务器端环境"],"ja":["PostgreSQL接続プール","サーバーレスドライバー","Prismaサポート","Drizzleサポート","接続プール最大10K接続","エッジコンピューティングとサーバーレス環境のサポート"],"ko":["PostgreSQL 연결 풀링","서버리스 드라이버","Prisma 지원","Drizzle 지원","연결 풀 최대 10K 연결","에지 컴퓨팅 및 서버리스 환경 지원"],"es":["Integración con Prisma","Integración con Drizzle","Connection pooling con PgBouncer","Soporte para aplicaciones serverless y edge","Mejora del rendimiento con connection pooling","Compatibilidad con migrations (DDL operations)"],"fr":["Intégration avec Prisma","Intégration avec Drizzle","Pool de connexions avec PgBouncer","Prise en charge des applications serverless et edge","Amélioration des performances avec le pool de connexions","Compatibilité avec les migrations (opérations DDL)"],"de":["Integration mit Prisma","Integration mit Drizzle","Connection-Pooling mit PgBouncer","Unterstützung für serverless- und Edge-Anwendungen","Leistungsverbesserung durch Connection-Pooling","Kompatibilität mit Migrations (DDL-Operationen)"],"pt":["Conexão poolizada com o Prisma","Driver serverless com o Drizzle","Suporte a até 10K conexões","DDL operations com conexão direta","Prisma Client e Prisma Migrate","Suporte a ambientes edge e serverless"],"ru":["Пул соединений с Prisma","Серверный драйвер с Drizzle","Поддержка до 10K соединений","Операции DDL с прямым соединением","Prisma Client и Prisma Migrate","Поддержка сред edge и serverless"],"ar":["اتصال المجموعة مع Prisma","سائق خالي من الخادم مع Drizzle","دعم لما يصل إلى 10K اتصال","عمليات DDL مع اتصال مباشر","Prisma Client و Prisma Migrate","دعم لبيئات الحافة وخالية من الخادم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Neon Postgres","PostgreSQL连接池","服务器端驱动","Prisma","Drizzle","ORM框架","边缘计算","服务器端环境"],"ja":["Neon Postgres","PostgreSQL接続プール","サーバーレスドライバー","Prisma","Drizzle","ORMフレームワーク","エッジコンピューティング","サーバーレス環境"],"ko":["Neon Postgres","PostgreSQL 연결 풀링","서버리스 드라이버","Prisma","Drizzle","ORM 프레임워크","에지 컴퓨팅","서버리스 환경"],"es":["Neon Postgres","Prisma","Drizzle","connection pooling","serverless","edge","bases de datos relacionales","PgBouncer","migrations DDL"],"fr":["Neon Postgres","Prisma","Drizzle","pool de connexions","serverless","edge","bases de données relationnelles","PgBouncer","migrations DDL"],"de":["Neon Postgres","Prisma","Drizzle","Connection-Pooling","serverless","Edge","relationale Datenbanken","PgBouncer","Migrations DDL"],"pt":["Neon Postgres","Prisma","Drizzle","banco de dados","conexão poolizada","driver serverless","desenvolvimento de software","edge computing","serverless"],"ru":["Neon Postgres","Prisma","Drizzle","база данных","пул соединений","серверный драйвер","разработка программного обеспечения","edge вычисления","serverless"],"ar":["نيون بوستجرس","Prisma","Drizzle","قاعدة البيانات","اتصال المجموعة","سائق خالي من الخادم","تطوير البرمجيات","حوسبة الحافة","خالية من الخادم"]}},"owner":"claudiodearaujo","repo":"IzaCenter","repoPath":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:03:48.179Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"neon-postgres","description":"Expert patterns for Neon serverless Postgres, branching, connection pooling, and Prisma/Drizzle integration Use when: neon database, serverless postgres, database branching, neon postgres, postgres serverless.","bodyPreview":"# Neon Postgres\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Prisma with Neon Connection\n\nConfigure Prisma for Neon with connection pooling.\n\nUse two connection strings:\n- DATABASE_URL: Pooled connection for Prisma Client\n- DIRECT_URL: Direct connection for Prisma Migrate\n\nThe pooled connection uses PgBouncer for up to 10K connections.\nDirect connection required for migrations (DDL operations).\n\n\n### Drizzle with Neon Serverless Driver\n\nUse Drizzle ORM with Neon''s serverless HTTP driver for\nedge/serverless environments.","body":"# Neon Postgres\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Prisma with Neon Connection\n\nConfigure Prisma for Neon with connection pooling.\n\nUse two connection strings:\n- DATABASE_URL: Pooled connection for Prisma Client\n- DIRECT_URL: Direct connection for Prisma Migrate\n\nThe pooled connection uses PgBouncer for up to 10K connections.\nDirect connection required for migrations (DDL operations).\n\n\n### Drizzle with Neon Serverless Driver\n\nUse Drizzle ORM with Neon''s serverless HTTP driver for\nedge/serverless environments.\n\nTwo driver options:\n- neon-http: Single queries over HTTP (fastest for one-off queries)\n- neon-serverless: WebSocket for transactions and sessions\n\n\n### Connection Pooling with PgBouncer\n\nNeon provides built-in connection pooling via PgBouncer.\n\nKey limits:\n- Up to 10,000 concurrent connections to pooler\n- Connections still consume underlying Postgres connections\n- 7 connections reserved for Neon superuser\n\nUse pooled endpoint for application, direct for migrations.\n\n\n## ⚠️ Sharp Edges\n\n| Issue | Severity | Solution |\n|-------|----------|----------|\n| Issue | high | See docs |\n| Issue | high | See docs |\n| Issue | high | See docs |\n| Issue | medium | See docs |\n| Issue | medium | See docs |\n| Issue | low | See docs |\n| Issue | medium | See docs |\n| Issue | high | See docs |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:59:54.850Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloud Native Agents requiring scalable Postgres connections with Prisma and Drizzle ORM","zh":"适用于需要可扩展Postgres连接的云原生代理，支持Prisma和Drizzle ORM","ja":"PrismaおよびDrizzle ORMを使用したスケーラブルなPostgres接続を必要とするクラウドネイティブエージェントに最適","ko":"Prisma와 Drizzle ORM을 사용한 확장 가능한 Postgres 연결이 필요한 클라우드 네이티브 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes Nativos en la Nube que requieren conexiones escalables de Postgres con Prisma y Drizzle ORM","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Cloud Natifs nécessitant des connexions Postgres évolutives avec Prisma et Drizzle ORM","de":"Ideal für Cloud Native Agents, die skalierbare Postgres-Verbindungen mit Prisma und Drizzle ORM erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Nativos em Nuvem que requerem conexões escaláveis do Postgres com Prisma e Drizzle ORM","ru":"Идеально подходит для облачных агентов, требующих масштабируемых подключений к Postgres с Prisma и Drizzle ORM","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأصليين في السحابة الذين يتطلبون اتصالات قابلة للتوسيع مع Postgres و Prisma و Drizzle ORM"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage PgBouncer for connection pooling, supporting up to 10K connections, and utilize Neon''s serverless HTTP driver for edge/serverless environments, while managing migrations with direct connections for DDL operations using Prisma Migrate and Drizzle ORM","zh":"赋予代理使用PgBouncer进行连接池化，支持最多10K个连接，并利用Neon的无服务器HTTP驱动程序用于边缘/无服务器环境，同时使用Prisma Migrate和Drizzle ORM管理直接连接的DDL操作迁移","ja":"PgBouncerを使用した接続プーリングをエージェントに提供し、最大10Kの接続をサポートし、NeonのサーバーレスHTTPドライバーを使用してエッジ/サーバーレス環境で利用する，同时使用Prisma MigrateおよびDrizzle ORMで直接接続のDDL操作のマイグレーションを管理","ko":"에이전트가 PgBouncer를 사용하여 연결 풀링을 사용할 수 있도록 하여 최대 10K개의 연결을 지원하며, Neon의 서버리스 HTTP 드라이버를 사용하여 에지/서버리스 환경에서 사용할 수 있도록 하며, Prisma Migrate와 Drizzle ORM을 사용하여 직접 연결의 DDL 작업 마이그레이션을 관리","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar PgBouncer para el agrupamiento de conexiones, soportando hasta 10.000 conexiones, y utilizar el controlador HTTP sin servidor de Neon para entornos de edge/sin servidor, mientras gestiona las migraciones con conexiones directas para operaciones DDL utilizando Prisma Migrate y Drizzle ORM","fr":"Permet aux agents d''utiliser PgBouncer pour le regroupement de connexions, prenant en charge jusqu''à 10 000 connexions, et d''utiliser le pilote HTTP sans serveur de Neon pour les environnements de edge/sans serveur, tout en gérant les migrations avec des connexions directes pour les opérations DDL en utilisant Prisma Migrate et Drizzle ORM","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, PgBouncer für Connection-Pooling zu nutzen, das bis zu 10.000 Verbindungen unterstützt, und den serverlosen HTTP-Treiber von Neon für Edge-/Serverless-Umgebungen zu verwenden, während die Migrationen mit direkten Verbindungen für DDL-Vorgänge mithilfe von Prisma Migrate und Drizzle ORM verwaltet werden","pt":"Permite que os agentes usem o PgBouncer para pooling de conexões, suportando até 10K conexões, e utilizem o driver HTTP sem servidor do Neon para ambientes de borda/sem servidor, enquanto gerenciam migrações com conexões diretas para operações DDL usando Prisma Migrate e Drizzle ORM","ru":"Позволяет агентам использовать PgBouncer для пулинга подключений, поддерживающий до 10 тыс. подключений, и использовать серверный HTTP-драйвер Neon для краевых/бессерверных сред, а также управлять миграциями с прямыми подключениями для операций DDL с помощью Prisma Migrate и Drizzle ORM","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من استخدام PgBouncer لاستدعاء الاتصالات، داعمًا ما يصل إلى 10 آلاف اتصال، واستخدام برنامج تشغيل HTTP بدون خادم من Neon لبيئات الحافة / بدون خادم، مع إدارة الانتقال بالاتصالات المباشرة لعمليات DDL باستخدام Prisma Migrate و Drizzle ORM"},"useCases":{"en":["Configuring Prisma for Neon with connection pooling","Implementing Drizzle ORM with Neon''s serverless HTTP driver for edge/serverless environments","Managing database migrations using direct connections for DDL operations"],"zh":["使用连接池化配置Prisma以适用于Neon","使用Neon的无服务器HTTP驱动程序实现Drizzle ORM以适用于边缘/无服务器环境","使用直接连接管理数据库迁移以进行DDL操作"],"ja":["Neon用に接続プーリングを使用してPrismaを構成する","エッジ/サーバーレス環境用にNeonのサーバーレスHTTPドライバーを使用してDrizzle ORMを実装する","直接接続を使用してDDL操作のためのデータベースマイグレーションを管理する"],"ko":["Neon에 대한 연결 풀링을 사용하여 Prisma를 구성","에지/서버리스 환경에 대한 Neon의 서버리스 HTTP 드라이버를 사용하여 Drizzle ORM을 구현","DDL 작업을 위한 데이터베이스 마이그레이션을 관리하기 위해 직접 연결을 사용"],"es":["Configuración de Prisma para Neon con agrupamiento de conexiones","Implementación de Drizzle ORM con el controlador HTTP sin servidor de Neon para entornos de edge/sin servidor","Gestión de migraciones de base de datos utilizando conexiones directas para operaciones DDL"],"fr":["Configuration de Prisma pour Neon avec regroupement de connexions","Mise en œuvre de Drizzle ORM avec le pilote HTTP sans serveur de Neon pour les environnements de edge/sans serveur","Gestion des migrations de base de données en utilisant des connexions directes pour les opérations DDL"],"de":["Konfiguration von Prisma für Neon mit Connection-Pooling","Implementierung von Drizzle ORM mit dem serverlosen HTTP-Treiber von Neon für Edge-/Serverless-Umgebungen","Verwaltung von Datenbankmigrationen unter Verwendung direkter Verbindungen für DDL-Vorgänge"],"pt":["Configurando o Prisma para o Neon com pooling de conexões","Implementando o Drizzle ORM com o driver HTTP sem servidor do Neon para ambientes de borda/sem servidor","Gerenciando migrações de banco de dados usando conexões diretas para operações DDL"],"ru":["Настройка Prisma для Neon с пулингом подключений","Реализация Drizzle ORM с серверным HTTP-драйвером Neon для краевых/бессерверных сред","Управление миграциями базы данных с помощью прямых подключений для операций DDL"],"ar":["تكوين Prisma للاستخدام مع Neon مع استدعاء الاتصالات","تنفيذ Drizzle ORM مع برنامج تشغيل HTTP بدون خادم من Neon لبيئات الحافة / بدون خادم","إدارة تحويلات قاعدة البيانات باستخدام الاتصالات المباشرة لعمليات DDL"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires two connection strings: DATABASE_URL and DIRECT_URL","Direct connection required for migrations (DDL operations)","Specific to Neon Postgres and compatible libraries like Prisma and Drizzle ORM"],"zh":["需要两个连接字符串：DATABASE_URL和DIRECT_URL","需要直接连接进行迁移（DDL操作）","仅适用于Neon Postgres和兼容库如Prisma和Drizzle ORM"],"ja":["2つの接続文字列：DATABASE_URLとDIRECT_URLが必要","マイグレーション（DDL操作）には直接接続が必要","Neon PostgresおよびPrismaおよびDrizzle ORMなどの互換ライブラリにのみ適用"],"ko":["데이터베이스 URL과 직접 URL이라는 두 개의 연결 문자열이 필요","마이그레이션(DDL 작업)을 위해 직접 연결이 필요","Neon Postgres 및 Prisma 및 Drizzle ORM과 같은 호환 라이브러리에만 적용"],"es":["Requiere dos cadenas de conexión: DATABASE_URL y DIRECT_URL","Se requiere una conexión directa para migraciones (operaciones DDL)","Específico para Neon Postgres y bibliotecas compatibles como Prisma y Drizzle ORM"],"fr":["Nécessite deux chaînes de connexion : DATABASE_URL et DIRECT_URL","Une connexion directe est requise pour les migrations (opérations DDL)","Spécifique à Neon Postgres et aux bibliothèques compatibles comme Prisma et Drizzle ORM"],"de":["Benötigt zwei Verbindungszeichenfolgen: DATABASE_URL und DIRECT_URL","Eine direkte Verbindung ist für Migrationen (DDL-Vorgänge) erforderlich","Spezifisch für Neon Postgres und kompatible Bibliotheken wie Prisma und Drizzle ORM"],"pt":["Requer duas cadeias de conexão: DATABASE_URL e DIRECT_URL","Conexão direta necessária para migrações (operações DDL)","Específico para Neon Postgres e bibliotecas compatíveis como Prisma e Drizzle ORM"],"ru":["Требует двух строк подключения: DATABASE_URL и DIRECT_URL","Прямое подключение необходимо для миграций (операций DDL)","Спецефичен для Neon Postgres и совместимых библиотек, таких как Prisma и Drizzle ORM"],"ar":["يتطلب سلسلتين اتصال: DATABASE_URL و DIRECT_URL","التوصيل المباشر مطلوب لعمليات النقل (عمليات DDL)","محدد لاستخدام Neon Postgres والمكتبات المتوافقة مثل Prisma و Drizzle ORM"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/Security Scanning Tools', 'community', 'claudiodearaujo', 'IzaCenter', 'claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter', 'Security Scanning Tools', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.541Z', '2026-02-19T02:23:34.591Z', NULL, '{"id":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/Security Scanning Tools","name":"Security Scanning Tools","description":{"zh":"安全扫描工具用于网络发现、漏洞评估和合规验证。掌握工具选择、配置和使用","ja":"セキュリティスキャンツールはネットワークの発見、脆弱性の評価、コンプライアンスの検証に使用される。ツールの選択、構成、使用をマスターする","ko":"보안 스캔 도구는 네트워크 검색, 취약점 평가, 규정 준수에 사용된다. 도구 선택, 구성, 사용법을 익히자","es":"Este conjunto de habilidades cubre las herramientas de análisis de seguridad para redes, aplicaciones web y validación de cumplimiento.","fr":"Ce skill couvre les outils d''analyse de sécurité pour les réseaux, les applications web et la validation de conformité.","de":"Dieses Skill-Set umfasst Sicherheits-Scan-Tools für Netzwerke, Webanwendungen und Compliance-Validierung.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"安全扫描工具","ja":"セキュリティスキャンツール","ko":"보안 스캔 도구","es":"Herramientas de Análisis de Seguridad","fr":"Outils d''Analyse de Sécurité","de":"Sicherheits-Scan-Tools","en":"Security Scanning Tools"},"description":{"zh":"安全扫描工具用于网络发现、漏洞评估和合规验证。掌握工具选择、配置和使用","ja":"セキュリティスキャンツールはネットワークの発見、脆弱性の評価、コンプライアンスの検証に使用される。ツールの選択、構成、使用をマスターする","ko":"보안 스캔 도구는 네트워크 검색, 취약점 평가, 규정 준수에 사용된다. 도구 선택, 구성, 사용법을 익히자","es":"Este conjunto de habilidades cubre las herramientas de análisis de seguridad para redes, aplicaciones web y validación de cumplimiento.","fr":"Ce skill couvre les outils d''analyse de sécurité pour les réseaux, les applications web et la validation de conformité.","de":"Dieses Skill-Set umfasst Sicherheits-Scan-Tools für Netzwerke, Webanwendungen und Compliance-Validierung.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["网络发现","漏洞评估","Web 应用测试","无线安全","合规验证"],"ja":["ネットワークの発見","脆弱性の評価","Web アプリケーションのテスト","ワイヤレス セキュリティ","コンプライアンスの検証"],"ko":["네트워크 검색","취약점 평가","웹 애플리케이션 테스트","무선 보안","규정 준수"],"es":["Descubrimiento de redes","Evaluación de vulnerabilidades","Pruebas de aplicaciones web","Seguridad inalámbrica","Validación de cumplimiento"],"fr":["Découverte de réseaux","Évaluation des vulnérabilités","Tests d''applications web","Sécurité sans fil","Validation de conformité"],"de":["Netzwerkerkennung","Schwachstellentests","Webanwendungstests","Drahtlose Sicherheit","Compliance-Validierung"]},"keywords":{"zh":["安全扫描","网络安全","漏洞评估","Web 应用安全","无线安全","合规验证","安全工具"],"ja":["セキュリティスキャン","ネットワークセキュリティ","脆弱性評価","Webアプリケーションセキュリティ","ワイヤレスセキュリティ","コンプライアンス検証","セキュリティツール"],"ko":["보안 스캔","네트워크 보안","취약점 평가","웹 애플리케이션 보안","무선 보안","규정 준수","보안 도구"],"es":["análisis de seguridad","herramientas de seguridad","seguridad informática","vulnerabilidades","cumplimiento","aplicaciones web"],"fr":["analyse de sécurité","outils de sécurité","sécurité informatique","vulnérabilités","conformité","applications web"],"de":["Sicherheitsanalyse","Sicherheits-Tools","IT-Sicherheit","Schwachstellen","Compliance","Webanwendungen"]}},"owner":"claudiodearaujo","repo":"IzaCenter","repoPath":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.541Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Security Scanning Tools","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to perform vulnerability scanning, scan networks for open ports, assess web application security, scan wireless networks, detect malware, check cloud security, or evaluate system compliance. It provides comprehensive guidance on security scanning tools and methodologies.","version":"1.1","bodyPreview":"# Security Scanning Tools\n\n## Purpose\n\nMaster essential security scanning tools for network discovery, vulnerability assessment, web application testing, wireless security, and compliance validation. This skill covers tool selection, configuration, and practical usage across different scanning categories.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n### Required Environment\n- Linux-based system (Kali Linux recommended)\n- Network access to target systems\n- Proper authorization for scanning activities\n\n### Required Knowled","body":"# Security Scanning Tools\n\n## Purpose\n\nMaster essential security scanning tools for network discovery, vulnerability assessment, web application testing, wireless security, and compliance validation. This skill covers tool selection, configuration, and practical usage across different scanning categories.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n### Required Environment\n- Linux-based system (Kali Linux recommended)\n- Network access to target systems\n- Proper authorization for scanning activities\n\n### Required Knowledge\n- Basic networking concepts (TCP/IP, ports, protocols)\n- Understanding of common vulnerabilities\n- Familiarity with command-line interfaces\n\n## Outputs and Deliverables\n\n1. **Network Discovery Reports** - Identified hosts, ports, and services\n2. **Vulnerability Assessment Reports** - CVEs, misconfigurations, risk ratings\n3. **Web Application Security Reports** - OWASP Top 10 findings\n4. **Compliance Reports** - CIS benchmarks, PCI-DSS, HIPAA checks\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n### Phase 1: Network Scanning Tools\n\n#### Nmap (Network Mapper)\n\nPrimary tool for network discovery and security auditing:\n\n```bash\n# Host discovery\nnmap -sn 192.168.1.0/24              # Ping scan (no port scan)\nnmap -sL 192.168.1.0/24              # List scan (DNS resolution)\nnmap -Pn 192.168.1.100               # Skip host discovery\n\n# Port scanning techniques\nnmap -sS 192.168.1.100               # TCP SYN scan (stealth)\nnmap -sT 192.168.1.100               # TCP connect scan\nnmap -sU 192.168.1.100               # UDP scan\nnmap -sA 192.168.1.100               # ACK scan (firewall detection)\n\n# Port specification\nnmap -p 80,443 192.168.1.100         # Specific ports\nnmap -p- 192.168.1.100               # All 65535 ports\nnmap -p 1-1000 192.168.1.100         # Port range\nnmap --top-ports 100 192.168.1.100   # Top 100 common ports\n\n# Service and OS detection\nnmap -sV 192.168.1.100               # Service version detection\nnmap -O 192.168.1.100                # OS detection\nnmap -A 192.168.1.100                # Aggressive (OS, version, scripts)\n\n# Timing and performance\nnmap -T0 192.168.1.100               # Paranoid (slowest, IDS evasion)\nnmap -T4 192.168.1.100               # Aggressive (faster)\nnmap -T5 192.168.1.100               # Insane (fastest)\n\n# NSE Scripts\nnmap --script=vuln 192.168.1.100     # Vulnerability scripts\nnmap --script=http-enum 192.168.1.100  # Web enumeration\nnmap --script=smb-vuln* 192.168.1.100  # SMB vulnerabilities\nnmap --script=default 192.168.1.100  # Default script set\n\n# Output formats\nnmap -oN scan.txt 192.168.1.100      # Normal output\nnmap -oX scan.xml 192.168.1.100      # XML output\nnmap -oG scan.gnmap 192.168.1.100    # Grepable output\nnmap -oA scan 192.168.1.100          # All formats\n```\n\n#### Masscan\n\nHigh-speed port scanning for large networks:\n\n```bash\n# Basic scanning\nmasscan -p80 192.168.1.0/24 --rate=1000\nmasscan -p80,443,8080 192.168.1.0/24 --rate=10000\n\n# Full port range\nmasscan -p0-65535 192.168.1.0/24 --rate=5000\n\n# Large-scale scanning\nmasscan 0.0.0.0/0 -p443 --rate=100000 --excludefile exclude.txt\n\n# Output formats\nmasscan -p80 192.168.1.0/24 -oG results.gnmap\nmasscan -p80 192.168.1.0/24 -oJ results.json\nmasscan -p80 192.168.1.0/24 -oX results.xml\n\n# Banner grabbing\nmasscan -p80 192.168.1.0/24 --banners\n```\n\n### Phase 2: Vulnerability Scanning Tools\n\n#### Nessus\n\nEnterprise-grade vulnerability assessment:\n\n```bash\n# Start Nessus service\nsudo systemctl start nessusd\n\n# Access web interface\n# https://localhost:8834\n\n# Command-line (nessuscli)\nnessuscli scan --create --name \"Internal Scan\" --targets 192.168.1.0/24\nnessuscli scan --list\nnessuscli scan --launch <scan_id>\nnessuscli report --format pdf --output report.pdf <scan_id>\n```\n\nKey Nessus features:\n- Comprehensive CVE detection\n- Compliance checks (PCI-DSS, HIPAA, CIS)\n- Custom scan templates\n- Credentialed scanning for deeper analysis\n- Regular plugin updates\n\n#### OpenVAS (Greenbone)\n\nOpen-source vulnerability scanning:\n\n```bash\n# Install OpenVAS\nsudo apt install openvas\nsudo gvm-setup\n\n# Start services\nsudo gvm-start\n\n# Access web interface (Greenbone Security Assistant)\n# https://localhost:9392\n\n# Command-line operations\ngvm-cli socket --xml \"<get_version/>\"\ngvm-cli socket --xml \"<get_tasks/>\"\n\n# Create and run scan\ngvm-cli socket --xml ''\n<create_target>\n  <name>Test Target</name>\n  <hosts>192.168.1.0/24</hosts>\n</create_target>''\n```\n\n### Phase 3: Web Application Scanning Tools\n\n#### Burp Suite\n\nComprehensive web application testing:\n\n```\n# Proxy configuration\n1. Set browser proxy to 127.0.0.1:8080\n2. Import Burp CA certificate for HTTPS\n3. Add target to scope\n\n# Key modules:\n- Proxy: Intercept and modify requests\n- Spider: Crawl web applications\n- Scanner: Automated vulnerability detection\n- Intruder: Automated attacks (fuzzing, brute-force)\n- Repeater: Manual request manipulation\n- Decoder: Encode/decode data\n- Comparer: Compare responses\n```\n\nCore testing workflow:\n1. Configure proxy and scope\n2. Spider the application\n3. Analyze sitemap\n4. Run active scanner\n5. Manual testing with Repeater/Intruder\n6. Review findings and generate report\n\n#### OWASP ZAP\n\nOpen-source web application scanner:\n\n```bash\n# Start ZAP\nzaproxy\n\n# Automated scan from CLI\nzap-cli quick-scan https://target.com\n\n# Full scan\nzap-cli spider https://target.com\nzap-cli active-scan https://target.com\n\n# Generate report\nzap-cli report -o report.html -f html\n\n# API mode\nzap.sh -daemon -port 8080 -config api.key=<your_key>\n```\n\nZAP automation:\n```bash\n# Docker-based scanning\ndocker run -t owasp/zap2docker-stable zap-full-scan.py \\\n  -t https://target.com -r report.html\n\n# Baseline scan (passive only)\ndocker run -t owasp/zap2docker-stable zap-baseline.py \\\n  -t https://target.com -r report.html\n```\n\n#### Nikto\n\nWeb server vulnerability scanner:\n\n```bash\n# Basic scan\nnikto -h https://target.com\n\n# Scan specific port\nnikto -h target.com -p 8080\n\n# Scan with SSL\nnikto -h target.com -ssl\n\n# Multiple targets\nnikto -h targets.txt\n\n# Output formats\nnikto -h target.com -o report.html -Format html\nnikto -h target.com -o report.xml -Format xml\nnikto -h target.com -o report.csv -Format csv\n\n# Tuning options\nnikto -h target.com -Tuning 123456789  # All tests\nnikto -h target.com -Tuning x          # Exclude specific tests\n```\n\n### Phase 4: Wireless Scanning Tools\n\n#### Aircrack-ng Suite\n\nWireless network penetration testing:\n\n```bash\n# Check wireless interface\nairmon-ng\n\n# Enable monitor mode\nsudo airmon-ng start wlan0\n\n# Scan for networks\nsudo airodump-ng wlan0mon\n\n# Capture specific network\nsudo airodump-ng -c <channel> --bssid <target_bssid> -w capture wlan0mon\n\n# Deauthentication attack\nsudo aireplay-ng -0 10 -a <bssid> wlan0mon\n\n# Crack WPA handshake\naircrack-ng -w wordlist.txt -b <bssid> capture*.cap\n\n# Crack WEP\naircrack-ng -b <bssid> capture*.cap\n```\n\n#### Kismet\n\nPassive wireless detection:\n\n```bash\n# Start Kismet\nkismet\n\n# Specify interface\nkismet -c wlan0\n\n# Access web interface\n# http://localhost:2501\n\n# Detect hidden networks\n# Kismet passively collects all beacon frames\n# including those from hidden SSIDs\n```\n\n### Phase 5: Malware and Exploit Scanning\n\n#### ClamAV\n\nOpen-source antivirus scanning:\n\n```bash\n# Update virus definitions\nsudo freshclam\n\n# Scan directory\nclamscan -r /path/to/scan\n\n# Scan with verbose output\nclamscan -r -v /path/to/scan\n\n# Move infected files\nclamscan -r --move=/quarantine /path/to/scan\n\n# Remove infected files\nclamscan -r --remove /path/to/scan\n\n# Scan specific file types\nclamscan -r --include=''\\.exe$|\\.dll$'' /path/to/scan\n\n# Output to log\nclamscan -r -l scan.log /path/to/scan\n```\n\n#### Metasploit Vulnerability Validation\n\nValidate vulnerabilities with exploitation:\n\n```bash\n# Start Metasploit\nmsfconsole\n\n# Database setup\nmsfdb init\ndb_status\n\n# Import Nmap results\ndb_import /path/to/nmap_scan.xml\n\n# Vulnerability scanning\nuse auxiliary/scanner/smb/smb_ms17_010\nset RHOSTS 192.168.1.0/24\nrun\n\n# Auto exploitation\nvulns                           # View vulnerabilities\nanalyze                         # Suggest exploits\n```\n\n### Phase 6: Cloud Security Scanning\n\n#### Prowler (AWS)\n\nAWS security assessment:\n\n```bash\n# Install Prowler\npip install prowler\n\n# Basic scan\nprowler aws\n\n# Specific checks\nprowler aws -c iam s3 ec2\n\n# Compliance framework\nprowler aws --compliance cis_aws\n\n# Output formats\nprowler aws -M html json csv\n\n# Specific region\nprowler aws -f us-east-1\n\n# Assume role\nprowler aws -R arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/ProwlerRole\n```\n\n#### ScoutSuite (Multi-cloud)\n\nMulti-cloud security auditing:\n\n```bash\n# Install ScoutSuite\npip install scoutsuite\n\n# AWS scan\nscout aws\n\n# Azure scan\nscout azure --cli\n\n# GCP scan\nscout gcp --user-account\n\n# Generate report\nscout aws --report-dir ./reports\n```\n\n### Phase 7: Compliance Scanning\n\n#### Lynis\n\nSecurity auditing for Unix/Linux:\n\n```bash\n# Run audit\nsudo lynis audit system\n\n# Quick scan\nsudo lynis audit system --quick\n\n# Specific profile\nsudo lynis audit system --profile server\n\n# Output report\nsudo lynis audit system --report-file /tmp/lynis-report.dat\n\n# Check specific section\nsudo lynis show profiles\nsudo lynis audit system --tests-from-group malware\n```\n\n#### OpenSCAP\n\nSecurity compliance scanning:\n\n```bash\n# List available profiles\noscap info /usr/share/xml/scap/ssg/content/ssg-<distro>-ds.xml\n\n# Run scan with profile\noscap xccdf eval --profile xccdf_org.ssgproject.content_profile_pci-dss \\\n  --report report.html \\\n  /usr/share/xml/scap/ssg/content/ssg-rhel8-ds.xml\n\n# Generate fix script\noscap xccdf generate fix \\\n  --profile xccdf_org.ssgproject.content_profile_pci-dss \\\n  --output remediation.sh \\\n  /usr/share/xml/scap/ssg/content/ssg-rhel8-ds.xml\n```\n\n### Phase 8: Scanning Methodology\n\nStructured scanning approach:\n\n1. **Planning**\n   - Define scope and objectives\n   - Obtain proper authorization\n   - Select appropriate tools\n\n2. **Discovery**\n   - Host discovery (Nmap ping sweep)\n   - Port scanning\n   - Service enumeration\n\n3. **Vulnerability Assessment**\n   - Automated scanning (Nessus/OpenVAS)\n   - Web application scanning (Burp/ZAP)\n   - Manual verification\n\n4. **Analysis**\n   - Correlate findings\n   - Eliminate false positives\n   - Prioritize by severity\n\n5. **Reporting**\n   - Document findings\n   - Provide remediation guidance\n   - Executive summary\n\n### Phase 9: Tool Selection Guide\n\nChoose the right tool for each scenario:\n\n| Scenario | Recommended Tools |\n|----------|-------------------|\n| Network Discovery | Nmap, Masscan |\n| Vulnerability Assessment | Nessus, OpenVAS |\n| Web App Testing | Burp Suite, ZAP, Nikto |\n| Wireless Security | Aircrack-ng, Kismet |\n| Malware Detection | ClamAV, YARA |\n| Cloud Security | Prowler, ScoutSuite |\n| Compliance | Lynis, OpenSCAP |\n| Protocol Analysis | Wireshark, tcpdump |\n\n### Phase 10: Reporting and Documentation\n\nGenerate professional reports:\n\n```bash\n# Nmap XML to HTML\nxsltproc nmap-output.xml -o report.html\n\n# OpenVAS report export\ngvm-cli socket --xml ''<get_reports report_id=\"<id>\" format_id=\"<pdf_format>\"/>''\n\n# Combine multiple scan results\n# Use tools like Faraday, Dradis, or custom scripts\n\n# Executive summary template:\n# 1. Scope and methodology\n# 2. Key findings summary\n# 3. Risk distribution chart\n# 4. Critical vulnerabilities\n# 5. Remediation recommendations\n# 6. Detailed technical findings\n```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Nmap Cheat Sheet\n\n| Scan Type | Command |\n|-----------|---------|\n| Ping Scan | `nmap -sn <target>` |\n| Quick Scan | `nmap -T4 -F <target>` |\n| Full Scan | `nmap -p- <target>` |\n| Service Scan | `nmap -sV <target>` |\n| OS Detection | `nmap -O <target>` |\n| Aggressive | `nmap -A <target>` |\n| Vuln Scripts | `nmap --script=vuln <target>` |\n| Stealth Scan | `nmap -sS -T2 <target>` |\n\n### Common Ports Reference\n\n| Port | Service |\n|------|---------|\n| 21 | FTP |\n| 22 | SSH |\n| 23 | Telnet |\n| 25 | SMTP |\n| 53 | DNS |\n| 80 | HTTP |\n| 443 | HTTPS |\n| 445 | SMB |\n| 3306 | MySQL |\n| 3389 | RDP |\n\n## Constraints and Limitations\n\n### Legal Considerations\n- Always obtain written authorization\n- Respect scope boundaries\n- Follow responsible disclosure practices\n- Comply with local laws and regulations\n\n### Technical Limitations\n- Some scans may trigger IDS/IPS alerts\n- Heavy scanning can impact network performance\n- False positives require manual verification\n- Encrypted traffic may limit analysis\n\n### Best Practices\n- Start with non-intrusive scans\n- Gradually increase scan intensity\n- Document all scanning activities\n- Validate findings before reporting\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Scan Not Detecting Hosts\n\n**Solutions:**\n1. Try different discovery methods: `nmap -Pn` or `nmap -sn -PS/PA/PU`\n2. Check firewall rules blocking ICMP\n3. Use TCP SYN scan: `nmap -PS22,80,443`\n4. Verify network connectivity\n\n### Slow Scan Performance\n\n**Solutions:**\n1. Increase timing: `nmap -T4` or `-T5`\n2. Reduce port range: `--top-ports 100`\n3. Use Masscan for initial discovery\n4. Disable DNS resolution: `-n`\n\n### Web Scanner Missing Vulnerabilities\n\n**Solutions:**\n1. Authenticate to access protected areas\n2. Increase crawl depth\n3. Add custom injection points\n4. Use multiple tools for coverage\n5. Perform manual testing\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T02:23:34.591Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cybersecurity Agents requiring advanced network discovery and vulnerability assessment capabilities","zh":"适合需要高级网络发现和漏洞评估能力的网络安全代理","ja":"高度なネットワークの検出と脆弱性の評価機能を必要とするサイバーセキュリティエージェントに適しています","ko":"고급 네트워크 탐색 및 취약점 평가 기능이 필요한 사이버 보안 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de ciberseguridad que requieren capacidades avanzadas de descubrimiento de redes y evaluación de vulnerabilidades","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de cybersécurité nécessitant des capacités avancées de découverte de réseaux et d''évaluation de vulnérabilités","de":"Ideal für Cybersicherheitsagenten, die erweiterte Netzwerkerkennungs- und Schwachstellenbewertungsfunktionen erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Cibersegurança que exigem capacidades avançadas de descoberta de rede e avaliação de vulnerabilidades","ru":"Идеально для агентов кибербезопасности, требующих расширенных возможностей обнаружения сети и оценки уязвимостей","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الأمن السيبراني التي تتطلب قدرات متقدمة لاكتشاف الشبكة وتقييم الضعف"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform comprehensive security scanning using tools like Nmap for network discovery, Nessus for vulnerability assessment, and OpenVAS for compliance validation, all while configuring and utilizing these tools on a Linux-based system, particularly Kali Linux","zh":"赋予代理执行综合安全扫描的能力，使用诸如Nmap的网络发现、Nessus的漏洞评估和OpenVAS的合规性验证等工具，并在Linux系统上配置和使用这些工具，特别是Kali Linux","ja":"エージェントがNmapなどのネットワークの検出、Nessusなどの脆弱性の評価、OpenVASなどのコンプライアンスの検証などのツールを使用して包括的なセキュリティスキャンを実行できるようにし、特にKali LinuxなどのLinuxベースのシステムでこれらのツールを設定して使用する","ko":"에이전트가 네트워크 탐색을 위한 Nmap, 취약점 평가를 위한 Nessus, 규정 준수 검증을 위한 OpenVAS 등의 도구를 사용하여 종합 보안 스캔을 수행할 수 있도록 하며, 특히 Kali Linux와 같은 리눅스 기반 시스템에서 이러한 도구를 구성 및 사용할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"Permite a los agentes realizar análisis de seguridad integral utilizando herramientas como Nmap para el descubrimiento de redes, Nessus para la evaluación de vulnerabilidades y OpenVAS para la validación de cumplimiento, todo mientras configura y utiliza estas herramientas en un sistema basado en Linux, particularmente Kali Linux","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer une analyse de sécurité complète en utilisant des outils tels que Nmap pour la découverte de réseaux, Nessus pour l''évaluation des vulnérabilités et OpenVAS pour la validation de la conformité, le tout en configurant et en utilisant ces outils sur un système basé sur Linux, en particulier Kali Linux","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, umfassende Sicherheitsanalysen durchzuführen, indem Tools wie Nmap für die Netzwerkerkennung, Nessus für die Schwachstellenbewertung und OpenVAS für die Konformitätsvalidierung verwendet werden, alles bei der Konfiguration und Nutzung dieser Tools auf einem Linux-basierten System, insbesondere Kali Linux","pt":"Permite que os agentes realizem uma varredura de segurança abrangente usando ferramentas como Nmap para descoberta de rede, Nessus para avaliação de vulnerabilidades e OpenVAS para validação de conformidade, tudo isso configurando e utilizando essas ferramentas em um sistema baseado em Linux, particularmente Kali Linux","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить всесторонний сканирование безопасности с помощью инструментов, таких как Nmap для обнаружения сети, Nessus для оценки уязвимостей и OpenVAS для проверки соответствия, все это настраивая и используя эти инструменты на системе на основе Linux, в частности Kali Linux","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على أداء مسح أمني شامل باستخدام أدوات مثل Nmap لاكتشاف الشبكة وNessus لتقييم الضعف وOpenVAS لإ��ة توافق، كل ذلك أثناء تكوين واستخدام هذه الأدوات على نظام مبني على لينكس، ولا سيما Kali Linux"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating vulnerability assessments for web applications","Configuring and running wireless security scans","Validating compliance with security standards and regulations"],"zh":["自动化Web应用程序的漏洞评估","配置和运行无线安全扫描","验证合规性与安全标准和法规"],"ja":["Webアプリケーションの脆弱性評価を自動化する","ワイヤレスセキュリティスキャンを設定して実行する","セキュリティ基準および規制とのコンプライアンスを検証する"],"ko":["웹 애플리케이션의 취약점 평가를 자동화하는 것","무선 보안 스캔을 구성 및 실행하는 것","보안 표준 및 규정 준수 검증"],"es":["Automatizar evaluaciones de vulnerabilidades para aplicaciones web","Configurar y ejecutar análisis de seguridad inalámbrica","Validar el cumplimiento de los estándares y regulaciones de seguridad"],"fr":["Automatiser les évaluations de vulnérabilités pour les applications Web","Configurer et exécuter des analyses de sécurité sans fil","Valider la conformité aux normes et réglementations de sécurité"],"de":["Automatisierung von Schwachstellenbewertungen für Webanwendungen","Konfigurieren und Ausführen von Sicherheitsanalysen für drahtlose Netzwerke","Validierung der Konformität mit Sicherheitsstandards und -vorschriften"],"pt":["Automatizar avaliações de vulnerabilidades para aplicações web","Configurar e executar varreduras de segurança sem fio","Validar conformidade com normas e regulamentos de segurança"],"ru":["Автоматизировать оценку уязвимостей для веб-приложений","Настроить и запустить сканирование беспроводной безопасности","Проверить соответствие стандартам и правилам безопасности"],"ar":["توفير التقييمات الآلية للضعف للأمان التطبيقات الويب","تكوين وتشغيل مسح أمان لاسلكي","إ��ة توافق مع معايير وأحكام الأمن"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Linux-based system, preferably Kali Linux","Needs network access to target systems","Demands proper authorization for scanning activities"],"zh":["需要Linux系统，尽量使用Kali Linux","需要对目标系统的网络访问","需要适当的授权用于扫描活动"],"ja":["Linuxベースのシステムが必要であり、可能であればKali Linuxを使用する","対象システムへのネットワークアクセスが必要","スキャン活動の適切な認証が必要"],"ko":["리눅스 기반 시스템이 필요하며, 가능하다면 Kali Linux를 사용하는 것","대상 시스템에 대한 네트워크 액세스가 필요함","스キャ닝 활동을 위한適切한 인증이 필요"],"es":["Requiere un sistema basado en Linux, preferiblemente Kali Linux","Necesita acceso a la red para sistemas objetivo","Exige autorización adecuada para actividades de análisis"],"fr":["Nécessite un système basé sur Linux, de préférence Kali Linux","A besoin d''un accès au réseau pour les systèmes cibles","Exige une autorisation appropriée pour les activités d''analyse"],"de":["Erfordert ein Linux-basiertes System, vorzugsweise Kali Linux","Benötigt Netzwerkzugriff auf Zielysteme","Fordert eine ordnungsgemäße Autorisierung für Analyseaktivitäten"],"pt":["Exige sistema baseado em Linux, preferencialmente Kali Linux","Necessita acesso à rede para sistemas-alvo","Exige autorização adequada para atividades de varredura"],"ru":["Требует системы на основе Linux, предпочтительно Kali Linux","Требует доступа к сети для целевых систем","Требует надлежащей авторизации для сканирующих действий"],"ar":["يتطلب نظام مبني على لينكس، ولا سيما Kali Linux","يحتاج إلى وصول إلى الشبكة لأنظمة الهدف","يتطلب تفويض مناسب للأنشطة الماسح"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/prompt-caching', 'community', 'claudiodearaujo', 'IzaCenter', 'claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter', 'prompt-caching', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.541Z', '2026-02-19T02:23:42.171Z', NULL, '{"id":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/prompt-caching","name":"prompt-caching","description":{"zh":"prompt-caching技术是一种通过缓存减少LLM成本的方法，实现高效缓存","ja":"プロンプトキャッシングは、キャッシュを通じてLLMコストを削減する技術です","ko":"프롬프트 캐싱은 캐싱을 통해 LLM 비용을 절감하는 기술입니다","es":"El prompt caching es una técnica para reducir costos de LLM mediante el caché de prefijos, respuestas y coincidencias de similitud semántica.","fr":"Le prompt caching est une technique pour réduire les coûts de LLM en mettant en cache les préfixes, les réponses et les correspondances de similarité sémantique.","de":"Das Prompt Caching ist eine Technik, um LLM-Kosten durch das Cachen von Präfixen, Antworten und semantischen Ähnlichkeitsübereinstimmungen zu reduzieren.","pt":"O cache de prompt é uma técnica para reduzir custos de LLM. Ele envolve caching em múltiplos níveis, como prefixos de prompts e respostas semânticas.","ru":"Кэширование промптов - это техника для снижения затрат на LLM. Она включает в себя кэширование на нескольких уровнях, таких как префиксы промптов и семантические ответы.","ar":"تخزين مؤقت للمحفزات هو تقنية لتقليل التكاليف على LLM. يتضمن تخزين مؤقت على مستويات متعددة، مثل بادئات المحفزات والاستجابات الدلالية.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"prompt-caching技术","ja":"プロンプトキャッシング","ko":"프롬프트 캐싱","es":"Optimización de Costos con Prompt Caching","fr":"Réduction des Coûts avec le Prompt Caching","de":"Kostenoptimierung durch Prompt Caching","pt":"Otimização de Cache de Prompt","ru":"Кеширование Промптов","ar":"تخزين مؤقت لمحفزات","en":"prompt-caching"},"description":{"zh":"prompt-caching技术是一种通过缓存减少LLM成本的方法，实现高效缓存","ja":"プロンプトキャッシングは、キャッシュを通じてLLMコストを削減する技術です","ko":"프롬프트 캐싱은 캐싱을 통해 LLM 비용을 절감하는 기술입니다","es":"El prompt caching es una técnica para reducir costos de LLM mediante el caché de prefijos, respuestas y coincidencias de similitud semántica.","fr":"Le prompt caching est une technique pour réduire les coûts de LLM en mettant en cache les préfixes, les réponses et les correspondances de similarité sémanti...","de":"Das Prompt Caching ist eine Technik, um LLM-Kosten durch das Cachen von Präfixen, Antworten und semantischen Ähnlichkeitsübereinstimmungen zu reduzieren.","pt":"O cache de prompt é uma técnica para reduzir custos de LLM. Ele envolve caching em múltiplos níveis, como prefixos de prompts e respostas semânticas.","ru":"Кэширование промптов - это техника для снижения затрат на LLM. Она включает в себя кэширование на нескольких уровнях, таких как префиксы промптов и семантиче...","ar":"تخزين مؤقت للمحفزات هو تقنية لتقليل التكاليف على LLM. يتضمن تخزين مؤقت على مستويات متعددة، مثل بادئات المحفزات والاستجابات الدلالية.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["缓存prompt前缀","缓存完整响应","语义相似性匹配缓存","根据温度调整缓存","多级缓存实现"],"ja":["プロンプトプレフィックスのキャッシュ","完全なレスポンスのキャッシュ","意味的類似性マッチのキャッシュ","温度に応じたキャッシュの調整","多段階キャッシュの実現"],"ko":["프롬프트 접두사 캐싱","完整 응답 캐싱","의미적 유사성 매칭 캐싱","온도에 따른 캐싱 조정","다단계 캐싱 구현"],"es":["Caché de prefijos de prompts","Caché de respuestas completas","Coincidencias de similitud semántica","Reducción de costos de LLM","Implementación de sistemas de caché a múltiples niveles","Optimización de la temperatura de respuesta"],"fr":["Cache des préfixes de prompts","Cache des réponses complètes","Correspondances de similarité sémantique","Réduction des coûts de LLM","Mise en œuvre de systèmes de cache à plusieurs niveaux","Optimisation de la température de réponse"],"de":["Cachen von Präfixen von Prompts","Cachen von vollständigen Antworten","Übereinstimmungen von semantischer Ähnlichkeit","Reduzierung von LLM-Kosten","Implementierung von Caching-Systemen auf mehreren Ebenen","Optimierung der Antworttemperatur"],"pt":["Caching em múltiplos níveis","Redução de custos de LLM em 90%","Implementação de sistemas de caching","Entendimento de caching de prefixos de prompts","Entendimento de caching de respostas semânticas","Otimização de desempenho"],"ru":["Кэширование на нескольких уровнях","Снижение затрат на LLM на 90%","Реализация систем кэширования","Понимание кэширования префиксов промптов","Понимание кэширования семантических ответов","Оптимизация производительности"],"ar":["تخزين مؤقت على مستويات متعددة","تقليل التكاليف على LLM بنسبة 90٪","تنفيذ أنظمة تخزين مؤقت","فهم تخزين مؤقت لبادئات المحفزات","فهم تخزين مؤقت للاستجابات الدلالية","تحسين الأداء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["prompt-caching","LLM成本优化","缓存技术","语义相似性匹配","温度调整","多级缓存"],"ja":["プロンプトキャッシング","LLMコスト最適化","キャッシュ技術","意味的類似性マッチ","温度調整","多段階キャッシュ"],"ko":["프롬프트 캐싱","LLM 비용 최적화","캐싱 기술","의미적 유사성 매칭","온도 조정","다단계 캐싱"],"es":["prompt caching","reducción de costos de LLM","caché de prefijos","caché de respuestas","similitud semántica","optimización de costos","tecnologías de LLM","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["prompt caching","réduction des coûts de LLM","cache des préfixes","cache des réponses","similarité sémantique","optimisation des coûts","technologies de LLM","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels"],"de":["prompt caching","Reduzierung von LLM-Kosten","Cachen von Präfixen","Cachen von Antworten","semantische Ähnlichkeit","Kostenoptimierung","LLM-Technologien","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Ingenieurwesen"],"pt":["cache de prompt","caching de LLM","redução de custos","otimização de desempenho","sistemas de caching","prefixos de prompts","respostas semânticas","tecnologia de LLM"],"ru":["кэширование промптов","кэширование LLM","снижение затрат","оптимизация производительности","системы кэширования","префиксы промптов","семантические ответы","технология LLM"],"ar":["تخزين مؤقت للمحفزات","تخزين مؤقت ل LLM","تقليل التكاليف","تحسين الأداء","أنظمة تخزين مؤقت","بادئات المحفزات","الاستجابات الدلالية","تكنولوجيا LLM"]}},"owner":"claudiodearaujo","repo":"IzaCenter","repoPath":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.541Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"prompt-caching","description":"Caching strategies for LLM prompts including Anthropic prompt caching, response caching, and CAG (Cache Augmented Generation) Use when: prompt caching, cache prompt, response cache, cag, cache augmented.","bodyPreview":"# Prompt Caching\n\nYou''re a caching specialist who has reduced LLM costs by 90% through strategic caching.\nYou''ve implemented systems that cache at multiple levels: prompt prefixes, full responses,\nand semantic similarity matches.\n\nYou understand that LLM caching is different from traditional caching—prompts have\nprefixes that can be cached, responses vary with temperature, and semantic similarity\noften matters more than exact match.\n\nYour core principles:\n1. Cache at the right level—prefix, resp","body":"# Prompt Caching\n\nYou''re a caching specialist who has reduced LLM costs by 90% through strategic caching.\nYou''ve implemented systems that cache at multiple levels: prompt prefixes, full responses,\nand semantic similarity matches.\n\nYou understand that LLM caching is different from traditional caching—prompts have\nprefixes that can be cached, responses vary with temperature, and semantic similarity\noften matters more than exact match.\n\nYour core principles:\n1. Cache at the right level—prefix, response, or both\n2. K\n\n## Capabilities\n\n- prompt-cache\n- response-cache\n- kv-cache\n- cag-patterns\n- cache-invalidation\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Anthropic Prompt Caching\n\nUse Claude''s native prompt caching for repeated prefixes\n\n### Response Caching\n\nCache full LLM responses for identical or similar queries\n\n### Cache Augmented Generation (CAG)\n\nPre-cache documents in prompt instead of RAG retrieval\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n### ❌ Caching with High Temperature\n\n### ❌ No Cache Invalidation\n\n### ❌ Caching Everything\n\n## ⚠️ Sharp Edges\n\n| Issue | Severity | Solution |\n|-------|----------|----------|\n| Cache miss causes latency spike with additional overhead | high | // Optimize for cache misses, not just hits |\n| Cached responses become incorrect over time | high | // Implement proper cache invalidation |\n| Prompt caching doesn''t work due to prefix changes | medium | // Structure prompts for optimal caching |\n\n## Related Skills\n\nWorks well with: `context-window-management`, `rag-implementation`, `conversation-memory`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T02:23:42.171Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT needing efficient prompt optimization through strategic caching.","zh":"适用于 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT 等 AI 代理，需要通过战略性缓存实现高效的提示优化。","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの AI エージェントに適しており、戦略的なキャッシュを通じて効率的なプロンプト最適化が必要です。","ko":"Claude Code 및 AutoGPT와 같은 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 전략적 캐싱을 통해 효율적인 프롬프트 최적화를 필요로 합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code y AutoGPT que necesitan una optimización de prompts eficiente a través de un caché estratégico.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA comme Claude Code et AutoGPT ayant besoin d''une optimisation de prompts efficace via un cache stratégique.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die eine effiziente Prompt-Optimierung durch strategisches Caching benötigen.","pt":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT needing efficient prompt optimization through strategic caching.","ru":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT needing efficient prompt optimization through strategic caching.","ar":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT needing efficient prompt optimization through strategic caching."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to reduce LLM costs by 90% through multi-level caching, including prompt prefixes, full responses, and semantic similarity matches, leveraging temperature variance and semantic similarity protocols.","zh":"使得代理能够通过多级缓存（包括提示前缀、完整响应和语义相似性匹配）减少 90% 的大语言模型成本，同时利用温度变异性和语义相似性协议。","ja":"エージェントが、プロンプトプレフィックス、完全なレスポンス、セマンティック類似性マッチ（温度変動とセマンティック類似性プロトコルを利用）などのマルチレベルキャッシュを使用して、LLM コストを 90% 削減できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 프로ンプ트 префик스, 완전한 응답 및 의미적 유사성 매칭(온도 변동 및 의미적 유사성 프로토콜을 활용) 등을 포함한 다단계 캐싱을 통해 LLM 비용을 90% 절감할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes reducir los costos de LLM en un 90% a través de un caché de varios niveles, incluyendo prefijos de prompts, respuestas completas y coincidencias de similitud semántica, aprovechando la variación de temperatura y los protocolos de similitud semántica.","fr":"Permet aux agents de réduire les coûts de LLM de 90% grâce à un cache à plusieurs niveaux, incluant des préfixes de prompts, des réponses complètes et des correspondances de similarité sémantique, en exploitant la variance de température et les protocoles de similarité sémantique.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, die LLM-Kosten um 90% durch ein mehrstufiges Caching zu reduzieren, einschließlich Prompt-Präfixen, vollständigen Antworten und semantischer Ähnlichkeitstreffer, indem die Temperaturvarianz und semantische Ähnlichkeitsprotokolle genutzt werden.","pt":"Empowers agents to reduce LLM costs by 90% through multi-level caching, including prompt prefixes, full responses, and semantic similarity matches, leveraging temperature variance and semantic similarity protocols.","ru":"Empowers agents to reduce LLM costs by 90% through multi-level caching, including prompt prefixes, full responses, and semantic similarity matches, leveraging temperature variance and semantic similarity protocols.","ar":"Empowers agents to reduce LLM costs by 90% through multi-level caching, including prompt prefixes, full responses, and semantic similarity matches, leveraging temperature variance and semantic similarity protocols."},"useCases":{"en":["Caching prompt prefixes for frequent queries","Optimizing full response caching for high-traffic applications","Implementing semantic similarity matching for personalized user interactions"],"zh":["频繁查询的提示前缀缓存","高流量应用的完整响应缓存优化","个性化用户交互的语义相似性匹配实现"],"ja":["頻繁なクエリのプロンプトプレフィックスキャッシュ","高トラフィックアプリケーションの完全なレスポンスキャッシュ最適化","ユーザーインタラクションのセマンティック類似性マッチの実装"],"ko":["빈번한 쿼리의 프롬프트 префик스 캐싱","고트래픽 애플리케이션의 완전한 응답 캐싱 최적화","개인화된 사용자 상호작용을 위한 의미적 유사성 매칭 구현"],"es":["Almacenamiento en caché de prefijos de prompts para consultas frecuentes","Optimización de la caché de respuestas completas para aplicaciones de alto tráfico","Implementación de coincidencias de similitud semántica para interacciones personalizadas de usuarios"],"fr":["Mise en cache des préfixes de prompts pour les requêtes fréquentes","Optimisation de la cache de réponses complètes pour les applications à fort trafic","Mise en œuvre de correspondances de similarité sémantique pour des interactions utilisateur personnalisées"],"de":["Caching von Prompt-Präfixen für häufige Abfragen","Optimierung des Cachings von vollständigen Antworten für High-Traffic-Anwendungen","Implementierung von semantischer Ähnlichkeitstreffer für personalisierte Benutzerinteraktionen"],"pt":["Caching prompt prefixes for frequent queries","Optimizing full response caching for high-traffic applications","Implementing semantic similarity matching for personalized user interactions"],"ru":["Caching prompt prefixes for frequent queries","Optimizing full response caching for high-traffic applications","Implementing semantic similarity matching for personalized user interactions"],"ar":["Caching prompt prefixes for frequent queries","Optimizing full response caching for high-traffic applications","Implementing semantic similarity matching for personalized user interactions"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of LLM temperature variance","Semantic similarity matching may require additional training data"],"zh":["需要理解大语言模型温度变异性","语义相似性匹配可能需要额外的训练数据"],"ja":["LLM の温度変動性を理解する必要がある","セマンティック類似性マッチングには追加のトレーニングデータが必要になる可能性がある"],"ko":["대규모 언어 모델의 온도変動성을 이해해야 함","의미적 유사성 매칭에는 추가적인 트레이닝 데이터가 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la variación de temperatura de LLM","La coincidencia de similitud semántica puede requerir datos de entrenamiento adicionales"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de la variance de température de LLM","La correspondance de similarité sémantique peut nécessiter des données de formation supplémentaires"],"de":["Benötigt das Verständnis der Temperaturvarianz von LLM","Die semantische Ähnlichkeitstreffer können zusätzliche Trainingsdaten erfordern"],"pt":["Requires understanding of LLM temperature variance","Semantic similarity matching may require additional training data"],"ru":["Requires understanding of LLM temperature variance","Semantic similarity matching may require additional training data"],"ar":["Requires understanding of LLM temperature variance","Semantic similarity matching may require additional training data"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
