ara principios de desarrollo y toma de decisiones en 2025. Aprende a pensar, no a memorizar patrones","fr":"Modèles Python pour les principes de développement et la prise de décision en 2025. Apprenez à réfléchir, pas à mémoriser des modèles","de":"Python-Muster für Entwicklungsprinzipien und Entscheidungsfindung in 2025. Lernen Sie, zu denken, nicht Muster auswendig zu lernen","pt":"Padrões Python para desenvolvimento de 2025, focando em princípios de decisão para um código mais eficaz.","ru":"Шаблоны Python для разработки 2025 года, ориентированные на принятие решений для более эффективного кода.","ar":"أنماط بايثون لتطوير 2025، تركز على مبادئ اتخاذ القرارات لكتابة كود أكثر فعالية.","en":"Extract codebase context for any LLM (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini) and safely apply AI-suggested patches with preview,"},"definition":{"en":"Extract codebase context for any LLM (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini) and safely apply AI-suggested patches with preview,"},"features":{"zh":["框架选择决策树","异步和同步编程的选择","不默认使用相同的框架","基于上下文的编程","安全地应用 AI 建议的补丁"],"ja":["フレームワーク選択の決断木","非同期と同期プログラミングの選択","同じフレームワークをデフォルトで使用しない","コンテキストに基づくプログラミング","AI の提案によるパッチを安全に適用"],"ko":["프레임워크 선택 결정 트리","비동기와 동기 프로그래밍의 선택","같은 프레임워크를 기본으로 사용하지 않음","컨텍스트에 기반한 프로그래밍","AI 제안에 의한 패치를 안전하게 적용"],"es":["Selección de framework basada en el contexto","Uso de programación asíncrona y síncrona","Toma de decisiones informadas en la codificación","Previsualización de parches sugeridos por IA","Compatibilidad con LLM como ChatGPT, Claude y Gemini"],"fr":["Sélection de framework basée sur le contexte","Utilisation de la programmation asynchrone et synchrone","Prise de décision éclairée dans la codification","Prévisualisation des correctifs suggérés par l''IA","Compatibilité avec les LLM comme ChatGPT, Claude et Gemini"],"de":["Framework-Auswahl basierend auf dem Kontext","Verwendung von asynchroner und synchroner Programmierung","Informierte Entscheidungsfindung bei der Codierung","Vorschau von von IA vorgeschlagenen Patches","Kompatibilität mit LLM wie ChatGPT, Claude und Gemini"],"pt":["Princípios de decisão para desenvolvimento Python","Escolha do framework certo para o projeto","Uso de async e sync com base no contexto","Evitar a repetição de padrões","Desenvolvimento de APIs e microserviços","Práticas de desenvolvimento para 2025"],"ru":["Принципы принятия решений для разработки на Python","Выбор правильного фреймворка для проекта","Использование async и sync на основе контекста","Избежание повторения шаблонов","Разработка API и микросервисов","Практики разработки для 2025 года"],"ar":["مبادئ اتخاذ القرارات لتطوير بايثون","اختيار الإطار الصحيح للمشروع","استخدام Async و Sync بالاعتماد على السياق","تجنب تكرار الأنماط","تطوير واجهات برمجة التطبيقات والميكروسيرفس","ممارسات التطوير لعام 2025"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Python 设计模式","Python 开发","Python 框架","异步编程","同步编程","AI 建议","代码质量","开发效率"],"ja":["Python パターン","Python 開発","Python フレームワーク","非同期プログラミング","同期プログラミング","AI の提案","コード品質","開発効率"],"ko":["파이썬 디자인 패턴","파이썬 개발","파이썬 프레임워크","비동기 프로그래밍","동기 프로그래밍","AI 제안","코드 품질","개발 효율성"],"es":["patrones de python","desarrollo de python","principios de codificación","toma de decisiones","programación asíncrona","programación síncrona","IA en la codificación","LLM","ChatGPT","Claude","Gemini"],"fr":["modèles python","développement python","principes de codage","prise de décision","programmation asynchrone","programmation synchrone","IA dans la codification","LLM","ChatGPT","Claude","Gemini"],"de":["python-muster","python-entwicklung","codierungsprinzipien","entscheidungsfindung","asynchrone programmierung","synchrone programmierung","KI in der codierung","LLM","ChatGPT","Claude","Gemini"],"pt":["desenvolvimento python","padrões python","princípios de decisão","framework python","async e sync","desenvolvimento de apis","microserviços","práticas de desenvolvimento","python 2025"],"ru":["разработка на python","шаблоны python","принципы принятия решений","фреймворк python","async и sync","разработка api","микросервисы","практики разработки","python 2025"],"ar":["تطوير بايثون","أنماط بايثون","مبادئ اتخاذ القرارات","إطار بايثون","async و sync","تطوير واجهات برمجة التطبيقات","الميكروسيرفس","ممارسات التطوير","بايثون 2025"]}},"owner":"HaoNgo232","repo":"Synapse-Desktop","repoPath":"HaoNgo232/Synapse-Desktop","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.540Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"python-patterns","description":"Python development principles and decision-making. Framework selection, async patterns, type hints, project structure. Teaches thinking, not copying.","bodyPreview":"# Python Patterns\n\n> Python development principles and decision-making for 2025.\n> **Learn to THINK, not memorize patterns.**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ How to Use This Skill\n\nThis skill teaches **decision-making principles**, not fixed code to copy.\n\n- ASK user for framework preference when unclear\n- Choose async vs sync based on CONTEXT\n- Don''t default to same framework every time\n\n---\n\n## 1. Framework Selection (2025)\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nWhat are you building?\n│\n├── API-first / Microservices\n│   └── Fas","body":"# Python Patterns\n\n> Python development principles and decision-making for 2025.\n> **Learn to THINK, not memorize patterns.**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ How to Use This Skill\n\nThis skill teaches **decision-making principles**, not fixed code to copy.\n\n- ASK user for framework preference when unclear\n- Choose async vs sync based on CONTEXT\n- Don''t default to same framework every time\n\n---\n\n## 1. Framework Selection (2025)\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nWhat are you building?\n│\n├── API-first / Microservices\n│   └── FastAPI (async, modern, fast)\n│\n├── Full-stack web / CMS / Admin\n│   └── Django (batteries-included)\n│\n├── Simple / Script / Learning\n│   └── Flask (minimal, flexible)\n│\n├── AI/ML API serving\n│   └── FastAPI (Pydantic, async, uvicorn)\n│\n└── Background workers\n    └── Celery + any framework\n```\n\n### Comparison Principles\n\n| Factor | FastAPI | Django | Flask |\n|--------|---------|--------|-------|\n| **Best for** | APIs, microservices | Full-stack, CMS | Simple, learning |\n| **Async** | Native | Django 5.0+ | Via extensions |\n| **Admin** | Manual | Built-in | Via extensions |\n| **ORM** | Choose your own | Django ORM | Choose your own |\n| **Learning curve** | Low | Medium | Low |\n\n### Selection Questions to Ask:\n1. Is this API-only or full-stack?\n2. Need admin interface?\n3. Team familiar with async?\n4. Existing infrastructure?\n\n---\n\n## 2. Async vs Sync Decision\n\n### When to Use Async\n\n```\nasync def is better when:\n├── I/O-bound operations (database, HTTP, file)\n├── Many concurrent connections\n├── Real-time features\n├── Microservices communication\n└── FastAPI/Starlette/Django ASGI\n\ndef (sync) is better when:\n├── CPU-bound operations\n├── Simple scripts\n├── Legacy codebase\n├── Team unfamiliar with async\n└── Blocking libraries (no async version)\n```\n\n### The Golden Rule\n\n```\nI/O-bound → async (waiting for external)\nCPU-bound → sync + multiprocessing (computing)\n\nDon''t:\n├── Mix sync and async carelessly\n├── Use sync libraries in async code\n└── Force async for CPU work\n```\n\n### Async Library Selection\n\n| Need | Async Library |\n|------|---------------|\n| HTTP client | httpx |\n| PostgreSQL | asyncpg |\n| Redis | aioredis / redis-py async |\n| File I/O | aiofiles |\n| Database ORM | SQLAlchemy 2.0 async, Tortoise |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Type Hints Strategy\n\n### When to Type\n\n```\nAlways type:\n├── Function parameters\n├── Return types\n├── Class attributes\n├── Public APIs\n\nCan skip:\n├── Local variables (let inference work)\n├── One-off scripts\n├── Tests (usually)\n```\n\n### Common Type Patterns\n\n```python\n# These are patterns, understand them:\n\n# Optional → might be None\nfrom typing import Optional\ndef find_user(id: int) -> Optional[User]: ...\n\n# Union → one of multiple types\ndef process(data: str | dict) -> None: ...\n\n# Generic collections\ndef get_items() -> list[Item]: ...\ndef get_mapping() -> dict[str, int]: ...\n\n# Callable\nfrom typing import Callable\ndef apply(fn: Callable[[int], str]) -> str: ...\n```\n\n### Pydantic for Validation\n\n```\nWhen to use Pydantic:\n├── API request/response models\n├── Configuration/settings\n├── Data validation\n├── Serialization\n\nBenefits:\n├── Runtime validation\n├── Auto-generated JSON schema\n├── Works with FastAPI natively\n└── Clear error messages\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Project Structure Principles\n\n### Structure Selection\n\n```\nSmall project / Script:\n├── main.py\n├── utils.py\n└── requirements.txt\n\nMedium API:\n├── app/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── main.py\n│   ├── models/\n│   ├── routes/\n│   ├── services/\n│   └── schemas/\n├── tests/\n└── pyproject.toml\n\nLarge application:\n├── src/\n│   └── myapp/\n│       ├── core/\n│       ├── api/\n│       ├── services/\n│       ├── models/\n│       └── ...\n├── tests/\n└── pyproject.toml\n```\n\n### FastAPI Structure Principles\n\n```\nOrganize by feature or layer:\n\nBy layer:\n├── routes/ (API endpoints)\n├── services/ (business logic)\n├── models/ (database models)\n├── schemas/ (Pydantic models)\n└── dependencies/ (shared deps)\n\nBy feature:\n├── users/\n│   ├── routes.py\n│   ├── service.py\n│   └── schemas.py\n└── products/\n    └── ...\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Django Principles (2025)\n\n### Django Async (Django 5.0+)\n\n```\nDjango supports async:\n├── Async views\n├── Async middleware\n├── Async ORM (limited)\n└── ASGI deployment\n\nWhen to use async in Django:\n├── External API calls\n├── WebSocket (Channels)\n├── High-concurrency views\n└── Background task triggering\n```\n\n### Django Best Practices\n\n```\nModel design:\n├── Fat models, thin views\n├── Use managers for common queries\n├── Abstract base classes for shared fields\n\nViews:\n├── Class-based for complex CRUD\n├── Function-based for simple endpoints\n├── Use viewsets with DRF\n\nQueries:\n├── select_related() for FKs\n├── prefetch_related() for M2M\n├── Avoid N+1 queries\n└── Use .only() for specific fields\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. FastAPI Principles\n\n### async def vs def in FastAPI\n\n```\nUse async def when:\n├── Using async database drivers\n├── Making async HTTP calls\n├── I/O-bound operations\n└── Want to handle concurrency\n\nUse def when:\n├── Blocking operations\n├── Sync database drivers\n├── CPU-bound work\n└── FastAPI runs in threadpool automatically\n```\n\n### Dependency Injection\n\n```\nUse dependencies for:\n├── Database sessions\n├── Current user / Auth\n├── Configuration\n├── Shared resources\n\nBenefits:\n├── Testability (mock dependencies)\n├── Clean separation\n├── Automatic cleanup (yield)\n```\n\n### Pydantic v2 Integration\n\n```python\n# FastAPI + Pydantic are tightly integrated:\n\n# Request validation\n@app.post(\"/users\")\nasync def create(user: UserCreate) -> UserResponse:\n    # user is already validated\n    ...\n\n# Response serialization\n# Return type becomes response schema\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Background Tasks\n\n### Selection Guide\n\n| Solution | Best For |\n|----------|----------|\n| **BackgroundTasks** | Simple, in-process tasks |\n| **Celery** | Distributed, complex workflows |\n| **ARQ** | Async, Redis-based |\n| **RQ** | Simple Redis queue |\n| **Dramatiq** | Actor-based, simpler than Celery |\n\n### When to Use Each\n\n```\nFastAPI BackgroundTasks:\n├── Quick operations\n├── No persistence needed\n├── Fire-and-forget\n└── Same process\n\nCelery/ARQ:\n├── Long-running tasks\n├── Need retry logic\n├── Distributed workers\n├── Persistent queue\n└── Complex workflows\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Error Handling Principles\n\n### Exception Strategy\n\n```\nIn FastAPI:\n├── Create custom exception classes\n├── Register exception handlers\n├── Return consistent error format\n└── Log without exposing internals\n\nPattern:\n├── Raise domain exceptions in services\n├── Catch and transform in handlers\n└── Client gets clean error response\n```\n\n### Error Response Philosophy\n\n```\nInclude:\n├── Error code (programmatic)\n├── Message (human readable)\n├── Details (field-level when applicable)\n└── NOT stack traces (security)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Testing Principles\n\n### Testing Strategy\n\n| Type | Purpose | Tools |\n|------|---------|-------|\n| **Unit** | Business logic | pytest |\n| **Integration** | API endpoints | pytest + httpx/TestClient |\n| **E2E** | Full workflows | pytest + DB |\n\n### Async Testing\n\n```python\n# Use pytest-asyncio for async tests\n\nimport pytest\nfrom httpx import AsyncClient\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_endpoint():\n    async with AsyncClient(app=app, base_url=\"http://test\") as client:\n        response = await client.get(\"/users\")\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n```\n\n### Fixtures Strategy\n\n```\nCommon fixtures:\n├── db_session → Database connection\n├── client → Test client\n├── authenticated_user → User with token\n└── sample_data → Test data setup\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. Decision Checklist\n\nBefore implementing:\n\n- [ ] **Asked user about framework preference?**\n- [ ] **Chosen framework for THIS context?** (not just default)\n- [ ] **Decided async vs sync?**\n- [ ] **Planned type hint strategy?**\n- [ ] **Defined project structure?**\n- [ ] **Planned error handling?**\n- [ ] **Considered background tasks?**\n\n---\n\n## 11. Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n### ❌ DON''T:\n- Default to Django for simple APIs (FastAPI may be better)\n- Use sync libraries in async code\n- Skip type hints for public APIs\n- Put business logic in routes/views\n- Ignore N+1 queries\n- Mix async and sync carelessly\n\n### ✅ DO:\n- Choose framework based on context\n- Ask about async requirements\n- Use Pydantic for validation\n- Separate concerns (routes → services → repos)\n- Test critical paths\n\n---\n\n> **Remember**: Python patterns are about decision-making for YOUR specific context. Don''t copy code—think about what serves your application best.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T01:59:31.632Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Python Analysis Agents needing advanced codebase context extraction and AI-suggested patch application capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级代码库上下文提取和 AI 建议修复应用能力的 Python 分析代理。","ja":"Python 分析エージェントが高度なコードベースコンテキスト抽出と AI によるパッチ適用機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 코드베이스 컨텍스트 추출 및 AI 제안 패치 적용 기능이 필요한 Python 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de Python que necesitan una extracción avanzada de contexto de código y capacidades de aplicación de parches sugeridos por IA.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse Python ayant besoin d''une extraction avancée de contexte de code et de capacités d''application de correctifs suggérés par l''IA.","de":"Perfekt für Python-Analyseagenten, die eine erweiterte Codebasis-Kontextextraktion und AI-vorgeschlagene Patchanwendungsfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise Python que necessitam de extração avançada de contexto de código e capacidades de aplicação de patches sugeridos por IA.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа Python, которым необходима расширенная экстракция контекста кодовой базы и возможности применения патчей, предложенных ИИ.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل بايثون الذي يحتاج إلى استخراج متقدم لسياق قاعدة الشفرة والقدرات المقترحة من قبل تطبيق التصحيح الاصطناعي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to extract codebase context for any LLM and safely apply AI-suggested patches with preview, leveraging decision-making principles and framework selection based on context, including async vs sync choices and API-first/microservices architecture considerations.","zh":"赋予代理从任何大型语言模型中提取代码库上下文的能力，并安全地应用 AI 建议的修复，利用基于上下文的决策原则和框架选择，包括异步与同步选择以及 API 首先/微服务架构考虑因素。","ja":"エージェントに、プレビューを使用して安全に AI によるパッチを適用し、コンテキストに基づいて意思決定原則とフレームワークの選択を行う機能を提供します。包括 async vs sync の選択と API ファースト/マイクロサービス アーキテクチャの考慮。","ko":"에이전트가 모든 대형 언어 모델에서 코드베이스 컨텍스트를 추출하고 미리 보기를 사용하여 안전하게 AI 제안 패치를 적용할 수 있는 기능을 제공합니다. 컨텍스트 기반 의사 결정 원칙과 프레임워크 선택을 활용하여 비동기 대 동기 선택 및 API 우선/마이크로 서비스 아키텍처 고려를 포함합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a extraer el contexto de la base de código para cualquier LLM y aplicar de forma segura parches sugeridos por la IA con vista previa, aprovechando los principios de toma de decisiones y la selección de marcos basada en el contexto, incluidas las opciones asíncronas vs síncronas y consideraciones de arquitectura de API-first/microservicios.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''extraire le contexte de la base de code pour tout LLM et d''appliquer en toute sécurité des correctifs suggérés par l''IA avec aperçu, en exploitant les principes de prise de décision et la sélection de frameworks basée sur le contexte, y compris les choix async vs sync et les considérations d''architecture API-first/microservices.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, den Kontext der Codebasis für jedes LLM zu extrahieren und vorgeschlagene Patches der künstlichen Intelligenz sicher mit Vorschau anzuwenden, indem Entscheidungsprinzipien und Framework-Auswahl basierend auf dem Kontext genutzt werden, einschließlich asynchroner vs synchroner Auswahlmöglichkeiten und Überlegungen zur API-First/Mikrodienstarchitektur.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a extrair o contexto da base de código para qualquer LLM e aplicar patches sugeridos por IA com pré-visualização, aproveitando princípios de tomada de decisão e seleção de estrutura com base no contexto, incluindo escolhas assíncronas vs síncronas e considerações de arquitetura de API-first/microservices.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью извлекать контекст кодовой базы для любого LLM и безопасно применять патчи, предложенные ИИ, с предварительным просмотром, используя принципы принятия решений и выбор框ворка на основе контекста, включая асинхронные и синхронные выборы, а также учет архитектур API-first/microservices.","ar":"تمكين العميل من استخراج سياق قاعدة الشفرة لأي LLM وتطبيق التصحيحات المقترحة من قبل الاصطناعي مع معاينة مسبقة، واستخدام مبادئ اتخاذ القرارات واختيار الإطار بناءً على السياق، بما في ذلك الخيارات غير المتزامنة مقابل المتزامنة واعتبارات هندسة أولويات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات /_microservices."},"useCases":{"en":["Extracting codebase context for large-scale Python projects","Applying AI-suggested patches with preview for safer code updates","Selecting optimal frameworks for API-first and microservices-based applications"],"zh":["为大规模 Python 项目提取代码库上下文","使用预览安全地应用 AI 建议的修复","为 API 首先和基于微服务的应用程序选择最佳框架"],"ja":["大規模 Python プロジェクトのコードベース コンテキストの抽出","プレビューを使用して安全に AI によるパッチを適用","API ファーストおよびマイクロサービス ベースのアプリケーションに最適なフレームワークを選択"],"ko":["대규모 Python 프로젝트의 코드베이스 컨텍스트 추출","미리 보기를 사용하여 안전하게 AI 제안 패치 적용","API 우선 및 마이크로 서비스 기반 애플리케이션을 위한 최적의 프레임워크 선택"],"es":["Extracción de contexto de código para proyectos Python a gran escala","Aplicación de parches sugeridos por la IA con vista previa para actualizaciones de código más seguras","Selección de frameworks óptimos para aplicaciones basadas en API-first y microservicios"],"fr":["Extraction du contexte de code pour les projets Python à grande échelle","Application de correctifs suggérés par l''IA avec aperçu pour des mises à jour de code plus sûres","Sélection de frameworks optimaux pour les applications basées sur API-first et microservices"],"de":["Extraktion von Codekontext für große Python-Projekte","Anwenden von AI-vorgeschlagenen Patches mit Vorschau für sicherere Code-Updates","Auswahl optimaler Frameworks für API-First- und Mikrodienst-basierte Anwendungen"],"pt":["Extração de contexto de base de código para projetos Python em larga escala","Aplicação de patches sugeridos por IA com pré-visualização para atualizações de código mais seguras","Seleção de estruturas óptimas para aplicações baseadas em API-first e microservices"],"ru":["Извлечение контекста кодовой базы для крупномасштабных проектов Python","Применение патчей, предложенных ИИ, с предварительным просмотром для более безопасных обновлений кода","Выбор оптимальных фреймворков для приложений, основанных на API-first и микросервисах"],"ar":["استخراج سياق قاعدة الشفرة لمشاريع بايثون على نطاق واسع","تطبيق التصحيحات المقترحة من قبل الاصطناعي مع معاينة مسبقة لتحديثات الشفرة الأكثر أمانًا","اختيار الإطارات المثالية للتطبيقات القائمة على الأولوية لبرمجة التطبيقات /microservices"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python expertise for effective use","Limited to Python development principles and decision-making"],"zh":["需要 Python 전문 지식才能有效地 사용","仅限于 Python 开发原则和决策"],"ja":["有効に使用するには Python の専門知識が必要","Python 開発の原則と意思決定に限定される"],"ko":["유효하게 사용하려면 Python 전문 지식이 필요함","Python 개발 원칙 및 의사 결정에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere experiencia en Python para un uso efectivo","Limitado a principios de desarrollo de Python y toma de decisiones"],"fr":["Nécessite une expertise Python pour une utilisation efficace","Limité aux principes de développement Python et à la prise de décision"],"de":["Erfordert Python-Expertenwissen für einen effektiven Einsatz","Begrenzt auf Python-Entwicklungsprinzipien und Entscheidungsfindung"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento de Python para uso eficaz","Limitado a princípios de desenvolvimento Python e tomada de decisão"],"ru":["Требует знания Python для эффективного использования","Ограничен принципами разработки Python и принятием решений"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بايثون للاستخدام الفعال","محدود بمبادئ تطوير بايثون وعمليات اتخاذ القرارات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
