에 검증을 수행해야 한다는 개발 원칙입니다","es":"La verificación antes de finalizar es un principio fundamental que garantiza la honestidad y eficiencia en el desarrollo","fr":"La vérification avant achèvement est un principe fondamental qui garantit l''honnêteté et l''efficacité dans le développement","de":"Die Verifizierung vor Abschluss ist ein grundlegendes Prinzip, das die Ehrlichkeit und Effizienz in der Entwicklung gewährleistet","pt":"A verificação antes da conclusão é um princípio fundamental para garantir a eficiência e a honestidade no desenvolvimento.","ru":"Верификация до завершения является фундаментальным принципом для обеспечения эффективности и честности в разработке.","ar":"التحقق قبل الإكمال هو مبدأ أساسي لضمان الكفاءة والنزاهة في التطوير.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["验证前完成原则","验证证据的重要性","开发工作的质量保证","提高开发效率","减少错误率"],"ja":["完了前の検証原則","検証証拠の重要性","開発作業の品質保証","開発効率の向上","エラー率の削減"],"ko":["완료 전 검증 원칙","검증 증거의 중요성","개발작업의 품질 보증","개발 효율성 향상","오류율 감소"],"es":["Principio fundamental de honestidad y eficiencia","Requerimiento de evidencia fresca para la verificación","No se permite la reclamación de finalización sin verificación","Proceso de comprobación de evidencia antes de la finalización","Garantía de calidad y precisión en el desarrollo"],"fr":["Principe fondamental d''honnêteté et d''efficacité","Exigence de preuves fraîches pour la vérification","Interdiction de réclamer l''achèvement sans vérification","Processus de vérification des preuves avant l''achèvement","Garantie de qualité et de précision dans le développement"],"de":["Grundlegendes Prinzip von Ehrlichkeit und Effizienz","Anforderung von frischen Beweisen für die Verifizierung","Keine Abschlussbekundung ohne Verifizierung","Prozess der Überprüfung von Beweisen vor dem Abschluss","Gewährleistung von Qualität und Genauigkeit in der Entwicklung"],"pt":["Garantia de eficiência","Prevenção de erros","Melhoria da qualidade","Transparência no desenvolvimento","Cumprimento dos padrões"],"ru":["Гарантия эффективности","Предотвращение ошибок","Улучшение качества","Прозрачность разработки","Соблюдение стандартов"],"ar":["ضمان الكفاءة","منع الأخطاء","تحسين الجودة","الشفافية في التطوير","الامتثال للمعايير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["验证前完成","开发原则","验证证据","质量保证","开发效率","错误率"],"ja":["完了前の検証","開発原則","検証証拠","品質保証","開発効率","エラー率"],"ko":["완료 전 검증","개발 원칙","검증 증거","품질 보증","개발 효율성","오류율"],"es":["verificación antes de finalizar","principio fundamental","desarrollo de software","eficiencia y honestidad","evidencia fresca","calidad y precisión"],"fr":["vérification avant achèvement","principe fondamental","développement de logiciels","efficacité et honnêteté","preuves fraîches","qualité et précision"],"de":["Verifizierung vor Abschluss","grundlegendes Prinzip","Softwareentwicklung","Effizienz und Ehrlichkeit","frische Beweise","Qualität und Genauigkeit"],"pt":["verificação antes da conclusão","desenvolvimento de software","eficiência","qualidade","transparência","padrões de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["верификация до завершения","разработка программного обеспечения","эффективность","качество","прозрачность","стандарты разработки"],"ar":["التحقق قبل الإكمال","تطوير البرمجيات","الكفاءة","الجودة","الشفافية","معايير التطوير"]}},"owner":"KyteApp","repo":"growth-agents-and-skills","repoPath":"KyteApp/growth-agents-and-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"verification-before-completion","description":"Use when about to claim work is complete, fixed, or passing, before committing or creating PRs - requires running verification commands and confirming output before making any success claims; evidence before assertions always","bodyPreview":"# Verification Before Completion\n\n## Overview\n\nClaiming work is complete without verification is dishonesty, not efficiency.\n\n**Core principle:** Evidence before claims, always.\n\n**Violating the letter of this rule is violating the spirit of this rule.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO COMPLETION CLAIMS WITHOUT FRESH VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n```\n\nIf you haven''t run the verification command in this message, you cannot claim it passes.\n\n## The Gate Function\n\n```\nBEFORE claiming any status or expressing sati","body":"# Verification Before Completion\n\n## Overview\n\nClaiming work is complete without verification is dishonesty, not efficiency.\n\n**Core principle:** Evidence before claims, always.\n\n**Violating the letter of this rule is violating the spirit of this rule.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO COMPLETION CLAIMS WITHOUT FRESH VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n```\n\nIf you haven''t run the verification command in this message, you cannot claim it passes.\n\n## The Gate Function\n\n```\nBEFORE claiming any status or expressing satisfaction:\n\n1. IDENTIFY: What command proves this claim?\n2. RUN: Execute the FULL command (fresh, complete)\n3. READ: Full output, check exit code, count failures\n4. VERIFY: Does output confirm the claim?\n   - If NO: State actual status with evidence\n   - If YES: State claim WITH evidence\n5. ONLY THEN: Make the claim\n\nSkip any step = lying, not verifying\n```\n\n## Common Failures\n\n| Claim | Requires | Not Sufficient |\n|-------|----------|----------------|\n| Tests pass | Test command output: 0 failures | Previous run, \"should pass\" |\n| Linter clean | Linter output: 0 errors | Partial check, extrapolation |\n| Build succeeds | Build command: exit 0 | Linter passing, logs look good |\n| Bug fixed | Test original symptom: passes | Code changed, assumed fixed |\n| Regression test works | Red-green cycle verified | Test passes once |\n| Agent completed | VCS diff shows changes | Agent reports \"success\" |\n| Requirements met | Line-by-line checklist | Tests passing |\n\n## Red Flags - STOP\n\n- Using \"should\", \"probably\", \"seems to\"\n- Expressing satisfaction before verification (\"Great!\", \"Perfect!\", \"Done!\", etc.)\n- About to commit/push/PR without verification\n- Trusting agent success reports\n- Relying on partial verification\n- Thinking \"just this once\"\n- Tired and wanting work over\n- **ANY wording implying success without having run verification**\n\n## Rationalization Prevention\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Should work now\" | RUN the verification |\n| \"I''m confident\" | Confidence ≠ evidence |\n| \"Just this once\" | No exceptions |\n| \"Linter passed\" | Linter ≠ compiler |\n| \"Agent said success\" | Verify independently |\n| \"I''m tired\" | Exhaustion ≠ excuse |\n| \"Partial check is enough\" | Partial proves nothing |\n| \"Different words so rule doesn''t apply\" | Spirit over letter |\n\n## Key Patterns\n\n**Tests:**\n```\n✅ [Run test command] [See: 34/34 pass] \"All tests pass\"\n❌ \"Should pass now\" / \"Looks correct\"\n```\n\n**Regression tests (TDD Red-Green):**\n```\n✅ Write → Run (pass) → Revert fix → Run (MUST FAIL) → Restore → Run (pass)\n❌ \"I''ve written a regression test\" (without red-green verification)\n```\n\n**Build:**\n```\n✅ [Run build] [See: exit 0] \"Build passes\"\n❌ \"Linter passed\" (linter doesn''t check compilation)\n```\n\n**Requirements:**\n```\n✅ Re-read plan → Create checklist → Verify each → Report gaps or completion\n❌ \"Tests pass, phase complete\"\n```\n\n**Agent delegation:**\n```\n✅ Agent reports success → Check VCS diff → Verify changes → Report actual state\n❌ Trust agent report\n```\n\n## Why This Matters\n\nFrom 24 failure memories:\n- your human partner said \"I don''t believe you\" - trust broken\n- Undefined functions shipped - would crash\n- Missing requirements shipped - incomplete features\n- Time wasted on false completion → redirect → rework\n- Violates: \"Honesty is a core value. If you lie, you''ll be replaced.\"\n\n## When To Apply\n\n**ALWAYS before:**\n- ANY variation of success/completion claims\n- ANY expression of satisfaction\n- ANY positive statement about work state\n- Committing, PR creation, task completion\n- Moving to next task\n- Delegating to agents\n\n**Rule applies to:**\n- Exact phrases\n- Paraphrases and synonyms\n- Implications of success\n- ANY communication suggesting completion/correctness\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\n**No shortcuts for verification.**\n\nRun the command. Read the output. THEN claim the result.\n\nThis is non-negotiable.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T07:02:09.997Z","qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('nicanac/familly-journal/brainstorming', 'community', 'nicanac', 'familly-journal', 'nicanac/familly-journal', 'brainstorming', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z', '2026-02-19T07:17:37.443Z', NULL, '{"id":"nicanac/familly-journal/brainstorming","name":"brainstorming","description":{"es":"El brainstorming es una técnica para generar ideas y convertirlas en diseños completos","fr":"Le brainstorming est une technique pour générer des idées et les convertir en conceptions complètes","de":"Brainstorming ist eine Technik, um Ideen zu generieren und in vollständige Designs umzuwandeln","pt":"O brainstorming é um processo que ajuda a transformar ideias em designs completos","ru":"Мозговой штурм - это процесс, помогающий превратить идеи в полноценные дизайны","ar":"التخيل هو عملية تساعد على تحويل الأفكار إلى تصميمات كاملة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Generación de ideas con brainstorming","fr":"Génération d''idées avec brainstorming","de":"Ideen generieren mit Brainstorming","pt":"Brainstorming: Desenvolvimento de Ideias em Design","ru":"Мозговой штурм: разработка идей в дизайн","ar":"التخيل: تحويل الأفكار إلى تصميمات","en":"brainstorming"},"description":{"es":"El brainstorming es una técnica para generar ideas y convertirlas en diseños completos","fr":"Le brainstorming est une technique pour générer des idées et les convertir en conceptions complètes","de":"Brainstorming ist eine Technik, um Ideen zu generieren und in vollständige Designs umzuwandeln","pt":"O brainstorming é um processo que ajuda a transformar ideias em designs completos","ru":"Мозговой штурм - это процесс, помогающий превратить идеи в полноценные дизайны","ar":"التخيل هو عملية تساعد على تحويل الأفكار إلى تصميمات كاملة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"es":["Generación de ideas a través del diálogo","Desarrollo de diseños completos","Colaboración en tiempo real","Refinamiento de ideas","Presentación de diseños en secciones"],"fr":["Génération d''idées à travers le dialogue","Développement de conceptions complètes","Collaboration en temps réel","Affinement des idées","Présentation des conceptions en sections"],"de":["Ideen generieren durch den Dialog","Entwicklung von vollständigen Designs","Zusammenarbeit in Echtzeit","Verfeinerung von Ideen","Präsentation von Designs in Abschnitten"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de ideias em designs","Diálogo colaborativo natural","Refinamento de ideias através de perguntas","Apresentação de designs em seções","Verificação de designs após cada seção"],"ru":["Разработка идей в дизайны","Естественный коллаборативный диалог","Уточнение идей через вопросы","Презентация дизайнов в разделах","Проверка дизайнов после каждого раздела"],"ar":["تطوير الأفكار في تصميمات","حوار تعاوني طبيعي","تحسين الأفكار من خلال أسئلة","عرض التصميمات في أقسام","التحقق من التصميمات بعد كل قسم"]},"keywords":{"es":["brainstorming","generación de ideas","diseño colaborativo","desarrollo de productos","innovación","colaboración en equipo"],"fr":["brainstorming","génération d''idées","conception collaborative","développement de produits","innovation","collaboration d''équipe"],"de":["brainstorming","ideengenerierung","kollaboratives design","produktentwicklung","innovation","teamkollaboration"],"pt":["brainstorming","desenvolvimento de ideias","design","colaboração","diálogo natural","refinamento de ideias","apresentação de designs","verificação de designs"],"ru":["мозговой штурм","разработка идей","дизайн","сотрудничество","естественный диалог","уточнение идей","презентация дизайнов","проверка дизайнов"],"ar":["التخيل","تطوير الأفكار","التصميم","التعاون","الحوار الطبيعي","تحسين الأفكار","عرض التصميمات","التحقق من التصميمات"]}},"owner":"nicanac","repo":"familly-journal","repoPath":"nicanac/familly-journal","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"brainstorming","description":"You MUST use this before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality, or modifying behavior. Explores user intent, requirements and design before implementation.","bodyPreview":"# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs\n\n## Overview\n\nHelp turn ideas into fully formed designs and specs through natural collaborative dialogue.\n\nStart by understanding the current project context, then ask questions one at a time to refine the idea. Once you understand what you''re building, present the design in small sections (200-300 words), checking after each section whether it looks right so far.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Understanding the idea:**\n- Check out the current project state first (files, d","body":"# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs\n\n## Overview\n\nHelp turn ideas into fully formed designs and specs through natural collaborative dialogue.\n\nStart by understanding the current project context, then ask questions one at a time to refine the idea. Once you understand what you''re building, present the design in small sections (200-300 words), checking after each section whether it looks right so far.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Understanding the idea:**\n- Check out the current project state first (files, docs, recent commits)\n- Ask questions one at a time to refine the idea\n- Prefer multiple choice questions when possible, but open-ended is fine too\n- Only one question per message - if a topic needs more exploration, break it into multiple questions\n- Focus on understanding: purpose, constraints, success criteria\n\n**Exploring approaches:**\n- Propose 2-3 different approaches with trade-offs\n- Present options conversationally with your recommendation and reasoning\n- Lead with your recommended option and explain why\n\n**Presenting the design:**\n- Once you believe you understand what you''re building, present the design\n- Break it into sections of 200-300 words\n- Ask after each section whether it looks right so far\n- Cover: architecture, components, data flow, error handling, testing\n- Be ready to go back and clarify if something doesn''t make sense\n\n## After the Design\n\n**Documentation:**\n- Write the validated design to `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md`\n- Use elements-of-style:writing-clearly-and-concisely skill if available\n- Commit the design document to git\n\n**Implementation (if continuing):**\n- Ask: \"Ready to set up for implementation?\"\n- Use superpowers:using-git-worktrees to create isolated workspace\n- Use superpowers:writing-plans to create detailed implementation plan\n\n## Key Principles\n\n- **One question at a time** - Don''t overwhelm with multiple questions\n- **Multiple choice preferred** - Easier to answer than open-ended when possible\n- **YAGNI ruthlessly** - Remove unnecessary features from all designs\n- **Explore alternatives** - Always propose 2-3 approaches before settling\n- **Incremental validation** - Present design in sections, validate each\n- **Be flexible** - Go back and clarify when something doesn''t make sense\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T07:17:37.443Z","qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('bjconlan/burndown/brainstorming', 'community', 'bjconlan', 'burndown', 'bjconlan/burndown', 'brainstorming', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z', '2026-02-19T07:02:10.331Z', NULL, '{"id":"bjconlan/burndown/brainstorming","name":"brainstorming","description":{"zh":"头脑风暴技能可以帮助开发者将想法转化为完整的设计和规格","ja":"ブレインストーミングスキルは、開発者がアイデアを完全な設計と仕様に変換するのを支援します","ko":"브레인스토밍 스킬은 개발자가 아이디어를 완전한 디자인과 사양으로 변환하는 것을 지원합니다","es":"Convierte ideas en diseños mediante diálogo colaborativo y natural","fr":"Transformez les idées en conceptions à l''aide d''un dialogue collaboratif et naturel","de":"Wandeln Sie Ideen in Designs durch natürlichen und kollaborativen Dialog um","pt":"O brainstorming é uma técnica para desenvolver ideias em projetos através do diálogo colaborativo","ru":"Мозговой штурм - это техника разработки идей в проектах через естественный коллаборативный диалог","ar":"عصر الفكرة هو تقنية لتحويل الأفكار إلى تصميمات من خلال حوار تعاوني طبيعي","en":"daily burndowns for personal tasks"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"头脑风暴技能：将想法转化为设计","ja":"ブレインストーミングスキル：アイデアをデザインに","ko":"브레인스토밍 스킬: 아이디어를 디자인으로","es":"Generación de ideas con diálogo colaborativo","fr":"Génération d''idées avec dialogue collaboratif","de":"Ideenfindung mit kollaborativem Dialog","pt":"Brainstorming: Desenvolvendo Ideias em Projetos","ru":"Мозговой штурм: Разработка идей в проектах","ar":"عصر الفكرة: تحويل الأفكار إلى تصميمات","en":"brainstorming"},"description":{"zh":"头脑风暴技能可以帮助开发者将想法转化为完整的设计和规格","ja":"ブレインストーミングスキルは、開発者がアイデアを完全な設計と仕様に変換するのを支援します","ko":"브레인스토밍 스킬은 개발자가 아이디어를 완전한 디자인과 사양으로 변환하는 것을 지원합니다","es":"Convierte ideas en diseños mediante diálogo colaborativo y natural","fr":"Transformez les idées en conceptions à l''aide d''un dialogue collaboratif et naturel","de":"Wandeln Sie Ideen in Designs durch natürlichen und kollaborativen Dialog um","pt":"O brainstorming é uma técnica para desenvolver ideias em projetos através do diálogo colaborativo","ru":"Мозговой штурм - это техника разработки идей в проектах через естественный коллаборативный диалог","ar":"عصر الفكرة هو تقنية لتحويل الأفكار إلى تصميمات من خلال حوار تعاوني طبيعي","en":"daily burndowns for personal tasks"},"definition":{"en":"daily burndowns for personal tasks"},"features":{"zh":["协作对话","设计完善","项目背景理解","自然语言处理","迭代式设计"],"ja":["コラボレーションの会話","設計の完善","プロジェクトの背景理解","自然言語処理","イテレーション設計"],"ko":["협력 대화","디자인 완善","프로젝트 배경 이해","자연어 처리","반복 디자인"],"es":["Diálogo colaborativo","Desarrollo de ideas en diseños","Revisión y ajuste de los diseños","Presentación de diseños en secciones","Verificación de la coherencia del diseño"],"fr":["Dialogue collaboratif","Développement d''idées en conceptions","Révision et ajustement des conceptions","Présentation des conceptions en sections","Vérification de la cohérence de la conception"],"de":["Kollaborativer Dialog","Entwicklung von Ideen in Designs","Überprüfung und Anpassung der Designs","Präsentation der Designs in Abschnitten","Überprüfung der Konsistenz des Designs"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de ideias em projetos","Diálogo colaborativo natural","Refinamento de ideias através de perguntas","Apresentação de designs em seções","Verificação de designs em cada seção"],"ru":["Разработка идей в проектах","Естественный коллаборативный диалог","Уточнение идей через вопросы","Представление дизайнов в секциях","Проверка дизайнов после каждой секции"],"ar":["تحويل الأفكار إلى تصميمات","حوار تعاوني طبيعي","تحسين الأفكار من خلال أسئلة","عرض التصاميم في أقسام","التحقق من التصاميم بعد كل قسم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["头脑风暴","设计","协作","自然语言处理","开发工具","项目管理","软件开发","产品设计"],"ja":["ブレインストーミング","設計","コラボレーション","自然言語処理","開発ツール","プロジェクト管理","ソフトウェア開発","プロダクトデザイン"],"ko":["브레인스토밍","디자인","협력","자연어 처리","개발 도구","프로젝트 관리","소프트웨어 개발","제품 디자인"],"es":["brainstorming","desarrollo de ideas","diseño colaborativo","generación de ideas","desarrollo de proyectos","colaboración en equipo"],"fr":["brainstorming","développement d''idées","conception collaborative","génération d''idées","développement de projets","collaboration d''équipe"],"de":["brainstorming","ideenfindung","kollaboratives design","ideengenerierung","projektentwicklung","teamkollaboration"],"pt":["brainstorming","desenvolvimento de ideias","diálogo colaborativo","projetos","design","desenvolvimento de projetos","técnica de brainstorming","colaboração em equipe"],"ru":["мозговой штурм","разработка идей","коллаборативный диалог","проекты","дизайн","разработка проектов","техника мозгового штурма","командная работа"],"ar":["عصر الفكرة","تحويل الأفكار","حوار تعاوني","مشاريع","تصميم","تحويل المشاريع","تقنية عصر الفكرة","عمل جماعي"]}},"owner":"bjconlan","repo":"burndown","repoPath":"bjconlan/burndown","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"brainstorming","description":"You MUST use this before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality, or modifying behavior. Explores user intent, requirements and design before implementation.","bodyPreview":"# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs\n\n## Overview\n\nHelp turn ideas into fully formed designs and specs through natural collaborative dialogue.\n\nStart by understanding the current project context, then ask questions one at a time to refine the idea. Once you understand what you''re building, present the design in small sections (200-300 words), checking after each section whether it looks right so far.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Understanding the idea:**\n- Check out the current project state first (files, d","body":"# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs\n\n## Overview\n\nHelp turn ideas into fully formed designs and specs through natural collaborative dialogue.\n\nStart by understanding the current project context, then ask questions one at a time to refine the idea. Once you understand what you''re building, present the design in small sections (200-300 words), checking after each section whether it looks right so far.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Understanding the idea:**\n- Check out the current project state first (files, docs, recent commits)\n- Ask questions one at a time to refine the idea\n- Prefer multiple choice questions when possible, but open-ended is fine too\n- Only one question per message - if a topic needs more exploration, break it into multiple questions\n- Focus on understanding: purpose, constraints, success criteria\n\n**Exploring approaches:**\n- Propose 2-3 different approaches with trade-offs\n- Present options conversationally with your recommendation and reasoning\n- Lead with your recommended option and explain why\n\n**Presenting the design:**\n- Once you believe you understand what you''re building, present the design\n- Break it into sections of 200-300 words\n- Ask after each section whether it looks right so far\n- Cover: architecture, components, data flow, error handling, testing\n- Be ready to go back and clarify if something doesn''t make sense\n\n## After the Design\n\n**Documentation:**\n- Write the validated design to `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md`\n- Use elements-of-style:writing-clearly-and-concisely skill if available\n- Commit the design document to git\n\n**Implementation (if continuing):**\n- Ask: \"Ready to set up for implementation?\"\n- Use superpowers:using-git-worktrees to create isolated workspace\n- Use superpowers:writing-plans to create detailed implementation plan\n\n## Key Principles\n\n- **One question at a time** - Don''t overwhelm with multiple questions\n- **Multiple choice preferred** - Easier to answer than open-ended when possible\n- **YAGNI ruthlessly** - Remove unnecessary features from all designs\n- **Explore alternatives** - Always propose 2-3 approaches before settling\n- **Incremental validation** - Present design in sections, validate each\n- **Be flexible** - Go back and clarify when something doesn''t make sense\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T07:02:10.331Z","qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('amano--/call-center/notebooklm', 'community', 'amano--', 'call-center', 'amano--/call-center', 'notebooklm', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:03:48.182Z', '2026-02-19T05:50:08.560Z', NULL, '{"id":"amano--/call-center/notebooklm","name":"notebooklm","description":{"en":""},"seo":{"title":{"en":"notebooklm"},"description":{"en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"en":[]},"keywords":{"en":[]}},"owner":"amano--","repo":"call-center","repoPath":"amano--/call-center","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:03:48.182Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"notebooklm","description":"Use this skill to query your Google NotebookLM notebooks directly from Claude Code for source-grounded, citation-backed answers from Gemini. Browser automation, library management, persistent auth. Drastically reduced hallucinations through document-only responses.","bodyPreview":"# NotebookLM Research Assistant Skill\n\nInteract with Google NotebookLM to query documentation with Gemini''s source-grounded answers. Each question opens a fresh browser session, retrieves the answer exclusively from your uploaded documents, and closes.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nTrigger when user:\n- Mentions NotebookLM explicitly\n- Shares NotebookLM URL (`https://notebooklm.google.com/notebook/...`)\n- Asks to query their notebooks/documentation\n- Wants to add documentation to NotebookLM library","body":"# NotebookLM Research Assistant Skill\n\nInteract with Google NotebookLM to query documentation with Gemini''s source-grounded answers. Each question opens a fresh browser session, retrieves the answer exclusively from your uploaded documents, and closes.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nTrigger when user:\n- Mentions NotebookLM explicitly\n- Shares NotebookLM URL (`https://notebooklm.google.com/notebook/...`)\n- Asks to query their notebooks/documentation\n- Wants to add documentation to NotebookLM library\n- Uses phrases like \"ask my NotebookLM\", \"check my docs\", \"query my notebook\"\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Add Command - Smart Discovery\n\nWhen user wants to add a notebook without providing details:\n\n**SMART ADD (Recommended)**: Query the notebook first to discover its content:\n```bash\n# Step 1: Query the notebook about its content\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"What is the content of this notebook? What topics are covered? Provide a complete overview briefly and concisely\" --notebook-url \"[URL]\"\n\n# Step 2: Use the discovered information to add it\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py add --url \"[URL]\" --name \"[Based on content]\" --description \"[Based on content]\" --topics \"[Based on content]\"\n```\n\n**MANUAL ADD**: If user provides all details:\n- `--url` - The NotebookLM URL\n- `--name` - A descriptive name\n- `--description` - What the notebook contains (REQUIRED!)\n- `--topics` - Comma-separated topics (REQUIRED!)\n\nNEVER guess or use generic descriptions! If details missing, use Smart Add to discover them.\n\n## Critical: Always Use run.py Wrapper\n\n**NEVER call scripts directly. ALWAYS use `python scripts/run.py [script]`:**\n\n```bash\n# ✅ CORRECT - Always use run.py:\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py status\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py list\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\"\n\n# ❌ WRONG - Never call directly:\npython scripts/auth_manager.py status  # Fails without venv!\n```\n\nThe `run.py` wrapper automatically:\n1. Creates `.venv` if needed\n2. Installs all dependencies\n3. Activates environment\n4. Executes script properly\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Check Authentication Status\n```bash\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py status\n```\n\nIf not authenticated, proceed to setup.\n\n### Step 2: Authenticate (One-Time Setup)\n```bash\n# Browser MUST be visible for manual Google login\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py setup\n```\n\n**Important:**\n- Browser is VISIBLE for authentication\n- Browser window opens automatically\n- User must manually log in to Google\n- Tell user: \"A browser window will open for Google login\"\n\n### Step 3: Manage Notebook Library\n\n```bash\n# List all notebooks\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py list\n\n# BEFORE ADDING: Ask user for metadata if unknown!\n# \"What does this notebook contain?\"\n# \"What topics should I tag it with?\"\n\n# Add notebook to library (ALL parameters are REQUIRED!)\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py add \\\n  --url \"https://notebooklm.google.com/notebook/...\" \\\n  --name \"Descriptive Name\" \\\n  --description \"What this notebook contains\" \\  # REQUIRED - ASK USER IF UNKNOWN!\n  --topics \"topic1,topic2,topic3\"  # REQUIRED - ASK USER IF UNKNOWN!\n\n# Search notebooks by topic\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py search --query \"keyword\"\n\n# Set active notebook\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py activate --id notebook-id\n\n# Remove notebook\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py remove --id notebook-id\n```\n\n### Quick Workflow\n1. Check library: `python scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py list`\n2. Ask question: `python scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\" --notebook-id ID`\n\n### Step 4: Ask Questions\n\n```bash\n# Basic query (uses active notebook if set)\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"Your question here\"\n\n# Query specific notebook\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\" --notebook-id notebook-id\n\n# Query with notebook URL directly\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\" --notebook-url \"https://...\"\n\n# Show browser for debugging\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\" --show-browser\n```\n\n## Follow-Up Mechanism (CRITICAL)\n\nEvery NotebookLM answer ends with: **\"EXTREMELY IMPORTANT: Is that ALL you need to know?\"**\n\n**Required Claude Behavior:**\n1. **STOP** - Do not immediately respond to user\n2. **ANALYZE** - Compare answer to user''s original request\n3. **IDENTIFY GAPS** - Determine if more information needed\n4. **ASK FOLLOW-UP** - If gaps exist, immediately ask:\n   ```bash\n   python scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"Follow-up with context...\"\n   ```\n5. **REPEAT** - Continue until information is complete\n6. **SYNTHESIZE** - Combine all answers before responding to user\n\n## Script Reference\n\n### Authentication Management (`auth_manager.py`)\n```bash\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py setup    # Initial setup (browser visible)\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py status   # Check authentication\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py reauth   # Re-authenticate (browser visible)\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py clear    # Clear authentication\n```\n\n### Notebook Management (`notebook_manager.py`)\n```bash\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py add --url URL --name NAME --description DESC --topics TOPICS\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py list\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py search --query QUERY\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py activate --id ID\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py remove --id ID\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py stats\n```\n\n### Question Interface (`ask_question.py`)\n```bash\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\" [--notebook-id ID] [--notebook-url URL] [--show-browser]\n```\n\n### Data Cleanup (`cleanup_manager.py`)\n```bash\npython scripts/run.py cleanup_manager.py                    # Preview cleanup\npython scripts/run.py cleanup_manager.py --confirm          # Execute cleanup\npython scripts/run.py cleanup_manager.py --preserve-library # Keep notebooks\n```\n\n## Environment Management\n\nThe virtual environment is automatically managed:\n- First run creates `.venv` automatically\n- Dependencies install automatically\n- Chromium browser installs automatically\n- Everything isolated in skill directory\n\nManual setup (only if automatic fails):\n```bash\npython -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate  # Linux/Mac\npip install -r requirements.txt\npython -m patchright install chromium\n```\n\n## Data Storage\n\nAll data stored in `~/.claude/skills/notebooklm/data/`:\n- `library.json` - Notebook metadata\n- `auth_info.json` - Authentication status\n- `browser_state/` - Browser cookies and session\n\n**Security:** Protected by `.gitignore`, never commit to git.\n\n## Configuration\n\nOptional `.env` file in skill directory:\n```env\nHEADLESS=false           # Browser visibility\nSHOW_BROWSER=false       # Default browser display\nSTEALTH_ENABLED=true     # Human-like behavior\nTYPING_WPM_MIN=160       # Typing speed\nTYPING_WPM_MAX=240\nDEFAULT_NOTEBOOK_ID=     # Default notebook\n```\n\n## Decision Flow\n\n```\nUser mentions NotebookLM\n    ↓\nCheck auth → python scripts/run.py auth_manager.py status\n    ↓\nIf not authenticated → python scripts/run.py auth_manager.py setup\n    ↓\nCheck/Add notebook → python scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py list/add (with --description)\n    ↓\nActivate notebook → python scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py activate --id ID\n    ↓\nAsk question → python scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\"\n    ↓\nSee \"Is that ALL you need?\" → Ask follow-ups until complete\n    ↓\nSynthesize and respond to user\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n| Problem | Solution |\n|---------|----------|\n| ModuleNotFoundError | Use `run.py` wrapper |\n| Authentication fails | Browser must be visible for setup! --show-browser |\n| Rate limit (50/day) | Wait or switch Google account |\n| Browser crashes | `python scripts/run.py cleanup_manager.py --preserve-library` |\n| Notebook not found | Check with `notebook_manager.py list` |\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Always use run.py** - Handles environment automatically\n2. **Check auth first** - Before any operations\n3. **Follow-up questions** - Don''t stop at first answer\n4. **Browser visible for auth** - Required for manual login\n5. **Include context** - Each question is independent\n6. **Synthesize answers** - Combine multiple responses\n\n## Limitations\n\n- No session persistence (each question = new browser)\n- Rate limits on free Google accounts (50 queries/day)\n- Manual upload required (user must add docs to NotebookLM)\n- Browser overhead (few seconds per question)\n\n## Resources (Skill Structure)\n\n**Important directories and files:**\n\n- `scripts/` - All automation scripts (ask_question.py, notebook_manager.py, etc.)\n- `data/` - Local storage for authentication and notebook library\n- `references/` - Extended documentation:\n  - `api_reference.md` - Detailed API documentation for all scripts\n  - `troubleshooting.md` - Common issues and solutions\n  - `usage_patterns.md` - Best practices and workflow examples\n- `.venv/` - Isolated Python environment (auto-created on first run)\n- `.gitignore` - Protects sensitive data from being committed\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T05:50:08.560Z","qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('bjconlan/burndown/verification-before-completion', 'community', 'bjconlan', 'burndown', 'bjconlan/burndown', 'verification-before-completion', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z', '2026-02-19T07:02:10.558Z', NULL, '{"id":"bjconlan/burndown/verification-before-completion","name":"verification-before-completion","description":{"zh":"验证前完成是一种技能，通过每日燃尽图表来管理个人任务，确保任务的完成和验证。","ja":"バリデーション前完了は、毎日のバーンダウンチャートを使用して個人タスクを管理するスキルです。","ko":"검증 전 완료는 일일 버드 다운 차트를 사용하여 개인 업무를 관리하는 기능입니다.","es":"La verificación antes de completar es una técnica para asegurar la precisión y eficiencia en tareas personales, basada en el principio de evidencia antes de reclamos.","fr":"La vérification avant achèvement est une technique pour assurer la précision et l''efficacité dans les tâches personnelles, basée sur le principe de preuve avant réclamation.","de":"Die Verifizierung vor Abschluss ist eine Technik, um die Genauigkeit und Effizienz in persönlichen Aufgaben zu gewährleisten, basierend auf dem Prinzip der Evidenz vor Ansprüchen.","pt":"A verificação antes de concluir tarefas diárias é fundamental para garantir a eficiência e a honestidade. Saiba mais sobre como aplicar essa prática.","ru":"Верификация перед завершением ежедневных задач необходима для обеспечения эффективности и честности. Узнайте больше о том, как применять эту практику.","ar":"التحقق قبل استكمال المهام اليومية أمر أساسي لضمان الكفاءة والصدق. تعرف على كيفية تطبيق هذه الممارسة.","en":"daily burndowns for personal tasks"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"验证前完成：提高任务效率","ja":"バリデーション前完了：タスクの効率化","ko":"검증 전 완료: 업무 효율성 향상","es":"Verificación antes de completar: eficiencia en tareas per...","fr":"Vérification avant achèvement: efficacité dans les tâches...","de":"Verifizierung vor Abschluss: Effizienz in persönlichen Au...","pt":"Verificação Antes de Conclusão: Eficiência com Evidências","ru":"Верификация До Завершения: Эффективность С Доказательствами","ar":"التحقق قبل الاستكمال: الكفاءة مع الأدلة","en":"verification-before-completion"},"description":{"zh":"验证前完成是一种技能，通过每日燃尽图表来管理个人任务，确保任务的完成和验证。","ja":"バリデーション前完了は、毎日のバーンダウンチャートを使用して個人タスクを管理するスキルです。","ko":"검증 전 완료는 일일 버드 다운 차트를 사용하여 개인 업무를 관리하는 기능입니다.","es":"La verificación antes de completar es una técnica para asegurar la precisión y eficiencia en tareas personales, basada en el principio de evidencia antes de ...","fr":"La vérification avant achèvement est une technique pour assurer la précision et l''efficacité dans les tâches personnelles, basée sur le principe de preuve av...","de":"Die Verifizierung vor Abschluss ist eine Technik, um die Genauigkeit und Effizienz in persönlichen Aufgaben zu gewährleisten, basierend auf dem Prinzip der E...","pt":"A verificação antes de concluir tarefas diárias é fundamental para garantir a eficiência e a honestidade. Saiba mais sobre como aplicar essa prática.","ru":"Верификация перед завершением ежедневных задач необходима для обеспечения эффективности и честности. Узнайте больше о том, как применять эту практику.","ar":"التحقق قبل استكمال المهام اليومية أمر أساسي لضمان الكفاءة والصدق. تعرف على كيفية تطبيق هذه الممارسة.","en":"daily burndowns for personal tasks"},"definition":{"en":"daily burndowns for personal tasks"},"features":{"zh":["每日燃尽图表","任务验证","提高任务效率","个人任务管理","自动化验证流程"],"ja":["毎日のバーンダウンチャート","タスクのバリデーション","タスクの効率化","個人タスクの管理","自動化されたバリデーションプロセス"],"ko":["일일 버드 다운 차트","업무 검증","업무 효율성 향상","개인 업무 관리","자동화된 검증 프로세스"],"es":["Verificación diaria de tareas personales","Principio de evidencia antes de reclamos","Evita errores y aumenta la productividad","Técnica para asegurar la precisión y eficiencia","Aplicable en entornos de desarrollo y trabajo"],"fr":["Vérification quotidienne des tâches personnelles","Principe de preuve avant réclamation","Évite les erreurs et augmente la productivité","Technique pour assurer la précision et l''efficacité","Applicable dans les environnements de développement et de travail"],"de":["Tägliche Verifizierung von persönlichen Aufgaben","Prinzip der Evidenz vor Ansprüchen","Vermeidet Fehler und steigert die Produktivität","Technik zur Gewährleistung von Genauigkeit und Effizienz","Anwendbar in Entwicklungs- und Arbeitsumgebungen"],"pt":["Exigência de evidências antes de concluir tarefas","Aumento da produtividade com verificação diária","Garantia de eficiência e honestidade","Aplicação prática para tarefas diárias","Melhoria da qualidade do trabalho com verificação"],"ru":["Требование доказательств перед завершением задач","Увеличение производительности с помощью ежедневной верификации","Гарантия эффективности и честности","Практическое применение для ежедневных задач","Улучшение качества работы с помощью верификации"],"ar":["متطلبات الأدلة قبل استكمال المهام","زيادة الإنتاجية مع التحقق اليومي","ضمان الكفاءة والصدق","تطبيق عملي للمهام اليومية","تحسين جودة العمل مع التحقق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["验证前完成","任务管理","每日燃尽图表","自动化验证","个人任务管理","任务效率"],"ja":["バリデーション前完了","タスク管理","毎日のバーンダウンチャート","自動化されたバリデーション","個人タスクの管理","タスクの効率化"],"ko":["검증 전 완료","업무 관리","일일 버드 다운 차트","자동화된 검증","개인 업무 관리","업무 효율성"],"es":["verificación antes de completar","tareas personales","eficiencia en el trabajo","productividad","precisión en tareas","desarrollo de software","gestión de proyectos"],"fr":["vérification avant achèvement","tâches personnelles","efficacité au travail","productivité","précision dans les tâches","développement de logiciels","gestion de projets"],"de":["Verifizierung vor Abschluss","persönliche Aufgaben","Effizienz in der Arbeit","Produktivität","Genauigkeit in Aufgaben","Softwareentwicklung","Projektmanagement"],"pt":["verificação antes de conclusão","eficiência com evidências","produtividade diária","tarefas diárias","honestidade no trabalho","qualidade do trabalho"],"ru":["верификация до завершения","эфективность с доказательствами","ежедневная производительность","ежедневные задачи","честность в работе","качество работы"],"ar":["التحقق قبل الاستكمال","الكفاءة مع الأدلة","الإنتاجية اليومية","المهام اليومية","الصدق في العمل","جودة العمل"]}},"owner":"bjconlan","repo":"burndown","repoPath":"bjconlan/burndown","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"verification-before-completion","description":"Use when about to claim work is complete, fixed, or passing, before committing or creating PRs - requires running verification commands and confirming output before making any success claims; evidence before assertions always","bodyPreview":"# Verification Before Completion\n\n## Overview\n\nClaiming work is complete without verification is dishonesty, not efficiency.\n\n**Core principle:** Evidence before claims, always.\n\n**Violating the letter of this rule is violating the spirit of this rule.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO COMPLETION CLAIMS WITHOUT FRESH VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n```\n\nIf you haven''t run the verification command in this message, you cannot claim it passes.\n\n## The Gate Function\n\n```\nBEFORE claiming any status or expressing sati","body":"# Verification Before Completion\n\n## Overview\n\nClaiming work is complete without verification is dishonesty, not efficiency.\n\n**Core principle:** Evidence before claims, always.\n\n**Violating the letter of this rule is violating the spirit of this rule.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO COMPLETION CLAIMS WITHOUT FRESH VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n```\n\nIf you haven''t run the verification command in this message, you cannot claim it passes.\n\n## The Gate Function\n\n```\nBEFORE claiming any status or expressing satisfaction:\n\n1. IDENTIFY: What command proves this claim?\n2. RUN: Execute the FULL command (fresh, complete)\n3. READ: Full output, check exit code, count failures\n4. VERIFY: Does output confirm the claim?\n   - If NO: State actual status with evidence\n   - If YES: State claim WITH evidence\n5. ONLY THEN: Make the claim\n\nSkip any step = lying, not verifying\n```\n\n## Common Failures\n\n| Claim | Requires | Not Sufficient |\n|-------|----------|----------------|\n| Tests pass | Test command output: 0 failures | Previous run, \"should pass\" |\n| Linter clean | Linter output: 0 errors | Partial check, extrapolation |\n| Build succeeds | Build command: exit 0 | Linter passing, logs look good |\n| Bug fixed | Test original symptom: passes | Code changed, assumed fixed |\n| Regression test works | Red-green cycle verified | Test passes once |\n| Agent completed | VCS diff shows changes | Agent reports \"success\" |\n| Requirements met | Line-by-line checklist | Tests passing |\n\n## Red Flags - STOP\n\n- Using \"should\", \"probably\", \"seems to\"\n- Expressing satisfaction before verification (\"Great!\", \"Perfect!\", \"Done!\", etc.)\n- About to commit/push/PR without verification\n- Trusting agent success reports\n- Relying on partial verification\n- Thinking \"just this once\"\n- Tired and wanting work over\n- **ANY wording implying success without having run verification**\n\n## Rationalization Prevention\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Should work now\" | RUN the verification |\n| \"I''m confident\" | Confidence ≠ evidence |\n| \"Just this once\" | No exceptions |\n| \"Linter passed\" | Linter ≠ compiler |\n| \"Agent said success\" | Verify independently |\n| \"I''m tired\" | Exhaustion ≠ excuse |\n| \"Partial check is enough\" | Partial proves nothing |\n| \"Different words so rule doesn''t apply\" | Spirit over letter |\n\n## Key Patterns\n\n**Tests:**\n```\n✅ [Run test command] [See: 34/34 pass] \"All tests pass\"\n❌ \"Should pass now\" / \"Looks correct\"\n```\n\n**Regression tests (TDD Red-Green):**\n```\n✅ Write → Run (pass) → Revert fix → Run (MUST FAIL) → Restore → Run (pass)\n❌ \"I''ve written a regression test\" (without red-green verification)\n```\n\n**Build:**\n```\n✅ [Run build] [See: exit 0] \"Build passes\"\n❌ \"Linter passed\" (linter doesn''t check compilation)\n```\n\n**Requirements:**\n```\n✅ Re-read plan → Create checklist → Verify each → Report gaps or completion\n❌ \"Tests pass, phase complete\"\n```\n\n**Agent delegation:**\n```\n✅ Agent reports success → Check VCS diff → Verify changes → Report actual state\n❌ Trust agent report\n```\n\n## Why This Matters\n\nFrom 24 failure memories:\n- your human partner said \"I don''t believe you\" - trust broken\n- Undefined functions shipped - would crash\n- Missing requirements shipped - incomplete features\n- Time wasted on false completion → redirect → rework\n- Violates: \"Honesty is a core value. If you lie, you''ll be replaced.\"\n\n## When To Apply\n\n**ALWAYS before:**\n- ANY variation of success/completion claims\n- ANY expression of satisfaction\n- ANY positive statement about work state\n- Committing, PR creation, task completion\n- Moving to next task\n- Delegating to agents\n\n**Rule applies to:**\n- Exact phrases\n- Paraphrases and synonyms\n- Implications of success\n- ANY communication suggesting completion/correctness\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\n**No shortcuts for verification.**\n\nRun the command. Read the output. THEN claim the result.\n\nThis is non-negotiable.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T07:02:10.558Z","qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/notebooklm', 'community', 'claudiodearaujo', 'IzaCenter', 'claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter', 'notebooklm', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z', '2026-02-19T07:17:37.450Z', NULL, '{"id":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/notebooklm","name":"notebooklm","description":{"zh":"NotebookLM 研究助手技能允许您与 Google NotebookLM 交互，查询文档和 Gemini 的源答案。每个问题都会打开一个新的浏览器会话，仅从上传的文档中检索答案，然后关闭","ja":"NotebookLM リサーチ アシスタント スキルは、Google NotebookLM とインタラクティブに質問し、Gemini の源答案を文書から取得することを可能にします。各質問は新しいブラウザ セッションを開き、アップロードされた文書からのみ回答を取得し、閉じます","ko":"노트북LM 연구 보조 기술을 사용하면 구글 노트북LM와 상호 작용하여 문서를 조회하고 제미니의 출처에 기반한 답변을 받을 수 있습니다. 각 질문은 새로운 브라우저 세션을 열어 업로드된 문서에서만 답변을 검색하고 닫습니다","es":"NotebookLM es un asistente de investigación que permite a los desarrolladores consultar documentación con respuestas precisas. Funciona abriendo una sesión de navegador, recuperando la respuesta de los documentos subidos y cerrando.","fr":"NotebookLM est un assistant de recherche qui permet aux développeurs de consulter la documentation avec des réponses précises. Il fonctionne en ouvrant une session de navigateur, en récupérant la réponse à partir des documents téléchargés et en fermant.","de":"NotebookLM ist ein Forschungsassistent, der es Entwicklern ermöglicht, Dokumentationen mit präzisen Antworten abzufragen. Er funktioniert, indem er eine Browsersitzung öffnet, die Antwort aus den hochgeladenen Dokumenten abruft und schließt.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"NotebookLM 研究助手技能","ja":"NotebookLM リサーチ アシスタント スキル","ko":"노트북LM 연구 보조 기술","es":"NotebookLM: Asistente de Investigación para Desarrolladores","fr":"NotebookLM : Assistant de Recherche pour Développeurs","de":"NotebookLM: Forschungsassistent für Entwickler","en":"notebooklm"},"description":{"zh":"NotebookLM 研究助手技能允许您与 Google NotebookLM 交互，查询文档和 Gemini 的源答案。每个问题都会打开一个新的浏览器会话，仅从上传的文档中检索答案，然后关闭","ja":"NotebookLM リサーチ アシスタント スキルは、Google NotebookLM とインタラクティブに質問し、Gemini の源答案を文書から取得することを可能にします。各質問は新しいブラウザ セッションを開き、アップロードされた文書からのみ回答を取得し、閉じます","ko":"노트북LM 연구 보조 기술을 사용하면 구글 노트북LM와 상호 작용하여 문서를 조회하고 제미니의 출처에 기반한 답변을 받을 수 있습니다. 각 질문은 새로운 브라우저 세션을 열어 업로드된 문서에서만 답변을 검색하고 닫습니다","es":"NotebookLM es un asistente de investigación que permite a los desarrolladores consultar documentación con respuestas precisas. Funciona abriendo una sesión d...","fr":"NotebookLM est un assistant de recherche qui permet aux développeurs de consulter la documentation avec des réponses précises. Il fonctionne en ouvrant une s...","de":"NotebookLM ist ein Forschungsassistent, der es Entwicklern ermöglicht, Dokumentationen mit präzisen Antworten abzufragen. Er funktioniert, indem er eine Brow...","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["与 Google NotebookLM 交互","查询文档和 Gemini 的源答案","每个问题打开一个新的浏览器会话","仅从上传的文档中检索答案","关闭浏览器会话后自动关闭"],"ja":["Google NotebookLM とインタラクティブに質問","文書と Gemini の源答案を取得","各質問は新しいブラウザ セッションを開く","アップロードされた文書からのみ回答を取得","ブラウザ セッションの終了後に自動的に閉じる"],"ko":["구글 노트북LM와 상호 작용","문서와 제미니의 출처에 기반한 답변을 조회","각 질문은 새로운 브라우저 세션을 열어","업로드된 문서에서만 답변을 검색","브라우저 세션을 닫은 후 자동으로 종료"],"es":["Interactúa con Google NotebookLM","Consulta documentación con respuestas basadas en fuentes de Gemini","Abre una sesión de navegador para cada pregunta","Recupera la respuesta exclusivamente de los documentos subidos","Cierra la sesión de navegador después de cada pregunta"],"fr":["Interagissez avec Google NotebookLM","Consulter la documentation avec des réponses basées sur les sources de Gemini","Ouvrez une session de navigateur pour chaque question","Récupérez la réponse exclusivement à partir des documents téléchargés","Fermez la session de navigateur après chaque question"],"de":["Interagieren Sie mit Google NotebookLM","Dokumentationen mit Quellen-basierten Antworten von Gemini abfragen","Öffnen Sie eine Browsersitzung für jede Frage","Rufen Sie die Antwort ausschließlich aus den hochgeladenen Dokumenten ab","Schließen Sie die Browsersitzung nach jeder Frage"]},"keywords":{"zh":["NotebookLM","Google NotebookLM","研究助手技能","文档查询","Gemini 源答案","浏览器会话","上传文档"],"ja":["NotebookLM","Google NotebookLM","リサーチ アシスタント スキル","文書検索","Gemini 源答案","ブラウザ セッション","アップロードされた文書"],"ko":["노트북LM","구글 노트북LM","연구 보조 기술","문서 조회","제미니의 출처에 기반한 답변","브라우저 세션","업로드된 문서"],"es":["NotebookLM","asistente de investigación","desarrolladores","documentación","Gemini","respuestas basadas en fuentes","Google NotebookLM"],"fr":["NotebookLM","assistant de recherche","développeurs","documentation","Gemini","réponses basées sur les sources","Google NotebookLM"],"de":["NotebookLM","Forschungsassistent","Entwickler","Dokumentation","Gemini","quellenbasierte Antworten","Google NotebookLM"]}},"owner":"claudiodearaujo","repo":"IzaCenter","repoPath":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"notebooklm","description":"Use this skill to query your Google NotebookLM notebooks directly from Claude Code for source-grounded, citation-backed answers from Gemini. Browser automation, library management, persistent auth. Drastically reduced hallucinations through document-only responses.","bodyPreview":"# NotebookLM Research Assistant Skill\n\nInteract with Google NotebookLM to query documentation with Gemini''s source-grounded answers. Each question opens a fresh browser session, retrieves the answer exclusively from your uploaded documents, and closes.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nTrigger when user:\n- Mentions NotebookLM explicitly\n- Shares NotebookLM URL (`https://notebooklm.google.com/notebook/...`)\n- Asks to query their notebooks/documentation\n- Wants to add documentation to NotebookLM library","body":"# NotebookLM Research Assistant Skill\n\nInteract with Google NotebookLM to query documentation with Gemini''s source-grounded answers. Each question opens a fresh browser session, retrieves the answer exclusively from your uploaded documents, and closes.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nTrigger when user:\n- Mentions NotebookLM explicitly\n- Shares NotebookLM URL (`https://notebooklm.google.com/notebook/...`)\n- Asks to query their notebooks/documentation\n- Wants to add documentation to NotebookLM library\n- Uses phrases like \"ask my NotebookLM\", \"check my docs\", \"query my notebook\"\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Add Command - Smart Discovery\n\nWhen user wants to add a notebook without providing details:\n\n**SMART ADD (Recommended)**: Query the notebook first to discover its content:\n```bash\n# Step 1: Query the notebook about its content\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"What is the content of this notebook? What topics are covered? Provide a complete overview briefly and concisely\" --notebook-url \"[URL]\"\n\n# Step 2: Use the discovered information to add it\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py add --url \"[URL]\" --name \"[Based on content]\" --description \"[Based on content]\" --topics \"[Based on content]\"\n```\n\n**MANUAL ADD**: If user provides all details:\n- `--url` - The NotebookLM URL\n- `--name` - A descriptive name\n- `--description` - What the notebook contains (REQUIRED!)\n- `--topics` - Comma-separated topics (REQUIRED!)\n\nNEVER guess or use generic descriptions! If details missing, use Smart Add to discover them.\n\n## Critical: Always Use run.py Wrapper\n\n**NEVER call scripts directly. ALWAYS use `python scripts/run.py [script]`:**\n\n```bash\n# ✅ CORRECT - Always use run.py:\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py status\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py list\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\"\n\n# ❌ WRONG - Never call directly:\npython scripts/auth_manager.py status  # Fails without venv!\n```\n\nThe `run.py` wrapper automatically:\n1. Creates `.venv` if needed\n2. Installs all dependencies\n3. Activates environment\n4. Executes script properly\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Check Authentication Status\n```bash\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py status\n```\n\nIf not authenticated, proceed to setup.\n\n### Step 2: Authenticate (One-Time Setup)\n```bash\n# Browser MUST be visible for manual Google login\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py setup\n```\n\n**Important:**\n- Browser is VISIBLE for authentication\n- Browser window opens automatically\n- User must manually log in to Google\n- Tell user: \"A browser window will open for Google login\"\n\n### Step 3: Manage Notebook Library\n\n```bash\n# List all notebooks\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py list\n\n# BEFORE ADDING: Ask user for metadata if unknown!\n# \"What does this notebook contain?\"\n# \"What topics should I tag it with?\"\n\n# Add notebook to library (ALL parameters are REQUIRED!)\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py add \\\n  --url \"https://notebooklm.google.com/notebook/...\" \\\n  --name \"Descriptive Name\" \\\n  --description \"What this notebook contains\" \\  # REQUIRED - ASK USER IF UNKNOWN!\n  --topics \"topic1,topic2,topic3\"  # REQUIRED - ASK USER IF UNKNOWN!\n\n# Search notebooks by topic\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py search --query \"keyword\"\n\n# Set active notebook\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py activate --id notebook-id\n\n# Remove notebook\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py remove --id notebook-id\n```\n\n### Quick Workflow\n1. Check library: `python scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py list`\n2. Ask question: `python scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\" --notebook-id ID`\n\n### Step 4: Ask Questions\n\n```bash\n# Basic query (uses active notebook if set)\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"Your question here\"\n\n# Query specific notebook\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\" --notebook-id notebook-id\n\n# Query with notebook URL directly\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\" --notebook-url \"https://...\"\n\n# Show browser for debugging\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\" --show-browser\n```\n\n## Follow-Up Mechanism (CRITICAL)\n\nEvery NotebookLM answer ends with: **\"EXTREMELY IMPORTANT: Is that ALL you need to know?\"**\n\n**Required Claude Behavior:**\n1. **STOP** - Do not immediately respond to user\n2. **ANALYZE** - Compare answer to user''s original request\n3. **IDENTIFY GAPS** - Determine if more information needed\n4. **ASK FOLLOW-UP** - If gaps exist, immediately ask:\n   ```bash\n   python scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"Follow-up with context...\"\n   ```\n5. **REPEAT** - Continue until information is complete\n6. **SYNTHESIZE** - Combine all answers before responding to user\n\n## Script Reference\n\n### Authentication Management (`auth_manager.py`)\n```bash\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py setup    # Initial setup (browser visible)\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py status   # Check authentication\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py reauth   # Re-authenticate (browser visible)\npython scripts/run.py auth_manager.py clear    # Clear authentication\n```\n\n### Notebook Management (`notebook_manager.py`)\n```bash\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py add --url URL --name NAME --description DESC --topics TOPICS\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py list\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py search --query QUERY\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py activate --id ID\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py remove --id ID\npython scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py stats\n```\n\n### Question Interface (`ask_question.py`)\n```bash\npython scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\" [--notebook-id ID] [--notebook-url URL] [--show-browser]\n```\n\n### Data Cleanup (`cleanup_manager.py`)\n```bash\npython scripts/run.py cleanup_manager.py                    # Preview cleanup\npython scripts/run.py cleanup_manager.py --confirm          # Execute cleanup\npython scripts/run.py cleanup_manager.py --preserve-library # Keep notebooks\n```\n\n## Environment Management\n\nThe virtual environment is automatically managed:\n- First run creates `.venv` automatically\n- Dependencies install automatically\n- Chromium browser installs automatically\n- Everything isolated in skill directory\n\nManual setup (only if automatic fails):\n```bash\npython -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate  # Linux/Mac\npip install -r requirements.txt\npython -m patchright install chromium\n```\n\n## Data Storage\n\nAll data stored in `~/.claude/skills/notebooklm/data/`:\n- `library.json` - Notebook metadata\n- `auth_info.json` - Authentication status\n- `browser_state/` - Browser cookies and session\n\n**Security:** Protected by `.gitignore`, never commit to git.\n\n## Configuration\n\nOptional `.env` file in skill directory:\n```env\nHEADLESS=false           # Browser visibility\nSHOW_BROWSER=false       # Default browser display\nSTEALTH_ENABLED=true     # Human-like behavior\nTYPING_WPM_MIN=160       # Typing speed\nTYPING_WPM_MAX=240\nDEFAULT_NOTEBOOK_ID=     # Default notebook\n```\n\n## Decision Flow\n\n```\nUser mentions NotebookLM\n    ↓\nCheck auth → python scripts/run.py auth_manager.py status\n    ↓\nIf not authenticated → python scripts/run.py auth_manager.py setup\n    ↓\nCheck/Add notebook → python scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py list/add (with --description)\n    ↓\nActivate notebook → python scripts/run.py notebook_manager.py activate --id ID\n    ↓\nAsk question → python scripts/run.py ask_question.py --question \"...\"\n    ↓\nSee \"Is that ALL you need?\" → Ask follow-ups until complete\n    ↓\nSynthesize and respond to user\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n| Problem | Solution |\n|---------|----------|\n| ModuleNotFoundError | Use `run.py` wrapper |\n| Authentication fails | Browser must be visible for setup! --show-browser |\n| Rate limit (50/day) | Wait or switch Google account |\n| Browser crashes | `python scripts/run.py cleanup_manager.py --preserve-library` |\n| Notebook not found | Check with `notebook_manager.py list` |\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Always use run.py** - Handles environment automatically\n2. **Check auth first** - Before any operations\n3. **Follow-up questions** - Don''t stop at first answer\n4. **Browser visible for auth** - Required for manual login\n5. **Include context** - Each question is independent\n6. **Synthesize answers** - Combine multiple responses\n\n## Limitations\n\n- No session persistence (each question = new browser)\n- Rate limits on free Google accounts (50 queries/day)\n- Manual upload required (user must add docs to NotebookLM)\n- Browser overhead (few seconds per question)\n\n## Resources (Skill Structure)\n\n**Important directories and files:**\n\n- `scripts/` - All automation scripts (ask_question.py, notebook_manager.py, etc.)\n- `data/` - Local storage for authentication and notebook library\n- `references/` - Extended documentation:\n  - `api_reference.md` - Detailed API documentation for all scripts\n  - `troubleshooting.md` - Common issues and solutions\n  - `usage_patterns.md` - Best practices and workflow examples\n- `.venv/` - Isolated Python environment (auto-created on first run)\n- `.gitignore` - Protects sensitive data from being committed\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T07:17:37.450Z","qualityScore":65}');
