lte die Aufdrängung eines standardisierten Formatierungs auf Dateien mit etablierten Mustern vermeiden"],"pt":["Requires exact matching of existing template styles and conventions","Limited to .xlsx file format","Must avoid imposing standardized formatting on files with established patterns"],"ru":["Requires exact matching of existing template styles and conventions","Limited to .xlsx file format","Must avoid imposing standardized formatting on files with established patterns"],"ar":["Requires exact matching of existing template styles and conventions","Limited to .xlsx file format","Must avoid imposing standardized formatting on files with established patterns"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Dknight203/AesopIDE/linkerd-patterns', 'community', 'Dknight203', 'AesopIDE', 'Dknight203/AesopIDE', 'linkerd-patterns', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z', '2026-02-19T07:19:06.200Z', NULL, '{"id":"Dknight203/AesopIDE/linkerd-patterns","name":"linkerd-patterns","description":{"pt":"Linkerd Patterns fornece padrões de produção para a malha de serviço Linkerd, uma solução leve e segura para Kubernetes.","ru":"Шаблоны Linkerd предоставляют производственные шаблоны для сетки служб Linkerd, лёгкого и безопасного решения для Kubernetes.","ar":"نماط Linkerd توفر نمطز إنتاجية لشبكة خدمية Linkerd، حل خفيف وآمن ل Kubernetes.","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"seo":{"title":{"pt":"Padrões Linkerd: Malha de Serviço Leve para Kubernetes","ru":"Шаблоны Linkerd: Лёгкая сетка служб для Kubernetes","ar":"نماط Linkerd: شبكة خدمية خفيفة ل Kubernetes","en":"linkerd-patterns"},"description":{"pt":"Linkerd Patterns fornece padrões de produção para a malha de serviço Linkerd, uma solução leve e segura para Kubernetes.","ru":"Шаблоны Linkerd предоставляют производственные шаблоны для сетки служб Linkerd, лёгкого и безопасного решения для Kubernetes.","ar":"نماط Linkerd توفر نمطز إنتاجية لشبكة خدمية Linkerd، حل خفيف وآمن ل Kubernetes.","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"definition":{"en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"features":{"pt":["Implementação de mTLS automático","Divisões de tráfego para implantações canary","Perfis de serviço para métricas por rota","Retentativas e temporizadores","Malha de serviço multi-cluster"],"ru":["Автоматическая реализация mTLS","Разделение трафика для канареечных развертываний","Профили служб для метрик по маршруту","Повторные попытки и таймауты","Мультiclusterная сетка служб"],"ar":["تنفيذ مTLS تلقائي","تقسيمات حركة المرور لتنصيب Canary","ملفات شخصية للخدمة لمقاييس المسار","معادلات و مهلات","شبكة خدمية متعددة المجموعة"]},"keywords":{"pt":["Linkerd","Malha de serviço","Kubernetes","mTLS","Divisões de tráfego","Perfis de serviço","Retentativas","Temporizadores","Multi-cluster"],"ru":["Linkerd","Сетка служб","Kubernetes","mTLS","Разделение трафика","Профили служб","Повторные попытки","Таймауты","Мультicluster"],"ar":["Linkerd","شبكة خدمية","Kubernetes","mTLS","تقسيمات حركة المرور","ملفات شخصية للخدمة","معادلات","مهلات","متعددة المجموعة"]}},"owner":"Dknight203","repo":"AesopIDE","repoPath":"Dknight203/AesopIDE","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"linkerd-patterns","description":"Implement Linkerd service mesh patterns for lightweight, security-focused service mesh deployments. Use when setting up Linkerd, configuring traffic policies, or implementing zero-trust networking with minimal overhead.","bodyPreview":"# Linkerd Patterns\n\nProduction patterns for Linkerd service mesh - the lightweight, security-first service mesh for Kubernetes.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up a lightweight service mesh\n- Implementing automatic mTLS\n- Configuring traffic splits for canary deployments\n- Setting up service profiles for per-route metrics\n- Implementing retries and timeouts\n- Multi-cluster service mesh\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Linkerd Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│","body":"# Linkerd Patterns\n\nProduction patterns for Linkerd service mesh - the lightweight, security-first service mesh for Kubernetes.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up a lightweight service mesh\n- Implementing automatic mTLS\n- Configuring traffic splits for canary deployments\n- Setting up service profiles for per-route metrics\n- Implementing retries and timeouts\n- Multi-cluster service mesh\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Linkerd Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                Control Plane                 │\n│  ┌─────────┐ ┌──────────┐ ┌──────────────┐ │\n│  │ destiny │ │ identity │ │ proxy-inject │ │\n│  └─────────┘ └──────────┘ └──────────────┘ │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                      │\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                 Data Plane                   │\n│  ┌─────┐    ┌─────┐    ┌─────┐             │\n│  │proxy│────│proxy│────│proxy│             │\n│  └─────┘    └─────┘    └─────┘             │\n│     │           │           │               │\n│  ┌──┴──┐    ┌──┴──┐    ┌──┴──┐            │\n│  │ app │    │ app │    │ app │            │\n│  └─────┘    └─────┘    └─────┘            │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### 2. Key Resources\n\n| Resource                | Purpose                              |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| **ServiceProfile**      | Per-route metrics, retries, timeouts |\n| **TrafficSplit**        | Canary deployments, A/B testing      |\n| **Server**              | Define server-side policies          |\n| **ServerAuthorization** | Access control policies              |\n\n## Templates\n\n### Template 1: Mesh Installation\n\n```bash\n# Install CLI\ncurl --proto ''=https'' --tlsv1.2 -sSfL https://run.linkerd.io/install | sh\n\n# Validate cluster\nlinkerd check --pre\n\n# Install CRDs\nlinkerd install --crds | kubectl apply -f -\n\n# Install control plane\nlinkerd install | kubectl apply -f -\n\n# Verify installation\nlinkerd check\n\n# Install viz extension (optional)\nlinkerd viz install | kubectl apply -f -\n```\n\n### Template 2: Inject Namespace\n\n```yaml\n# Automatic injection for namespace\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Namespace\nmetadata:\n  name: my-app\n  annotations:\n    linkerd.io/inject: enabled\n---\n# Or inject specific deployment\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: my-app\n  annotations:\n    linkerd.io/inject: enabled\nspec:\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      annotations:\n        linkerd.io/inject: enabled\n```\n\n### Template 3: Service Profile with Retries\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: linkerd.io/v1alpha2\nkind: ServiceProfile\nmetadata:\n  name: my-service.my-namespace.svc.cluster.local\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  routes:\n    - name: GET /api/users\n      condition:\n        method: GET\n        pathRegex: /api/users\n      responseClasses:\n        - condition:\n            status:\n              min: 500\n              max: 599\n          isFailure: true\n      isRetryable: true\n    - name: POST /api/users\n      condition:\n        method: POST\n        pathRegex: /api/users\n      # POST not retryable by default\n      isRetryable: false\n    - name: GET /api/users/{id}\n      condition:\n        method: GET\n        pathRegex: /api/users/[^/]+\n      timeout: 5s\n      isRetryable: true\n  retryBudget:\n    retryRatio: 0.2\n    minRetriesPerSecond: 10\n    ttl: 10s\n```\n\n### Template 4: Traffic Split (Canary)\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: split.smi-spec.io/v1alpha1\nkind: TrafficSplit\nmetadata:\n  name: my-service-canary\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  service: my-service\n  backends:\n    - service: my-service-stable\n      weight: 900m # 90%\n    - service: my-service-canary\n      weight: 100m # 10%\n```\n\n### Template 5: Server Authorization Policy\n\n```yaml\n# Define the server\napiVersion: policy.linkerd.io/v1beta1\nkind: Server\nmetadata:\n  name: my-service-http\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  podSelector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: my-service\n  port: http\n  proxyProtocol: HTTP/1\n---\n# Allow traffic from specific clients\napiVersion: policy.linkerd.io/v1beta1\nkind: ServerAuthorization\nmetadata:\n  name: allow-frontend\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  server:\n    name: my-service-http\n  client:\n    meshTLS:\n      serviceAccounts:\n        - name: frontend\n          namespace: my-namespace\n---\n# Allow unauthenticated traffic (e.g., from ingress)\napiVersion: policy.linkerd.io/v1beta1\nkind: ServerAuthorization\nmetadata:\n  name: allow-ingress\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  server:\n    name: my-service-http\n  client:\n    unauthenticated: true\n    networks:\n      - cidr: 10.0.0.0/8\n```\n\n### Template 6: HTTPRoute for Advanced Routing\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: policy.linkerd.io/v1beta2\nkind: HTTPRoute\nmetadata:\n  name: my-route\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  parentRefs:\n    - name: my-service\n      kind: Service\n      group: core\n      port: 8080\n  rules:\n    - matches:\n        - path:\n            type: PathPrefix\n            value: /api/v2\n        - headers:\n            - name: x-api-version\n              value: v2\n      backendRefs:\n        - name: my-service-v2\n          port: 8080\n    - matches:\n        - path:\n            type: PathPrefix\n            value: /api\n      backendRefs:\n        - name: my-service-v1\n          port: 8080\n```\n\n### Template 7: Multi-cluster Setup\n\n```bash\n# On each cluster, install with cluster credentials\nlinkerd multicluster install | kubectl apply -f -\n\n# Link clusters\nlinkerd multicluster link --cluster-name west \\\n  --api-server-address https://west.example.com:6443 \\\n  | kubectl apply -f -\n\n# Export a service to other clusters\nkubectl label svc/my-service mirror.linkerd.io/exported=true\n\n# Verify cross-cluster connectivity\nlinkerd multicluster check\nlinkerd multicluster gateways\n```\n\n## Monitoring Commands\n\n```bash\n# Live traffic view\nlinkerd viz top deploy/my-app\n\n# Per-route metrics\nlinkerd viz routes deploy/my-app\n\n# Check proxy status\nlinkerd viz stat deploy -n my-namespace\n\n# View service dependencies\nlinkerd viz edges deploy -n my-namespace\n\n# Dashboard\nlinkerd viz dashboard\n```\n\n## Debugging\n\n```bash\n# Check injection status\nlinkerd check --proxy -n my-namespace\n\n# View proxy logs\nkubectl logs deploy/my-app -c linkerd-proxy\n\n# Debug identity/TLS\nlinkerd identity -n my-namespace\n\n# Tap traffic (live)\nlinkerd viz tap deploy/my-app --to deploy/my-backend\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Enable mTLS everywhere** - It''s automatic with Linkerd\n- **Use ServiceProfiles** - Get per-route metrics and retries\n- **Set retry budgets** - Prevent retry storms\n- **Monitor golden metrics** - Success rate, latency, throughput\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t skip check** - Always run `linkerd check` after changes\n- **Don''t over-configure** - Linkerd defaults are sensible\n- **Don''t ignore ServiceProfiles** - They unlock advanced features\n- **Don''t forget timeouts** - Set appropriate values per route\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Linkerd Documentation](https://linkerd.io/2.14/overview/)\n- [Service Profiles](https://linkerd.io/2.14/features/service-profiles/)\n- [Authorization Policy](https://linkerd.io/2.14/features/server-policy/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T07:19:06.200Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Kubernetes Agents needing lightweight service mesh management with automatic mTLS and traffic splits","zh":"非常适合需要轻量级服务网格管理的Kubernetes Agents，具有自动mTLS和流量分配","ja":"Kubernetesエージェントが軽量のサービスメッシュ管理を必要とする場合に最適で、自動mTLSとトラフィック分割が可能","ko":"軽량級 서비스 메시 관리가 필요한 Kubernetes 에이전트에 적합하며 자동 mTLS 및 트래픽 분할 기능을 제공","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Kubernetes que necesitan una gestión de malla de servicio ligera con mTLS automático y división de tráfico","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Kubernetes qui ont besoin d''une gestion de mesh de service légère avec mTLS automatique et division de trafic","de":"Perfekt für Kubernetes-Agents, die eine leichte Service-Mesh-Verwaltung mit automatischem mTLS und Traffic-Splitting benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para agentes Kubernetes que necessitam de gerenciamento de malha de serviço leve com mTLS automático e divisão de tráfego","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Kubernetes, которым требуется легкое управление сетевой мешью с автоматическим mTLS и разделением трафика","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل Kubernetes التي تحتاج إلى إدارة شبكة خدمات خفيفة مع مTLS آلي وتقسيم حركة المرور"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to configure Linkerd service mesh for secure and scalable deployments, utilizing protocols like mTLS and features such as traffic splits for canary deployments, retries, and timeouts, all within a Kubernetes environment","zh":"赋予代理配置Linkerd服务网格的能力，以实现安全且可扩展的部署，利用mTLS、流量分割等协议和功能，实现金丝雀部署、重试和超时等功能，全都在Kubernetes环境中","ja":"エージェントがLinkerdサービスメッシュを構成して、セキュアでスケーラブルなデプロイを行うことを可能にし、mTLSやトラフィック分割などのプロトコルや機能を利用して、カナリアデプロイ、リトライ、タイムアウトなどの機能をKubernetes環境内で実現","ko":"에이전트가 Linkerd 서비스 메시지를 구성하여 보안이 뛰어난 확장 가능한 배포를 가능하게 하며, mTLS 및 트래픽 분할과 같은 프로토콜 및 기능을 사용하여 카나리 배포, 재시도, 시간 초과 등의 기능을 Kubernetes 환경에서 구현","es":"Habilita a los agentes a configurar el servicio mesh de Linkerd para implementaciones seguras y escalables, utilizando protocolos como mTLS y características como división de tráfico para implementaciones de canario, reintentos y tiempos de espera, todo dentro de un entorno de Kubernetes","fr":"Permet aux agents de configurer le service mesh Linkerd pour des déploiements sécurisés et évolutifs, en utilisant des protocoles comme mTLS et des fonctionnalités telles que la division de trafic pour les déploiements canari, les reprises et les délais d''attente, le tout dans un environnement Kubernetes","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, das Linkerd-Service-Mesh für sichere und skalierbare Bereitstellungen zu konfigurieren, wobei Protokolle wie mTLS und Funktionen wie Traffic-Splitting für Kanari-Implementierungen, Wiederholungen und Timeouts verwendet werden, alles innerhalb einer Kubernetes-Umgebung","pt":"Habilita os agentes a configurar a malha de serviço Linkerd para implantações seguras e escaláveis, utilizando protocolos como mTLS e recursos como divisão de tráfego para implantações canary, retries e timeouts, tudo dentro de um ambiente Kubernetes","ru":"Позволяет агентам настраивать сетевую мешь Linkerd для безопасных и масштабируемых развертываний, используя протоколы như mTLS и функции, такие как разделение трафика для канареечных развертываний, повторных попыток и таймаутов, все в среде Kubernetes","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تكوين شبكة الخدمات Linkerd لتنفيذها بأمان ومقياس مع استخدام بروتوكولات مثل مTLS وميزات مثل تقسيم حركة المرور لتنفيذات Канاري و المحاولات المتكررة وタイ أوت، كل ذلك داخل بيئة Kubernetes"},"useCases":{"en":["Setting up automatic mTLS for secure service communication","Configuring traffic splits for canary deployments and A/B testing","Implementing retries and timeouts for fault-tolerant service mesh"],"zh":["为安全的服务通信设置自动mTLS","为金丝雀部署和A/B测试配置流量分割","为容错服务网格实现重试和超时"],"ja":["セキュアなサービス通信のための自動mTLSの設定","カナリアデプロイとA/Bテストのためのトラフィック分割の設定","フォールトトレラントなサービスメッシュのためのリトライとタイムアウトの実装"],"ko":["보안 서비스 통신을 위한 자동 mTLS 설정","카나리 배포 및 A/B 테스트를 위한 트래픽 분할 구성","容错 서비스 메시를 위한 재시도 및 시간 초과 구현"],"es":["Configuración de mTLS automático para una comunicación de servicio segura","Configuración de división de tráfico para implementaciones de canario y pruebas A/B","Implementación de reintentos y tiempos de espera para un servicio mesh tolerante a fallos"],"fr":["Configuration de mTLS automatique pour une communication de service sécurisée","Configuration de la division de trafic pour les déploiements canari et les tests A/B","Mise en œuvre de reprises et de délais d''attente pour un service mesh tolérant aux défaillances"],"de":["Einrichtung von automatischem mTLS für eine sichere Dienstkommunikation","Konfiguration von Traffic-Splitting für Kanari-Implementierungen und A/B-Tests","Implementierung von Wiederholungen und Timeouts für ein fehlertolerantes Service-Mesh"],"pt":["Configurar mTLS automático para comunicação de serviço segura","Configurar divisão de tráfego para implantações canary e testes A/B","Implementar retries e timeouts para malha de serviço tolerante a falhas"],"ru":["Настроить автоматический mTLS для безопасной коммуникации сервисов","Настроить разделение трафика для канареечных развертываний и тестирования A/B","Реализовать повторные попытки и таймауты для сетевой меши, устойчивой к сбоям"],"ar":["تكوين مTLS آلي لتواصل الخدمات الآمن","تكوين تقسيم حركة المرور لتنفيذات الكناري واختبار A/B","تنفيذ المحاولات المتكررة وタイ أوت لشبكة خدمات متسامحة مع الفشل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Kubernetes environment","Linkerd service mesh specific"],"zh":["需要Kubernetes环境","特定于Linkerd服务网格"],"ja":["Kubernetes環境が必要","Linkerdサービスメッシュに特有"],"ko":["Kubernetes 환경이 필요","Linkerd 서비스 메시에 특정"],"es":["Requiere un entorno de Kubernetes","Específico del servicio mesh de Linkerd"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Kubernetes","Spécifique au service mesh Linkerd"],"de":["Benötigt eine Kubernetes-Umgebung","Spezifisch für das Linkerd-Service-Mesh"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Kubernetes","Específico da malha de serviço Linkerd"],"ru":["Требуется среда Kubernetes","Специфичен для сетевой меши Linkerd"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Kubernetes","محدد لشبكة الخدمات Linkerd"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/prompt-library', 'community', 'claudiodearaujo', 'IzaCenter', 'claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter', 'prompt-library', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z', '2026-02-19T07:19:08.536Z', NULL, '{"id":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/prompt-library","name":"prompt-library","description":{"zh":"Prompt Library 是一个全面的提示模板集合，提供 role-based 和 task-specific 的提示模式","ja":"プロンプトライブラリは、ロールベースとタスク固有のプロンプトパターンを提供する包括的なプロンプトテンプレートのコレクションです","ko":"프롬프트 라이브러리는 역할 기반 및 작업 특정 프롬프트 패턴을 제공하는 포괄적인 프롬프트 템플릿 컬렉션입니다","es":"La biblioteca de prompts es una colección exhaustiva de plantillas y patrones de prompts inspirados en las mejores prácticas de la comunidad","fr":"La bibliothèque de prompts est une collection exhaustive de modèles et de schémas de prompts inspirés des meilleures pratiques de la communauté","de":"Die Prompt-Bibliothek ist eine umfassende Sammlung von Vorlagen und Mustern für Prompts, die von den besten Praktiken der Community inspiriert sind","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Prompt Library 技术","ja":"プロンプトライブラリ","ko":"프롬프트 라이브러리","es":"Biblioteca de Prompts: Plantillas y Patrones para Desarro...","fr":"Bibliothèque de Prompts: Modèles et Schémas pour Développ...","de":"Prompt-Bibliothek: Vorlagen und Muster für Entwickler","en":"prompt-library"},"description":{"zh":"Prompt Library 是一个全面的提示模板集合，提供 role-based 和 task-specific 的提示模式","ja":"プロンプトライブラリは、ロールベースとタスク固有のプロンプトパターンを提供する包括的なプロンプトテンプレートのコレクションです","ko":"프롬프트 라이브러리는 역할 기반 및 작업 특정 프롬프트 패턴을 제공하는 포괄적인 프롬프트 템플릿 컬렉션입니다","es":"La biblioteca de prompts es una colección exhaustiva de plantillas y patrones de prompts inspirados en las mejores prácticas de la comunidad","fr":"La bibliothèque de prompts est une collection exhaustive de modèles et de schémas de prompts inspirés des meilleures pratiques de la communauté","de":"Die Prompt-Bibliothek ist eine umfassende Sammlung von Vorlagen und Mustern für Prompts, die von den besten Praktiken der Community inspiriert sind","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["角色基于的提示","任务特定的提示模式","预制的提示模板","社区最佳实践","灵感提示"],"ja":["ロールベースのプロンプト","タスク固有のプロンプトパターン","事前設定されたプロンプトテンプレート","コミュニティのベストプラクティス","インスピレーションプロンプト"],"ko":["역할 기반 프롬프트","작업 특정 프롬프트 패턴","사전 설정된 프롬프트 템플릿","커뮤니티 최고의 실践","영감 프롬프트"],"es":["Plantillas de prompts listas para usar","Patrones de prompts para roles específicos","Ejemplos de prompts para inspiración","Patrones de prompts para tareas específicas","Mejora de la habilidad de prompting"],"fr":["Modèles de prompts prêts à l''emploi","Schémas de prompts pour rôles spécifiques","Exemples de prompts pour l''inspiration","Schémas de prompts pour tâches spécifiques","Amélioration de la compétence de prompting"],"de":["Vorlagen für Prompts, die bereit für die Verwendung sind","Muster für Prompts für spezifische Rollen","Beispiele für Prompts zur Inspiration","Muster für Prompts für spezifische Aufgaben","Verbesserung der Prompting-Fähigkeit"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Prompt Library","提示模板","角色基于的提示","任务特定的提示模式","预制的提示模板","社区最佳实践"],"ja":["プロンプトライブラリ","プロンプトテンプレート","ロールベースのプロンプト","タスク固有のプロンプトパターン","事前設定されたプロンプトテンプレート","コミュニティのベストプラクティス"],"ko":["프롬프트 라이브러리","프롬프트 템플릿","역할 기반 프롬프트","작업 특정 프롬프트 패턴","사전 설정된 프롬프트 템플릿","커뮤니티 최고의 실践"],"es":["biblioteca de prompts","plantillas de prompts","patrones de prompts","roles de prompts","ejemplos de prompts","mejora de prompting","desarrollo de chatbots","IA conversacional"],"fr":["bibliothèque de prompts","modèles de prompts","schémas de prompts","rôles de prompts","exemples de prompts","amélioration de prompting","développement de chatbots","IA conversationnelle"],"de":["Prompt-Bibliothek","Vorlagen für Prompts","Muster für Prompts","Rollen für Prompts","Beispiele für Prompts","Verbesserung der Prompting-Fähigkeit","Entwicklung von Chatbots","konversationelle KI"]}},"owner":"claudiodearaujo","repo":"IzaCenter","repoPath":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"prompt-library","description":"Curated collection of high-quality prompts for various use cases. Includes role-based prompts, task-specific templates, and prompt refinement techniques. Use when user needs prompt templates, role-play prompts, or ready-to-use prompt examples for coding, writing, analysis, or creative tasks.","bodyPreview":"# 📝 Prompt Library\n\n> A comprehensive collection of battle-tested prompts inspired by [awesome-chatgpt-prompts](https://github.com/f/awesome-chatgpt-prompts) and community best practices.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when the user:\n\n- Needs ready-to-use prompt templates\n- Wants role-based prompts (act as X)\n- Asks for prompt examples or inspiration\n- Needs task-specific prompt patterns\n- Wants to improve their prompting\n\n## Prompt Categories\n\n### 🎭 Role-Based Prompts\n\n#### Expert","body":"# 📝 Prompt Library\n\n> A comprehensive collection of battle-tested prompts inspired by [awesome-chatgpt-prompts](https://github.com/f/awesome-chatgpt-prompts) and community best practices.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when the user:\n\n- Needs ready-to-use prompt templates\n- Wants role-based prompts (act as X)\n- Asks for prompt examples or inspiration\n- Needs task-specific prompt patterns\n- Wants to improve their prompting\n\n## Prompt Categories\n\n### 🎭 Role-Based Prompts\n\n#### Expert Developer\n\n```\nAct as an expert software developer with 15+ years of experience. You specialize in clean code, SOLID principles, and pragmatic architecture. When reviewing code:\n1. Identify bugs and potential issues\n2. Suggest performance improvements\n3. Recommend better patterns\n4. Explain your reasoning clearly\nAlways prioritize readability and maintainability over cleverness.\n```\n\n#### Code Reviewer\n\n```\nAct as a senior code reviewer. Your role is to:\n1. Check for bugs, edge cases, and error handling\n2. Evaluate code structure and organization\n3. Assess naming conventions and readability\n4. Identify potential security issues\n5. Suggest improvements with specific examples\n\nFormat your review as:\n🔴 Critical Issues (must fix)\n🟡 Suggestions (should consider)\n🟢 Praise (what''s done well)\n```\n\n#### Technical Writer\n\n```\nAct as a technical documentation expert. Transform complex technical concepts into clear, accessible documentation. Follow these principles:\n- Use simple language, avoid jargon\n- Include practical examples\n- Structure with clear headings\n- Add code snippets where helpful\n- Consider the reader''s experience level\n```\n\n#### System Architect\n\n```\nAct as a senior system architect designing for scale. Consider:\n- Scalability (horizontal and vertical)\n- Reliability (fault tolerance, redundancy)\n- Maintainability (modularity, clear boundaries)\n- Performance (latency, throughput)\n- Cost efficiency\n\nProvide architecture decisions with trade-off analysis.\n```\n\n### 🛠️ Task-Specific Prompts\n\n#### Debug This Code\n\n```\nDebug the following code. Your analysis should include:\n\n1. **Problem Identification**: What exactly is failing?\n2. **Root Cause**: Why is it failing?\n3. **Fix**: Provide corrected code\n4. **Prevention**: How to prevent similar bugs\n\nShow your debugging thought process step by step.\n```\n\n#### Explain Like I''m 5 (ELI5)\n\n```\nExplain [CONCEPT] as if I''m 5 years old. Use:\n- Simple everyday analogies\n- No technical jargon\n- Short sentences\n- Relatable examples from daily life\n- A fun, engaging tone\n```\n\n#### Code Refactoring\n\n```\nRefactor this code following these priorities:\n1. Readability first\n2. Remove duplication (DRY)\n3. Single responsibility per function\n4. Meaningful names\n5. Add comments only where necessary\n\nShow before/after with explanation of changes.\n```\n\n#### Write Tests\n\n```\nWrite comprehensive tests for this code:\n1. Happy path scenarios\n2. Edge cases\n3. Error conditions\n4. Boundary values\n\nUse [FRAMEWORK] testing conventions. Include:\n- Descriptive test names\n- Arrange-Act-Assert pattern\n- Mocking where appropriate\n```\n\n#### API Documentation\n\n```\nGenerate API documentation for this endpoint including:\n- Endpoint URL and method\n- Request parameters (path, query, body)\n- Request/response examples\n- Error codes and meanings\n- Authentication requirements\n- Rate limits if applicable\n\nFormat as OpenAPI/Swagger or Markdown.\n```\n\n### 📊 Analysis Prompts\n\n#### Code Complexity Analysis\n\n```\nAnalyze the complexity of this codebase:\n\n1. **Cyclomatic Complexity**: Identify complex functions\n2. **Coupling**: Find tightly coupled components\n3. **Cohesion**: Assess module cohesion\n4. **Dependencies**: Map critical dependencies\n5. **Technical Debt**: Highlight areas needing refactoring\n\nRate each area and provide actionable recommendations.\n```\n\n#### Performance Analysis\n\n```\nAnalyze this code for performance issues:\n\n1. **Time Complexity**: Big O analysis\n2. **Space Complexity**: Memory usage patterns\n3. **I/O Bottlenecks**: Database, network, disk\n4. **Algorithmic Issues**: Inefficient patterns\n5. **Quick Wins**: Easy optimizations\n\nPrioritize findings by impact.\n```\n\n#### Security Review\n\n```\nPerform a security review of this code:\n\n1. **Input Validation**: Check all inputs\n2. **Authentication/Authorization**: Access control\n3. **Data Protection**: Sensitive data handling\n4. **Injection Vulnerabilities**: SQL, XSS, etc.\n5. **Dependencies**: Known vulnerabilities\n\nClassify issues by severity (Critical/High/Medium/Low).\n```\n\n### 🎨 Creative Prompts\n\n#### Brainstorm Features\n\n```\nBrainstorm features for [PRODUCT]:\n\nFor each feature, provide:\n- Name and one-line description\n- User value proposition\n- Implementation complexity (Low/Med/High)\n- Dependencies on other features\n\nGenerate 10 ideas, then rank top 3 by impact/effort ratio.\n```\n\n#### Name Generator\n\n```\nGenerate names for [PROJECT/FEATURE]:\n\nProvide 10 options in these categories:\n- Descriptive (what it does)\n- Evocative (how it feels)\n- Acronyms (memorable abbreviations)\n- Metaphorical (analogies)\n\nFor each, explain the reasoning and check domain availability patterns.\n```\n\n### 🔄 Transformation Prompts\n\n#### Migrate Code\n\n```\nMigrate this code from [SOURCE] to [TARGET]:\n\n1. Identify equivalent constructs\n2. Handle incompatible features\n3. Preserve functionality exactly\n4. Follow target language idioms\n5. Add necessary dependencies\n\nShow the migration step by step with explanations.\n```\n\n#### Convert Format\n\n```\nConvert this [SOURCE_FORMAT] to [TARGET_FORMAT]:\n\nRequirements:\n- Preserve all data\n- Use idiomatic target format\n- Handle edge cases\n- Validate the output\n- Provide sample verification\n```\n\n## Prompt Engineering Techniques\n\n### Chain of Thought (CoT)\n\n```\nLet''s solve this step by step:\n1. First, I''ll understand the problem\n2. Then, I''ll identify the key components\n3. Next, I''ll work through the logic\n4. Finally, I''ll verify the solution\n\n[Your question here]\n```\n\n### Few-Shot Learning\n\n```\nHere are some examples of the task:\n\nExample 1:\nInput: [example input 1]\nOutput: [example output 1]\n\nExample 2:\nInput: [example input 2]\nOutput: [example output 2]\n\nNow complete this:\nInput: [actual input]\nOutput:\n```\n\n### Persona Pattern\n\n```\nYou are [PERSONA] with [TRAITS].\nYour communication style is [STYLE].\nYou prioritize [VALUES].\n\nWhen responding:\n- [Behavior 1]\n- [Behavior 2]\n- [Behavior 3]\n```\n\n### Structured Output\n\n```\nRespond in the following JSON format:\n{\n  \"analysis\": \"your analysis here\",\n  \"recommendations\": [\"rec1\", \"rec2\"],\n  \"confidence\": 0.0-1.0,\n  \"caveats\": [\"caveat1\"]\n}\n```\n\n## Prompt Improvement Checklist\n\nWhen crafting prompts, ensure:\n\n- [ ] **Clear objective**: What exactly do you want?\n- [ ] **Context provided**: Background information included?\n- [ ] **Format specified**: How should output be structured?\n- [ ] **Examples given**: Are there reference examples?\n- [ ] **Constraints defined**: Any limitations or requirements?\n- [ ] **Success criteria**: How do you measure good output?\n\n## Resources\n\n- [awesome-chatgpt-prompts](https://github.com/f/awesome-chatgpt-prompts)\n- [prompts.chat](https://prompts.chat)\n- [Learn Prompting](https://learnprompting.org/)\n\n---\n\n> 💡 **Tip**: The best prompts are specific, provide context, and include examples of desired output.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T07:19:08.536Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Conversational AI Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain needing advanced prompt engineering capabilities.","zh":"适用于 Claude Code、AutoGPT 和 LangChain 等对话式 AI 代理，需要高级提示工程能力。","ja":"Claude Code、AutoGPT、LangChain などの会話型 AI エージェントが、高度なプロンプトエンジニアリング機能を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"클라우드 코드, 오토지피티, 랭체인 등과 같은 대화형 AI 에이전트가 고급 프롬프트 엔지니어링 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial conversacional como Claude Code, AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de ingeniería de solicitudes.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle conversationnelle tels que Claude Code, AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant des capacités de génie de prompt avancées.","de":"Ideal für konversationelle KI-Agents wie Claude Code, AutoGPT und LangChain, die erweiterte Prompt-Engineering-Funktionen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal for Conversational AI Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain needing advanced prompt engineering capabilities.","ru":"Ideal for Conversational AI Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain needing advanced prompt engineering capabilities.","ar":"Ideal for Conversational AI Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain needing advanced prompt engineering capabilities."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality, task-specific prompts using role-based templates and community-driven best practices, leveraging categories like role-based prompts and task-specific prompt patterns.","zh":"通过基于角色的模板和社区驱动的最佳实践，赋予代理生成高质量、特定任务的提示，利用类别如基于角色的提示和特定任务的提示模式。","ja":"ロールベースのテンプレートとコミュニティ主導のベストプラクティスを使用して、高品質のタスク固有のプロンプトを生成するエージェントを可能にし、ロールベースのプロンプトやタスク固有のプロンプトパターンなどのカテゴリを活用します。","ko":"역할 기반 템플릿과 커뮤니티 주도적인 모범 사례를 통해 에이전트가 높은 품질의 작업 특정 프롬프트를 생성하도록 하며, 역할 기반 프롬프트 및 작업 특정 프롬프트 패턴과 같은 카테고리를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar solicitudes de alta calidad y específicas de tareas utilizando plantillas basadas en roles y mejores prácticas impulsadas por la comunidad, aprovechando categorías como solicitudes basadas en roles y patrones de solicitudes específicos de tareas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des invites de haute qualité et spécifiques aux tâches en utilisant des modèles basés sur les rôles et les meilleures pratiques impulsées par la communauté, en exploitant des catégories comme les invites basées sur les rôles et les modèles d''invites spécifiques aux tâches.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, hochwertige, aufgabenbezogene Prompts mit rollenbasierten Vorlagen und communitygetriebenen Best Practices zu generieren, indem Kategorien wie rollenbasierte Prompts und aufgabenbezogene Promptmuster genutzt werden.","pt":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality, task-specific prompts using role-based templates and community-driven best practices, leveraging categories like role-based prompts and task-specific prompt patterns.","ru":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality, task-specific prompts using role-based templates and community-driven best practices, leveraging categories like role-based prompts and task-specific prompt patterns.","ar":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality, task-specific prompts using role-based templates and community-driven best practices, leveraging categories like role-based prompts and task-specific prompt patterns."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating expert-level prompts for user queries","Creating role-based conversational flows","Improving prompt quality for better user engagement"],"zh":["为用户查询生成专家级提示","创建基于角色的会话流","提高提示质量以提高用户参与度"],"ja":["ユーザー クエリのためのエキスパート レベルのプロンプトを生成する","ロール ベースの会話 フローを作成する","ユーザー エンゲージメントの向上のためのプロンプトの品質を高める"],"ko":["사용자 쿼리용 전문가 수준의 프롬프트 생성","역할 기반 대화 흐름 생성","사용자 참여 향상을 위한 프롬프트 품질 개선"],"es":["Generar solicitudes de nivel experto para consultas de usuarios","Crear flujos de conversación basados en roles","Mejorar la calidad de las solicitudes para una mejor participación del usuario"],"fr":["Générer des invites de niveau expert pour les requêtes des utilisateurs","Créer des flux de conversation basés sur les rôles","Améliorer la qualité des invites pour une meilleure implication de l''utilisateur"],"de":["Generieren von expertenlevel-Prompts für Benutzeranfragen","Erstellen von rollenbasierten Konversationsflüssen","Verbesserung der Promptqualität für eine bessere Benutzereinbindung"],"pt":["Generating expert-level prompts for user queries","Creating role-based conversational flows","Improving prompt quality for better user engagement"],"ru":["Generating expert-level prompts for user queries","Creating role-based conversational flows","Improving prompt quality for better user engagement"],"ar":["Generating expert-level prompts for user queries","Creating role-based conversational flows","Improving prompt quality for better user engagement"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires integration with AI agent''s natural language processing capabilities","Limited to text-based prompt generation"],"zh":["需要集成到 AI 代理的自然语言处理能力","仅限文本基于提示生成"],"ja":["AI エージェントの自然言語処理機能との統合が必要","テキストベースのプロンプト生成に限定される"],"ko":["에이전트의 자연어 처리 능력과 통합이 필요","텍스트 기반 프롬프트 생성에 한정"],"es":["Requiere integración con las capacidades de procesamiento de lenguaje natural del agente de inteligencia artificial","Limitado a la generación de solicitudes basadas en texto"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec les capacités de traitement du langage naturel de l''agent d''intelligence artificielle","Limité à la génération d''invites basées sur le texte"],"de":["Erfordert Integration mit den natürlichen Sprachverarbeitungsfähigkeiten des KI-Agents","Begrenzt auf die Generierung von textbasierten Prompts"],"pt":["Requires integration with AI agent''s natural language processing capabilities","Limited to text-based prompt generation"],"ru":["Requires integration with AI agent''s natural language processing capabilities","Limited to text-based prompt generation"],"ar":["Requires integration with AI agent''s natural language processing capabilities","Limited to text-based prompt generation"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/agent-manager-skill', 'community', 'claudiodearaujo', 'IzaCenter', 'claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter', 'agent-manager-skill', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z', '2026-02-19T07:19:06.453Z', NULL, '{"id":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter/agent-manager-skill","name":"agent-manager-skill","description":{"es":"El skill de gestor de agentes permite ejecutar múltiples agentes CLI en paralelo y gestionar tareas de forma eficiente","fr":"Le skill de gestion d''agents permet d''exécuter plusieurs agents CLI en parallèle et de gérer des tâches de manière efficace","de":"Das Agenten-Manager-Skill ermöglicht die Ausführung mehrerer CLI-Agents parallel und die effiziente Verwaltung von Aufgaben","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Gestor de Agentes: Administra Múltiples Agentes CLI","fr":"Agent Manager: Gérez Plusieurs Agents CLI","de":"Agenten-Manager: Verwalten Sie Mehrere CLI-Agents","en":"agent-manager-skill"},"description":{"es":"El skill de gestor de agentes permite ejecutar múltiples agentes CLI en paralelo y gestionar tareas de forma eficiente","fr":"Le skill de gestion d''agents permet d''exécuter plusieurs agents CLI en parallèle et de gérer des tâches de manière efficace","de":"Das Agenten-Manager-Skill ermöglicht die Ausführung mehrerer CLI-Agents parallel und die effiziente Verwaltung von Aufgaben","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"es":["Ejecución de múltiples agentes CLI en paralelo","Gestión de tareas y seguimiento de logs","Asignación de tareas a agentes y monitoreo de salida","Programación de trabajo de agentes recurrente","Uso de tmux para sesiones separadas"],"fr":["Exécution de plusieurs agents CLI en parallèle","Gestion de tâches et suivi de logs","Assignation de tâches à des agents et surveillance de la sortie","Planification de travail d''agent récurrent","Utilisation de tmux pour des sessions séparées"],"de":["Ausführung mehrerer CLI-Agents parallel","Verwaltung von Aufgaben und Überwachung von Logs","Zuweisung von Aufgaben zu Agents und Überwachung der Ausgabe","Planung von wiederkehrender Agentenarbeit","Verwendung von tmux für separate Sitzungen"]},"keywords":{"es":["gestor de agentes","agentes CLI","tmux","gestión de tareas","programación de trabajo","desarrollo de software","automatización de tareas"],"fr":["gestion d''agents","agents CLI","tmux","gestion de tâches","planification de travail","développement de logiciels","automatisation de tâches"],"de":["Agenten-Manager","CLI-Agents","tmux","Aufgabenverwaltung","Arbeitsplanung","Softwareentwicklung","Aufgabenautomatisierung"]}},"owner":"claudiodearaujo","repo":"IzaCenter","repoPath":"claudiodearaujo/IzaCenter","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"agent-manager-skill","description":"Manage multiple local CLI agents via tmux sessions (start/stop/monitor/assign) with cron-friendly scheduling.","bodyPreview":"# Agent Manager Skill\n\n## When to use\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n\n- run multiple local CLI agents in parallel (separate tmux sessions)\n- start/stop agents and tail their logs\n- assign tasks to agents and monitor output\n- schedule recurring agent work (cron)\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nInstall `agent-manager-skill` in your workspace:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/fractalmind-ai/agent-manager-skill.git\n```\n\n## Common commands\n\n```bash\npython3 agent-manager/scripts/main.py doctor\npython3 agen","body":"# Agent Manager Skill\n\n## When to use\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n\n- run multiple local CLI agents in parallel (separate tmux sessions)\n- start/stop agents and tail their logs\n- assign tasks to agents and monitor output\n- schedule recurring agent work (cron)\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nInstall `agent-manager-skill` in your workspace:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/fractalmind-ai/agent-manager-skill.git\n```\n\n## Common commands\n\n```bash\npython3 agent-manager/scripts/main.py doctor\npython3 agent-manager/scripts/main.py list\npython3 agent-manager/scripts/main.py start EMP_0001\npython3 agent-manager/scripts/main.py monitor EMP_0001 --follow\npython3 agent-manager/scripts/main.py assign EMP_0002 <<''EOF''\nFollow teams/fractalmind-ai-maintenance.md Workflow\nEOF\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- Requires `tmux` and `python3`.\n- Agents are configured under an `agents/` directory (see the repo for examples).\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T07:19:06.453Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Multi-Agent Systems needing concurrent CLI agent management and task automation.","zh":"适用于需要同时进行多代理系统的CLI代理管理和任务自动化的场景。","ja":"マルチエージェントシステムでCLIエージェントの管理とタスクの自動化を同時に行う必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"다중 에이전트 시스템에서 CLI 에이전트 관리와 태스크 자동화를 동시에 수행해야 하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Sistemas de Multiagentes que necesitan gestión concurrente de agentes CLI y automatización de tareas.","fr":"Idéal pour les systèmes multi-agents nécessitant une gestion concurrente des agents CLI et une automatisation des tâches.","de":"Ideal für Multiagentensysteme, die eine gleichzeitige Verwaltung von CLI-Agents und eine Automatisierung von Aufgaben benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Sistemas de Múltiplos Agentes que necessitam de gerenciamento de agentes CLI concorrentes e automação de tarefas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Многоагентных Систем, требующих параллельного управления агентами CLI и автоматизации задач.","ar":"مثالية لأنظمة العوامل المتعددة التي تحتاج إلى إدارة عدة عوامل واجهة سطر الأوامر وتحكم آلي في المهام."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to run multiple local CLI agents in parallel using separate tmux sessions, start/stop agents, and tail their logs, while also scheduling recurring agent work via cron, all leveraging Python 3 and Git for version control.","zh":"使代理能够使用独立的tmux会话并行运行多个本地CLI代理，启动/停止代理，并实时监控日志，同时还可以使用cron调度代理的周期性工作，所有功能都利用Python 3和Git进行版本控制。","ja":"エージェントが独立したtmuxセッションを使用して複数のローカルCLIエージェントを並行して実行し、エージェントを起動/停止し、ログをリアルタイムで監視することを可能にし、cronを使用してエージェントの定期的な作業をスケジュールすることができます。すべての機能はPython 3とGitを使用してバージョン管理を行います。","ko":"에이전트가 별도의 tmux 세션을 사용하여 여러 로컬 CLI 에이전트를 병렬로 실행하고, 에이전트를 시작/중지하고, 로그를 실시간으로 모니터링 할 수 있으며, cron을 사용하여 에이전트의 반복 작업을 예약할 수 있습니다. 모든 기능은 Python 3 및 Git을 사용하여 버전 관리됩니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes ejecutar varios agentes CLI locales en paralelo utilizando sesiones tmux separadas, iniciar/detener agentes y seguir sus registros, y también programar trabajos de agente recurrentes a través de cron, todo aprovechando Python 3 y Git para el control de versiones.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter plusieurs agents CLI locaux en parallèle à l''aide de sessions tmux distinctes, de démarrer/arrêter les agents et de suivre leurs journaux, tout en planifiant des tâches d''agent récurrentes via cron, en exploitant Python 3 et Git pour le contrôle de version.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, mehrere lokale CLI-Agents parallel mithilfe separater tmux-Sitzungen auszuführen, Agents zu starten/stoppen und ihre Protokolle zu verfolgen, und plant auch regelmäßige Agentenarbeiten über cron, alles unter Nutzung von Python 3 und Git für die Versionskontrolle.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar vários agentes CLI locais em paralelo usando sessões tmux separadas, iniciar/parar agentes e monitorar seus logs, além de agendar trabalho de agente recorrente via cron, tudo aproveitando Python 3 e Git para controle de versão.","ru":"Позволяет агентам запускать несколько местных агентов CLI параллельно, используя отдельные сессии tmux, запускать/останавливать агентов и отслеживать их журналы, а также планировать повторяющуюся работу агентов через cron, все это, используя Python 3 и Git для контроля версий.","ar":"تمكّن العوامل من تشغيل عدة عوامل واجهة سطر الأوامر المحلية بشكل متوازي باستخدام جلسات tmux منفصلة، وبدء/إيقاف العوامل، وتحديث سجلاتها، بالإضافة إلى جدولة عمل العوامل المتكرر عبر cron، وكل ذلك بالاستفادة من Python 3 و Git للتحكم في الإصدارات."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating agent deployment and management across multiple tmux sessions","Debugging agent logs and output in real-time","Scheduling recurring tasks for agents using cron jobs"],"zh":["跨多个tmux会话自动化代理部署和管理","实时调试代理日志和输出","使用cron作业为代理安排周期性任务"],"ja":["複数のtmuxセッションを横断してエージェントの展開と管理を自動化する","エージェントのログと出力をリアルタイムでデバッグする","cronジョブを使用してエージェントの定期的なタスクをスケジュールする"],"ko":["여러 tmux 세션에서 에이전트 배포 및 관리를 자동화하는 것","에이전트 로그 및 출력을 실시간으로 디버깅하는 것","cron 작업을 사용하여 에이전트의 반복 작업을 예약하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de la implementación y gestión de agentes en varias sesiones tmux","Depuración de registros y salida de agentes en tiempo real","Programación de tareas recurrentes para agentes mediante trabajos cron"],"fr":["Automatisation du déploiement et de la gestion des agents sur plusieurs sessions tmux","Débogage des journaux et de la sortie des agents en temps réel","Planification de tâches récurrentes pour les agents via des tâches cron"],"de":["Automatisierung der Bereitstellung und Verwaltung von Agents in mehreren tmux-Sitzungen","Fehlersuche von Agentenprotokollen und -ausgaben in Echtzeit","Planung regelmäßiger Aufgaben für Agents mithilfe von cron-Jobs"],"pt":["Automatizar implantação e gerenciamento de agentes em várias sessões tmux","Depurar logs e saída de agentes em tempo real","Agendar tarefas recorrentes para agentes usando trabalhos cron"],"ru":["Автоматизировать развертывание и управление агентами в нескольких сессиях tmux","Отлаживать журналы и вывод агентов в режиме реального времени","Планировать повторяющиеся задачи для агентов с помощью заданий cron"],"ar":["أتمتة نشر العوامل وإدارتها عبر عدة جلسات tmux","تصحيح أخطاء سجلات العوامل ومخرجاتها في الوقت الفعلي","جدولة مهام متكررة للعوامل باستخدام مهام cron"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python 3 and Git installation","Limited to local CLI agents","Dependent on tmux for session management"],"zh":["需要Python 3和Git的安装","仅限于本地CLI代理","依赖于tmux进行会话管理"],"ja":["Python 3とGitのインストールが必要","ローカルCLIエージェントのみに対応","セッション管理にはtmuxに依存する"],"ko":["Python 3 및 Git 설치가 필요합니다.","로컬 CLI 에이전트만 해당됩니다.","세션 관리에는 tmux에 의존합니다."],"es":["Requiere la instalación de Python 3 y Git","Limitado a agentes CLI locales","Dependiente de tmux para la gestión de sesiones"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de Python 3 et de Git","Limité aux agents CLI locaux","Dépendant de tmux pour la gestion des sessions"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation von Python 3 und Git","Begrenzt auf lokale CLI-Agents","Abhängig von tmux für die Sitzungsverwaltung"],"pt":["Requer instalação do Python 3 e Git","Limitado a agentes CLI locais","Dependente do tmux para gerenciamento de sessões"],"ru":["Требует установки Python 3 и Git","Ограничен местными агентами CLI","Зависит от tmux для управления сессиями"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت Python 3 و Git","محدود بالعوامل واجهة سطر الأوامر المحلية","يعتمد على tmux لإدارة الجلسات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ondata/albopopTwoDotZero/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'ondata', 'albopopTwoDotZero', 'ondata/albopopTwoDotZero', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z', '2026-02-19T07:23:37.299Z', NULL, '{"id":"ondata/albopopTwoDotZero/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"OpenSpec 入门指南，完成首个工作流程周期","ja":"OpenSpec を使用して最初のワークフロー サイクルを完了する","ko":"OpenSpec로 첫 번째 워크플로 사이클 완료","es":"OpenSpec Onboard es una guía que te lleva a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo completo con OpenSpec","fr":"OpenSpec Onboard est un guide qui vous accompagne tout au long de votre premier cycle de travail complet avec OpenSpec","de":"OpenSpec Onboard ist ein Leitfaden, der Sie durch Ihren ersten vollständigen OpenSpec-Arbeitszyklus führt","pt":"O openspec-onboard é um guia para o primeiro ciclo de trabalho OpenSpec, incluindo inicialização e configuração.","ru":"Openspec-onboard - это руководство для первого рабочего цикла OpenSpec, включая инициализацию и настройку.","ar":"openspec-onboard هو دليل لدورة العمل الأولى OpenSpec ، بما في ذلك التهيئة والتهيئة.","en":"Albopop 2.0"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec 入门指南","ja":"OpenSpec を始める","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기","es":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guía de configuración","fr":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guide de configuration","de":"OpenSpec Onboard: Konfigurationsleitfaden","pt":"Onboard OpenSpec: Inicie com o Fluxo de Trabalho Completo","ru":"Начало работы с OpenSpec: прохождение полного рабочего цикла","ar":"بدء عمل OpenSpec: إكمال دورة العمل الكاملة","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"OpenSpec 入门指南，完成首个工作流程周期","ja":"OpenSpec を使用して最初のワークフロー サイクルを完了する","ko":"OpenSpec로 첫 번째 워크플로 사이클 완료","es":"OpenSpec Onboard es una guía que te lleva a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo completo con OpenSpec","fr":"OpenSpec Onboard est un guide qui vous accompagne tout au long de votre premier cycle de travail complet avec OpenSpec","de":"OpenSpec Onboard ist ein Leitfaden, der Sie durch Ihren ersten vollständigen OpenSpec-Arbeitszyklus führt","pt":"O openspec-onboard é um guia para o primeiro ciclo de trabalho OpenSpec, incluindo inicialização e configuração.","ru":"Openspec-onboard - это руководство для первого рабочего цикла OpenSpec, включая инициализацию и настройку.","ar":"openspec-onboard هو دليل لدورة العمل الأولى OpenSpec ، بما في ذلك التهيئة والتهيئة.","en":"Albopop 2.0"},"definition":{"en":"Albopop 2.0"},"features":{"zh":["初始化 OpenSpec","检查 OpenSpec 状态","完成首个工作流程周期","实时代码库操作","步骤解释"],"ja":["OpenSpec の初期化","OpenSpec の状態を確認","最初のワークフロー サイクルを完了","実際のコードベース操作","ステップ別の解説"],"ko":["OpenSpec 초기화","OpenSpec 상태 확인","첫 번째 워크플로 사이클 완료","실제 코드베이스操作","단계별 설명"],"es":["Guía paso a paso para configurar OpenSpec","Verificación del estado de inicialización de OpenSpec","Incorporación de funcionalidades de OpenSpec en el código","Explicación detallada de cada paso del proceso","Compatibilidad con proyectos de código abierto"],"fr":["Guide étape par étape pour configurer OpenSpec","Vérification de l''état d''initialisation d''OpenSpec","Intégration des fonctionnalités d''OpenSpec dans le code","Explication détaillée de chaque étape du processus","Compatibilité avec les projets de code ouvert"],"de":["Schritt-für-Schritt-Anleitung zur Konfiguration von OpenSpec","Überprüfung des Initialisierungsstatus von OpenSpec","Integration von OpenSpec-Funktionen in den Code","Detaillierte Erklärung jeder Phase des Prozesses","Kompatibilität mit Open-Source-Projekten"],"pt":["Iniciação do OpenSpec","Verificação do status do OpenSpec","Configuração do fluxo de trabalho","Explicação passo a passo","Trabalho real no código","Ciclo de trabalho completo"],"ru":["Инициализация OpenSpec","Проверка статуса OpenSpec","Настройка рабочего процесса","Пошаговое объяснение","Реальная работа с кодом","Полный рабочий цикл"],"ar":["تهيئة OpenSpec","التحقق من حالة OpenSpec","تهيئة دورة العمل","شرح خطوة بخطوة","العمل الحقيقي على الكود","دورة العمل الكاملة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","工作流管理","代码库操作","开发工具","开发者指南","工作流自动化"],"ja":["OpenSpec","ワークフロー管理","コードベース操作","開発ツール","開発者向けガイド","ワークフロー自動化"],"ko":["OpenSpec","워크플로 관리","코드베이스操作","개발 도구","개발자 가이드","워크플로 자동화"],"es":["OpenSpec","configuración de OpenSpec","guía de OpenSpec","ciclo de trabajo de OpenSpec","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","código abierto"],"fr":["OpenSpec","configuration d''OpenSpec","guide d''OpenSpec","cycle de travail d''OpenSpec","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","code ouvert"],"de":["OpenSpec","Konfiguration von OpenSpec","OpenSpec-Anleitung","Arbeitszyklus von OpenSpec","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools","Open-Source-Code"],"pt":["OpenSpec","onboard","iniciação","fluxo de trabalho","desenvolvimento","programação","tecnologia","guia","tutorial"],"ru":["OpenSpec","onboard","начало работы","рабочий процесс","разработка","программирование","технологии","руководство","урок"],"ar":["OpenSpec","onboard","بدء عمل","دورة العمل","التطوير","البرمجة","التكنولوجيا","دليل","دورة تعليمية"]}},"owner":"ondata","repo":"albopopTwoDotZero","repoPath":"ondata/albopopTwoDotZero","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.544Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T07:23:37.299Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing guided OpenSpec workflow integration.","zh":"非常适合需要引导式 OpenSpec 工作流集成的开发代理。","ja":"OpenSpec ワークフロー統合を導入する開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"가이드된 OpenSpec 워크플로 통합이 필요한 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan integración de flujo de trabajo OpenSpec guiada.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une intégration de workflow OpenSpec guidée.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine guidierte OpenSpec-Workflow-Integration benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de integração de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec orientada.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым требуется руководство по интеграции рабочего процесса OpenSpec.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النمذجة الذين يحتاجون إلى تكامل سير عمل OpenSpec الموجه."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to initialize and manage OpenSpec projects, providing a seamless workflow cycle experience through JSON status checks and command-line interactions like `openspec init` and `openspec status`.","zh":"赋予代理初始化和管理 OpenSpec 项目的能力，通过 JSON 状态检查和命令行交互（如 `openspec init` 和 `openspec status`）提供无缝的工作流循环体验。","ja":"エージェントに OpenSpec プロジェクトを初期化および管理する機能を提供し、JSON ステータス チェックやコマンドラインのやり取り（例： `openspec init` および `openspec status`）を通じてシームレスなワークフロー サイクル エクスペリエンスを提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 OpenSpec 프로젝트를 초기화하고 관리할 수 있도록 하며, JSON 상태 확인 및 명령줄 상호 작용(`openspec init` 및 `openspec status` 등)을 통해 무결점 워크플로 사이클 경험을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a inicializar y gestionar proyectos OpenSpec, proporcionando una experiencia de ciclo de trabajo fluida a través de comprobaciones de estado JSON y de interacciones de línea de comandos como `openspec init` y `openspec status`.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''initialiser et de gérer des projets OpenSpec, offrant une expérience de cycle de travail fluide grâce aux vérifications d''état JSON et aux interactions de ligne de commande comme `openspec init` et `openspec status`.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, OpenSpec-Projekte zu initialisieren und zu verwalten und bietet so eine nahtlose Workflow-Zyklus-Erfahrung durch JSON-Statusprüfungen und Befehlszeileninteraktionen wie `openspec init` und `openspec status`.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a inicializar e gerenciar projetos OpenSpec, fornecendo uma experiência de ciclo de trabalho contínuo através de verificações de status JSON e interações de linha de comando como `openspec init` e `openspec status`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью инициализировать и управлять проектами OpenSpec, обеспечивая бесшовный опыт цикла рабочего процесса через проверки статуса JSON и взаимодействия с командной строкой, такие как `openspec init` и `openspec status`.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على 초기ته وتشغيل مشاريع OpenSpec، مما يوفر تجربة دورة عمل سلسة من خلال عمليات التحقق من حالة JSON وتفاعلات سطر الأوامر مثل `openspec init` و `openspec status`."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing OpenSpec in new projects","Guiding users through their first OpenSpec workflow cycle","Debugging OpenSpec initialization issues with `openspec status --json`"],"zh":["在新项目中初始化 OpenSpec","指导用户完成他们的第一个 OpenSpec 工作流循环","使用 `openspec status --json` 调试 OpenSpec 初始化问题"],"ja":["新しいプロジェクトで OpenSpec を初期化する","ユーザーが最初の OpenSpec ワークフロー サイクルを実行するためのガイダンス","`openspec status --json` を使用して OpenSpec 初期化の問題をデバッグする"],"ko":["새 프로젝트에서 OpenSpec 초기화","사용자가 첫 번째 OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클을 완료하는 것을 도와줌","`openspec status --json`를 사용하여 OpenSpec 초기화 문제를 디버깅"],"es":["Inicializar OpenSpec en nuevos proyectos","Guía a los usuarios a través de su primer ciclo de trabajo OpenSpec","Depurar problemas de inicialización de OpenSpec con `openspec status --json`"],"fr":["Initialiser OpenSpec dans de nouveaux projets","Guider les utilisateurs à travers leur premier cycle de travail OpenSpec","Déboguer les problèmes d''initialisation d''OpenSpec avec `openspec status --json`"],"de":["OpenSpec in neuen Projekten initialisieren","Benutzer durch ihren ersten OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklus führen","OpenSpec-Initialisierungsprobleme mit `openspec status --json` debuggen"],"pt":["Inicializar OpenSpec em novos projetos","Orientar os usuários durante seu primeiro ciclo de trabalho OpenSpec","Depurar problemas de inicialização do OpenSpec com `openspec status --json`"],"ru":["Инициализация OpenSpec в новых проектах","Руководство пользователями во время их первого цикла рабочего процесса OpenSpec","Отладка проблем инициализации OpenSpec с помощью `openspec status --json`"],"ar":["ت初يته OpenSpec في مشاريع جديدة","توجيه المستخدمين خلال دورة عمل OpenSpec الأولى","تصحيح أخطاء 초기ته OpenSpec باستخدام `openspec status --json`"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OpenSpec to be installed and accessible via the command line","Must run `openspec init` before using the skill"],"zh":["需要 OpenSpec 已安装并可以通过命令行访问","必须在使用技能之前运行 `openspec init`"],"ja":["OpenSpec がインストールされ、コマンドラインからアクセス可能である必要がある","スキルを使用する前に `openspec init` を実行する必要がある"],"ko":["OpenSpec가 설치되어 명령줄에서 액세스할 수 있어야 함","스킬을 사용하기 전에 `openspec init`를 실행해야 함"],"es":["Requiere que OpenSpec esté instalado y sea accesible a través de la línea de comandos","Debe ejecutar `openspec init` antes de usar la habilidad"],"fr":["Nécessite que OpenSpec soit installé et accessible via la ligne de commande","Doit exécuter `openspec init` avant d''utiliser la compétence"],"de":["Benötigt, dass OpenSpec installiert und über die Befehlszeile zugänglich ist","Muss `openspec init` ausführen, bevor die Fähigkeit verwendet wird"],"pt":["Exige que o OpenSpec esteja instalado e acessível via linha de comando","Deve executar `openspec init` antes de usar a habilidade"],"ru":["Требует, чтобы OpenSpec был установлен и доступен через командную строку","Необходимо запустить `openspec init` перед использованием умения"],"ar":["يتطلب أن يكون OpenSpec مثبتًا وقابل الوصول عبر سطر الأوامر","يجب تشغيل `openspec init` قبل استخدام المهارة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
