大的设计系统的技能，确保视觉一致性和优异的用户体验","ja":"デザインシステムスターターは、信頼性の高い設計システムを構築するためのスキルで、視覚的一貫性と優れたユーザー エクスペリエンスを実現します","ko":"디자인 시스템 시작하기는 강력한 디자인 시스템을 구축하기 위한 스킬로, 시각적 일관성과优秀한 사용자 경험을 제공합니다","es":"El skill design-system-starter te permite crear sistemas de diseño robustos y escalables con tokens, componentes y pautas de accesibilidad","fr":"Le skill design-system-starter vous permet de créer des systèmes de conception robustes et évolutifs avec des jetons, des composants et des directives d''acce...","de":"Der Skill design-system-starter ermöglicht es Ihnen, robuste und skalierbare Designsysteme mit Token, Komponenten und Barrierefreiheitsrichtlinien zu erstellen","pt":"Construa sistemas de design robustos e escaláveis para garantir consistência visual e experiências de usuário excepcionais","ru":"Постройте надежные и масштабируемые системы дизайна для обеспечения визуальной согласованности и исключительных пользовательских trải nghiệm","ar":"ابني أنظمة تصميم متينة وقابلة للتحجيم لضمان الاتساق البصري وتجارب المستخدم الاستثنائية","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"definition":{"en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"features":{"zh":["构建可扩展的设计系统","确保视觉一致性","提供优异的用户体验","支持暗黑模式","提供设计令牌和组件","提供无障碍指南"],"ja":["拡張可能な設計システムを構築","視覚的一貫性を確保","優れたユーザー エクスペリエンスを提供","ダーク モードをサポート","設計トークンとコンポーネントを提供","アクセシビリティ ガイドラインを提供"],"ko":["확장 가능한 디자인 시스템을 구축","시각적 일관성을 제공","优秀한 사용자 경험을 제공","다크 모드 지원","디자인 토큰과 컴포넌트 제공","접근성 가이드라인 제공"],"es":["Tokens de diseño personalizables","Componentes reutilizables","Pautas de accesibilidad","Compatibilidad con modos de diseño oscuro","Integración con React"],"fr":["Jetons de conception personalisés","Composants réutilisables","Directives d''accessibilité","Compatibilité avec les modes de conception sombre","Intégration avec React"],"de":["Anpassbare Design-Tokens","Wiederverwendbare Komponenten","Barrierefreiheitsrichtlinien","Kompatibilität mit dunklen Designmodi","Integration mit React"],"pt":["Crie tokens de design personalizados","Desenvolva componentes reutilizáveis","Garanta acessibilidade e usabilidade","Suporte a modos de exibição personalizados","Integração com frameworks populares"],"ru":["Создайте пользовательские дизайн-токены","Разработайте многократно используемые компоненты","Обеспечьте доступность и удобство использования","Поддержка пользовательских режимов отображения","Интеграция с популярными фреймворками"],"ar":["أنشئ رموز تصميم مخصصة","طور مكونات قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام","ضمن إمكانية الوصول وسلاسة الاستخدام","دعم أوضاع العرض المخصصة","التكامل مع الإطارات الشائعة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["设计系统","可扩展设计","视觉一致性","用户体验","暗黑模式","设计令牌","组件","无障碍指南"],"ja":["設計システム","拡張可能な設計","視覚的一貫性","ユーザー エクスペリエンス","ダーク モード","設計トークン","コンポーネント","アクセシビリティ ガイドライン"],"ko":["디자인 시스템","확장 가능한 디자인","시각적 일관성","사용자 경험","다크 모드","디자인 토큰","컴포넌트","접근성 가이드라인"],"es":["sistema de diseño","design system","tokens de diseño","componentes reutilizables","accesibilidad","modo oscuro","React","desarrollo de software","experiencia de usuario"],"fr":["système de conception","design system","jetons de conception","composants réutilisables","accessibilité","mode sombre","React","développement de logiciels","expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Designsystem","design system","Design-Tokens","wiederverwendbare Komponenten","Barrierefreiheit","dunkles Design","React","Software-Entwicklung","Benutzererfahrung"],"pt":["sistema de design","design system","tokens de design","componentes reutilizáveis","acessibilidade","usabilidade","modos de exibição personalizados","frameworks populares"],"ru":["система дизайна","дизайн-система","дизайн-токены","многократно используемые компоненты","доступность","удобство использования","пользовательские режимы отображения","популярные фреймворки"],"ar":["نظام التصميم","تصميم نظام","رموز التصميم","مكونات قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام","إمكانية الوصول","سلاسة الاستخدام","أوضاع العرض المخصصة","الإطارات الشائعة"]}},"owner":"Dknight203","repo":"AesopIDE","repoPath":"Dknight203/AesopIDE","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:03:48.183Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"design-system-starter","description":"Create and evolve design systems with design tokens, component architecture, accessibility guidelines, and documentation templates. Ensures consistent, scalable, and accessible UI across products.","version":"1.0.0","tags":["design-system","ui","components","design-tokens","accessibility","frontend"],"bodyPreview":"# Design System Starter\n\nBuild robust, scalable design systems that ensure visual consistency and exceptional user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\nJust describe what you need:\n\n```\nCreate a design system for my React app with dark mode support\n```\n\nThat''s it. The skill provides tokens, components, and accessibility guidelines.\n\n---\n\n## Triggers\n\n| Trigger | Example |\n|---------|---------|\n| Create design system | \"Create a design system for my app\" |\n| Design tokens | \"Set up design tokens fo","body":"# Design System Starter\n\nBuild robust, scalable design systems that ensure visual consistency and exceptional user experiences.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\nJust describe what you need:\n\n```\nCreate a design system for my React app with dark mode support\n```\n\nThat''s it. The skill provides tokens, components, and accessibility guidelines.\n\n---\n\n## Triggers\n\n| Trigger | Example |\n|---------|---------|\n| Create design system | \"Create a design system for my app\" |\n| Design tokens | \"Set up design tokens for colors and spacing\" |\n| Component architecture | \"Design component structure using atomic design\" |\n| Accessibility | \"Ensure WCAG 2.1 compliance for my components\" |\n| Dark mode | \"Implement theming with dark mode support\" |\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Output |\n|------|--------|\n| Design tokens | Color, typography, spacing, shadows JSON |\n| Component structure | Atomic design hierarchy (atoms, molecules, organisms) |\n| Theming | CSS variables or ThemeProvider setup |\n| Accessibility | WCAG 2.1 AA compliant patterns |\n| Documentation | Component docs with props, examples, a11y notes |\n\n---\n\n## Bundled Resources\n\n- `references/component-examples.md` - Complete component implementations\n- `templates/design-tokens-template.json` - W3C design token format\n- `templates/component-template.tsx` - React component template\n- `checklists/design-system-checklist.md` - Design system audit checklist\n\n---\n\n## Design System Philosophy\n\n### What is a Design System?\n\nA design system is more than a component library—it''s a collection of:\n\n1. **Design Tokens**: Foundational design decisions (colors, spacing, typography)\n2. **Components**: Reusable UI building blocks\n3. **Patterns**: Common UX solutions and compositions\n4. **Guidelines**: Rules, principles, and best practices\n5. **Documentation**: How to use everything effectively\n\n### Core Principles\n\n**1. Consistency Over Creativity**\n- Predictable patterns reduce cognitive load\n- Users learn once, apply everywhere\n- Designers and developers speak the same language\n\n**2. Accessible by Default**\n- WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance minimum\n- Keyboard navigation built-in\n- Screen reader support from the start\n\n**3. Scalable and Maintainable**\n- Design tokens enable global changes\n- Component composition reduces duplication\n- Versioning and deprecation strategies\n\n**4. Developer-Friendly**\n- Clear API contracts\n- Comprehensive documentation\n- Easy to integrate and customize\n\n---\n\n## Design Tokens\n\nDesign tokens are the atomic design decisions that define your system''s visual language.\n\n### Token Categories\n\n#### 1. Color Tokens\n\n**Primitive Colors** (Raw values):\n```json\n{\n  \"color\": {\n    \"primitive\": {\n      \"blue\": {\n        \"50\": \"#eff6ff\",\n        \"100\": \"#dbeafe\",\n        \"200\": \"#bfdbfe\",\n        \"300\": \"#93c5fd\",\n        \"400\": \"#60a5fa\",\n        \"500\": \"#3b82f6\",\n        \"600\": \"#2563eb\",\n        \"700\": \"#1d4ed8\",\n        \"800\": \"#1e40af\",\n        \"900\": \"#1e3a8a\",\n        \"950\": \"#172554\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Semantic Colors** (Contextual meaning):\n```json\n{\n  \"color\": {\n    \"semantic\": {\n      \"brand\": {\n        \"primary\": \"{color.primitive.blue.600}\",\n        \"primary-hover\": \"{color.primitive.blue.700}\",\n        \"primary-active\": \"{color.primitive.blue.800}\"\n      },\n      \"text\": {\n        \"primary\": \"{color.primitive.gray.900}\",\n        \"secondary\": \"{color.primitive.gray.600}\",\n        \"tertiary\": \"{color.primitive.gray.500}\",\n        \"disabled\": \"{color.primitive.gray.400}\",\n        \"inverse\": \"{color.primitive.white}\"\n      },\n      \"background\": {\n        \"primary\": \"{color.primitive.white}\",\n        \"secondary\": \"{color.primitive.gray.50}\",\n        \"tertiary\": \"{color.primitive.gray.100}\"\n      },\n      \"feedback\": {\n        \"success\": \"{color.primitive.green.600}\",\n        \"warning\": \"{color.primitive.yellow.600}\",\n        \"error\": \"{color.primitive.red.600}\",\n        \"info\": \"{color.primitive.blue.600}\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Accessibility**: Ensure color contrast ratios meet WCAG 2.1 Level AA:\n- Normal text: 4.5:1 minimum\n- Large text (18pt+ or 14pt+ bold): 3:1 minimum\n- UI components and graphics: 3:1 minimum\n\n#### 2. Typography Tokens\n\n```json\n{\n  \"typography\": {\n    \"fontFamily\": {\n      \"sans\": \"''Inter'', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, ''Segoe UI'', sans-serif\",\n      \"serif\": \"''Georgia'', ''Times New Roman'', serif\",\n      \"mono\": \"''Fira Code'', ''Courier New'', monospace\"\n    },\n    \"fontSize\": {\n      \"xs\": \"0.75rem\",     // 12px\n      \"sm\": \"0.875rem\",    // 14px\n      \"base\": \"1rem\",      // 16px\n      \"lg\": \"1.125rem\",    // 18px\n      \"xl\": \"1.25rem\",     // 20px\n      \"2xl\": \"1.5rem\",     // 24px\n      \"3xl\": \"1.875rem\",   // 30px\n      \"4xl\": \"2.25rem\",    // 36px\n      \"5xl\": \"3rem\"        // 48px\n    },\n    \"fontWeight\": {\n      \"normal\": 400,\n      \"medium\": 500,\n      \"semibold\": 600,\n      \"bold\": 700\n    },\n    \"lineHeight\": {\n      \"tight\": 1.25,\n      \"normal\": 1.5,\n      \"relaxed\": 1.75,\n      \"loose\": 2\n    },\n    \"letterSpacing\": {\n      \"tight\": \"-0.025em\",\n      \"normal\": \"0\",\n      \"wide\": \"0.025em\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### 3. Spacing Tokens\n\n**Scale**: Use a consistent spacing scale (commonly 4px or 8px base)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"spacing\": {\n    \"0\": \"0\",\n    \"1\": \"0.25rem\",   // 4px\n    \"2\": \"0.5rem\",    // 8px\n    \"3\": \"0.75rem\",   // 12px\n    \"4\": \"1rem\",      // 16px\n    \"5\": \"1.25rem\",   // 20px\n    \"6\": \"1.5rem\",    // 24px\n    \"8\": \"2rem\",      // 32px\n    \"10\": \"2.5rem\",   // 40px\n    \"12\": \"3rem\",     // 48px\n    \"16\": \"4rem\",     // 64px\n    \"20\": \"5rem\",     // 80px\n    \"24\": \"6rem\"      // 96px\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Component-Specific Spacing**:\n```json\n{\n  \"component\": {\n    \"button\": {\n      \"padding-x\": \"{spacing.4}\",\n      \"padding-y\": \"{spacing.2}\",\n      \"gap\": \"{spacing.2}\"\n    },\n    \"card\": {\n      \"padding\": \"{spacing.6}\",\n      \"gap\": \"{spacing.4}\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### 4. Border Radius Tokens\n\n```json\n{\n  \"borderRadius\": {\n    \"none\": \"0\",\n    \"sm\": \"0.125rem\",   // 2px\n    \"base\": \"0.25rem\",  // 4px\n    \"md\": \"0.375rem\",   // 6px\n    \"lg\": \"0.5rem\",     // 8px\n    \"xl\": \"0.75rem\",    // 12px\n    \"2xl\": \"1rem\",      // 16px\n    \"full\": \"9999px\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### 5. Shadow Tokens\n\n```json\n{\n  \"shadow\": {\n    \"xs\": \"0 1px 2px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05)\",\n    \"sm\": \"0 1px 3px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 1px 2px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)\",\n    \"base\": \"0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 2px 4px -2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)\",\n    \"md\": \"0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 4px 6px -4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)\",\n    \"lg\": \"0 20px 25px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 8px 10px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)\",\n    \"xl\": \"0 25px 50px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25)\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Component Architecture\n\n### Atomic Design Methodology\n\n**Atoms** → **Molecules** → **Organisms** → **Templates** → **Pages**\n\n#### Atoms (Primitive Components)\nBasic building blocks that can''t be broken down further.\n\n**Examples:**\n- Button\n- Input\n- Label\n- Icon\n- Badge\n- Avatar\n\n**Button Component:**\n```typescript\ninterface ButtonProps {\n  variant?: ''primary'' | ''secondary'' | ''outline'' | ''ghost'';\n  size?: ''sm'' | ''md'' | ''lg'';\n  disabled?: boolean;\n  loading?: boolean;\n  icon?: React.ReactNode;\n  children: React.ReactNode;\n}\n```\n\nSee `references/component-examples.md` for complete Button implementation with variants, sizes, and styling patterns.\n\n#### Molecules (Simple Compositions)\nGroups of atoms that function together.\n\n**Examples:**\n- SearchBar (Input + Button)\n- FormField (Label + Input + ErrorMessage)\n- Card (Container + Title + Content + Actions)\n\n**FormField Molecule:**\n```typescript\ninterface FormFieldProps {\n  label: string;\n  name: string;\n  error?: string;\n  hint?: string;\n  required?: boolean;\n  children: React.ReactNode;\n}\n```\n\nSee `references/component-examples.md` for FormField, Card (compound component pattern), Input with variants, Modal, and more composition examples.\n\n#### Organisms (Complex Compositions)\nComplex UI components made of molecules and atoms.\n\n**Examples:**\n- Navigation Bar\n- Product Card Grid\n- User Profile Section\n- Modal Dialog\n\n#### Templates (Page Layouts)\nPage-level structures that define content placement.\n\n**Examples:**\n- Dashboard Layout (Sidebar + Header + Main Content)\n- Marketing Page Layout (Hero + Features + Footer)\n- Settings Page Layout (Tabs + Content Panels)\n\n#### Pages (Specific Instances)\nActual pages with real content.\n\n---\n\n## Component API Design\n\n### Props Best Practices\n\n**1. Predictable Prop Names**\n```typescript\n// ✅ Good: Consistent naming\n<Button variant=\"primary\" size=\"md\" />\n<Input variant=\"outlined\" size=\"md\" />\n\n// ❌ Bad: Inconsistent\n<Button type=\"primary\" sizeMode=\"md\" />\n<Input style=\"outlined\" inputSize=\"md\" />\n```\n\n**2. Sensible Defaults**\n```typescript\n// ✅ Good: Provides defaults\ninterface ButtonProps {\n  variant?: ''primary'' | ''secondary'';  // Default: primary\n  size?: ''sm'' | ''md'' | ''lg'';          // Default: md\n}\n\n// ❌ Bad: Everything required\ninterface ButtonProps {\n  variant: ''primary'' | ''secondary'';\n  size: ''sm'' | ''md'' | ''lg'';\n  color: string;\n  padding: string;\n}\n```\n\n**3. Composition Over Configuration**\n```typescript\n// ✅ Good: Composable\n<Card>\n  <Card.Header>\n    <Card.Title>Title</Card.Title>\n  </Card.Header>\n  <Card.Body>Content</Card.Body>\n  <Card.Footer>Actions</Card.Footer>\n</Card>\n\n// ❌ Bad: Too many props\n<Card\n  title=\"Title\"\n  content=\"Content\"\n  footerContent=\"Actions\"\n  hasHeader={true}\n  hasFooter={true}\n/>\n```\n\n**4. Polymorphic Components**\nAllow components to render as different HTML elements:\n```typescript\n<Button as=\"a\" href=\"/login\">Login</Button>\n<Button as=\"button\" onClick={handleClick}>Click Me</Button>\n```\n\nSee `references/component-examples.md` for complete polymorphic component TypeScript patterns.\n\n---\n\n## Theming and Dark Mode\n\n### Theme Structure\n\n```typescript\ninterface Theme {\n  colors: {\n    brand: {\n      primary: string;\n      secondary: string;\n    };\n    text: {\n      primary: string;\n      secondary: string;\n    };\n    background: {\n      primary: string;\n      secondary: string;\n    };\n    feedback: {\n      success: string;\n      warning: string;\n      error: string;\n      info: string;\n    };\n  };\n  typography: {\n    fontFamily: {\n      sans: string;\n      mono: string;\n    };\n    fontSize: Record<string, string>;\n  };\n  spacing: Record<string, string>;\n  borderRadius: Record<string, string>;\n  shadow: Record<string, string>;\n}\n```\n\n### Dark Mode Implementation\n\n**Approach 1: CSS Variables**\n```css\n:root {\n  --color-bg-primary: #ffffff;\n  --color-text-primary: #000000;\n}\n\n[data-theme=\"dark\"] {\n  --color-bg-primary: #1a1a1a;\n  --color-text-primary: #ffffff;\n}\n```\n\n**Approach 2: Tailwind CSS Dark Mode**\n```tsx\n<div className=\"bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 text-gray-900 dark:text-white\">\n  Content\n</div>\n```\n\n**Approach 3: Styled Components ThemeProvider**\n```typescript\nconst lightTheme = { background: ''#fff'', text: ''#000'' };\nconst darkTheme = { background: ''#000'', text: ''#fff'' };\n\n<ThemeProvider theme={isDark ? darkTheme : lightTheme}>\n  <App />\n</ThemeProvider>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Accessibility Guidelines\n\n### WCAG 2.1 Level AA Compliance\n\n#### Color Contrast\n- **Normal text** (< 18pt): 4.5:1 minimum\n- **Large text** (≥ 18pt or ≥ 14pt bold): 3:1 minimum\n- **UI components**: 3:1 minimum\n\n**Tools**: Use contrast checkers like [WebAIM Contrast Checker](https://webaim.org/resources/contrastchecker/)\n\n#### Keyboard Navigation\n```typescript\n// ✅ All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible\n<button\n  onClick={handleClick}\n  onKeyDown={(e) => e.key === ''Enter'' && handleClick()}\n>\n  Click me\n</button>\n\n// ✅ Focus management\n<Modal>\n  <FocusTrap>\n    {/* Modal content */}\n  </FocusTrap>\n</Modal>\n```\n\n#### ARIA Attributes\nEssential ARIA patterns:\n- `aria-label`: Provide accessible names\n- `aria-expanded`: Communicate expanded/collapsed state\n- `aria-controls`: Associate controls with content\n- `aria-live`: Announce dynamic content changes\n\n#### Screen Reader Support\n- Use semantic HTML elements (`<button>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`)\n- Avoid div/span soup for interactive elements\n- Provide meaningful labels for all controls\n\nSee `references/component-examples.md` for complete accessibility examples including Skip Links, focus traps, and ARIA patterns.\n\n---\n\n## Documentation Standards\n\n### Component Documentation Template\n\nEach component should document:\n- **Purpose**: What the component does\n- **Usage**: Import statement and basic example\n- **Variants**: Available visual styles\n- **Props**: Complete prop table with types, defaults, descriptions\n- **Accessibility**: Keyboard support, ARIA attributes, screen reader behavior\n- **Examples**: Common use cases with code\n\nUse Storybook, Docusaurus, or similar tools for interactive documentation.\n\nSee `templates/component-template.tsx` for the standard component structure.\n\n---\n\n## Design System Workflow\n\n### 1. Design Phase\n- **Audit existing patterns**: Identify inconsistencies\n- **Define design tokens**: Colors, typography, spacing\n- **Create component inventory**: List all needed components\n- **Design in Figma**: Create component library\n\n### 2. Development Phase\n- **Set up tooling**: Storybook, TypeScript, testing\n- **Implement tokens**: CSS variables or theme config\n- **Build atoms first**: Start with primitives\n- **Compose upward**: Build molecules, organisms\n- **Document as you go**: Write docs alongside code\n\n### 3. Adoption Phase\n- **Create migration guide**: Help teams adopt\n- **Provide codemods**: Automate migrations when possible\n- **Run workshops**: Train teams on usage\n- **Gather feedback**: Iterate based on real usage\n\n### 4. Maintenance Phase\n- **Version semantically**: Major/minor/patch releases\n- **Deprecation strategy**: Phase out old components gracefully\n- **Changelog**: Document all changes\n- **Monitor adoption**: Track usage across products\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start Checklist\n\nWhen creating a new design system:\n\n- [ ] Define design principles and values\n- [ ] Establish design token structure (colors, typography, spacing)\n- [ ] Create primitive color palette (50-950 scale)\n- [ ] Define semantic color tokens (brand, text, background, feedback)\n- [ ] Set typography scale and font families\n- [ ] Establish spacing scale (4px or 8px base)\n- [ ] Design atomic components (Button, Input, Label, etc.)\n- [ ] Implement theming system (light/dark mode)\n- [ ] Ensure WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance\n- [ ] Set up documentation (Storybook or similar)\n- [ ] Create usage examples for each component\n- [ ] Establish versioning and release strategy\n- [ ] Create migration guides for adopting teams\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T07:19:12.173Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing to create robust, scalable, and visually consistent design systems with dark mode support","zh":"非常适合需要创建强大、可扩展、视觉一致的设计系统并支持暗黑模式的前端代理","ja":"暗黒モードのサポートを備えた堅牢でスケーラブルで視覚的に一貫性のあるデザインシステムを作成する必要があるフロントエンドエージェントに最適","ko":"다크 모드 지원이 있는 강력하고 확장 가능하며 시각적으로 일관된 디자인 시스템을 만들 필요가 있는 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Frontend que necesitan crear sistemas de diseño robustos, escalables y visualmente coherentes con soporte para modo oscuro","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend qui ont besoin de créer des systèmes de conception robustes, évolutifs et visuellement cohérents avec une prise en charge du mode sombre","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die robuste, skalierbare und visuell konsistente Designs mit Unterstützung für Dark-Mode erstellen müssen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que precisam criar sistemas de design robustos, escaláveis e visualmente consistentes com suporte a modo escuro","ru":"Идеально для агентов Frontend, которым необходимо создавать прочные, масштабируемые и визуально последовательные системы дизайна с поддержкой темного режима","ar":"مثالي لويب فرنت-إند الذين يحتاجون إلى إنشاء أنظمة تصميم قوية وقابلة للتوسيع وثابتة من الناحية البصرية مع دعم للوضع الداكن"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate design systems with tokens, components, and accessibility guidelines, utilizing React for seamless integration and ensuring exceptional user experiences with features like dark mode support","zh":"赋予代理创建设计系统的能力，利用令牌、组件和无障碍指南，并利用React实现无缝集成，确保具有暗黑模式支持等功能的异常用户体验","ja":"トークン、コンポーネント、無障碍ガイドラインを使用してデザインシステムを生成するエージェントをエンパワーメントし、Reactを使用してシームレスな統合を実現し、ダークモードのサポートなどの機能で優れたユーザーエクスペリエンスを確保する","ko":"토큰, 컴포넌트 및 접근성 지침을 사용하여 디자인 시스템을 생성할 수 있는 에이전트를 권장하고 React를 사용하여 무결점 통합을 제공하며 다크 모드 지원과 같은 기능으로卓越한 사용자 경험을 보장","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar sistemas de diseño con tokens, componentes y pautas de accesibilidad, utilizando React para una integración sin problemas y garantizando experiencias de usuario excepcionales con características como el soporte para modo oscuro","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des systèmes de conception avec des jetons, des composants et des lignes directrices d''accessibilité, en utilisant React pour une intégration transparente et en garantissant des expériences utilisateur exceptionnelles avec des fonctionnalités telles que la prise en charge du mode sombre","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Designs mit Tokens, Komponenten und Barrierefreiheitsrichtlinien zu erstellen, indem React für eine nahtlose Integration verwendet wird und außergewöhnliche Benutzererfahrungen mit Funktionen wie Dark-Mode-Unterstützung gewährleistet","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar sistemas de design com tokens, componentes e diretrizes de acessibilidade, utilizando React para integração perfeita e garantindo experiências de usuário excepcionais com recursos como suporte a modo escuro","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать системы дизайна с токенами, компонентами и руководящими принципами доступности, используя React для бесшовной интеграции и обеспечивая исключительные пользовательские trải nghiệm с функциями, такими как поддержка темного режима","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إنشاء أنظمة تصميم باستخدام الرموز والعناصر الإرشادية وإمكانية الوصول، باستخدام React من أجل التكامل السلس وضمان تجارب المستخدم الاستثنائية مع ميزات مثل دعم الوضع الداكن"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating design systems for React applications","Generating design tokens for consistent branding","Setting up accessibility guidelines for inclusive UI"],"zh":["为React应用程序创建设计系统","为一致的品牌形象生成设计令牌","为包容性UI设置无障碍指南"],"ja":["Reactアプリケーションのデザインシステムを作成する","一貫したブランディングのためにデザイントークンを生成する","包括的なUIのために無障碍ガイドラインを設定する"],"ko":["React 애플리케이션을 위한 디자인 시스템 생성","일관된 브랜딩을 위한 디자인 토큰 생성","포괄적인 UI를 위한 접근성 지침 설정"],"es":["Crear sistemas de diseño para aplicaciones React","Generar tokens de diseño para una marca coherente","Configurar pautas de accesibilidad para una interfaz de usuario inclusiva"],"fr":["Créer des systèmes de conception pour les applications React","Générer des jetons de conception pour une marque cohérente","Configurer des lignes directrices d''accessibilité pour une interface utilisateur inclusive"],"de":[" Designs für React-Anwendungen erstellen","Design-Tokens für eine konsistente Markenidentität generieren","Barrierefreiheitsrichtlinien für eine inclusive Benutzeroberfläche einrichten"],"pt":["Criação de sistemas de design para aplicações React","Geração de tokens de design para marcação consistente","Configuração de diretrizes de acessibilidade para UI inclusiva"],"ru":["Создание систем дизайна для приложений React","Генерация токенов дизайна для последовательного брендинга","Настройка руководящих принципов доступности для инклюзивного UI"],"ar":["إنشاء أنظمة تصميم للتطبيقات التي تعمل بالريآكت","توليد رموز التصميم للتسويق المتسق","تكوين إرشادات إمكانية الوصول لواجهة المستخدم الشاملة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires React app setup","Limited to design system creation and not for overall UI development"],"zh":["需要React应用程序设置","仅限于设计系统创建，不适用于整体UI开发"],"ja":["Reactアプリの設定が必要","デザインシステムの作成のみに限定され、全体的なUI開発には不向き"],"ko":["React 애플리케이션 설정 필요","디자인 시스템 생성만으로 제한되며, 전체 UI 개발에는 부적합"],"es":["Requiere configuración de aplicación React","Limitado a la creación de sistemas de diseño y no para el desarrollo general de la interfaz de usuario"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration d''application React","Limité à la création de systèmes de conception et non pour le développement général de l''interface utilisateur"],"de":["Benötigt React-App-Konfiguration","Begrenzt auf die Erstellung von Designs und nicht für die allgemeine Entwicklung der Benutzeroberfläche"],"pt":["Exige configuração de aplicativo React","Limitado à criação de sistema de design e não para desenvolvimento de UI geral"],"ru":["Требует настройки приложения React","Ограничен созданием системы дизайна и не для общего развития UI"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد تطبيق ريآكت","محدود بإنشاء نظام التصميم وليس لتطوير واجهة المستخدم بشكل عام"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('tkknot/work-settings/devcontainer-cli', 'community', 'tkknot', 'work-settings', 'tkknot/work-settings', 'devcontainer-cli', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:03:48.183Z', '2026-02-19T07:19:07.078Z', NULL, '{"id":"tkknot/work-settings/devcontainer-cli","name":"devcontainer-cli","description":{"zh":"devcontainer CLI是用于管理开发容器环境的命令行工具，提供基本命令和高级功能","ja":"devcontainer CLIは、Dev Container環境を操作するためのコマンドラインツールであり、基本コマンドと高度な機能を提供する","ko":"devcontainer CLI는 개발 컨테이너 환경을 관리하는 명령줄 도구로서 기본 명령어와 고급 기능을 제공합니다","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"devcontainer CLI技能：开发容器环境管理","ja":"devcontainer CLIスキル：Dev Container環境操作","ko":"devcontainer CLI 스킬: 개발 컨테이너 환경 관리","en":"devcontainer-cli"},"description":{"zh":"devcontainer CLI是用于管理开发容器环境的命令行工具，提供基本命令和高级功能","ja":"devcontainer CLIは、Dev Container環境を操作するためのコマンドラインツールであり、基本コマンドと高度な機能を提供する","ko":"devcontainer CLI는 개발 컨테이너 환경을 관리하는 명령줄 도구로서 기본 명령어와 고급 기능을 제공합니다","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["基本命令：up、remove-existing-container等","支持特定设置文件","高效管理开发容器环境","提高开发效率","支持Docker环境"],"ja":["基本コマンド：up、remove-existing-containerなど","特定の設定ファイルをサポート","Dev Container環境を効率的に管理","開発の効率を上げる","Docker環境をサポート"],"ko":["기본 명령어：up, remove-existing-container 등","특정 설정 파일 지원","개발 컨테이너 환경을 효율적으로 관리","개발 효율성을 높여줌","Docker 환경 지원"]},"keywords":{"zh":["devcontainer CLI","开发容器环境","命令行工具","Docker","开发效率","容器管理"],"ja":["devcontainer CLI","Dev Container環境","コマンドラインツール","Docker","開発の効率","コンテナ管理"],"ko":["devcontainer CLI","개발 컨테이너 환경","명령줄 도구","Docker","개발 효율성","컨테이너 관리"]}},"owner":"tkknot","repo":"work-settings","repoPath":"tkknot/work-settings","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:03:48.183Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"devcontainer-cli","description":"devcontainer CLIを使用してDev Container環境の作成・起動・管理・実行などの操作を行うスキル","bodyPreview":"# Devcontainer CLI スキル\n\ndevcontainer CLIを使用してDev Container環境を操作するためのスキルです。\n\n## 前提条件\n\n```bash\n# devcontainer CLIのインストール確認\nwhich devcontainer\ndevcontainer --version\n\n# インストールされていない場合\nnpm install -g @devcontainers/cli\n\n# Dockerが起動していること\ndocker info\n```\n\n---\n\n## 基本コマンド\n\n### up - コンテナの起動\n\n```bash\n# 基本起動\ndevcontainer up --workspace-folder <project-path>\n\n# 既存コンテナを削除して起動\ndevcontainer up --workspace-folder <project-path> --remove-existing-container\n\n# 特定の設定ファイルを指定\ndevcontainer up --workspace-folder <pro","body":"# Devcontainer CLI スキル\n\ndevcontainer CLIを使用してDev Container環境を操作するためのスキルです。\n\n## 前提条件\n\n```bash\n# devcontainer CLIのインストール確認\nwhich devcontainer\ndevcontainer --version\n\n# インストールされていない場合\nnpm install -g @devcontainers/cli\n\n# Dockerが起動していること\ndocker info\n```\n\n---\n\n## 基本コマンド\n\n### up - コンテナの起動\n\n```bash\n# 基本起動\ndevcontainer up --workspace-folder <project-path>\n\n# 既存コンテナを削除して起動\ndevcontainer up --workspace-folder <project-path> --remove-existing-container\n\n# 特定の設定ファイルを指定\ndevcontainer up --workspace-folder <project-path> --config <path-to-devcontainer.json>\n```\n\n### exec - コンテナ内でコマンド実行\n\n```bash\n# シェル起動\ndevcontainer exec --workspace-folder <project-path> bash\n\n# 特定コマンド実行\ndevcontainer exec --workspace-folder <project-path> npm install\ndevcontainer exec --workspace-folder <project-path> npm run dev\n\n# 複数コマンド\ndevcontainer exec --workspace-folder <project-path> sh -c \"npm install && npm run build\"\n```\n\n### build - イメージのビルド\n\n```bash\n# 基本ビルド\ndevcontainer build --workspace-folder <project-path>\n\n# キャッシュなしでビルド\ndevcontainer build --workspace-folder <project-path> --no-cache\n\n# イメージ名を指定\ndevcontainer build --workspace-folder <project-path> --image-name my-devcontainer:latest\n```\n\n### read-configuration - 設定の読み取り\n\n```bash\n# 設定内容をJSON形式で出力\ndevcontainer read-configuration --workspace-folder <project-path>\n\n# jqで特定項目を抽出\ndevcontainer read-configuration --workspace-folder <project-path> | jq ''.configuration.image''\n```\n\n### features - Feature情報\n\n```bash\n# 利用可能なFeature一覧\ndevcontainer features list\n\n# Feature情報の詳細\ndevcontainer features info ghcr.io/devcontainers/features/node\n```\n\n---\n\n## よくある操作パターン\n\n### パターン1: 新規プロジェクトでDevcontainer起動\n\n```bash\n# 1. .devcontainerの存在確認\nls -la <project-path>/.devcontainer/\n\n# 2. 設定確認\ncat <project-path>/.devcontainer/devcontainer.json\n\n# 3. 起動\ndevcontainer up --workspace-folder <project-path>\n\n# 4. シェル接続\ndevcontainer exec --workspace-folder <project-path> bash\n```\n\n### パターン2: 開発サーバー起動\n\n```bash\n# コンテナ起動後、開発サーバーを実行\ndevcontainer exec --workspace-folder <project-path> npm run dev\n```\n\n### パターン3: リビルド\n\n```bash\n# 設定変更後のリビルド\ndevcontainer up --workspace-folder <project-path> --remove-existing-container --rebuild-if-exists\n```\n\n### パターン4: デバッグ\n\n```bash\n# 詳細ログ付きで起動\ndevcontainer up --workspace-folder <project-path> --log-level debug\n\n# ビルドログ確認\ndevcontainer build --workspace-folder <project-path> 2>&1 | tee build.log\n```\n\n---\n\n## トラブルシューティング\n\n| 問題 | 原因 | 解決策 |\n|------|------|--------|\n| `Docker daemon not running` | Docker未起動 | `sudo systemctl start docker` |\n| `No devcontainer.json found` | 設定ファイルなし | `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json` を作成 |\n| `Port already in use` | ポート競合 | `docker ps` で確認、競合コンテナを停止 |\n| `Build failed` | Dockerfile/Feature問題 | `--no-cache` でリビルド |\n| `Permission denied` | 権限問題 | `sudo` またはdockerグループに追加 |\n\n---\n\n## devcontainer.json の基本構造\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  // ベースイメージ\n  \"image\": \"mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/base:ubuntu\",\n\n  // または Dockerfile を使用\n  // \"build\": { \"dockerfile\": \"Dockerfile\" },\n\n  // 追加機能\n  \"features\": {\n    \"ghcr.io/devcontainers/features/node:1\": {},\n    \"ghcr.io/devcontainers/features/docker-in-docker:2\": {}\n  },\n\n  // ポートフォワード\n  \"forwardPorts\": [3000, 5432],\n\n  // コンテナ作成後に実行\n  \"postCreateCommand\": \"npm install\",\n\n  // 起動時に実行\n  \"postStartCommand\": \"npm run dev\",\n\n  // VS Code 拡張機能\n  \"customizations\": {\n    \"vscode\": {\n      \"extensions\": [\n        \"dbaeumer.vscode-eslint\",\n        \"esbenp.prettier-vscode\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## CI/CDでの利用\n\n```bash\n# GitHub Actionsなどで利用\ndevcontainer up --workspace-folder . --skip-post-create\ndevcontainer exec --workspace-folder . npm test\ndevcontainer exec --workspace-folder . npm run build\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T07:19:07.078Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Environment Agents needing automated containerized workspace management.","zh":"Perfect for Development Environment Agents needing automated containerized workspace management.","ja":"Perfect for Development Environment Agents needing automated containerized workspace management.","ko":"Perfect for Development Environment Agents needing automated containerized workspace management.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de entorno de desarrollo que necesitan una gestión de espacio de trabajo automatizada y contenerizada.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''environnement de développement ayant besoin d''une gestion de workspace conteneurisée automatisée.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsumgebungsagenten, die eine automatisierte Verwaltung von Containern im Arbeitsbereich benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Ambiente de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de gerenciamento de espaço de trabalho containerizado automatizado.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов среды разработки, требующих автоматизированного управления контейнеризированной рабочей средой.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء بيئة التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة مساحة العمل المُحَوسَبَة آليًا."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to programmatically manage Dev Container environments using the devcontainer CLI. Provides direct control over container lifecycle operations including startup, configuration, and cleanup through npm-installed command-line interface.","zh":"Enables agents to programmatically manage Dev Container environments using the devcontainer CLI. Provides direct control over container lifecycle operations including startup, configuration, and cleanup through npm-installed command-line interface.","ja":"Enables agents to programmatically manage Dev Container environments using the devcontainer CLI. Provides direct control over container lifecycle operations including startup, configuration, and cleanup through npm-installed command-line interface.","ko":"Enables agents to programmatically manage Dev Container environments using the devcontainer CLI. Provides direct control over container lifecycle operations including startup, configuration, and cleanup through npm-installed command-line interface.","es":"Permite a los agentes gestionar de forma programática entornos de Dev Container mediante la CLI de devcontainer. Proporciona un control directo sobre las operaciones del ciclo de vida del contenedor, incluidas la inicialización, configuración y limpieza a través de la interfaz de línea de comandos instalada mediante npm.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer de manière programmatique les environnements de Dev Container à l''aide de la CLI de devcontainer. Fournit un contrôle direct sur les opérations de cycle de vie du conteneur, y compris le démarrage, la configuration et la suppression via l''interface de ligne de commande installée via npm.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Dev-Container-Umgebungen programmgesteuert über die devcontainer-CLI zu verwalten. Bietet direkte Kontrolle über die Lebenszyklusoperationen des Containers, einschließlich Start, Konfiguration und Bereinigung über die via npm installierte Kommandozeilenoberfläche.","pt":"Permite que os agentes gerenciem programaticamente ambientes de contêiner de desenvolvimento usando a CLI devcontainer. Fornece controle direto sobre operações de ciclo de vida de contêiner, incluindo inicialização, configuração e limpeza, por meio da interface de linha de comando instalada via npm.","ru":"Позволяет агентам программно управлять средами разработки с помощью CLI devcontainer. Предоставляет прямой контроль над операциями жизненного цикла контейнеров, включая запуск, конфигурацию и очистку, через командную строку, установленную с помощью npm.","ar":"يسمح للوكلاء بإدارة بيئات حاويات التطوير برمجيًا باستخدام واجهة سطر الأوامر devcontainer. يوفر التحكم المباشر في عمليات دورة حياة الحاوية، بما في ذلك التشغيل والتهيئة والتنظيف، من خلال واجهة سطر الأوامر المثبتة عبر npm."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating development environment setup for projects","Managing container lifecycle with --remove-existing-container flag","Configuring specific devcontainer.json configurations","Validating Docker and devcontainer CLI prerequisites"],"zh":["Automating development environment setup for projects","Managing container lifecycle with --remove-existing-container flag","Configuring specific devcontainer.json configurations","Validating Docker and devcontainer CLI prerequisites"],"ja":["Automating development environment setup for projects","Managing container lifecycle with --remove-existing-container flag","Configuring specific devcontainer.json configurations","Validating Docker and devcontainer CLI prerequisites"],"ko":["Automating development environment setup for projects","Managing container lifecycle with --remove-existing-container flag","Configuring specific devcontainer.json configurations","Validating Docker and devcontainer CLI prerequisites"],"es":["Automatización de la configuración del entorno de desarrollo para proyectos","Gestión del ciclo de vida del contenedor con la marca --remove-existing-container","Configuración de configuraciones específicas de devcontainer.json","Validación de los requisitos previos de Docker y la CLI de devcontainer"],"fr":["Automatisation de la configuration de l''environnement de développement pour les projets","Gestion du cycle de vie du conteneur avec le drapeau --remove-existing-container","Configuration des configurations spécifiques de devcontainer.json","Validation des prérequis de Docker et de la CLI de devcontainer"],"de":["Automatisierung der Einrichtung der Entwicklungsumgebung für Projekte","Verwaltung des Container-Lebenszyklus mit der --remove-existing-container-Flag","Konfiguration spezifischer devcontainer.json-Konfigurationen","Validierung der Voraussetzungen für Docker und die devcontainer-CLI"],"pt":["Automatizar a configuração do ambiente de desenvolvimento para projetos","Gerenciar o ciclo de vida do contêiner com a flag --remove-existing-container","Configurar configurações específicas do devcontainer.json","Validar os pré-requisitos do Docker e da CLI devcontainer"],"ru":["Автоматизировать настройку среды разработки для проектов","Управлять жизненным циклом контейнера с помощью флага --remove-existing-container","Настроить конкретные конфигурации devcontainer.json","Проверить условия использования Docker и CLI devcontainer"],"ar":["تأتمتة إعداد بيئة التطوير للمشاريع","إدارة دورة حياة الحاوية مع علم --remove-existing-container","تهيئة تهيئة محددة من devcontainer.json","التحقق من مسبقات Docker وواجهة سطر الأوامر devcontainer"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires npm installation of @devcontainers/cli","Docker runtime must be installed and running","Dependent on workspace-folder parameter structure"],"zh":["Requires npm installation of @devcontainers/cli","Docker runtime must be installed and running","Dependent on workspace-folder parameter structure"],"ja":["Requires npm installation of @devcontainers/cli","Docker runtime must be installed and running","Dependent on workspace-folder parameter structure"],"ko":["Requires npm installation of @devcontainers/cli","Docker runtime must be installed and running","Dependent on workspace-folder parameter structure"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de @devcontainers/cli mediante npm","El tiempo de ejecución de Docker debe estar instalado y en ejecución","Dependiente de la estructura de parámetros de la carpeta de trabajo"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de @devcontainers/cli via npm","Le runtime Docker doit être installé et en cours d''exécution","Dépend de la structure des paramètres du dossier de travail"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation von @devcontainers/cli über npm","Die Docker-Laufzeitumgebung muss installiert und ausgeführt werden","Abhängig von der Parameterstruktur des Arbeitsordner"],"pt":["Exige instalação do npm do @devcontainers/cli","O tempo de execução do Docker deve estar instalado e em execução","Dependente da estrutura do parâmetro pasta de trabalho"],"ru":["Требует установки npm @devcontainers/cli","Время выполнения Docker должно быть установленным и запущенным","Зависит от структуры параметра папки работы"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت npm من @devcontainers/cli","يجب أن يكون وقت تشغيل Docker مثبتًا و正在 التشغيل","يعتمد على هيكل معلمة مجلد العمل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Dknight203/AesopIDE/cqrs-implementation', 'community', 'Dknight203', 'AesopIDE', 'Dknight203/AesopIDE', 'cqrs-implementation', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:03:48.183Z', '2026-02-19T07:19:15.454Z', NULL, '{"id":"Dknight203/AesopIDE/cqrs-implementation","name":"cqrs-implementation","description":{"zh":"CQRS实现是一种软件架构模式，用于分离读写关注点，提高系统的可扩展性和性能","ja":"CQRS実装は、読み取りと書き込みの関心事を分離してシステムの拡張性とパフォーマンスを向上させるソフトウェアアーキテクチャパターンです","ko":"CQRS 구현은 시스템의 확장성과 성능을 높이는 소프트웨어 아키텍처 패턴입니다.","es":"La implementación de CQRS es una arquitectura que separa las preocupaciones de lectura y escritura, mejorando el rendimiento y la escalabilidad","fr":"La mise en œuvre de CQRS est une architecture qui sépare les préoccupations de lecture et d''écriture, améliorant les performances et la scalabilité","de":"Die Implementierung von CQRS ist eine Architektur, die die Belange von Lese- und Schreibvorgängen trennt, um die Leistung und Skalierbarkeit zu verbessern","pt":"O CQRS é um padrão de arquitetura que permite separar as preocupações de leitura e escrita, melhorando a escalabilidade e o desempenho dos sistemas","ru":"CQRS — это шаблон архитектуры, который позволяет разделить проблемы чтения и записи, улучшая масштабируемость и производительность систем","ar":"CQRS هو نمط هندسي يسمح بفصل اهتمامات القراءة والكتابة، مما يحسن من قابليّة التوسّع وأداء النظم","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"CQRS实现指南","ja":"CQRS実装ガイド","ko":"CQRS 구현 가이드","es":"Implementación de CQRS: Guía para desarrolladores","fr":"Mise en œuvre de CQRS : Guide pour les développeurs","de":"CQRS-Implementierung: Leitfaden für Entwickler","pt":"Implementação CQRS: Guia Completo para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Реализация CQRS: Всесторонний гид для разработчиков","ar":"تنفيذ CQRS: دليل شامل للمطورين","en":"cqrs-implementation"},"description":{"zh":"CQRS实现是一种软件架构模式，用于分离读写关注点，提高系统的可扩展性和性能","ja":"CQRS実装は、読み取りと書き込みの関心事を分離してシステムの拡張性とパフォーマンスを向上させるソフトウェアアーキテクチャパターンです","ko":"CQRS 구현은 시스템의 확장성과 성능을 높이는 소프트웨어 아키텍처 패턴입니다.","es":"La implementación de CQRS es una arquitectura que separa las preocupaciones de lectura y escritura, mejorando el rendimiento y la escalabilidad","fr":"La mise en œuvre de CQRS est une architecture qui sépare les préoccupations de lecture et d''écriture, améliorant les performances et la scalabilité","de":"Die Implementierung von CQRS ist eine Architektur, die die Belange von Lese- und Schreibvorgängen trennt, um die Leistung und Skalierbarkeit zu verbessern","pt":"O CQRS é um padrão de arquitetura que permite separar as preocupações de leitura e escrita, melhorando a escalabilidade e o desempenho dos sistemas","ru":"CQRS — это шаблон архитектуры, который позволяет разделить проблемы чтения и записи, улучшая масштабируемость и производительность систем","ar":"CQRS هو نمط هندسي يسمح بفصل اهتمامات القراءة والكتابة، مما يحسن من قابليّة التوسّع وأداء النظم","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"definition":{"en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"features":{"zh":["读写关注点的分离","可扩展的读取操作","事件源系统的构建","复杂查询场景的优化","高性能报告"],"ja":["読み取りと書き込みの関心事の分離","拡張可能な読み取り操作","イベントソーシングシステムの構築","複雑なクエリシナリオの最適化","高パフォーマンスのレポート"],"ko":["읽기/쓰기 관심사 분리","확장 가능한 읽기 작업","이벤트 소싱 시스템 구축","복잡한 쿼리 시나리오 최적화","고성능 보고서"],"es":["Separación de preocupaciones de lectura y escritura","Escalabilidad de lecturas de forma independiente","Construcción de sistemas con origen de eventos","Optimización de escenarios de consultas complejas","Modelos de datos de lectura y escritura diferentes","Requisitos de informes de alto rendimiento"],"fr":["Séparation des préoccupations de lecture et d''écriture","Scalabilité des lectures de manière indépendante","Construction de systèmes à source d''événements","Optimisation de scénarios de requêtes complexes","Modèles de données de lecture et d''écriture différents","Exigences de rapports de haute performance"],"de":["Trennung von Lese- und Schreibbelangen","Skalierbarkeit von Lesevorgängen unabhängig","Aufbau von Systemen mit Ereignisquelle","Optimierung komplexer Abfrageszenarien","Verschiedene Lese- und Schreibdatenmodelle","Anforderungen an Hochleistungsberichte"],"pt":["Separação de preocupações de leitura e escrita","Escalabilidade de leituras independentemente de escritas","Construção de sistemas baseados em eventos","Otimização de cenários de consulta complexos","Modelos de dados de leitura e escrita diferentes","Requisitos de relatórios de alto desempenho"],"ru":["Разделение проблем чтения и записи","Масштабируемость чтения независимо от записи","Строительство систем на основе событий","Оптимизация сложных сценариев запросов","Разные модели данных для чтения и записи","Требования к отчетам с высоким уровнем производительности"],"ar":["فصل اهتمامات القراءة والكتابة","توسّع القراءة بشكل مستقل عن الكتابة","بناء نظم مبنيّة على الأحداث","تحسين سيناريوهات الاستفسار المعقّدة","نماذج بيانات قراءة وكتابة مختلفة","متطلبات تقارير أداء عالية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["CQRS","软件架构","读写分离","可扩展性","高性能","事件源","复杂查询"],"ja":["CQRS","ソフトウェアアーキテクチャ","読み取りと書き込みの分離","拡張性","高パフォーマンス","イベントソーシング","複雑なクエリ"],"ko":["CQRS","소프트웨어 아키텍처","읽기/쓰기 분리","확장성","고성능","이벤트 소싱","복잡한 쿼리"],"es":["CQRS","arquitectura de software","patrones de diseño","escalabilidad","rendimiento","sistemas de origen de eventos","consultas complejas","modelos de datos"],"fr":["CQRS","architecture logicielle","modèles de conception","scalabilité","performances","systèmes à source d''événements","requêtes complexes","modèles de données"],"de":["CQRS","Software-Architektur","Entwurfsmuster","Skalierbarkeit","Leistung","Systeme mit Ereignisquelle","komplexe Abfragen","Datenmodelle"],"pt":["CQRS","Padrão de arquitetura","Escalabilidade","Desempenho","Sistemas baseados em eventos","Otimização de consultas","Modelos de dados","Relatórios de alto desempenho"],"ru":["CQRS","Шаблон архитектуры","Масштабируемость","Производительность","Системы на основе событий","Оптимизация запросов","Модели данных","Отчеты с высоким уровнем производительности"],"ar":["CQRS","نمط هندسي","قابليّة التوسّع","أداء","نظم مبنيّة على الأحداث","تحسين الاستفسارات","نماذج بيانات","تقارير أداء عالية"]}},"owner":"Dknight203","repo":"AesopIDE","repoPath":"Dknight203/AesopIDE","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:03:48.183Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cqrs-implementation","description":"Implement Command Query Responsibility Segregation for scalable architectures. Use when separating read and write models, optimizing query performance, or building event-sourced systems.","bodyPreview":"# CQRS Implementation\n\nComprehensive guide to implementing CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) patterns.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Separating read and write concerns\n- Scaling reads independently from writes\n- Building event-sourced systems\n- Optimizing complex query scenarios\n- Different read/write data models needed\n- High-performance reporting requirements\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. CQRS Architecture\n\n```\n                    ┌─────────────┐\n                    │   Client    │","body":"# CQRS Implementation\n\nComprehensive guide to implementing CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) patterns.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Separating read and write concerns\n- Scaling reads independently from writes\n- Building event-sourced systems\n- Optimizing complex query scenarios\n- Different read/write data models needed\n- High-performance reporting requirements\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. CQRS Architecture\n\n```\n                    ┌─────────────┐\n                    │   Client    │\n                    └──────┬──────┘\n                           │\n              ┌────────────┴────────────┐\n              │                         │\n              ▼                         ▼\n       ┌─────────────┐          ┌─────────────┐\n       │  Commands   │          │   Queries   │\n       │    API      │          │    API      │\n       └──────┬──────┘          └──────┬──────┘\n              │                         │\n              ▼                         ▼\n       ┌─────────────┐          ┌─────────────┐\n       │  Command    │          │   Query     │\n       │  Handlers   │          │  Handlers   │\n       └──────┬──────┘          └──────┬──────┘\n              │                         │\n              ▼                         ▼\n       ┌─────────────┐          ┌─────────────┐\n       │   Write     │─────────►│    Read     │\n       │   Model     │  Events  │   Model     │\n       └─────────────┘          └─────────────┘\n```\n\n### 2. Key Components\n\n| Component           | Responsibility                  |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| **Command**         | Intent to change state          |\n| **Command Handler** | Validates and executes commands |\n| **Event**           | Record of state change          |\n| **Query**           | Request for data                |\n| **Query Handler**   | Retrieves data from read model  |\n| **Projector**       | Updates read model from events  |\n\n## Templates\n\n### Template 1: Command Infrastructure\n\n```python\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import TypeVar, Generic, Dict, Any, Type\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport uuid\n\n# Command base\n@dataclass\nclass Command:\n    command_id: str = None\n    timestamp: datetime = None\n\n    def __post_init__(self):\n        self.command_id = self.command_id or str(uuid.uuid4())\n        self.timestamp = self.timestamp or datetime.utcnow()\n\n\n# Concrete commands\n@dataclass\nclass CreateOrder(Command):\n    customer_id: str\n    items: list\n    shipping_address: dict\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass AddOrderItem(Command):\n    order_id: str\n    product_id: str\n    quantity: int\n    price: float\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass CancelOrder(Command):\n    order_id: str\n    reason: str\n\n\n# Command handler base\nT = TypeVar(''T'', bound=Command)\n\nclass CommandHandler(ABC, Generic[T]):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def handle(self, command: T) -> Any:\n        pass\n\n\n# Command bus\nclass CommandBus:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._handlers: Dict[Type[Command], CommandHandler] = {}\n\n    def register(self, command_type: Type[Command], handler: CommandHandler):\n        self._handlers[command_type] = handler\n\n    async def dispatch(self, command: Command) -> Any:\n        handler = self._handlers.get(type(command))\n        if not handler:\n            raise ValueError(f\"No handler for {type(command).__name__}\")\n        return await handler.handle(command)\n\n\n# Command handler implementation\nclass CreateOrderHandler(CommandHandler[CreateOrder]):\n    def __init__(self, order_repository, event_store):\n        self.order_repository = order_repository\n        self.event_store = event_store\n\n    async def handle(self, command: CreateOrder) -> str:\n        # Validate\n        if not command.items:\n            raise ValueError(\"Order must have at least one item\")\n\n        # Create aggregate\n        order = Order.create(\n            customer_id=command.customer_id,\n            items=command.items,\n            shipping_address=command.shipping_address\n        )\n\n        # Persist events\n        await self.event_store.append_events(\n            stream_id=f\"Order-{order.id}\",\n            stream_type=\"Order\",\n            events=order.uncommitted_events\n        )\n\n        return order.id\n```\n\n### Template 2: Query Infrastructure\n\n```python\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import TypeVar, Generic, List, Optional\n\n# Query base\n@dataclass\nclass Query:\n    pass\n\n\n# Concrete queries\n@dataclass\nclass GetOrderById(Query):\n    order_id: str\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass GetCustomerOrders(Query):\n    customer_id: str\n    status: Optional[str] = None\n    page: int = 1\n    page_size: int = 20\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass SearchOrders(Query):\n    query: str\n    filters: dict = None\n    sort_by: str = \"created_at\"\n    sort_order: str = \"desc\"\n\n\n# Query result types\n@dataclass\nclass OrderView:\n    order_id: str\n    customer_id: str\n    status: str\n    total_amount: float\n    item_count: int\n    created_at: datetime\n    shipped_at: Optional[datetime] = None\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass PaginatedResult(Generic[T]):\n    items: List[T]\n    total: int\n    page: int\n    page_size: int\n\n    @property\n    def total_pages(self) -> int:\n        return (self.total + self.page_size - 1) // self.page_size\n\n\n# Query handler base\nT = TypeVar(''T'', bound=Query)\nR = TypeVar(''R'')\n\nclass QueryHandler(ABC, Generic[T, R]):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def handle(self, query: T) -> R:\n        pass\n\n\n# Query bus\nclass QueryBus:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._handlers: Dict[Type[Query], QueryHandler] = {}\n\n    def register(self, query_type: Type[Query], handler: QueryHandler):\n        self._handlers[query_type] = handler\n\n    async def dispatch(self, query: Query) -> Any:\n        handler = self._handlers.get(type(query))\n        if not handler:\n            raise ValueError(f\"No handler for {type(query).__name__}\")\n        return await handler.handle(query)\n\n\n# Query handler implementation\nclass GetOrderByIdHandler(QueryHandler[GetOrderById, Optional[OrderView]]):\n    def __init__(self, read_db):\n        self.read_db = read_db\n\n    async def handle(self, query: GetOrderById) -> Optional[OrderView]:\n        async with self.read_db.acquire() as conn:\n            row = await conn.fetchrow(\n                \"\"\"\n                SELECT order_id, customer_id, status, total_amount,\n                       item_count, created_at, shipped_at\n                FROM order_views\n                WHERE order_id = $1\n                \"\"\",\n                query.order_id\n            )\n            if row:\n                return OrderView(**dict(row))\n            return None\n\n\nclass GetCustomerOrdersHandler(QueryHandler[GetCustomerOrders, PaginatedResult[OrderView]]):\n    def __init__(self, read_db):\n        self.read_db = read_db\n\n    async def handle(self, query: GetCustomerOrders) -> PaginatedResult[OrderView]:\n        async with self.read_db.acquire() as conn:\n            # Build query with optional status filter\n            where_clause = \"customer_id = $1\"\n            params = [query.customer_id]\n\n            if query.status:\n                where_clause += \" AND status = $2\"\n                params.append(query.status)\n\n            # Get total count\n            total = await conn.fetchval(\n                f\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM order_views WHERE {where_clause}\",\n                *params\n            )\n\n            # Get paginated results\n            offset = (query.page - 1) * query.page_size\n            rows = await conn.fetch(\n                f\"\"\"\n                SELECT order_id, customer_id, status, total_amount,\n                       item_count, created_at, shipped_at\n                FROM order_views\n                WHERE {where_clause}\n                ORDER BY created_at DESC\n                LIMIT ${len(params) + 1} OFFSET ${len(params) + 2}\n                \"\"\",\n                *params, query.page_size, offset\n            )\n\n            return PaginatedResult(\n                items=[OrderView(**dict(row)) for row in rows],\n                total=total,\n                page=query.page,\n                page_size=query.page_size\n            )\n```\n\n### Template 3: FastAPI CQRS Application\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Depends\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n# Request/Response models\nclass CreateOrderRequest(BaseModel):\n    customer_id: str\n    items: List[dict]\n    shipping_address: dict\n\n\nclass OrderResponse(BaseModel):\n    order_id: str\n    customer_id: str\n    status: str\n    total_amount: float\n    item_count: int\n    created_at: datetime\n\n\n# Dependency injection\ndef get_command_bus() -> CommandBus:\n    return app.state.command_bus\n\n\ndef get_query_bus() -> QueryBus:\n    return app.state.query_bus\n\n\n# Command endpoints (POST, PUT, DELETE)\n@app.post(\"/orders\", response_model=dict)\nasync def create_order(\n    request: CreateOrderRequest,\n    command_bus: CommandBus = Depends(get_command_bus)\n):\n    command = CreateOrder(\n        customer_id=request.customer_id,\n        items=request.items,\n        shipping_address=request.shipping_address\n    )\n    order_id = await command_bus.dispatch(command)\n    return {\"order_id\": order_id}\n\n\n@app.post(\"/orders/{order_id}/items\")\nasync def add_item(\n    order_id: str,\n    product_id: str,\n    quantity: int,\n    price: float,\n    command_bus: CommandBus = Depends(get_command_bus)\n):\n    command = AddOrderItem(\n        order_id=order_id,\n        product_id=product_id,\n        quantity=quantity,\n        price=price\n    )\n    await command_bus.dispatch(command)\n    return {\"status\": \"item_added\"}\n\n\n@app.delete(\"/orders/{order_id}\")\nasync def cancel_order(\n    order_id: str,\n    reason: str,\n    command_bus: CommandBus = Depends(get_command_bus)\n):\n    command = CancelOrder(order_id=order_id, reason=reason)\n    await command_bus.dispatch(command)\n    return {\"status\": \"cancelled\"}\n\n\n# Query endpoints (GET)\n@app.get(\"/orders/{order_id}\", response_model=OrderResponse)\nasync def get_order(\n    order_id: str,\n    query_bus: QueryBus = Depends(get_query_bus)\n):\n    query = GetOrderById(order_id=order_id)\n    result = await query_bus.dispatch(query)\n    if not result:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Order not found\")\n    return result\n\n\n@app.get(\"/customers/{customer_id}/orders\")\nasync def get_customer_orders(\n    customer_id: str,\n    status: Optional[str] = None,\n    page: int = 1,\n    page_size: int = 20,\n    query_bus: QueryBus = Depends(get_query_bus)\n):\n    query = GetCustomerOrders(\n        customer_id=customer_id,\n        status=status,\n        page=page,\n        page_size=page_size\n    )\n    return await query_bus.dispatch(query)\n\n\n@app.get(\"/orders/search\")\nasync def search_orders(\n    q: str,\n    sort_by: str = \"created_at\",\n    query_bus: QueryBus = Depends(get_query_bus)\n):\n    query = SearchOrders(query=q, sort_by=sort_by)\n    return await query_bus.dispatch(query)\n```\n\n### Template 4: Read Model Synchronization\n\n```python\nclass ReadModelSynchronizer:\n    \"\"\"Keeps read models in sync with events.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, event_store, read_db, projections: List[Projection]):\n        self.event_store = event_store\n        self.read_db = read_db\n        self.projections = {p.name: p for p in projections}\n\n    async def run(self):\n        \"\"\"Continuously sync read models.\"\"\"\n        while True:\n            for name, projection in self.projections.items():\n                await self._sync_projection(projection)\n            await asyncio.sleep(0.1)\n\n    async def _sync_projection(self, projection: Projection):\n        checkpoint = await self._get_checkpoint(projection.name)\n\n        events = await self.event_store.read_all(\n            from_position=checkpoint,\n            limit=100\n        )\n\n        for event in events:\n            if event.event_type in projection.handles():\n                try:\n                    await projection.apply(event)\n                except Exception as e:\n                    # Log error, possibly retry or skip\n                    logger.error(f\"Projection error: {e}\")\n                    continue\n\n            await self._save_checkpoint(projection.name, event.global_position)\n\n    async def rebuild_projection(self, projection_name: str):\n        \"\"\"Rebuild a projection from scratch.\"\"\"\n        projection = self.projections[projection_name]\n\n        # Clear existing data\n        await projection.clear()\n\n        # Reset checkpoint\n        await self._save_checkpoint(projection_name, 0)\n\n        # Rebuild\n        while True:\n            checkpoint = await self._get_checkpoint(projection_name)\n            events = await self.event_store.read_all(checkpoint, 1000)\n\n            if not events:\n                break\n\n            for event in events:\n                if event.event_type in projection.handles():\n                    await projection.apply(event)\n\n            await self._save_checkpoint(\n                projection_name,\n                events[-1].global_position\n            )\n```\n\n### Template 5: Eventual Consistency Handling\n\n```python\nclass ConsistentQueryHandler:\n    \"\"\"Query handler that can wait for consistency.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, read_db, event_store):\n        self.read_db = read_db\n        self.event_store = event_store\n\n    async def query_after_command(\n        self,\n        query: Query,\n        expected_version: int,\n        stream_id: str,\n        timeout: float = 5.0\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Execute query, ensuring read model is at expected version.\n        Used for read-your-writes consistency.\n        \"\"\"\n        start_time = time.time()\n\n        while time.time() - start_time < timeout:\n            # Check if read model is caught up\n            projection_version = await self._get_projection_version(stream_id)\n\n            if projection_version >= expected_version:\n                return await self.execute_query(query)\n\n            # Wait a bit and retry\n            await asyncio.sleep(0.1)\n\n        # Timeout - return stale data with warning\n        return {\n            \"data\": await self.execute_query(query),\n            \"_warning\": \"Data may be stale\"\n        }\n\n    async def _get_projection_version(self, stream_id: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Get the last processed event version for a stream.\"\"\"\n        async with self.read_db.acquire() as conn:\n            return await conn.fetchval(\n                \"SELECT last_event_version FROM projection_state WHERE stream_id = $1\",\n                stream_id\n            ) or 0\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Separate command and query models** - Different needs\n- **Use eventual consistency** - Accept propagation delay\n- **Validate in command handlers** - Before state change\n- **Denormalize read models** - Optimize for queries\n- **Version your events** - For schema evolution\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t query in commands** - Use only for writes\n- **Don''t couple read/write schemas** - Independent evolution\n- **Don''t over-engineer** - Start simple\n- **Don''t ignore consistency SLAs** - Define acceptable lag\n\n## Resources\n\n- [CQRS Pattern](https://martinfowler.com/bliki/CQRS.html)\n- [Microsoft CQRS Guidance](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/patterns/cqrs)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-19T07:19:15.454Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Architect Agents needing advanced event-sourced system design capabilities using CQRS patterns.","zh":"Perfect for Architect Agents needing advanced event-sourced system design capabilities using CQRS patterns.","ja":"Perfect for Architect Agents needing advanced event-sourced system design capabilities using CQRS patterns.","ko":"Perfect for Architect Agents needing advanced event-sourced system design capabilities using CQRS patterns.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Arquitectura que necesitan capacidades de diseño de sistemas con origen de eventos avanzados utilizando patrones CQRS.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''architecture ayant besoin de capacités de conception de systèmes à source d''événements avancées utilisant des modèles CQRS.","de":"Perfekt für Architekturagenten, die erweiterte Ereignisquellensystem-Designfunktionen mit CQRS-Mustern benötigen.","pt":"Perfect for Architect Agents needing advanced event-sourced system design capabilities using CQRS patterns.","ru":"Perfect for Architect Agents needing advanced event-sourced system design capabilities using CQRS patterns.","ar":"Perfect for Architect Agents needing advanced event-sourced system design capabilities using CQRS patterns."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement Command Query Responsibility Segregation architectures, optimizing complex query scenarios and scaling reads independently from writes using event-sourced systems and high-performance reporting requirements.","zh":"Empowers agents to implement Command Query Responsibility Segregation architectures, optimizing complex query scenarios and scaling reads independently from writes using event-sourced systems and high-performance reporting requirements.","ja":"Empowers agents to implement Command Query Responsibility Segregation architectures, optimizing complex query scenarios and scaling reads independently from writes using event-sourced systems and high-performance reporting requirements.","ko":"Empowers agents to implement Command Query Responsibility Segregation architectures, optimizing complex query scenarios and scaling reads independently from writes using event-sourced systems and high-performance reporting requirements.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar arquitecturas de segregación de responsabilidad de comando de consulta, optimizando escenarios de consulta complejos y escalando lecturas de forma independiente a las escrituras utilizando sistemas con origen de eventos y requisitos de informes de alto rendimiento.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des architectures de ségrégation de responsabilité de commande de requête, optimisant les scénarios de requête complexes et mettant à l''échelle les lectures de manière indépendante des écritures en utilisant des systèmes à source d''événements et des exigences de rapport de haute performance.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten zur Implementierung von Architekturen zur Trennung von Befehls- und Abfrageverantwortung, optimiert komplexe Abfrageszenarien und skaliert Lesevorgänge unabhängig von Schreibvorgängen unter Verwendung von Ereignisquellensystemen und Hochleistungs-Berichterstellungsanforderungen.","pt":"Empowers agents to implement Command Query Responsibility Segregation architectures, optimizing complex query scenarios and scaling reads independently from writes using event-sourced systems and high-performance reporting requirements.","ru":"Empowers agents to implement Command Query Responsibility Segregation architectures, optimizing complex query scenarios and scaling reads independently from writes using event-sourced systems and high-performance reporting requirements.","ar":"Empowers agents to implement Command Query Responsibility Segregation architectures, optimizing complex query scenarios and scaling reads independently from writes using event-sourced systems and high-performance reporting requirements."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing CQRS patterns for separating read and write concerns","Scaling reads independently from writes in high-traffic applications","Building event-sourced systems for auditing and logging"],"zh":["Implementing CQRS patterns for separating read and write concerns","Scaling reads independently from writes in high-traffic applications","Building event-sourced systems for auditing and logging"],"ja":["Implementing CQRS patterns for separating read and write concerns","Scaling reads independently from writes in high-traffic applications","Building event-sourced systems for auditing and logging"],"ko":["Implementing CQRS patterns for separating read and write concerns","Scaling reads independently from writes in high-traffic applications","Building event-sourced systems for auditing and logging"],"es":["Implementar patrones CQRS para separar las preocupaciones de lectura y escritura","Escalabilidad de lecturas de forma independiente a las escrituras en aplicaciones de alto tráfico","Construir sistemas con origen de eventos para auditorías y registro de actividades"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des modèles CQRS pour séparer les préoccupations de lecture et d''écriture","Mettre à l''échelle les lectures de manière indépendante des écritures dans les applications à fort trafic","Construire des systèmes à source d''événements pour l''audit et la journalisation"],"de":["Implementierung von CQRS-Mustern zur Trennung von Lese- und Schreibbelangen","Skalierung von Lesevorgängen unabhängig von Schreibvorgängen in Anwendungen mit hohem Datenverkehr","Erstellung von Ereignisquellensystemen für Auditing und Protokollierung"],"pt":["Implementing CQRS patterns for separating read and write concerns","Scaling reads independently from writes in high-traffic applications","Building event-sourced systems for auditing and logging"],"ru":["Implementing CQRS patterns for separating read and write concerns","Scaling reads independently from writes in high-traffic applications","Building event-sourced systems for auditing and logging"],"ar":["Implementing CQRS patterns for separating read and write concerns","Scaling reads independently from writes in high-traffic applications","Building event-sourced systems for auditing and logging"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of CQRS architecture and event-sourced systems","May require additional infrastructure for high-performance reporting"],"zh":["Requires understanding of CQRS architecture and event-sourced systems","May require additional infrastructure for high-performance reporting"],"ja":["Requires understanding of CQRS architecture and event-sourced systems","May require additional infrastructure for high-performance reporting"],"ko":["Requires understanding of CQRS architecture and event-sourced systems","May require additional infrastructure for high-performance reporting"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la arquitectura CQRS y los sistemas con origen de eventos","Puede requerir infraestructura adicional para informes de alto rendimiento"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de l''architecture CQRS et des systèmes à source d''événements","Peut nécessiter une infrastructure supplémentaire pour les rapports de haute performance"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis der CQRS-Architektur und der Ereignisquellensysteme","Kann zusätzliche Infrastruktur für Hochleistungs-Berichterstellung erfordern"],"pt":["Requires understanding of CQRS architecture and event-sourced systems","May require additional infrastructure for high-performance reporting"],"ru":["Requires understanding of CQRS architecture and event-sourced systems","May require additional infrastructure for high-performance reporting"],"ar":["Requires understanding of CQRS architecture and event-sourced systems","May require additional infrastructure for high-performance reporting"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
